package com.darkshamanism.lotcscholar.services

@Suppress("LongMethod", "MagicNumber")
internal object StaticBooksData_ANTHOS {

    private fun _ANTHOS_0(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("!", "xSPULLERx", "~They Should not be bothered!~", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Abresi\"", "Devon Overland", "*The letter appears to be poorly written, by somone with little to no writting skill. The word 'Abresi' can be seen poorly labeled on the paper.*\nHail brother,  \n  As of the Twenty-First of The Grand Harvest 1444, I am nay able to go to Abresi, my home will sit empty for about an Elven Week, until I have means of returning. If yer wish to talk to me, do so via bird.\n*The writing becomes even worse at this point as the charcoal believed to be used to write the letter starts to break.*\n-Devon Hunter Overland, Rover of The Wolvengard.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Vladios\"", "Lomrun", "===================         \"Vladios\"\n===================\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nA book by:\nSamael Fleur\n\"What are you doing?\" A man shouted from behind the counter of a butchershop.\nA young man, in his early 20's glanced at the butcher with his blue eyes, quickly hiding the piece of steak behind his long black cloak.\nThe butcher leaned forward towards the \ncounter. He then reached below the counter and pulled something from underneath it.\nThe young man turned around in the blink of an eye, kicking motion into his feet and storming out of the butchershop. The butcher had taken out a handcrossbow.\nAs the young man, Valdios, ran out of the butchershop the butcher shot an arrow at Valdios, missing him by just an inch.\nValdios looked up as he was running through the streets of Kralta. It had started raining, and it was soaking his clothes. \nBehind him, he heard the butcher still yelling and screaming in pure anger. \nValdios smirked widely. He had stolen a steak from the butcher. \nValdios finally reached his house. He extended his right hand and just about as he was to open the door, the door\nopened and bumped into his hand. \"Ouch~!\" he yelled out. \nValdios looked right into his mother's eyes. He noticed she had been crying again.\n\"M-.. Mom. A kind noble sir gave me this steak. We'll be less hungry tonight.\" \nHis mother wiped her eyes, and\nwrapped her arms around Valdios whilst whispering into his ears. \n\"I miss your father so much. Why did he have to die? Why didn't the other soldier get killed by the orc instead?\nWhy, oh.. Why!\" \nValdios pushed his mother off of him.\nHis voice trembling, and an angry expression was seen on his face.\n\"Stop talking about it! Stop it!\" \nHis mother looked at him, shocked by the outrage of her son.\n\"You can't forget him, can you? He was a coward!\" Valdios screamed.\nA guard stopped in his path. He turned towards the scream and walked up to Vladios and his mother. \"What's going on here?\" The guard said, as he looked at Valdios and his mother. He soon recognized the young man, as the butcher had complained to the \nguard about a young man in a black cloak  had stolen his meat.\n\"Hey\" The guard said. \"Why don't you come over here? Don't run away.\" The guard reached for his sword, unsheathing it.\nValdios nodded his head, slowly walking over to the guard.\n\"What can I do for you?\" Vladios responded.\n\"Look, you can give me the meat and receive a fine or we can do this the hard way, and I'll have to take it by force.\" \nVladios sighed, trying to explain to the guard\n\nthat his family did not have any money, and they desperately needed some food.\n\"Mhm-... In that case, keep it. I'll refund the butcher the costs.\" the guard told Vladios.\n\"You would do that for me?\" Vladios smiled, and his face seemed uplifting.\n\"No.\" The guard responded, whilst laughing out loud.\n\"Give it to me, or face punishment.\"\nVladios rubbed his chin, thinking about his next move. He sighed briefly, moving both hands behind his waist and pulling two small daggers from it.\nThe guard responded by lifting his sword, gripping it with two hands. Raising the sword above his head and swinging the sword at Vladios' chest. Vladios jumps backwards, throwing a dagger at the guard. \nWho in returns steps to the side quickly. \nHowever, the dagger still hit him in the process. It pierced through the small leather armor he was wearing. \"Y-.. YOU LITTLE BASTARD!\" \nThe guard pulled the dagger from his left shoulder, dropping it on the floor. \"You're going to pay for this.\" \nThe guard ran forward towards Vladios, his sword ready to stab. \n\"Stop it, you're making this worse on yourself!\" His mother cried out, as she ran towards Vladios, hugging him in the process and kissing on his forehead.\nSuddenly it got silent.\nThe birds stopped chirping and the wind stopped blowing. It felt as if the world had come to an end. \nVladios felt an incredible pain in his stomach and he moved his hand down to his stomach. He gasped, he felt blood.\nThe guard couldn't stop in time, and stabbed both Vladios and his mother whilst she was hugging her son. \nHis mother looked him in the eyes.\n\"I-.. I love you.\" She said, as she took her final breath.\nVladios eyes started to tear up. He had not apologized to his mother about his sudden outrage. \nHe started to feel more and more drowsy as well, as he was losing so much blood from the wound. A minute after his mother died, Vladios died as well, with a\nfeeling of guilt and the stolen steak still on him. \nA book by Samael Fleur.\n\nThe moral of this book is to always apologize and kiss your loved ones. You never know when it's the last time you'll see them.", ""),
        StaticBook("%Y&!%\$^&*?!", "SapphireShard", " adafjwfipojwfpeoijewpoigjfwpgfjewprgjieiorgjeiogjeiogrvjemrgivoljergibovemjgoejgeoiprnyjerybreyrevjgtpoiwektwopejowpesikrvowperkiwvoprikweopirfwpfiwepfkwpoegfjwegwgggggggbgggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggg\n fefwfojwpefjwoipefjwpefjwpoifjwpoiefjwioefjewhnjghoeuigheiogjgvbjmeopigjemgpeiogjepogrke  egreg egre gege ge gergergege ggegegrege gegeg", ""),
        StaticBook("'ealing Soup", "Tradional Recipe", "'urt 'alfling Soup", ""),
        StaticBook("'Electromancy'", "Gauldrim Irongut", "\n\n\nElECTROMANcY\n\nby Gauldrim Ir0nguT\nElectromancy is the fine art of controlling the magic of the gods themselves.\n\nIt is the element of the heavens: the God's express their wrath from the heavens through lightning.\n\nElectromancy is the harnessing of the heavens by a mortal for their own\nends. But before you learn, you must know the origin of the power.\n\nThe power, comes from cake.\n\nYou are now probably wondering, \"what the hell\", well you must think about it. Every power has a source. Electromancy comes from cake.\n\nIn fact, the God's\npull their power from a special buttercake which we will detail later on in this book.\n\nThis buttercake provides the energy and the fun and happiness to vent pure energy in the form of lightning.\n\nSo, in the beginning, you MUST bake and eat the cake!\nSo, if you are willing, turn the page and learn the secrets of the divine buttercake.\n\nBe ready to learn and turn the page!\n\nYes! Turn the page!\nNo! Piss off and give the book to a real chef!\nDivine Buttercake of the Gods!\n\nINGREDIENTS:\n2 blocks butter\n1 cup sugar\n3 eggs\n3 cups flour\n1 teaspoon yeast\nvanilla\n2/3 cups good milk\nlemon rind\n1. Find lightning bolt shaped cake tin. Imperative! The shape of the cake provides the power!\n\n2. Put the butter, sugar and lemon rind all together and beat until fluffy, like a storm cloud.\n\n3. Add eggs, one at a time and beating until the eggs are mixed\n4. Add milk and stir to combine.\n\n5. Spread the mixture into the cake tin! Evenly or your powers will be unbalanced.\n\n6. Bake for one hour and remove from heat.\n\n7. Allow the cake to stand for a six hundred count until cool.\n8. Dust with sugar and serve while still warm.\n\n9. Enjoy your new found cake-derived power.\n\nThere you have compeleted your electromancy cake and have the power of the God's themselves.\n\nAnd now you see why everyone enjoys \"Divine Buttercake\".\nIn case by know you didn't notice, we haven't actually reached the proper instructions, so skip ahead and start reading how to use the magic itself.\n\nYou must eat a cake before each casting or it will not work.\n\nYou will end up quite fat eventually.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIn case you didn't notice...\nThis has nothing to do with magic.\n\nWell it is to do with the magic of baking.\n\nYou fool.\n\nThank you for the Money.", ""),
        StaticBook("'Elkin Nage", "JoshIsTooCool", "Conjuration, the forgotten art.\n\n\nOrman seeks you.\n\n\nSeek the Delvers, seek Orman.\n\n*the remainder of the note is scribbled out.*", ""),
        StaticBook("'Land Contract'", "Sunny Adelban", "Land Contract\n-----------------\nThis plot has been transferred Gat 'Sunny' Collard Adelban from the Treasury for the sum of 1,500 minas and a set of armor.\nTerms & conditions\n0----------------\n1. This plot is non-transferable\n2. Exterior renovations must be approved\n3. Opening a business must be approved\n~~Signed\n\nTuv\n\n~~Signed\n\nGat Collard Adelban", ""),
        StaticBook("'Magical Book'", "MinecraftMish", "The Void, Mana, what are they? The Void, it is endless. With the void is mana, which you can use to create 'fake' elements of some types, for example Water, Fire, Air, Earth. Mana is basically 'life energy', but it may have some hidden secrets, which-\ncould lead to immortality. \n\nStaffs, and Wands-\nStaffs and Wands function as a point to focus on when creating something. They are not essential, and one could use hands, but be careful you can harm yourself", ""),
        StaticBook("'The Zero'", "[Hooded] Mythras Sylvari", "Chapter 1\n      Scared Moon\nAfter many atempts on achieving true happiness.. I am unable to continue my journey with others.. Its been years since I've seen or heard from Zero.. Ive begin to think that he is gone forever. If i could remeber where he last \nwent off to I'd know where to start.. Abresi is full of different people and which none has heard of a wisp.. Ive gone to thnik there is no hope me and him will be reunited again..Times out in this world alone has no place for someone like me.. No family \nor friends. where do i belong in this world.. What and who am i to anyone.. \n\nEnd of Chapter 1  \n\nChapter 2 \nFragments of Sorrow\n\nMore days have passed by and still nothing new.. I have met some new people but I still question on who to trust... these voices in my head wont stop... ive gone too many days with them and grown not to tell anyone..\nAs trust is very thin with everyone. It is hard to know if everyone can be trusted.. The days are getting harder with the voice.. i dont know how much i can take of there talking.. they talk about trying to become one... I dont know how much they are \nplanning and who are they.. what are they...\nI must know what do they want and why are they in my head..\n\nEnd of Chapter 2\n\n Chapter 3\n Night of Fate\nI've begin to listen close to there ideas,\nthey are not bad..\ntheir goal is very clear.. they want to become whole as one and stronger.. but they need a vessal... My thoughts as the power is what I would love to gain the powerto protect everyone. but deep down i feel theres something else..\n\nChapeter 4\n   Fragments\nIts been month, Ive grown to understand there ambitions. I have also gotten to get there names. There are 7 fragments of them. Eta meaning Failure, Gamma meaning Deceit,Delta meaning Logic,Iota meaning Memory,\nTheta meaning Trust,\nSigma meaning Ambition, Omega meaning Rage and Epsilon meaning Failure. All of those meanings are something us a being have.. Is that why they want to become whole.. Sigma seems to be the leader matches the meaning of ambition.. \nChapter 5\n Off The edge \n", ""),
        StaticBook("(( If Found ))", "CorprlSkyler", "(( This inventory and book belong to CorprlSkyler. Please return to such as soon as possible; message and inform me of your finding of it. \nThank you. ))\nRise of the King of Anthos.\nIntroduction:\ngetting poorer. \ne", ""),
        StaticBook("((Untitled))", "everblue2er101", "It is time, for the Humans to fall. For too long have they sought control over the entirety of Anthos, seeking to take and hold what is not theirs. All races have felt the pain that comes with the rule of sons of Horen and no longer seek to stand silent. \nWith the Empire gone, the time is nigh to strike back against such blatant oppression and fight for what belongs to all others...\n\n((It is clearly unfinished and unsigned))", ""),
        StaticBook("** A Scroll **", "Head-Master Mythras", "If thy finds this tome, thy shall seek apprenticeship to thry magic. Thy shall do the following tests.\n\n1. Thy shall bring me two books.\n\n2. Thy shall seek Mythras, and ask thee for more information.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n--< The Mystic Mage >--", ""),
        StaticBook("*A letter*", "Salavin", "Dear Evelyn,\nI'm sorry, but I feel as our relationship can continue no longer. I rarely every see you, and you kissed somone else... Somone brought it to my attention you may only like me for my wealth. I just can't stand you'd betray me as you have. -S", ""),
        StaticBook("*A Message*", "_Kraal_", "\"To my Child,\n\n I have yet to master the power of Illusion, I feel my strength almost doubling as I get more knowledge in the Arcane arts. In time I can forfill your wishes to become an Illusionist... In time...\"\n\n((One month until I ca\nn make a teacher app, hold in there!))", ""),
        StaticBook("*A note to Faiz*", "'Panther'", "Dear Faiz,", ""),
        StaticBook("*A note*", "wardog4445", "Elorna, Lenniel'onn, I write this in the case that I do not have a chance to see you.\nI love you both very much, Avern'len", ""),
        StaticBook("*A note*", "I_Am_Still_Alive", "I would like a blade forged of black ferrum (if unable to be forged with black ferrum, regular iron works well). The blade should match the hilt, which will be included. The sword should be made for one-handed uses. If possible, carvings of flora and \nfauna upon the blade would be liked, but it is not required. I will leave you to decide the amount of minas I will pay, within reason.\n\nThank you.\n\n- Oropher Deathsbane.\nAramil's Logbook~\nHow LogBook Works:\nNow it may be hard to do this while taking many orders so the best thing to do is just write:\n*It is required that you format your logbook like this or you will get 10% less of your full pay. This helps Spike log his sellings and profits, also helps receive your pay faster!*\nWeek Seven Logs~:\nValiant's Drinks And Recipes~:\nCarrot Cider:\nFuzzy Beer:\n\nSealover's Whiskey:\n\nBlack Dragon Ale:\nMead:\nValiant's House Ale:\n\nValiant's Wine:\nHoney Wine:\nPomegranate Wine:\nRed Grape Wine:\n", ""),
        StaticBook("*A Note*", "Shaela", "*The following page is scribed in imaculate handwriting*\n      \n      Meet me at the lakes region of the Dwarven lands.\n  ~Shaela Sacatria\n\n§-((-465, 65, 1155 ))", ""),
        StaticBook("*A note*", "AnoN_EX", "((This is for when you decide to play Syb))\n*The note has a few specks of blood on it*\n\"Dear Syb, Lark invited us to his wedding in a few days time. -Alp\"", ""),
        StaticBook("*A Note*", "Rexx8", "Dear Vulathri,\n\nPlease meet me in Lenniel. I have something important to tell you.\n\n-Ahlysaaria", ""),
        StaticBook("*A Notepad*", "Vex Faelcyn", "-Charles Napier\nName: Charles Napier\nName: Panther/Lucas\nName: Jakir Axem\nName: Brand Gores\nName: Dingo\nName: Corvo and Crona\nName: Leap", ""),
