        StaticBook("[!]Neatly Folded", "Sir Edward Meadowbloom-Armas", "Hello, Sir..\n   This is Edward, and before I tell you anything, I'd like to meet somewhere.. Where things can be explained. I apologize for any inconvenience and would like you to send one last letter with the location that you would like to meet and when\nI will not be able to reply, however. But I will be on time.\n\n              Thank you.\n  ~Sir Edward Meadowbloom.", ""),
        StaticBook("[4/16/13]", "TEEbrown", "Written by Remembrancer Bazian Grandaxe.\n\nHigh Princess Titania of Malinor brings gifts to the newly crowned King of Urguan Thorin Grandaxe. The gift containing many gems, precious metals and homely goods such as salted meats and breads.\n\nKing Thorin send\n-s invitation to the High Princess to his corination next elven day in an attempt to improve relations with the nation.\n\n[4/16/13]", ""),
        StaticBook("[4/17/13]", "TEEbrown", "Written by Remembrancer Bazian Grandaxe.\n\nThe corination of King Thorin Grandaxe begins with Farren Starbreaker placing the crown on his head.\n\nKing Thorin swears the oath that all kings must swear.\n\nThe two lords present, Telchar Azaghul and Farren Starbreaker, make blood oaths to King Thorin.\n\nThe leaders of Malinor, the elves, Karakatua, the kharajyr, and Oren, the humans attended this coronation.\nAll brought gifts, Oren brought gifts of gold and iron.\nItem: Armor Set and Sword", ""),
        StaticBook("[[Description]]", "SirSmithers", "*Upon the old, battered wooden table sits a series of iron cogs of varying height, width and thickness. Each and every one of the strange ribbed wheels is decorated with intricately carved spirals and swirls. There are slightly more than twenty cogs in\nall, each one the same size as one of the cogs that were previously laid upon the brightsteel anvil in the Elefer'bilokal workshop. The design of the gears has obviously been improved upon; each gear shines in the light like a mirror, buffed and polished\nto a finish reminiscent of the unparalleled craftsmanship of the Mali'aheral. The gears are fabricated out of a wrought iron, making them both more durable and more solid than any of the previous gears. A small letter lies upon the table, reading...\n\"Mr. Sullas, your first batch is complete.", ""),
        StaticBook("[Flower of Love]", "OOC Info", "((Rasmot Item, Flower of Love Info & Rules:\n\n1. When you possess the flower, you will fall in love with the first person you see.\n2. You will want to give the Flower of Love to that person.\n3. When you have given away the Flower, the enchantment will be\nbroken and you will return to normal.\n4. The next person who touches the Flower falls in love with the first person they see, and so on.", ""),
        StaticBook("[Poetry]Realm", "Amfionas", "     The Collected\n          Works\n            Of\n\n     Anecia Sorrow\n\n       Volume IV\n\n\n      \"A Peak into the\n            Realm\"\nThere was no lucidity,\nFor as they'd encompassed me,\nI felt my senses leaving me,\nThey'd slit my wrists bloody open.\n\nI've never given..\nMuch thought on the act of death,I've never had a reason,\n-Until now- to repent.\nThe darkness had swallowed me whole,\nImperceptible as it was,\nWhence the suffered insanity\nHad breached into my skull,\nI knew then, that I was out of luck.\nThey tugged on the cadence,\nOf my heart,\nI felt the pain pervading,\nAll about...\n\n\nIt was hard to understand,\nThe monster's way of locution,\nBut oddly \n-Since I had no doubt I'd perish.-\nI attained full appreciation...\nI closed my lids,\nWaiting to return,\nTo relapse,\nBefore it was too late.\nI sighed beginning,\nTo accept\nThe act of faith,\n\n\nEven if it was unbearable...\nAnd... Insuperable...\nI opened my eyes,\nStaring into the eyes,\nOf the bloodthirsty beast,\nWaiting to be tortured,\nWaiting to be eaten..\n\nCopied by Larky at the 14th of Malin's Welcome,1451\nVaerhaven", ""),
        StaticBook("[Poetry]Sanct.", "Amfionas", "     The Collected\n          Works\n            Of\n\n     Anecia Sorrow\n\n       Volume II\n\n\n      \"Sanctuary\"\nShould I deny my courtly love,\nFor a man who is forever deceased?\nShould I give up on the fallacy,\nSo that maybe I'll finally find peace?\n\nFor thee & only thee,\nBlessed be my love!\nIn return, shower me,\nWith thy divine beauty.\nEmbrace me, 'til the end of time,\nBe mine & only mine.\nOf pure serenity & folly,\nOf agonizing pain & melancholy.\n\n\n\"Time bears no fruit for my delusions.\"\nThis I uttered to Holly, in warbled locution.\nShould I give up on my courtly love\nFor a man I will never meet?\nShould I simply reject the fallacy\n& make a hasty retreat?\nA map that feeds me an endless trail\nLike an elven checkers board game,\nI am lost, I am shamed.\n\nMy love & I will never meet\nFor it is not our destiny,& so the hymn echoes across the sea:\n\"There is no sanctuary for you & me.\"\n\nCoppied by Larky at the 14th of Malin's Welcome, 1451\n\nVaerhaven", ""),
        StaticBook("[Req] Hysagi", "CaptainSheepy", "MC Name: WaZeBoomBox\n\nRP Name: Hysagi Shuuhei \n\nRequest: Either completely new outfit that would make him look smart or some new robes that would make him look magical.\n\nColour:  White Blue Gol", ""),
