        StaticBook("A", "Rurikk", "*the journal in your hands is covered with tanned leather and tied shut with a leather chord, branded upon the cover is: \"A Huntsman's Guide to Surviving the Wilderness\"\n\nIntro:\n\nHello everyone, this book was written by an experienced survivalist in hopes that all who wish to venture out into the wilds will be prepared for the trials and hardships they may face along the way.\n\nAfter reading this booklet you will be able to\nsurvive on your own without any extra aid from outside sources. \n\nNow let us begin then.\nChapter One \"What You\nWill Need\":\n\nThe most important items that a survivalist needs to well... survive, are the tools that he/she either finds or brings with him/her on the way to their journey into the wilds.\nHere is a list of helpful items:\n\n1. Flint & Steel\n2. A Small Hatchet\n3. Preserving Salts\n4. Needle and Thread\n5. Skinning Knife\n6. Waterproofed Satchel\n7. Small Fishing Hook\n8. Sturdy Clothing\n9. Sufficient Rations\n10. Common Sense\nChapter Two \"What To Expect\":\n\nOnce you have acquired all the supplies listed in the previous chapter you are now ready to begin your journey.\n\nFirst things first, to survive in the wilds you need to know at least a basic background of the\nenvironment you plan on venturing into, such as weather patterns, what kinds of vegetation grows in the region, as well as the different beasts that make their home in the area.\n\nRemember to study maps and acquire as much information about the region if \npossible before you decide to make the trip. Failing to do so could result in dismemberment or even death.\n\nOnce you have done your research and acquired all of your supplies for the trek into the unknown, you will finally be ready to begin.\nChapter Three \"Setting Up Camp\"\n\nIn this chapter you will learn the basics of setting up a safe and reliable camp site to live in during your stay in the wilderness.\n\nOnce you have found a suitable place to set up camp, you need to make\nsure that the area you have picked is in fact a safe place to stay in. To do so, please check off everything on this list:\n\n1. Is it dry and warm?\n2. Does it protect you from the elements?\n3. Is it close to a source of water?\n4. Can you easily find it if\nlost?\n5. Does it protect you from unwanted visitors?\n\nIf all of the above checks off as okay, then you have done a great job in picking out a location for your campsite!\nChapter Four \"Exploring The Wilderness\"\n\nSo far so good, if you've gotten this far then that means you haven't killed yourself yet. Good job!\n\nIn this chapter we will be going over the basics of wilderness exploration.\n\nWhen an experienced survivalist arrives in uncharted lands, they usually do one or more of these things listed:\n\n1. Find a high place and survey the lands before you, taking notes of key land marks in the immediate area.\n\n\n2. Preparing themselves for long treks away from the safety of their camps, make sure to pack extra food, you may be away from home for a while!\n\n3. Preparing for all possible outcomes, make sure to think of everything that could happen while you are away\nfrom the camp; things such as being captured by jungle pigmy's to the occasional bear destroying your camp can easily be prevented if you just prepare ahead of time.\n\nCarrying out with at least one of these tips can make your life out in the wilderness\nmuch easier, and could possibly save your life.\nChapter Five \"Returning Home\":\n\nCongratulations, you've survived your trip and are ready to break camp and return home with a multitude of new stories from your trip.\n\nRemember that when you are ready to leave to make sure you try to leave\nthings just as they were when you first arrived at the location you chose for your camp.\n\nOnce you have finished returning things as they once were, you can then begin to journey back home. Make sure not to forget any trinkets or trophies that you might\nhave found while exploring the wilderness!\n\nThanks for reading \nA little bit about the Author:\n\nCharles Silverblade:\nCharles was born in the small farming town of Riven, where his cousin Uthor Silverblade helped to raise him and teach him to become a fine young man in terms of Oren society. When he turned 18 years of \nage, he enlisted in the Oren Military as a conscript and quickly ascended the ranks of hierarchy in the military until he finally acquired the title of Ser and received Knighthood in the Order of the Red Dragon. Charles now lives with his Wife and four\nchildren with the rest of the Silverblade family who reside in the Duchy of Furnestock.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Battered Book", "Patriotic_Fool", "*The old, weathered tome is full of writing. The title reads 'Raven Manifesto'.*\n\n\nThere are two types of beings; good and evil. Any alignment results from a mixture of these two essences. A pendulum swinging from side to side, one being the most heinous evil, the other being the purest good.\nThere is a term many are familiar with - Justice. Should the scale be tipped too far in one direction, Justice is the force that returns the scale back to neutral. A problem arises, however, when the scale is tipped too far in one direction, for too long.\nFocusing on being good and just is the most noble of goals, and these good actions allow negative ones to be cancelled out. What if one commits horrendous crimes, and continually escapes Justice?  What if the scale is never balanced; Justice is never\nserved? The Ravens are Justice. We right the wrongs of evil men, and they suffer as their victims have suffered. The Law is an instrument that allows for criminals to escape Justice, and it allows corrupt men to profit from the demise of others.\nThere is only one Law, and that is of the Ravens. \n\n=Disobedience is Justice=\nBy atoning for the wrongs of the past, the Ravens open a path for salvation and restitution for the criminals. By paying for what they have done, the wicked free themselves and are restored to the natural balance. \nThrough their suffering, they are freed.\n\n=Cruelty is Grace=\n==Edicts of the Raven==\n\n1.  A Raven must have absolute loyalty to the Ravens, and they must always come first, regardless of all else.\n\n2. A Raven must never kill an Innocent.\n3. No Raven shall harm or steal from another Raven, we are brothers and sisters. \n\n4. Secrecy is paramount, for the Ravens do not go around proclaiming their affiliations.\n\nAbove all, our secrets and status must be kept close to a Raven’s heart, even through torture, even to the grave.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A Beginning...", "The Drunk Wizard...", "\nHello students of AL!\ninto my training years ago.", ""),
        StaticBook("A book.", "Joe_Blackman", "Ah, Conjuration; the rarest Arcane Art known... Well, it won't be rare anytime soon. Of course, once you begin to learn the art, you will be reffered to as a \"Conjurer. A conjurer is an individual who access the Void and construct living organisms which\nare fueled wholly by the mana of their creator. Through the depths of thhe Void, a Conjuration user will be able to summon almight creatures and pretty flowers into reality. Alas, as a conjurer you will be constantly delivering your mana for virtually\nevery second your ersatz summon exists. You will soon come to a realisation that Conjuration uses the most of your mana unlike any other Arcane Science. In order to uphold the existance of your faux creature in reality, you must feed it precisely\na great portion of mana to flow within it. As the creature you summon will be downright complex, the process of building it within the Void will be rather tiresome and there is a good chance you may be drained completely of your mana until you reach\nunconsciousness, as tha thappens, your beast will be removed from the physical realm and be sent to Void. Yes, you can decide to desist the flow of mana beforehand, in which case the fauna will vanish to no consequence.\nNow, for you to construct an organism within the void, you must first have a sharp and great understanding of both the interior and exterior of the living entity you wish to formulate. This can be achieved by oftenly killing and dissecting the creature\nyou wish to summon. However, it is also best to keep very detailed anatomical diagrams of the beast you wish to conjure. Remember to have notes on the animal's exterior, interior and bone structure if you want to have an accurate understanding of it.\nIn the opaque void, the fabrics which generate the entity are summoned bone by bone, organ by organ and layer by layer the Conjurer crafts and sculpts their being into an exact copy of their previously existing self. As a result of poor research, the \nConjurer may fail at this point, producing a being unlike of its true and real form will result in an even and revolting entity which would certainly turn to a sludge once conjured. After a while of practice, the Conjurer would be able to summon the \ncreature exactly how it was before it was slain and have it formed with sheer stability. As it will behave akin to the life form it represents, it will follow its creator's commands.\nAs a Conjurer myself,  would highly reccomend you begin studying roses, then petite insects until you grow stronger and confident enough to move on to study and conjure anything larger.\nThink of Conjuration as art. You are the painter and the Void is the frame. What you paint in that frame will need to look beautiful and make sense in the judge's eyes. Bear in mind that the \"judge\" is the physical realm. If the judge thinks your work of \nart is good, it wll be acceped and be brought into reality. However, if it's horrible, it will be stamped on and crushed and it will appear as an abomination the mortal plane and you will be smakced in the face for your poor effort, that smack will tire \nyou. Keep practising and your artistic skills will improve and the judge will continue to accept your art. Overtime, your frame will expand (this, being your mana) and leave you open to produce larger paintings which the judge can view. Be warned though,\nthe larger the harder.\n\nAnd yes, you can produce hybrid fauna. I'll that for you to grasp the concept of that alone.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Broken Wall", "Amfionas", "The Wall Shatters\n------------------\nShared by Menos the Ranger\n\nI was patrolling the ice wall that used to block all contacts with the icy north plains.\n\nThe night was cold and I decided I would spend the night in \nruins filled with sculls and moss.\n\nThere where a few travellers nearby but we shared not many words.\n\nI was wandering what was the least unpleasant place to sleep, when I heard a thundering crack.\nWe all knew what it was.\n\nAfter a brief patrol we found that the wall was broken in a single place. \n\nThe same hole remains today as the only entrance to the north.\n\nThe wall was impenetrable\nand yet somehow it was breached. \n\nWe never found what was the force that caused that.\n\nArriving there we found many men gathering to investigate.\n\nMen with the same \nideas as us.\n\nJust beyond the hole there where stone ruins of a single structure.\n\nAn old man was there to greet us.\n\nHe kept insisting that we should depart and that we where in \nimmediate danger.\n\nWe, of course, did not heed his call.\n\nThe Flays where asking where asking for valuables and gold but he had none.\nAfter some time The Prince August Flay decided to depart.\nThere where dwarven legionnaires and orenian troops. Many where simple travelers or self-proclaimed protectors, like my self.\n\nI believe I even saw a woman with no armor there. But perhaps I was wrong.\nIt did not take long to understand why he insisted we leave.\n\nThe tribes that lived beyond the wall started raining arrows at us.\nTheir location hidden by the dense snow and clouds that existed on the height of the stone arch.\nMany of got wounded, and soon we were divided. Half took refuge in the stone ruin that the old man claimed to be his home. Others stayed outside trying to guard us.\n\nHe kept on telling the same thing. \"Leave now while you still can.\"\nWe still did not listen. I was trying to retyrn fire while taking cover in the entrance of the ruins, and dashed aside in the last minute when the snow covered the entrance. \nWhile others tried to remove the snow that blocked us from the outside world,\nI stepped further inside the underground ruins.\n\nThe old man had a pretty cosy house, with a fireplace and about half a dozen bookcases. Many of the troops that had remained started scavenging for anything usefull\nthrowing books all over the small crowded area.\n\nI believe they where men of the teutonic order judging by their uniforms.\nThere was an average sized fireplace and a small fire as well on the side burning on a stone altar of sorts.\nThe old man warned us again, but this time to avoid the fire. \n\n\"For it is Dragon fire, and it burns everything.\" where his words.\n\nI decided to take care of the wounded being one of the few with any medical skills there.\nOr perhaps because I was one of the even fewer that cared.\nA man or a \"being\" that was with us was bleeding heavily from the stomach.\n\nPurple blood was spraying all over the place. He was a rare occurence and one of a kind.\nI knew that stiching him up would not be enough and that I required some medicine to prevent the infection.\n\nI asked the old man, which was claiming to be named \"Aruzond\".\nHe gave me a leaf from a rare plant that grows on the north.\nIt did not do much to the wounded man. But I am certain to this day that it was due to the man's strange nature and that the leaf would have a different result in another patient. By the time I was finished and watched the man die, I decided it was time \nto retreat. The old man yet stayed there despite the dangers as long as with the teutonic order and others.\n\nTwo drakes had appeared in the mean time but I am uncertain of when exactly. They obliterated most of us and seemed as allied\nto the bandits as they where not fearing them, neither were the drakes attacking them. Dwarven legionnaires were still fighting and my pride took the better of me. I would be the last man to leave. This ruthless black creature most call as a drake \ndescended down in the end and teared me almost apart with its jaws.\n\nIt's unbelievable the monks rescued me still alive and an even greater miracle that I was still half conscious.  \nDo not underestimate the North. We know a mere fraction of what it still hides.\n\nWritten by Larky at the 30th of the Deep Cold,1450\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A common letter", "[Vanguard] Sync", "Eilthana,\n\nSorry for the short conversation. I had to leave that city before.. well that doesn't matter. You should visit Malinor sometime! If you don't know the way I'd gladly show you, err.. though I'd have to meet you outside Abresi. \n-Nikolas Synclair", ""),
        StaticBook("A crumpled note.", "Delzio Alor", "Dear Artimec,\nI've been informed by someone that you are an illusionist. I would very much like to speak with you if you have the chance, perhaps we could meet near the fountain in Abresi, Thank you.\n\n\n*A small signature in jet black ink reads \"Delzio Alor\"*", ""),
        StaticBook("A Damaged Diary", "SpamShok", "Day 1 - Sure was a hell of a walk here, finnally made it to this \"Kingston\" place. Hope it's as good as they say. Lost track of the date on the walk, will have to ask someone the date later.\n\nDay 2 - Had to sleep on the damn street last night because\nI'm piss-poor, surprised I even had anything left on me over the night, maybe this place is as good as it seems.\n\nDay 3 - Met some guy named Toby Williams today, he seemed nice enough and told me about the Valigants or something? Next thing\nI knew I was traveling to who know's where following this guy telling me he might have a place for me in their ranks, would be nice to actually sleep in a bed and get some food if nothing else. He also introduced me to James Lillis, don't know what to\nthink of him yet.\n\nDay 4((5/30/2013)) - Got accepted in the Valiants today, feel really honored to even be allowed with these guys. Nothing really beats a warm bed either. This Guren guy seems alright, but they warned me about some guy I shouldn't get on\nthe bad side of, unfortuneately he's also training me.\n\nDay 5((5/31/2013)) -Boring day, nothing worth writing about.\n\nDay 6((6/1/2013)) - Had some crazy shit today, I wake up and go outside, next thing I know Dvari is screami \nabout going to war. I end up at some damned outpost with rains of arrows flying onto our heads. As far as I know all of the Valiants made it out of it, they say we won the war but I can't even tell. The outpost is decimated, but the others were slaughtere\nDay 7((6/2/13)) - Heard something about a dragon today, probably just a rumor but who knows. Met some guy who wanted to join the guys at the Dreadfort, didn't think to ask for his name until it was to late.\n\nDay 11((6/6/2013)) - Lost this damn thing,\nfinnally found it again. Been boring last couple days, hope something happens.\n\n*a large portion of the page is torn.*\n\"Watch your back\" is srawled aross the page.\n\n\n*Another  note is scrawled across.* \"Serouisly, this stuff you 'gave' me all throughout t\nhis site, is serouisly going to help!\"", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dark Message", "Grant Kamura", "Dear Khel Oussana,\nYour daughter, the little black fuck you assaulted the darling lady earlier, will die. ", ""),
        StaticBook("A Deed", "CorprlSkyler", "This property, upon the road that the Treasurey is upon, just North of such, and East of the Salvian Clinic ((salvus_home6)) has been purchased by Gunnar Valorheart temporarily until full payment has been given. Upon this date ((8/30)), a total of one\nhundred minas has been payed with the requirements of three hundred mina per Elven Week until fully payed off with the total price of 700 mina. If Gunnar Valorheart fails to pay a single payment, he will be evicted and all property within will now be seen\nas Kingdom property with all rights to it. This selling and loan has been given out by the authority of Jericho Rylin, Godfather of Relenkai Bedevere-- the King of Salvus-- and Conte di Sunfall.\n\n[i.imgur.com/sL5PYFk.png]\n-A wax seal can be found here, it\nbearing two white wings with an orange background.-", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dream Theory", "mjlover231", "As I walked into the Library searching for a new book. Then one caught my eye. Just an old brown book with like neon blue writing which read: \"The Dream Theory.\"\nbook\" I asked. \"Of course, lad! Jus' make sure to bring it back\" He responded. His voice was really raspy and old sounding, though his face was very young looking. \"Be careful, lad. That book will change\" He added before I left. When I got home I avoided \nparents so they don't question me about my new book, but of course they talk to me. \"Hey Lokir! How was training?\" She asks. \"It was fine, I learned how to ride a horse!\" I responded eagerly. Just wanting to go to my room. After I answer I quickly run up \nto my room. I place the book down on my desk and run down stairs and get a piece a bread and melon. I go up to my room and eat. When I finished eating I open the book. All the text is neon blue like the title. The feeling is rough and dry. Like it hasn't \nbeen touched for years. As I flip to the first page, my stomach sank. Suddenly feeling uneasy. There was a big octagon shaped alchemical board. It glowed a blood red. Like some alien crop circle. Strange symbols in every corner looked like people made \nthem with Elven Magic. On the next page there was a list of recipes.\nwith my father when I was younger. I took it out and cut a chuck of skin from my calf. I put a clothe rag under my let as I cut it. The pain was terrible but it was worth it. I hope. Eventually the blood soaked through the rag. A little pool of blood sits\nthere. I put the chunk of flesh in the middle of the Alchemical Circle and a blinding purple light shined and lit my entire room. When I looked back the skin was gone. I squeezed the the rag so the blood drips out on the book. Once again another purple \nlight shone and lit up my room. A pink and blue orb popped out.\nconfused. I hit it off the floor. Nothing happened... I end up getting frusterated and I just put it on my desk and go to sleep. It wake up in the middle of the night to a dull chiming sounds with cracks in the orb and a bright sky blue shining from the \ncracks. I pick the orb up and hold it in my hands. Staring at it. It breaks open and inside was two little clear capsules with red liquid inside. A little note lay under the capsules. It reads: \"Swallow capsules before going to sleep\" So I go back to \nsleep. I place the capsules on my desk. I wait until the next night to take the pills. As I wake up the next morning I quickly get dressed and go to the carriage to go to training. We have to carry iron to a smith. Not for any learning purposes, just\nbecause our Guild Master needed help. When I came home I read boring child stories that I read one million times. Just before I go to sleep I take the pill. Atleast five minutes after I take the pill I feel sick. I regret taking the pill. Then I fall \nasleep. I wake up in a broken floating place. Somewhere. I'm walking on floating chucks of buildings and ground. The sky is a deep purple and a dazed blue. I feel dizzy and uneasy. I'm controlling, living my dreams. It's a paradise. Every dream I ever had\nin one dream. When I wake up a feel restless. I feel crazy. I can't think straight. I hear a high pitched ringing noise in the background. I try and try to get it out of my head. I just lie down and scream into my bed. Am I insane? What has this capsule \ndone?! I hear screams of girls. Of adult girls. I think it's just my mind. So I continue to lay in bed. Until the screams are louder. I start hearing the screams say my name. I feel much warmer. Almost on fire. My eyes bolt open. Darting everywhere. Then \nI realize, my house is on fire! I get out of the bed sprinting down starts dodging flaming hot coals and smoke. Then I see her. My mother. In the kitchen burning. I fall to my knees. Screaming as loud as I can. I look around me. The ashes of a building I \nonce called home. Ruined. It's all ruined. I look to my right. Through the fire and the flames I see him. Captain Caros. The leader of the gaurds here in RorikStead. I hated him. Now he and his gaurd burn my home and slaughter my family. I won't let this \nact go unavenged. Fueled by rage, I get up and sprint over the Captain Curos. I grab his throat choking and choking. I stop when I feel his resisting stop. I let go. The gaurds are chasing me. I take Curos's sword and stab him in the chest to be safe.\nI leave the sword there. Then I sprint to the nearest horse and I hop on it. I'm almost out of to Cyrodiil but then I run into and Imperial ambush. They capture me and bring me to an execution. I can't die. Not like this, not like this. I run. Knowing if \n I get far enough I will be safe. Then suddenly and arrow hits my knee. I fall to the ground. holding my leg in pain. I make no noise. I close my eyes... Then I wake up. On the floor of the Library. I search around. I look at my leg. No wound. I look over\nto the end of the isle. I see that book. The Dream Theory. Glowing with that neon blue letters. Then I fall on the floor. Seeing nothing but black... I can't open my eyes. I can't move, but I can think. I can feel. I can hope. Then I wake up to my mom\nshouting my name to come down for breakfast. Maybe it all a dream... Although, it's just a dream... A Dream Theory.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Eastern Letter", "Tengoku Musuko", "To Sheriff Khagan\nup a tome? I am willing to pay up to 500 minas if that pleases you.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Farewell", "_Aengoth_", "First off, I'd like to say I'm sorry. I had full intentions to stick with the monks, to help everyone I could. I still do hope to help people, yet now I must focus on my people. I can't live with myself knowing the Dwarves stand against the brute force of\ntwo nations and not even lend my axe, be it rusted or not. I hope you do not feel as if I have wasted your time and I wish each of you the best of luck. The short time of peace spent with you lot taught me quite a bit.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Final Note", "theflyingpen", "When you open your bag you will find several things, this book will attempt to give you everything you need to know about your life.\n\nPeople will call you either Val or Valmir, this is not your real name.  Your real name is Uhierir.\nAs Valmir you have become a member of the lower council of Malinor as well as the Laurir of Lenniel, south of Malinor.\n\nThe robes you wear are that of the Arcane Delvers, a group of people you once were close too.\nYou choose to do this to you in an attempt to circumvent another attempt at your own life.  There is another book in your bags which speaks of a war, you need to bring this to a beautiful woman named Isabella, or as most call her 'Izzy' she is the last\nreason for you to attempt this new life.  You should only become Valmir to mvoe amongst your old friends as they have since turned against you, hoping to create more pain in your life than before.  You must remember to remain as Valmir Audane amongst the\nprecense of a pale darkelf with white hair by the name of Mythras as he is teaching you minor magic, and your true teacher of Illusion by the name of Cyrus, a tan elf with black hair and green eyes.\n\nWhile these two might have been your\nfriends before it is important that you cut ties with them all except in your lessons  as you will only grow to despise your life as you did before.  You had been beaten and struck down in your affections by anyone who had been lucky enough to have EARNED\nyour love and you must make all those who wronged you pay.\n\nThe world has turned a willing hero into the man that you are now, you have killed your once best friends and hung them up to dry, you have been subjected to all kinds of torture, and you\nwill take no more.\n\nYou must seek to harm those who once USED you for their own gains, the only friend you have now is you, everyone else is simply a toy.\n\nYou need to dye your skin back with ink, Use the council and the false identity of Valmir to your advantage, take what you want in life, don't be a slave to another's will any more.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Folded Note", "Unknown", "*The note is written in blood, although it seems to be fresh still; the color is a vibrant red.*\n\n\" Hello again, Elorna. I assume you have the animals I was asking for. If not, then I will have to fulfill my promise. \nYou will bring the animals to the sandstone arch near the Cloud Temple, on the path that leads from the Temple to Malinor and Darkhaven.\n\nCome alone, and do not disappoint me. \"\n\n\n(( I would probably be ready around 3-4 PM PST. If you have any questions, send me a pm - Patriotic_Fool. \n\nThanks~ ))", ""),
        StaticBook("A frontline Man", "Ser Arhadir", "Day 365 of war with dworfs, we are currently the best in world, dworfs think they have taller than us, but we more taller cause we have huge ***** and we use them better.\n\nAnd yes you dwarf reading this I love you kay?.\nrepur this lel", ""),
        StaticBook("A further note", "Mithradites", "My Book-Keeper,\n\nThough, I hesitate to call you \"mine,\" as such a concept is an ugly thing when we have not even spoken truly to one another. We have spoken, yes, but never as two who would love one-another. \nAgain, an ugly word.\nI apologise for both, but excuse my presumptions, for when I saw you in the dress I gave you, when I heard you playing the music I left you, my heart could be heard beating throughout the Tomb itself. Its rhythm still makes me tremble as I see you.\nPlease, for I can no longer contain my longing, we simply must end this false dalliance. I desire for one that is real. But I dare not embarrass you. I require a show of mutual desire. Next to this message lies a single flower. Plant it by your tree, and \nI will know. Leave it, throw it away, or broil it upon a spit, and I shall bother you only in my dreams.\n\nYours, \n\nYour Ardent Admirer.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Graceful Note", "CorprlSkyler", "hi\n\n-Siege", ""),
        StaticBook("A Guide To Magic", "PiercingDarkness", "§LA guide on void connection.\nBy, Mythras\n---------------:\n\nHello! This is a book to explain void connection, and the use of staves. This will be very useful to a new magic-user. Enjoy, and thank you.\n§LMagic History:\n\n\"Magic's dangerous, it leads to a never to be finished path.\" -Talis Ardere.\n------------------:\nYou say you want to learn magic? Well, magic's a pretty hard thing to learn.\n--> Turn to page 3\nMagic's hard for a reason, it's constant hard work and study, and takes many years to even understand the concept of void-connection. It helps, for many things. You should know it's history first though.\n------------------:\nTurn to page 4 ->\n\"In the beginning, the creator made the world, he made spirits to uphold the realm, along with the Aenguels and Daemons, the two elder races. And then, the four brothers. After the war with Iblee's, Malin taught his blood Druidism.\"\n--> Page 5\n\"And Krug, his descendants the arts of the shaman. Each race had a special art. Though, Humans and Dwarves, didn't have a destinct one.\nAerial, created the sages with and fueled them with her power, and taught them holy magic.\" --> Page 6\n\"Over time, the art lost it's value. The sword was just as affective as a spell, and quicker to learn. King's were needed to lead and not study, and magic held no appeal for farmers. So only a select few had the art, and continued to pass it on.\" -> 7\n§LArch-Types of Magic:\n\n- Arcane\n- Shaman\n- Druidic\n- Clerical\n- The Dark-Arts\n===============:\n\"Magic's infinite.\"\n-Mage Guild saying\n\"Magic's a never ending process.\"\n-Ambros\n------------------:\nTo make a connectioj of the void, it'll take years of hard work. You've got to be able to clear your mind of the constant over-lapping thoughts that living beings have.\nYou'll have to learn how to do that, and perfect your connection to the point of it working to a good point, so you can pull forth the mana in the void, and shape it into your spells.\n------------------:\nSome things that can help your connection.\n\n1. being well rested.\n2. Being calm.\n\nThey things can help your connection to the void.\n\n]------------------[\n\"Magic, if delved too deep, can lead to obsession, and then insanity.\" - Unknown\n===================\n\"Magic can be dangerous, I for once, blew myself up the other day, while attempting to cast something when I was tired. \nMagic can also be dangerous, because, not all magic's are used for good, nor is all magic used for evil. The actions of the users, will tell what the magic's used for.\n]-----------------[\n\"Magic's not determined by types, and other descriptions, it's the actions of the user that can decide the fate of all man kind.\"\n- Mage's Guild Saying\n-------------------\nMagic as said up there, is able to be used for anything.\n§LMagic Evocation Types: \n\n- Fire Evocation\n- Water Evocation\n- Air Evocation\n- Earth Evocation\n- Electric Evocation\n- Arcane Shielding Theory\n§LHoly Magic:\n\n\n- Clerical Magic\n- Druidic magic\n- Ascended Magic\n:]----------------:]\n§LPs: In no way, is this complete. Also, anything derived from a holy outwordly being is counted.\n§LIllusion:\n- Mind Magic\n- Light Illusion\n§L\nPs: May be more, this is all that's discovered currently. \n§LDark-Magic:\n\n- Shade Magic\n- Lich Magic\n- Undead Magic\n- Necromancy/Life Drain\n\n§LPS:\nMay be more to be discovered. Anything unholy goes here.\n§LQuotes pages, these will go on for 3 pages or so. \n\"Magic, comes to those who don't search for it.\" Artimec Akkaris\n\n\"Magic, cannot be defined, it's ever-changing.\"\n- Unknown\n\"The Void is all yet nothing.\" -Magician Saying\n\n\"Magic's neither good nor evil, only the choices of the user.\"\n-Mages Guild\n\n\"Magic? WHO needs magic?\" -Crazed Guy\n§LGood and Evil, how it affects magic.§\n\nMagic, is used by all. Mana is everywhere, in all living beings. Livings beings, use their mana, or, life energy, to connect to the void, an endless place filled with mana, and pull forth more mana to create ->\nspells, due to this, the void's possibilities are infinite. Evoking, pulls forth mana, and lets you turn it into your element. Dark-Magic's not evil, nor, is lighter magic's good. Anyone can abuse magic for their own purposes, and use it to further ->\ntheir goals. Greed of a user, leads to \"evil,\" acts to others for the greedy users benefit. Though, necromancy's not \"evil,\" persay.  As a necromancer, you pull mana from living beings around you. And use it for animating corpses, and etc...\nThough, \"Holy Magic,\" is supposedly good, it's because they pick from people they trust, and it's fueled by outworldly beings whom believe fully in good, and honor. There have been clerics gone rogue, who became evil, and went to killing people.\nHoly Magic, unlike Dark-Arts, is fueled, as said, by Aenguels and other immortal, powerful beings. The Ascended were even using Holy Magic, derived from their immortal patron, Aerial. ------------------:\n\nThis is why, magic cannot be described as one group of either good or evil, it fully doesn't matter, it's the actions of the magician, that decide all. Good and Evil are petty descriptions for people who differ, people can't be fully good or fully evil.\n§LThe Void, And you.\n------------------:\nThe Void, is where we pull forth mana to use to form the spells of our element. We use the mana we have, to form a connection with the void, and pull forth it's mana in huge amounts to cast what's known as, ->\n\"Magic.\" We cast our spells, knowingly aware if we pull forth too much mana, we can kill ourselves from overtaxing ourselves when we summon it. Casting things you don't know how to cast yourself, can be dangerous. You can literally blow stuff up.\n§LHow to connect to the void.\n\nVoid connection, is important to most magic. Evoking things requires your own mana which you use to draw from the void. It takes years, and it's not clear how it can be.\n§LFirst Lesson:\n------------------:\nCalmly close your eyes, inhale calmly, and exhale, do this for as long as you can, as you do so, clear your mind. And practice this often. \n§LSecond lesson:\n------------------:\nStudy your element, feel it, carefully examine it, study it, learn as much on it as possible. Carefully examine how it works. Do this often, and you'll be able to conjure your element.\n§LLesson 3: \n------------------:\nConnect to the void, imagine your element and everything you know on it. Carefully, imagine it, and it's workings. Practice this constantly. Eventually, you'll knock yourself out when conjuring it. But with time and ->\npractice, you'll get better. With this, you'll learn, continue your studies with your teacher after, and carefully use your element and practice it's use.\n------------------:\n§LSources:\n\n- Master Richard's teachings.\n\n- History of Magic\n\n- Water Evocation, by Ev.\n\n- Electric Evocation, by Gauldrim\n- My experiences.\n§LWritten by, Mythras Ardere.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Guide to Music", "danielz1998", "Within this bound leather, you'll find:\n\n-5 songs to learn and practice along to.\n\n-Tips and hints on entertaining from a professional and experianced bard\n\n-Making money and tips as a bard.\n-GUIDE TO NOTES AND NOTE LENGTHS-\n-[ ♩ ] musical quarter note\n-[ ♪ ] musical eighth note\n-[ ♫ ] musical single bar note\n-[ ♬ ] musical double bar note\n-[ ♭ ] flat accidental symbol (Indicates the suggested note is 1/2\ninterval lowered)\n-[ ♮ ] natural note (Cancels out accidentals)\n-[ ♯ ] sharp note (Indicates the suggested note is raised by 1/2 interval)\n\nThis information is crucial to any aspiring bard wanting to document music.\nThis first tune is one of my favorites, as I always played it as I learned. I still play it today! It's a good starting song, very catchy.\n♫ A prince invited me to tea, ♫ In a faraway country. ♫\n\n♫ He offered rare delights galore, ♫\n♫ Stuffed pigeon and hearts of boar. ♫\n\n♫ Black truffles snuffled up by pigs, ♫ \n\n♫ Goat cheese stuffed in tiny figs. ♫\n\n♫ And for dessert some minced meat pies, ♫ Ick! I’m taking him for fries! ♫\nSome notes on this piece:\nIt's a fun song! Play it in an appropriate situation, not to a widow, or a warrior wanting a 'fightin' song'\nAlso maybe do a little dance! Dynamic bards are way cooler than static ones.\nThis on is titled, The Lute Player\n\n♬♫ The King heard some musical sounds, ♬♫\n\n♬♫ A lute player, down in the grounds ♬♫\n\n♬♫ When he hit a wrong note, ♫ The King cleared his throat ♬♫\n\n♬♫ And shouted out loud \"Loose the hounds! ♬♫\n\n♬♫ Oh how did the bard run, ♬♫\n\n♬♫ Faster than the sun!?♬♫\n\n♬♫ Never to be heard again! ♬♫\n\nThis song is also very fun to play, since it talks about a 'Lute Player' which makes this sort of a fictitious memory of your own accord, as if you Are this supposed lute player. \n\nThis next song is perhaps a better song for a male audience.\nThe Joust\n\n♫ I jousted and fell from my horse, ♫\n\n♫ The Princess was my nurse, of course, ♫\n\n♫ When I fondled her breast ♫\n\n\n♫ The clever girl guessed, ♫\n\n♫ That the blood was just tomato sauce! ♫\n\nIt's a bit shorter of a song, but sing the versus a few times, and you'll be set for a fun night.\nThe Gambling Demons\n\n♬♫ It starts with just a coin at stake ♬♫\n\n♬♫ Till lust has gained its height ♬♫\n\n♬♫ How vast great hoards we’d love to make ♬♫\n\n\n♬♫ When gambling demons bite ♬♫\n\n♬♫ ♪ ♬♫ ♪ (Instrumental)\n\n♬♫ Many a man has lost his head ♬♫\n\n♬♫ Through sums beyond belief ♬♫\n\n♬♫ They lie, they steal, some end up dead ♬♫\n\n♬♫ To wife and family’s grief ♬♫\n\nThis song is fun to play while people are playing games of dice, a common pastime in Anthos.\n\n\nSurrendered Love\n\n♬♫ My love is like an ocean, it goes down so deep ♫♬\n\n♬♫ My love is like a rose, whose beauty you want to keep. ♫♬\n\n\n♬♫ My love is like a river that will never end. ♫♬\n\n♬♫ My love is like a dove, with a beautiful message to send. ♫♬\n\n♬♫ My love is like a song that goes on and on forever ♫♬\n\n♬♫ My love is like a prisoner, it’s to you that I surrender. ♫♬\n\n\nI admit that I've played this song to a few women in my experiances, and they've all loved it!\nIt's sweet, and sure to win you that female elf you've been after.\nTips, Tricks, and Hints\n\n-No matter what, playing should be about the experiance, and not about the Mina reward. Playing music can open doorways to relationships, friendships, jobs, and is an all-around useful skill to posses.\n-No one likes a rude bard. You should always smile, and be courtious, especially to women. I always kiss my female listener's hands before they leave, as a sign of respect and appreciation for them taking time to hear my music.\n\nYou should finish\nsongs with a bow, and a smile, and then thank the listener for listening. Be kind, regardless of if you get tipped or not. \n\n-Choose your venues wisely. Playing locations can be very crutial if you want people to hear your music. You can get \ndesignated 'Gigs' or you can just play for people on the streets! Either way, make sure you're in a place where people can see you, hear you, and know who to thank for the music. Don't stand inside of a store, and expect to get the attention of everyone \n\npassing on the street.\n\n-Know when, and when NOT to play. Situational playing can be the most entertaining. For example, if two orcs are about to brawl, perhaps play a fast, action-packed song to put everyone in the mood! It makes people\nappreciate you more, and it gives everything theme music! \nIt's also important to know when NOT to play. If a woman's husband just was be-headed, don't play music about it. Be respectful. Minstrel's are kind and respectful.\n-If someone wants a song about fighting, for example, and you don't have one ready, don't turn them down! Improvise! You have the skill, it's not so difficult! Perhaps if the song is good, you can keep it! Grab a quill, and some paper, write it down, and\nsing it another time! When people request certain topics to sing about, it's probably a common topic, likely to come up again. If someone ever asks for that topic again, you can have a song ready this time.\n\n-Be ready if the person says 'No, I \ndon't want a song.' This will often be the case. Some people know a tip is customary, and don't wanna get tangled into tipping if they don't want to. Some people might not like music. \nSome people might just be in a rush. If they say this, perhaps just as\nif they're sure, than let them be on their way.\n\n-Keep you songs documented.\nThis could be one of the most important rules as a bard. It's easy to carry a quill and some paper around, there's no excuse as to why\nyou have to improvise a song everytime you play, it shouldn't be that difficult. \n(OOC: I recommend some sort of text document, then copy and paste)\nSongs aren't as good when they're improvised, and the listener is less likely to enjoy it. Only\nimprovise when you don't have a song ready (But you should!).\n\n\nTips on Tips; making a profit\n\nI quote from my earlier writings, 'No matter what, playing should be about the experiance, not the Mina reward'\nThis is very true, but the life of a bard is a difficult one when you devote yourself to it,\nand have no other source of income, making tips your only money-flow.\n\nLots of the information in the prior section will also help the Minstrel make money. Make sure to read that as well.\n\nSome crutial points of making money in a \nperformance are based on how much the listener is entertained. If they're astounded, you'll likely walk away with quite the tip. \nIf they dislike, they might recommend something to help you improve, and walk away, with no tip. \n\nPeople might often not\nhave money themselves to tip. An alternative to minas you'll often likely recieve is food. Don't take this as an offense! That money you make is likely going to food anyways? They're saving you a trip, in theory. \n\nWhen playing, you should take in to\naccount who you're playing for. Lots of common folk will tip anywhere from 1-20 minas, depending on the subject. \n\nOn the other hand, gigs, and nobles pay significantly healthier amounts.\n\nNobles may tip 100\nminas for a single song if they enjoy it!  They turn quite the large profit, so take in to consideration §iwhere you're playing if you'd like to play for nobles. They won't be as common, and they're more likely to be in higher class areas.\nEntertain the listener! Give them a show! Don't sing your song in a monotonous tone, while anchored to the ground!\n\nIt's important that while singing, you give it your own custom flair. You accent might make the song more enjoyable, make sure \nto highlight these beneficial factors. \nAnd like I said, don't anchor yourself to the ground. The least you can do is rock back-and-forth to your own music. Dancing to your music, while simultaneously playing an instrument and singing makes you that much \nmore entertaining, and appearing as if you know what you're doing. Not all people can multitask. Use it to your advantage. Dancing bards are happy, wealthy bards. \n\nBefore playing, make sure to designate an area for tips. Drop a hat, drop a can, drop\nsomething, reminding the listener, \"Oh, yeah! I can drop tips here!\" which in turn, makes them much more likely to tip. \n\nPlay them a custom song!\nOr fake it, and make it seem custom! They don't know the difference, honest!\nThey wouldn't know if this song about love is improvised, or if you've played it for 100 women. Just the fact that you came up with it especially for them (supposedly) makes it that much more special to them. \n\nDress accordingly, and wear something that \nwon't scare away your potential tippers. Clothes that seem nice, and appropriate will make you seem devoted, and make you appear as if you're not a homeless musician trying to make money for bread.\n\nGigs, shows, and events are BIG mina-makers.\nAsk around, and learn about tournaments, competitions, openings, weddings, races, fights, plays, feasts, and festivals that you could play at. These events will bring a big crowd, and a big amount of people who can tip you, PLUS the money you got paid\nto even play at this event, will sure leave your pockets heavy. \n\nImportant: Get your name out there.\n\nALWAYS say your name before, or after you play your music. Always. Introducing yourself will put your name into the \nlistener's head, and make them know your name. Next time they need a musician, 'Hey, what about that one bard... Olivander Maso? He's good. Hire him.'\nUsing my name as an example above, this shows that people will remember your name, and come back for \nbusiness knowing who you are. Spread your name.\n\nDuets are a lot of fun. Playing with another musician will surely be more entertaining than just one. The tips may be split, but seeing as there are 2 musicians to pay, they might tip a bit more. Not only\nare duets good money-makers, they're a lot of fun, and a good way to make musical friends with the same interests.\n\nRemember their as well. Not only is it important for them to know who to contact, but it's useful for you to know who to \ncontact for possible work in the future. Not only do you need to know names for work, playing music is a a good way to make friends, and be an all-around social person. On the tip side of the scenario, remembering their name will make them possibly tip \nlarger in their next encounter with you. \n\n-------------------\n\nRemembering all of these tips and tricks will gurantee to make you a better minstrel, or a better entertainer, regardless of your art. Entertaining is a  \nfun career to devote yourself to, and it's one that I recommend. It makes you a lot of friends, takes you to a lot of places, and creates a lot of stories. \n\nI've been a musician nearly all my life, playing different instruments, traveling\nto different cities, and playing for different audiences. I don't regret a thing. \n\nI wish you luck in all your musical endeavors!\n\n\nOlivander Maso\nExperianced & Professional Minstrel\nFromFlamesBringsKings", ""),
        StaticBook("A hastily writee", "[Face Wrapped] Sentinel Valmir Audane", "Izzy, this is Val.  I need you to come to Lenniel right away and look for me, my home is near the waterfall of the town.  I need you to come as soon as you can.  I cannot stress how urgent this is.  One of your children was attacked by another druid but I\nmanaged to save her and bring her to safety.", ""),
        StaticBook("A hidden book", "'Camie'", "Day 1:\nI have arrived at the Mage College, meeting quite the interesting group of people. One appears to be a kharajyr, and the others all elves. The headmaster, seems to think me weak, and I intend to prove him otherwise whilst I study here. I've found \nmyself extremely bored, sitting around, not even learning... There's this one elf, who just sits there, and writes as I am now, who keeps stating that he is waiting for the Arch-Mage, whomever that is. Suddenly, a odd child has appeared, he seems to have\nflawless skin, and beady little eyes... I miss Albion, I wish he had stayed with me... I miss the hugs he gave me, the nice names he called me. I now wish he had stayed, and had held me closer, I now fear this lonely place.. I now fear.. This lonely place", ""),
        StaticBook("A home.", "[Teen] Haadi Mubdee", "Father,\nHave you managed to find us a place to live yet? I don't wish to spend my days traveling from city-to-city without a real home. I'm certain that you could get us a house in New Malinor if you asked.\n                Signed,\n                Haadi\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A house request", "booklight12", "Hello this is Blake. I wanted to request a possibe home for my family to live in. It does not not need to be too large but I simply request a home so me and my family may live together again. I have a few possible locations for the home to be in and I \nwould like to talk with you about them face to face. I will be in New Malinor if you get the time to speak. Or send a bird back. But the main locaitons I had were next to the camoryn manor. Near the mountains beside the city. Or possibly on or near the\nbeach/coastal region. I have all the money to give. And I have donated many of my resources to the city to be built. Please contact me so we may speak again \n-Blake Whitewolf\n \nTreaty of New Malinor\nTerms upheld by New Malinor and the High Council\n-nds.\nTerms upheld by Oren", ""),
        StaticBook("A Knights Report", "Knight Captain Vectis", "Vectis, Radiant of the Holy Chapter of the Creator's Sons. I have slain an enemy. A powerful one, at that. I have retrieved it's staff and stored it in my room. I felt an innate, dark, magical force for a second before it overwhelmed me with pain and -\n- suffering. It's unholy powers have been locked away for the time being. End.\nThe one I slew returned. Is it possible they were spared the same grace granted to regular men by the Monks? Is it possible they have souls like us?\n\"- correct,\" or something to that length. I was terrified. Who was it? What do they want?\nI have taken Novice Sylen's artifact, the odd blade, and the dark staff I collected. I don't know yet what I will do with them, but I need more information.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Kaelys Kaden Hightower", "Dear Friend,\nA Man by the name of Adorellan has began to hunt me, with him are beyond counting connections. \nIt is my family, My sister and Wife. I seek your advice with this.\nI do not know who I can trust or turn to. If you could, please offer advice.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "TheCleaningCrew", "", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "pianoplayer123", "Spencer,\ncare and love our friendship.... I thought I made it clear that I do too. Come for dinner.. please? ", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Nordulo Sudo", "Dear sir,\nInstitute of Language.", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Aerion", "Dear kravos,", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Resia", "Dear Nienna,", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "legoman315", "Dear Art,", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Salavin", "Dear Irene,\n I'm ending the relation as of this point, wether it be a bad time or not. I still care about you, and wish to be your friend, but I can't love you in that way anymore.\n- Irene Willow Ovain -\nYear 37, Day 14/356\nYear 37, Day 24/356\nYear 37, Day 75/365\nYear 37, Day 83/365\n- Irene Willow Ovain -\nEntry one\nEntry two\n\"I bet they are planning to do something silly... I should probably figure out before I get pranked or something.\"\nEntry three\nThey want to marry me off to some rich family. I don't like it, not one bit. I don't even know the man.\"\nEntry four\n\"I almost feel bad... Killing him, watching the blood fall from his throat. It's for the best though, I didn't want to be forced into that.\"\nEntry five\nor so. I might be allowed to start working for my parents soon, it should be fun.\nEntry Six\nSo... I guess I'll be careful around him.\"\nEntry 7\nMicheal never really worked out, my family didn't like him... I don't know exactly what they did to him, but he's left me alone since. I'll have to ask.\"\nEntry eight\n\"I'm really sick of it. I was thinking about leaving, but I don't want to betray my family. I guess the only way to leave would be to marry someone and leave.\"\nEntry nine\nthink they are right. I'm an Ovain, a killer, an assassin by birth. I don't need any others to make me happy... Just my family, and myself... I hope.\"\nEntry Ten\nI lost hope of seeing it again. But it's here! Lots of things have happened, among others is that I've finally been left alone. My parents are no longer bothering me, nor my siblings or anyone else. I enjoy the freedom and the lonliness. I wonder what I \nshould do next, it's so relaxing. I'm still working on my fighting skill, I've begun to favor a scimitar, it is by far one of the more impressive weapons I have seen.", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Vex", "Dear to whom it may consern,\n\nCecile's Book!\nPrefixes!\nSuffixes!\nWords!\nheretic\nlae: Him\nIto!\nito (kae,nae,lea,hea)\n\nDiz am dah diari ub\nThis Journal belongs to-___~Alex Elric~___ Please return if found  \n14th of The Deep Cold 1449-\nare coming up onto the walls.If nothing else is writen in this it probably dead or I dropped it if found at least try to bring it back or just burn it to be honest I don't really care to much about it yet since there is barley anything writen in it.\n20th of The Deep Cold 1449-I've been back from the battle for a while but I havn't really had anything to write about the past few days,but at least we won the battle and got some really great loot.While I was coming back I thought about my family and \nwhere they might be.The last I saw them was before I ran away from home and traveled to Abresi. There isn't any reason to go back to salvus (which was where I lived before I ran away) Since its destroyed and full of orcs.I Don't think I'll ever see my\nfamily again but it doesn't bother me much.Anyways All I have to remember the good old days in Salvus is a little map.", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Eladriendil Theados", "Dear David,\n\nI'm not whetehr or not you will ever read this, but I saw the orcs in Kingston and assumed we have lost. If you are alive, please send a letter back of any Legion goings on. If I do not hear a reply soon, I would assume the Legion is dead.\nIf so, I would like to say that I shall be sailing with a High Elf by the name of Xulore Ardere. I hope you can get back to me soon.\n\nYours truly,\nEladriendil Theados", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "PianoEby", "Dear Duke of Auvergne,\n\nIt has been reflected to me, that many is confused when travelling to the Duchy of Furnestock. \n\n\nIf you have seen the the current state, there is only one sign\ndirecting to the Duchy. The gravel and dirt made path is confusing. And the path itself is in mist of stalls, cobwebs, vines and water puddles. Visitors and employees also have to \"jump\" over a small stream\n\nYou might be confused why I sent this to you.\nIf you knew the path to the Duchy of Furnestock is in Auvergne land.\n\nI would like to request a better path made. Preferably stone or wooden. More directions to the Duchy of Funestock. And a raised platform for the small stream.\nIf this is an unavalible option, I'd gladly volunteer with the rest of my employees to have your esteemed permission to build the road ourselves. \n\nI look forward to your reply.\n\nWith respect,\nCountess Amber de Stolistes\nOn behalf of the Duchy of Furnestock and the County of Yamoto.", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Thorten", "Dearest Marcel Valois,\n\nI recently read the notice that states the intended removal of the hovels in the duchy of Auvergne. While I understand things such as this are out of the power of commoners such as I, I also read the mention of compensation. To \nbe honest, I am confused on such a proposition. Should you arrange a time to meet me or could it be explained by letter?\n\nThank you for your time,\n\n- Thorten Raynor\n\nP.S. From my farming\nduties for House Valois, I have several crates of wheat and potatoes. I was unsure of where to put the harvests, so I left it in my house. I apologize for any inconvenience.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Ceruberr Asul'Ailer", "Commander Starke", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Beast720", "To my Dearest Vex,\nI will love you. I hope one day you will return my love. ", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Roxforbraynz", "I have recieved your letter and I will consider it. For now, I must lay low with the High Elves. Keep an eye out for me and when we next meet, we will discuss it.\n\nFor now, try to learn the basics of the laws of motion...\nMomentum\nFriction\nWeight\nSurface area\nGravity\n\nStudy these and how they interact with each other and when we next meet, you will be considered.\n*The letter is signed with an elegant;* E", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Tristanm1", "Vierna,\n\nYour sister has come to the grove. She's looking for you, and by the sound of her problem, it sounds like she may need glasses. Come back when you can.\n\nLeyun", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Patriotic_Fool", "*The note is written in fancy handwriting, the text in blood.*\n\n\"We need to have tea sometime. Let me know when you're not busy, perhaps we can meet up.\n\n-Aislinn\"\n\n(( \n\n#yolo\n\n#swag\n\n#not\n\n#gonna\n\n#let\n\n#a\n#full\n\n#book\n\n#go\n\n#to\n\n#waste\n\n#elves\n\n#roleplay\n#lordofthecraft\n\n#nolife\n\n#please\n\n#help\n\n#dragins\n\n#permabannoapple\n\n#darkelves\n#highelves\n\n#woodelves\n\n#elves\n\n#orcs\n\n#humans\n\n#hashtag\n\n#turtles\n#pie\n\n#notes\n\n\n\n\n                     \n\n\n                        ))", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "confusedemo_o", "*The first page has been ripped out*\nIzzy,\n\nI can understand you'd be mad at me for being away all these years, and I apologize. Trust me, I did not want to be away from you for such an extended period of time...I hope that\nyou can forgive me, and come see me, as I dearly miss you. Please send a response when you can love, as I'll be around places.\n\n*The next part is written in seed braile that is glued by a sticky substance to the\npage ((Mistakes are on purpose))*\n\nI lnve ynu, kae leyu'celia.\n\n~Afnor", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "birdwhisperer", "To Nienna Calm\n\nI have a vial of unknown substance and need to find out what it does. You seem to be the most qualified to study it, so I'd like to ask you for help. I can give you more details when I give you the vial, \nplease meet me in Malinor or send a letter with a more suitable place.\n\nThank you, llir.\n~Elorna", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Darkdragon274", "I've seen an amount of newcomers very unusual for Leanniel. Something is likely amiss.\n\nStay safe, for we all targets of Malinor.\n-Rel", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Elwen", "The note is penned hastily but elegantly.\n\nTitania\n\n  I must speak with you immediately. It is about Kyral, and it is very urgent. Meet me at the New Malinor gates as soon as you're able.\n\n                ((-->))\nSigned, Elwen Evaglno Fiance of Kyral\nHigh Princess Titania,\nleader of Malin's people for many years. Infact, longer than any high prince(ss) before you. Together, the time of Native and Indelwhen expands larger than your own. \nunder you who have been worthy or capable of holding the position.\npeople cry for change, and the change of a high princee will at the very least create an illusion of change, sedating the illogical nonsense that at times runs in the streets.\nposition of high prince, with haste. I fear the elven populace will take up arms, in a few days time.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "SupremacyOps", "Aislinn,\n\nYour presence is somewhat desired in Haelun'or proper. One may have found a solution to a particular problem.\n\n~ Kalenz Uradir", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Merches", "To whom it may concern,\n\nI have a few books on my person I would like to sell to your shop. Please respond when able.\n\n- Merches", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Noble Aerion", "Dear Vierna;\n\nI was hoping to buy \"What I love in Nature\". Please contact me when you have the time.\n\nSincerely,\n\nAerion Hoffstine\nMay you follow thy purpose!", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Apple Druid Leyun", "Vierna,\n\nFor your next task, seek out Izzy and ask her for the task her and I talked about.\n\nI'm sorry in advance.\n\nLeyun", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "[Acolyte] Iler Ibar'ker", "Kefi, Get to the grove! Beth is here waiting for you and so am I!", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Hooded Man", "Dear Lord Varodyr,\n\nI do wish to have a meeting with you in the new cloud temple in the old Sky God's village. Perhaps in a few days time we may meet, until then, I look forward to it. -Alexander Valois\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Anonymous Delver", "Dear Guildmaster Art,\n\nI've noticed and seen sightings of some sort of evil spirit roaming through out the base, I've seen it's horrifying appearance and heard it's blood curdling shrieks, it normally will seek a certain target which was once myself but\nit has moved from me and onto another yet I do not know who, if you could gather a group of Delvers near the gate for us to begin a hunt through the base to find it and rid of it, that would be the best.\n\n- Anonymous Delver\n              OOC:\n\nThis isn't Rethu mailing you about the event but just a random Delver (no one really) to get the event started at 1:30PM, I felt I should make this to give you RP reason for the event.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "scharfjamie", "Dear Princess Titania,\nI would like to inform you that the Northern Engineer's taking work requests for redstone contraptions, infrastrcuture (bridges, roads), buildings, and destruction jobs (to destroy any buildings that you own and would like to return\nto as close a natural state as possible (( or ruins, since the new recipe's make those easier)). If you have a project in mind for us then I invite you to propose a price for it and we can negotiate.\nSincerely,\nCelendor De'Mattis\n\n(( We will be setting \nup a guild page as soon as we can confirm any projects.))\nReserved foals.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Foreman Golrodir Eritaf", "High Princess! You must come quickly. I will meet you in the main square.", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "wardog4445", "Titania, \n\nYour presence is requested by the gate to the docks. There has been another display by the \"Black Scourge\". \n\n -Avery", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "'Neu'", "The WolvenGard have stolen a lot of my stuff, and Vex's. Brownhair, deep voice, Took tons. Wolvengard arent taking too nicely to us. ((Describing SirWhisper)) \n\n\n\n-n.,", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "MrWizardGorlock", "Dear Isabella,\n    You are an amazing mali. SO bright and happy, even when that horrible tragedy happened you pulled through. I am so happy you survived. Please come see me soon. I wish you a fast recovery.\n     Sincerely,\n           Av'Ibar Rose\n\n((P.S. come with an empty stomach!))", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "[Hooded]Aelidar", "\nA LETTER\nfor\n-*-*-*-*-*-\nThe Okarir'tir,\nMr Lucion Sullas\n-*-*-*-*-*-\n\n\n\nFrom\nAelidar Elsil'sirame,\nCitizen of Haelun'or\nMr Sullas,\nI write to you in response to the poster hung in the blessed city of Lin'evaral, detailing the need for its citizens to uphold the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya. \n\nI, Aelidar Elsil'sirame, wish to enlist in this force, amongst the\nranks of the Evariran. \nI accept this responsibility to protect and preserve our way of life, and do so in acting upon the desire to do that which I can in serving our blessed enclave.\n\nUnfortunately, however, I cannot\ntake up this task immediately, having sustained injuries at the hands of those which dare to defy our supremacy.\nThis period of recovery should not be overly extensive, and I expect to be fit for training as soon as possible.\nPlease do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nVan'ayla,\n\n~Aelidar\n\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Knyghtfalcon", "Dear Salavin,\nDon't worry about it, its quite alright. I didn't expect it to work, really. I can never hold down relationships anyway.\nI'm just used and forgotten, as usual.\nI suppose I'll be talking to you soon.\n\n~Irene Ovain", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Minst46", "Clavonita, I would like to talk. Therefore, I will be coming to Kingston, alone. Have whoever you like with you. I wish for no fighting, however. I'll see you soon.\n\n- Stark", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Glaewen", "This is addressed to the owner or proprieter of Wondrous Writings in Vaerhaven.\n\nI have come across a rather rare and valuable tome recounting the tales and legends of the Volsung family who sailed to Asulon from their homeland of Skjoldier. Only one\nother copy of this tome exists in all of Anthos, and it is securely locked away in a labrynthian library.\n\nI am willing to part with this tome should you be willing to make it worth my while.\n\nBe swift, for other parties have also expressed interest in\nthis tome.\n\nI await your response.\n\n-T ((Frosted_Petal))", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Ned_Lud", "Dear Wondrous Writings,\n\nI be lookin' ter buy some o' them readin' materials. Fer starters, mayhaps a copy o' History o' Magic and Hydromancy will do. I'll send th' money along soon enough. Ye' kin send th' snow owl along ter\nth' ole lighthouse in Lenfarthin'. Ole Pete th' mailer will ter it tha' they get ter me burrow at One Treetop Terrace. Thank ye'. Also, tried ter feed yer owl a nice juicy rat, but he was nae very friendly.\n\n- Bango Blackfoot", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Unknown", "[] A bloody handprint is pressed against the page, with a large A drawn near the bottom. \n I am in need of you once more, Elorna. You will meet me at the Arch in the North. If you do not, the Grove near the High Elves will be destroyed. Every living thing will be corrupted or slain.\n\nBest you hurry! ", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "[Sentinel] Aerion", "Dear Kina,\nI just wanted to forget, to move on, and be happy with you. We could have had a happy life and instead you left me in the inn with a man who hates me. I thought I loved you but you left me just like everyone else did.\nWith no regret I inform \nyou that I have died or forgotten you. Thankyou for being like every other person who has left me.\nLove,\nAerion.", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Athri", "Delonna,\n\nPlease meet me at my home (Elibar'acal Tower), for I have something to show and tell you about. \n\n-Athri", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "YourFriendEarl", "Dear General Store Owner,\nas well as any quiver of arrows. To be exact I am looking for 20 arrows and one bow. Please reply to my mailbox stating if you own these items and they are for sale. ", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Aislinn", "*The note is written quite well, although a splotch of blood or two stains the note.*\n\n\"I'm going to come by the Delvers soon, Leyu! I have two new interesting books, and I really hope you like them. Maybe Nienna will let me into the library this time.\"\n\n-Aislinn", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "TehLulu", "Prince Warwick,\nIn regards to a matter of some import, I wish to speak with you sometime soon.  I will keep this brief so as to not give away any unneeded information to any who may come in contact with it. Please send word to me to meet here, or visit me\nin the Imperial Palace, located at the topmost point in the Capital of Oren, Abresi. \n\nSincerely,\nAri Horen\nImperial Crown Princess\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Dove Druid Elorna", "To the High Princess Titania\n\nMy sincerest regards to you. I would prefer to speak to you in person, however as you would seem to be very busy and this is urgent, a letter will have to do.\n\nFirstly, the grove of \nthe Equinox circle is under threat from the creatures of the north and their cult, the Black Scourge. They have threatened me in the past, and most recently gave me a vial of poison with orders to either feed it to Prince Khel, or see my grove destroyed. \nObviously, I have not attempted to murder him, and have in fact spoken to him and Prince Ebs about this issue. I believe this should show my trustworthiness, as Khel himself stated.\n\nI had Nienna study the poison, and she determined that it\nwould cause frostbite, then death. If you see Khel before I do, I ask that you relay this to him, and he can choose the best action from there.\n\nI also request aid from Malinor's Lumidrim and your Teuton friends. I do not know when exactly this attack\nwill occur, however they stated that it would be in the next Elven day. ((Probably Satuday, 26th.)) I realize that we have recently conflicted over a pack of wolves, but this circle and grove are in great need. I believe that Gavin, the founder of the\nEquinox circle, is still on your council, so we do have ties to Malinor.\n\n\nThe issue about the wolves is something I would rather discuss in person, but for now I ask that no more action be taken against them until such a meeting can occur.\nTo put things plainly, I need Malinor's help. Unless Khel can convincingly fake frostbite in time to turn this attack away, a sacred place will be corrupted.\n\nMay Cerridwen bless and Cernunnos strengthen you.\nElorna the Dove Druid", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "LolitaDoll", "To Katlyn Horen,\n\nI must firstly congratulate you on your wedding. I am more than honore that you have decied to get your dress at my establishment. I apologize that I was not there to receive you personally. This is why, I have closed\nthe shop for the next Elven day. Should you pay a visit to Malinor I will take your order in private and begin my work. Please send notice before you depart from your home so that I may be there to welcome you when you arrive.\n\n-Resia Los'iirae", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "~", "My dearest...\n\nW, I hope you're not suprised to find this letter. I'm alive and, for the most part, well. I still love you. Nothing has changed. I want to come see you... I can find you. Miss me until we meet again.\n*The letter has no signature but is sealed with black wax, but no sigil stamped into the seal. The paper is crinkled but seems as if it were smoothed.*", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Chieftain Thurak'Braduk", "Gronkk\nDa Urukz ob Gronkkstun ned ah dok. Da Braduk klan haz a zhip dokkd ad da bdlandz, agh if wi ged ah dok heer, wi kan eezily get zupliyz frum uwah dezerd. Blah tu meh wen lat peep meh nekzd.\nThurak", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Beggin_Bill", "Sigmun is dwunk!\n*Ale is spilt here*\n\n\nFER THe FeKun ELVUZ Are fecki!N GweENM!\n*More ale here*\n\n\n\nILL FLAT LAT", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "CorprlSkyler", "Trajan Mercer,\n\nIn response to the burning of your crops within Salvus, I would like to meet now for the reimbursement at the scene. If you would, simply travel there now, and we shall speak of the deal.\n\n-Jericho Rylin\n\n-The orange wax seal can\nbe found once again at the bottom of the letter, two white wings within.-\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Saviordude", "To King William Horen III,\n\nThe writer of this letter wishes to let you know of a chance to gain glory for Oren. A chance to wipe out the filthy worshipers of Iblees. Not only would this bring you honor, but it would avenge all the humans who died as Oren\nfell in Aegis. Please respond if you wish to learn more of their nest. You may send your letter to no. 1 Witch Woods, Lenfarthing.\n\nSigned,\nOl' Treehugger\nWizard of the Witch Woods", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Oormo the Ice Gnome", "    !!!WANTED!!!\n\nRecent sightings suggest an odd creature has been seen lurking about in the dwarven forests, it has taken many lives and needs slaying! Dear reader, please hear my pleas and hunt down this beast! It has been noted that it has a \nweakness against fire but is strong in some odd magical art of ice! It is very slim and slender yet not too tall but what it lacks in strength, it makes up in agility and swiftness.\n\nHear my cries!\n\n- Anonymous\nA map is attached to the back of the letter, the map covered in red dots, showing one their way to the monster's location.\nOOC:\n\nGreetings Delvers! You guys asked for a monster hunt event, so here you are! The event will take place at 7PM PST, the map would lead to these coords:\nx: -948 and z: 664!\n\n-Nug", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "imepic2704", "Dear Tuv,\n\nPlease expect within the next day for me to arrive in Abresi to discuss something of much importance with you. I would detail it in this letter, but I do not want them intercepting it.\n\nSigned - Maer Joferik", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "SirNublet", "\"Dear Tuv,\n\n\n\n\nI am writing this to you at the Monk Cloud Temple. I woke up here briefly ago, and I belive I know why. A few Elven hours ago, the Hatters stormed the Abresi Jail. I came\nout of the jail to see their leader talking to the Doctor Charles Brae. The Hatter thugs tried to attack me, but I retreated into the jail. The Leader ended up forcing Charles to give him the key to the jail, and he and his thugs (About 4) came into the\njail. I tried to hold my ground, but they were all armored and armed. They said that they didn't want to hurt me, but would if I didn't listen to them. They wanted me to become \"corrupt\", so as to turn a blind eye when they attacked or hurt someone. I'm\ntelling you Tuv, they gave me no choice, and I really wasn't interested in dying by their blades, so I accepted. I don't know what I did past that point, but I'm sorry for it. I myself will probably never come back to Abresi, but I wish that you don't put\nup any warrants for my arrest or death for being a \"traitor\", as most men would do the same. They gave the same offer to all the other guards. I know that Edmurd, the other guard on duty, was given the same choice and accepted. I don't know what I shall \ndo know, but I plan on maybe going down the mage's path, as I've always wanted to become one. I wish you good luck Tuv, and hope you wish me the same.\n\nSigned,\nSheon Ryder, former Abresi Guard\n((Also Tuv, technically I didn't commit any traitorous acts, as I hid in a building for most of the fight, as Sheon IC'ly didn't want to kill you, so when the fight finished he came out. I think that because my name said [corrupt guard] and their was just\nthis fight, you thought that I helped the Hatters, but you wouldn't have if my name was [abresi guard], as I could easily had that, and still be corrupt. I didn't attack /anybody/, hatters or Tuv-loyalists. I don't blame you though, as things were\nhappening so fast. Well, I have no ending for this OOC explanation, so I'll give you one word.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nswag.))", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "timzuiderveld", "Dear Kaila,\n\nWe must have Tea or do something togheter or something, I really miss you and I have great news for you.\n\nWith love,\n\nSarah Archdiamond", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "scornofhell", "Hello my Brother, I Received Your Message and I would Love To Have a Drink with you.\nI Began Building A Mannor on the Emerald Islands so, if you ever want to drop by Just Let me Know.\nYours. Valdis Frostbeard\n\n(reguarding the note\nMy character is blind so it would have to be in brail, remember for future ones, ill reguard the last one as brail writeing. )", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "everblue2er101", "Dearest Salandra,\n\nI know we have had our ups and downs, but surely our love can overcome these obstacles. I beg you to return to the city of the Elves and speak to me once more so that we can try and be together again.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Kralek", "Dear Daniel Taves,\n\nGreetings. This is Count Alester Herenden. I have heard about you and your family and would like to extend an invitation to my Barony. We need to set up a meeting. Please get back to me as soon as possible.\nSIncerely\nCount Alester Herenden", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Elder Aerion Sulliran", "Dear Ahlystraaria,\nI hope all is well, and that Kina's scene didn't get anyone hurt. My apologies for everything, and I really do hope all is well. Take care and visit soon.\nSincerely,\nAerion S.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter For Her", "Unknown", "My dear beloved Ariante...\n\n... News have arrived of changes in my people's land. Adunia, is to be reborn, and I am forced, by means of a curse cast upon my bloodline, to assist Lachlan Mor Elendil I in the reconstruction of our nation as a new beginning.\nDespite being told not to inform anyone else about the orders I received, I find myself in the need of telling you I am leaving for Vaerhaven, where I am to lead a new branch of the Adunian military: The Bloodriders...\n\n\nIt pains me to leave you on such a short notice, without the opportunity to bid farewell and hold you in my arms once last time before I am to abandon all that links me to society in order to train what is to become the ultimate weapon.\n... I ask of you to forget me, no matter how painful it is to live without you. I beg of you, do not try and find me, for it is far too late to have a future together. I am to become nothing but a miserable pile of secrets; a man with no name, no future..\n... and no past. \n\nThere is so much I would've loved to tell you, so many things I wanted to teach you and share with you, but I stand no chance against the forces that control my existence in this realm we call reality..\n... I close my eyes at night and day, just to dream of you, my love; to see your heart warming smile, to feel alive before the ethereal gaze of your eyes, and to exist within the godly embrace of your arms, just for once in my demonic existence.\nTo live, knowing of someone I love, who has shown me I am capable of experiencing that which makes existing bearable, and worth every second of this eternal dream, at your side.\n\nForever yours,\nCymrych Douglas\n\n20th of The Grand Harvest, 1450.\nForget the man, but remember his dream.\nForget the man, but remember his heart.\nForget the man, but remember his soul.\n\nForget, then remember and ask yourself...\n\n\"Who was this man?\"", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter of Need", "RocketHaul", "I require the materials to make more arrows. I have decided to become a fletcher, and sell the arrows to the shops in town.\n\nAdditonally, many of the chests in my house still have locks, which means I cannot get into them.\nFinally, I would like to have my own locks set on my chests as a precaution against theives.", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter of note", "Z3r05t4r", "*a letter written in purple inc*\n\nDear Triss,\n\nI recently went through my possessions of books and remembered the night back then, when we were discussing these things. Hence, I considered, this little\ngift of books would be adequate for you to read, should you ever take a break from your duties.\n\nFurthermore, as I discovered you lack a mailbox, I built one for you. The key is attached to this letter. A fine craft I considered, using my\nskills in fine mechanics and engineering for something else than constructing artificial beings.\n\nThird, and I believe last, I would like to invite you to visit the ruins of the Imperial palace with me once. It is a last reminder of a time which was and a\ntime I miss so dearly.\n\nRunning short on paper, I conclude this letter with best regards.\n\n- Silus\nMerchant Lane, #15\nSummit Boulevard, #5\nHouse of Duke Vectis Vekon.\nRaevir Overlook, #5\nSummit Boulevard, #11", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter to Otto", "Jonathan Elers", "To his holyness Ostromic Carrion, crown prince of Ruska, destroyer of Ager and half brother of Tuv\n\nMy name is Jonathan Elers. You don't know me and chances are you never will. But I am one of the many current residents of Ager who is soon to \nbe without a home. Obviously when I heard this news I was both devestated and angry.\n\nI have spent a good 100 horens on what had been my 'dream home'. The place has been good to me. But now, it is to be snatched from me. I approached your half\nbrother, Tuv and asked what can be done, and that is why I am writing this letter to you. I demand compensation for the home I love being unjustly snatched from me. Please send me a bird so we may discuss further\nSincerely,\nJonathan Elers", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter to Vex", "[Masked/Helmeted] Panther", "Dear Vex.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter to Vie", "Mandru \"The Doctor\" Scott", "Dear Vierna,\n\nThis is Mandru. Mandru Scott. I'm PRETTY sure you haven't forgotten me, but if you have, immagine a beared human fellow with a white cloak, laughably big medal, and unkempt hair. That's me. Anyways, I send this letter asking for help\nfrom you.\n\nYou see, I am launching an expiditioin to visit Kha Island, and we need a mediator who's on good personal terms with them. You have often said you are friends with the Kha; I'd like to ask if you could\njoin us aboard the Endeavour and be our guide. Among the crew of this exploration ship, for its maiden voyage, will be myself, the captain, Commander Gestahl VonSchlicten, our helmsman, Lt. Commander Varstivius, our science officer, and Lt. Commander\nDavid LaGorge, our Cheif Engineer.\n\nWe can't explore Kha Island without a mediator; we're not asking you to become a perminant member of our crew. We just need someone to reassure the Kha that we come in peace\nthat they trust.\n\nPlease reply to this letter as soon as possible.\n\n~M. Scott\n  Captain of the G.R.S Endeavour\n\n((OOC NOTES:\n\nWe'd proably hold the trip sometime on Sunday the 15th of September. Feel free to reply via text letter if you can't access a written book. We won't mind.))", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter to you!", "SortedJarhead", "*The letter is written in the beautiful and artistic writings of a Monk*\n\nDearest Vaerhaven Book Store Owner,\n\nI have written a single book of many yet to come on the language of the Adunian people. I wish to supply your \nstore with such books. For whatever you wish to sell them for, I ask for half the profit. As well I would like three copies set aside for me when I visit Vaerhaven. I will send you my only copy along with this letter, and send it back if you aren't \ninterested.\n\n,Monk Argyll of the Wilven Sanctuary", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter to Yuln", "Eenhoornheid", "*The letter is sealed\nwith a wax stamp*\n\n\n\n\n\n     To Vallel'Yuln\n  For her eyes only.\nDear Vallel'Yuln,\n\nWe need to talk. It is not your choice if you want to talk or not. If you refuse to do so I will find you and force you to talk to me.\nMeet me as quickly as you can at the ruins in the forest, the oem with the fire in the middle.-Lelien", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter.", "Minuscule_Evil", "Dear merchant,\n\nIn my previous letter [your thread] I gave you the order of the books that I want sent to my mailbox. \nHere is the payment for them.\n\n-Athri Elibar'acal.", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter~", "candydeath13", "*The words are scrawled here messily*\nyou come visit. I'll give you a hint: I've decided I like woodcarving. That's your only hint okay? Anyways... hope to see you soon! Love you and miss you...", ""),
        StaticBook("A little note.", "[False Left-arm] Tybalt Smith", "Hello Nienna, I wish to speak to you at any location, the Inn, or the Delvers Keep. ((MSG me for a reply, IGN: SkyLord_Leo ))", ""),
        StaticBook("A longSword", "Alana Chase", "Im need an iron longsword with silver engravings that has the Cillion Chase", ""),
        StaticBook("A Love Poem", "KibagoKid", "For golden locks of hair so fine\nAnd eyes that like the starlight shine\nSkin soft as lace\nHer endless grace\nMakes me long for her to be mine\n\nBut beauty such as this can be\nOnly outmatched by her, you see\nNo desire to harm\nHer wit and charm\nHave certainly stolen words from me\n\nHer words are of the kindest way\nAnd forevermore her heart does stay\nSo sweet and demure\nThis maiden pure\nNever fails to take my breath away\nBut fear I do of her reply\nAnd wait here with the softest sigh\nFlawless I'm not\nDark past I've got\nI believe she deserves a better guy\n\nOne who can fill her every desire\nWho'll always stoke the burning fire\nHe'll give her flowers\nAs well as hours\nAnd save her from situations dire\n\nThese are the things that I can do\nAbove all I would always be true\nBut weak I am\nNot a good man\nMy greatest fear is I'd hurt you\nSo alone I remain, day after day\nWanting to go, yet here I stay\nInside, my fire\nBurns with desire\nFor the maiden who steals my breath away\n\nIf I should find ways to make her see\nThat I'm the man she needs me to be\nThen I shall request\nAt her behest\nTo be a lock, her heart my key\n\nUntil the day comes to my sight\nWhen finally I don't have to fight\nI'll make my advance\nAsk her to dance\nAnd cleanse my darkness with her \nlight.\n\nWhen that day comes I shall be ready\nPerhaps my luck will make me heady\nIf I should guess\nThat she'd say yes\nTo be with her, I'd move back to Abresi", ""),
        StaticBook("A Merchant Guide", "Josh3738", "Starting a Business\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-There are a few basic steps that must be  met in order to become a successful business man.\n\n~Step 1~\nOne must have starting money. Without this it is nearly impossible to aquire any sort of\nstable business enviroment. This can be aquired through personal means of labor or servantry.\n\n~Step 2~\nSurplus. What are you, as a merchant, going to sell to the general public in order to turn a profit? Will you buy and resell for a \nhigher price? Or will you sell goods obtained by yourself? Any way you go, you will need to have a stable flow of goods into your shop(s).\n\n~Step 3~\nLocation. Without a proper location you are just a random merchant selling\nhis wares off of a carpet. The best place is a store on a main road of a major city. Stalls are profitable but don't have the amount of room needed in order to host a large scale company.\n~Step 4~\nAttitude. One can not simply be rude to your customers. You must treat them kindly and with respect if you want them to be regular patrons to your business.\nOwning a Business\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-When owning a business it is very important to keep up on your tax payments. This may sound odd, but in the long run it is crucial. It is important to keep a balance on how much you spend in order to keep your business\nopen and how much you earn though sales and deals.\n\nYou must also be well informed on the local prices of items and goods in your area of business. If someone nextdoor sells bread for 1 minas, you shouldn't sell it for 5. Competition is\na key skill that you as a business man must know alot about. There is a balance here that is extremely delicate. You should have a lower price, or at least equal, than your competitor but not so low that you don't make a profit.\nMonopoly!!!\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-When you get successful enough it is possible to open more businesses that are all run by you. Own an entire industry! Be the only log supplier in the Dwarven lands! The possibilities are endless.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Message", "Blocky_the_Block", "*While walking through the streets of Haelun'or Elwyn notices Ev Ar'ahern's house directly in front of her. Elywn Míriel begins to hastily write a letter, as it is about the rain and leaves it behind in Ev's mailbox.*\nDear Mr Ar'ahern, \nwater evocation I immediately ask who his teacher was. He directed me to you and here I am writing this letter. I understand any reluctancy you might have to teach a stranger who you haven't even met in person yet, but I would like to assure you that I \ncan be trusted. To ease you worries about teaching me if you wish to take on another apprentice I would like to meet in person and dicuss this matter. I current reside at Seth's home or will be around Haelun'or if you wish to get in contact with me.\nYours sincerely, ", ""),
        StaticBook("A Missive", "Darkdragon274", "Get to Ac'talareh.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Neat Letter", "Claudi Masson", "Tomorrow night. I'll leave next morning.\nI'm coming by horse.\nI'll also bring a trusted friend as protection, as spoken about in the last letter. Please feel free to do the same.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Nobody Like Me", "zach211w", "         Nobody\n Life ain't easy for us    kind of people.\n You should try it but\n parents proud, not \n grow up as. But I think   you'll find another \n sugar, ain't spice its \n          ", ""),
        StaticBook("A note", "SAGE221", "Regarding your question.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "RabidAminal", "\"Sorry abou' yer stuff. I's ours now! Hahahahahaha :)\"", ""),
        StaticBook("A note", "TechnoMack", "Dearest daughter Vara,\nto continue. This necklace will change your memories and appearance, to Vieth, our Guardian. He will be able to keep both of you safe, but he will not return to the necklace easily. Be weary, Vara.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "[Servant] Aerion", "Dear Gaeril,", ""),
        StaticBook("A note", "confusedemo_o", "You didn't come today, again...Is everything alright? I'm worried, and wonder if these letters are even getting to you. I hope you are safe Izzy, if you receive this letter. I'm at the house if you do want to come...I miss you.\nSasha does too, I can tell. She's...She's not doing too well Izzy...I love you, and tell the children I said hello...\n\nHope you are safe,\nAenor\n\nP.S. I made beef \nand carrot stew if you come to the house. I thought it'd be nice if I cooked for you for once.", ""),
        StaticBook("A note", "Spikehaserd", "We took the liberty of taking your mighty and well-cooked sword fish before it spoiled. We'd hate to have your kitchen wreaking of old fish.\n\n-Benedict and Aenor,\n  Malinor Highguard", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Relgard Sintel", "Nobody's seen you in a while. I'm getting worried.\n\nAre you alright?\n-Relbel", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Hooded Female Elf", " Meet by the Malinor \nsoulstone pillar. This is your only chance. \nCome alone. ", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Anna Koldings", "To whoever this may concern- \n\nHelp! I am but a old woman with her son, we used to be vassals under Lord Uthor Silverblade. But after his dissapearance, the castle has been inhabited by a strange man\n\nWeird sounds are heard every night, and I fear for my surrounding villagers as well for my son and I's safety!\n\nWont you save us?\n\n~Anna Koldings", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Unknown", "Jemain Clayton\n---------------\nClaims Hatters came to him, offering to buy Casino. Jemain refused, Hatters broke up place, leads to Jemain working for Hatters under threat of violence.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Eenhoornheid", "*A note is left on the chest. It reads:*\n\"Dear Calaedran,\n\nSeeing that your house hasn't been furnished yet, I decided to be so kind and help you acquire the basic needs for living.\n\nI do hope you enjoy these things to their\nfull extent.\n\nMaehr'sae hiylun'ehya,\nFrederick (a.k.a. Lelien Aeléyèlsa).", ""),
        StaticBook("A note", "Teerz", "Dear Adorellan\n\nI formally request that you run a competitor out of buisness and out of their lands, as they harbor Kaelys, who has admited to defiling who I guess to be laila's grave.  \n\nHe lives near gronkkston, and \nwould make a good target.  \n\nSincerely Sha", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Raxxtus99", "Valmir,\nI have spoken to Kalenz, and he has given you one last chance to leave the company of the impure Delvers, and join the Pure. If you decide to stay, you will be marked as impure and will be outcast from your kind. Choose wisely.\n~Rolen Veryan.\n\n*The name is written in elegant cursive*", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Aislinn", "*The note is written in bad handwriting, but it looks like the writer was trying really hard.*\n\n\"Hello Leyu! I haven't talked to you in some time. I hope you are doing okay.\n\nI was hoping to come by and see you! I\nalso have a book that I want you to have! It is a really interesting story, and I think you will like it! I will stop by the Delvers as soon as I can.\n\nAlso, Snowy hatched a short while ago, and she is the best owl ever! \n- Aislinn\"", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Unknown.", " We have given you warning after warning, we have been merciful. You had many chances to surrender, to avoid suffering from his wrath.\n\nNone shall be spared for what is to come.\n\nPray to your gods, for we have just begun. ", ""),
        StaticBook("A note", "Patriotic_Fool", "*The note is written in blood.*\n\n\"Come to Adunia.\"\n((\n\n\nyolo\n\n2 chainz\n\nswag\n\nthug lyfe\n\n\n))", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Unknown Author", "*You receive a folded note*\n\n\" We warned you. An elf once per week, otherwise you would receive an elven head every day. \n\nThe punishments will become more severe.\n\nYou will give us what\nwe want, or Malinor will suffer for it. \"\n\n( unsigned )", ""),
        StaticBook("A note", "GreatSmirnovius", "Val!\n\n\nBrilliant. Rain is a great totem, and it fits you, too! Remember that you can change your totem as you advance as a Dedicant, but not after Attunement. I suggest you choose wisely, your career as a Druid depends on it. \nNo pressure. None at all.\n\n\nThe staff is great as well, though I could not identify the wood... what is it? You should keep it around at all times, it bears great symbolism, and should you ever decide to learn to manipulate Druidic\nenergy, it shall be your channel.\n\nI shall be leaving for a prolonged stay in Vaerhaven ((Going camping with some friends for most of the week :D)) so it might be a bit difficult getting tasks. I recommend asking some of the other Guides\nfor tasks... especially Verden. He's a Guardian now, but if you tell him I sent you, he should give you one.\n\nRemember, take it easy! Doing many tasks doesn't make you a better Druid, /understanding/ them does! \nGood Luck, and try not to miss me too much.\n\nYour mentor, Guide, and friend...\n\n\n*-Gavin Cervidus-*\nMember of the Inner Circle and Guide of the Druidic Order", ""),
        StaticBook("A note", "~N~", "A big -=R=- wax seal seals the grayish envelope, the smell of faint roses travels to your nose as you open it.\n                 [!]\n~By sunlight I glare,\nBy moonlight I stare,\nBeauty in the day,\nMystery in the night,\nNever can I approach,\nAs you blind me with your light,\nIf only I can touch you,\nHear your voice,\nSee your eyes,\nIf only you admire, \nI can satisfy my desire~\nThe note ends with an -=N=- signature and a single wisp of silver white hair.\n                 [!]", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "The Black Scourge", "*A large black raven drops this note at your feet, before flying off. The note itself is written in blood, turned a brownish-red color over time.*\n\n\n\" Hello. As you read this, I want you to think upon the past few weeks. The attack on Lenniel, your experience with Arzota. Allow that to be fresh in your mind before you continue reading.\n\nNow, with those images in your head, you will be able to \nunderstand the seriousness of what I am going to say.\n\nDove Druid Elorna - I require you to prove yourself. You will prove that He is superior than your pathetic Aspects, and you will prove that you are a compassionate and caring individual.\nThe task is simple - you are to get three healthy, happy animals, and deliver them to me. They will be used as an offering to the Master.\n\nPerhaps you are now thinking that it may be easier to just ignore this letter, and get on with your pathetic waste \nof a life. Should you refuse, I will kidnap three of your fellow Druids. They will be subject to some of the most horrifying torture I have to offer, before I kill them and use them as the offering to Him.\n\n\nI hope you make the right decision. You will receive another note in one elven day, with the location you will drop off the animals.\n\nIf you don't show up, I will take that as a refusal. Don't disappoint me.\n\n- A", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Rexx8", "Dear Darius,\n\n I would be elated if you would come to Velkyn Keep, so we may discuss its future in a civilized manner. I hope to see you here within the next few days.\n\n-Ahlysaaria Vincrute", ""),
        StaticBook("a note", "emberhard", "I hear you are the man to speak to for some sailing needs. Meet me at the Malinor docks if so.\n\n-Emberhard", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note and Minas", "TheCleaningCrew", "I would like to buy all of the spruce that you have advertised. I have sent several of the large, strong birds from orcish lands with this note. Fastened to the largest's leg is the appropriate 300 minas. These birds should be able to deliver the logs to\nme over several trips. I expect to get what I paid for.", ""),
        StaticBook("A note for Ado", "'Panther'", "Dark Brotherhood.\nI have heard of ye, from few of my men, I believe it is time we meet.\n\n\n\n-^%!@\$(#^\"{:-", ""),
        StaticBook("A note for Aria", "Salamandra", "Dear Aria,\n\nI hope the holiday season brings joy to you, wherever you may be. To see what a wonderful young\nwoman you have become has been a\npleasure to me. I first met you on the Malinor bridge with your mother... I was\nnothing but a silent bystander. Mother and\nchild should never behave that way, I thought and so intervened, and to have seen you come so far warms my heart. Though I have not seen you in a long while, I will rejoice at your return and accept the Aria\nI know with open arms. Please give your gifts to others, as we are more fortunate than some. You are a good person, and I would be proud to call myself your father. I hope Art feels the same.\n\n-Salamandra", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note for Help", "Melodystar", "(The writing on the page is larger then normal and very untidy, as if the person writing it was in great pain when they were doing so. There are a few splotches of blood and dirt, aswell as ink spots where the pen paused for too long...)\nDad,", ""),
        StaticBook("A note for Loche", "minitoot2", "*The handwriting is shaky and confused but still readable\nhave placed shackles on me. Ones deeper than any mortal chain so i am going away ... away from you and will live in the wilderness alown, don't come looking for me pain will only come of it.", ""),
        StaticBook("A note for Relik", "iBoaz", "Thank you, Relik. For your warm welcome and gifts.\n\nI have read your book with pleasure. \n\nPlease accept my humble gift.\n\n- Boaz.", ""),
        StaticBook("A note in a head", "Masked Judge", "The followers of Setherien had warned the nation of Malinor. We offered salvation to it, if one elf is delievered to us every elven week. Until such happens... a head shall arrive at the gates of Leumalin every elven day.", ""),
        StaticBook("A note to Ambros", "Geoboy66", "To the hallow old fellow in the mountains: Ambros.  Our last communication, you may remember.  The one that involved the uninvited presence of the great Shaman Mogroka and the Druid of Storm, we basked such communion upon the Equillibrium stone.\nOur journey to the arctic lands of the above ended fortuitous with the marvelling unveiling of the warden that dwells there.  Whilst a grand secret within itself, there is much more that Jynx has discovered.  Much more that must be discussed with you.\nIf this book reaches safely into your hands, Jynx shall discuss what it has been able to uncover with the use of its dark arts.  It believes it understands finally, just what poses this mass threat that Anthos is about to lay waste from.\nPerhaps there is a way we can stop it, a way that we can prepare.  We must find a way to involve the mortal races in this, and band them together for soon I dread they will not have the same choice no longer.\nDo not let on that you are to meet with Jynx, and inform the others if you are able to.  Meet with Jynx upon the equilibrium stone, and together we shall witness a secret of grave potential destruction.  \n\nWait not, for minute time do we hold.", ""),
        StaticBook("A note to Delonn", "Eenhoornheid", "\nMaln,\n\nI know what you did.\n\n- Lelien", ""),
        StaticBook("A note to mum", "[!]", "Deer mumz i miz u plz contrart mi", ""),
        StaticBook("A note.", "Anonymous", "A young, dark elf girl\nAlyhstra. Said a man, \nwas being man too her. A white haired Elven man.  I later took her too eat, and she begin drinking from a bottle. and call the fluid 'Nums' where she told me after, it was blood.\n\nNote: the bottle of blood was\ngiven to the girl by her mother. We don't know her name yet. This was all witnessed by a young girl, who was very shaken up, so some of the details are not clear.", ""),
        StaticBook("A note.", "tilly13", "*The note is written in familiar slanted cursive.*\nDear Laurir Raven'kor,\nI must express my thanks for your approval of my application, as I was waiting anxiously for any sort of reply. If you are available we could possibly meet at the square in but a\nfew moments, as I am travelling to Malinor after I send this bird.\nSigned, \nFaervel", ""),
        StaticBook("A note.", "~", "~By sunlight I glare,\nBy moonlight I stare,\nBeauty in the day,\nVicious in the night,\nNever can I approach,\nAs i would lose my soul,\nIf only I can touch you,\nHear your voice,\nAnd see your eyes,\nIf only you admire,\nI can satisfy my desire.~\nAn -=A=- signature is written at the end, with a single wisp of white hair on it.\n                  [!]\n*a book lays in Nalro's mail box with a brochure attacthed to the front page. The book enscribes:\ncapitol but I'm sure it will make an exception for 5,000 minas. The brochure will show you the company's informatino ((Just look up Adalhard's Architecture on the dwarven roleplay forums)) and if your interested, confirm it through me and bring\nthis book back to me. If not, still bring it back to me. ", ""),
        StaticBook("A old faded poem", "Bolar the Gold", "I saw them riding in a dream, Hell bent upont heir course.\n\nAnd each one with a sickening scheme as he rode on his horse...\n\nAnd so they moved, this world to claim with utmost misery,\n\nWith death and suffering as theur aim, their shame and infamy!\n\nI saw them riding coast to coast, on sturdy steeds at night\n\nAnd evil had them all engrossed, as if they were held tight..\nAnd so they mvoed, one thought in mind, to bring the worl despair, \n\n\nUntil the time four horsemen find their victims unaware!", ""),
        StaticBook("A Old Musty Tome", "Mythras Sylvari", "A guide to Pyromancy.\nBy, Mythras Ardere*\nMagic, is a ancient art used through using energy to form complex spells, or simple sometimes. \n\nIt is said that the creator used magic to form the existing plains of reality.\nTo use Pyromancy you must be quite intelligent. Magic's quite not simple, and leads to be explosions when you mis think a spell, or cast it incorrectly.\n\nTo master Pyromancy you must know lots on your element.\nYou must study your element, and know how it works.\n\nYou don't become a mage over night, you must know how the element works, and why. \nWhat is fire?\n\nFire is a energy element which can be 'created,' or that dumb word 'evoked,' into the physical realm.\n\nYou must think of how the element works as you conjure it, and therefore try hard to conjure it correctly.\nLesson 1\n\nYou must study the fire, and even burn yourself. You must know how it feels, and it's inner workings, you must know how to use the magic correctly less you invoke problems upon yourself.\nLesson 2:\n\nPyromancy is quite easy to understand the basics if you try. \n\nSimply, after your first lesson, you must conjure the fire into use, and use your mind to form it.\n\n\nYou don't simply create fire.\n\n-The Rest is blurred-", ""),
        StaticBook("A package", "tthorn3", "Dear Sir,", ""),
        StaticBook("A parcel", "Unknown", "Kalenz Uradir,\n\nYou may not have met me, but I know who you are. I guess you could call me somewhat of an admirer.\n\nI find myself in quite a pickle at the moment, and I believe that this may concern you.\nIf you are willing to lend your talents to my cause, your help will not go unrewarded.\n\nWe will be in touch.\n\n- Charm", ""),
        StaticBook("A Pelt and Note", "kanrath", "*A small note accompanies the pelt*\n\n\"I return this to your people as it is only proper. I recovered it from the corpse of a human who had been carrying it with them. \nI can only hope that they find peace in being returned to their people.\" -Tenshar", ""),
        StaticBook("A Petition", "Drazker", "A Petition Regarding the Discipline and Conduct of the Oren Military Branches.\nThe men and women to sign this petition have noticed and agreed that the discipline and conduct of the Oren military branches, including the King's Watch guards and other such things, are lacking in the ability to protect the\npeople of this nation due to lack of discipline, arms, armour and manpower. The following petitioners hope for the King's agreement on the following issue, to create a more militarized nation for the protection\nand safekeeping of it's people. \n\nLong Live the King.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSigned By:\n\nMullraugh Hoxton.\nMatheus \nEricus Sarino\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A plea for help", "Ever", "[] You notice a large flock of messenger birds flying overhead as the note drops into your palm.\n\nTo whoever receives my message: Please, help a merchant in his darkest hour! Orcs have stolen a large amount of artifacts from my caravan.\nI will not stand for such wanton acts of theft! Please, track them down. I followed them into their jungles, to a clearing. ( 307, 67, 650). I dared not to go any further. If you manage to retrieve my wares, I will reward you greatly! Do not worry,\nI will contact you in time.\n\n[] The note is left unsigned.\n\n[] WARNING: Combat Event! ", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem", "Patriotic_Fool", "*A folded piece of paper has a poem on it, written in blood.*\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nRoses are red,\n\nViolets are blue,\n\nI flay people alive,\n\nWill my next target be\nyou?", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem", "A Poet", "   Where love is planted oh there it grows\n   It grows and blossoms like a rose\n   It has a sweet and pleasant smell\n   No flower on earth can it excel\n   Oh, love is gentle, love is kind\n   The sweetest flower when first it's new\n   But love grows old and waxes cold\n   And fades away like morning dew.", "")
    )

    private fun _ANTHOS_2(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("A Poem", "Sofetios", "             The Cobbler\n                   and\n               The Crow\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                    -By Sofetios\nI was working in the night,\nAs I bent over a shoe,\nI was working very hard,\nto finish before the morning dew.\n\nI was just about finished,\nWhen what was this I hear?\nA tapping, slight tapping,\nAnd it seemed to be so near.\n\nI turned to the window,\nAnd what did I see?\nA crow tapping at my glass,\nStaring at me.\n\n\"Go away.\" I said,\nSternly as I did stand.\n\"Don't you know I have work to do?\"\nThough I know it didn't understand.\n\nBut the crow kept tapping at the glass,\nAnd I began to get mad,\nThis crow just would not stop,\nNot even a tad.\n\nI turned to my unfinished shoe,\nTo work as long as I could bear,\nBut then I noticed something missing,\nThat would stop me from completing the pair.\n\nThe golden lace that I needed,\nFor this order to be complete,\nI couldn't find it anywhere,\nAs the glass the crow did beat.\n\nI checked my table, checked my pockets,\nAnd then to my surprise,\nThere was a hole in one,\nThat was just the right size.\n\nI would never finish this shoe,\nBy the morning light,\nNow things were dire,\nand my situation was quite tight.\n\n\"I must have dropped it,\nOn the way back from the store!\"\nBut it was too far I thought,\nAs my confidence tore.\n\nBut then I realized \"What's this?\"\n\"Where was the tapping I couldn't bare?\"\nI looked to the window,\nAnd the crow wasn't there.\n\nI went to the window,\nAnd what was in its place?\nIt was simple and divine,\nThe golden lace.\n\nI opened the window,\nAnd took it with care,\nBecause of who gave this gift,\nI was certainly aware.\n\nI went to my table,\nAnd finished the shoe.\nBut then thought of the crow,\nIf I only knew!\n\nI then went to bed,\nWith not much I could say,\nI only did hope,\nThe crow would come back some day.\n\nThe End", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem ((1))", "Sofetios", "              The Cobbler\nI was working in the night,\nI was just about finished,\nI turned to the window,\n\"Go away.\" I said,\nBut the crow kept tapping at the glass,\nI turned to my unfinished shoe,\nThe golden lace that I needed,\nI checked my table, checked my pockets,\nI would never finish this shoe,\n\"I must have dropped it,\nBut then I realized \"What's this?\"\nI went to the window,\nI opened the window,\nI went to my table,\nI then went to bed,", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem I found?", "CupCwakez", "Why does azure deck the sky? 'Tis to be like thy looks of blue;\nWhy is porcelain your white? Because it is thy blushes' hue.\nAll that's fair, by Love's decree, Has been made resembling thee!\n\n\nWhy is falling snow so white, But to be like thy bosom fair! Why are solar beams so bright? That they may seem thy porcelain hair; All that's bright, by Love's Decree, Has been made resembling thee. Why are nature's beauties felt?\nOh! 'tis thine in her we see! Why has music power to melt? Oh! Because it speaks like thee. All that's sweet, by Love's decree, Has been made resembling thee! \n\n~ 'Harren', your admirer.\nDucks.... <3", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem of", "wardog4445", "Soon I'll have you travel with me, you'll see each city and sight, whether it is Salvus' splashfruit tree, or the Bortu mountain night,\nI'll show you where to find the apple trees, and we'll listen to the tavern's drunken chorus,\nAnd as great as my journeys have been, my fondest stories are of you, whether it is the archery games I always win, or our quiet strolls in the forests without shoes,\nWhen I have the potential to be called father, and hold you under the birch,", ""),
        StaticBook("A Printed Sheet", "Mandru VonSchlichten", "THE FIRST PRINTED WORK OF THE 15th CENTURY\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\nIn the beginning was nothing. Then a most supreme being created our world, Aegis. He made Man and Woman, whom had 4 sons: Malin, Horen, Urguan, and Krug.\nAll of them were created with their own strengths and abilities. All of them were created equal. They fought Iblees, eventually, in a great war. Each of them were cursed by him: Orcs to be ugly, Humans to have shot lives, Elves to be\ninfertile, and Dwarves to be greedy.\n\nThis is the short version of the beginning of our history, as according to the Works of the Wandering Wizard.\n        SEA TREK\nChapter 1\nexploration.\nGestahl was not just a navigator. Gestahl was, indeed, a wizard as well. A fire wizard. Therefore, he also served as tactical officer in addition to navigator.\nstocked for our journey,\" A blue elf, who's name was Varstivus, remarked.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Promise", "Unknown Author", "*The note is written in neat handwriting, with blue ink.*\n\n\"\n\nWe warned you. Our offer was an act of mercy - we had no obligation to do so. All you needed to do was give us a single elf, every elven week.\nYou have proven the incompetence and foolishness of your race, preferring to have scores of your own kind taken and defiled. \n\nYou calmly watch while the heads pile up around your city.\n\nYou will be punished for your lack of reverence, and you will be made to fear.\n\n- The Black Scourge\n\n\"\nWe don't appreciate your shit, elfski's... This is a warning, don't fuck with Abresi OR the Humans.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Prophecy", "BUBnbojo", "§§\nWoe to all, the dårk approaches\nOn but one decision\n-------------------\nDear Mela,\nthan the world. You are my light. You are my sky. You are my home, my heart, the air I breathe, and ground I walk on. My darling girl... I love you dearly.\nwe decided to name you Mela.... the Elvish word for LOVE. Faerue, at that point, was my light also. He was my sky, my ground, etc.... \nIn these letters, by darling, I will be sharing with you some things that aren't all that pleasent... That aren't all that happy and aren't all that good. But, I feel that I need to explain to you everything so that you don't quesiton my love. My Mela. \nFirstly, I would like to explain your last name, Drake. \nI had an affair with a man by the name of Dante. Dante Oussana Drake. \nI need to be honest and say that yes, I did still love your father, Faerue. There was no second guessing that. In fact, I broke things off with Dante in order to marry Faerue and choose HIM once and for all. \nbaby girl. As you grow older... you will quickly see how the world isn't always black and white. Sometimes.... you love two. Sometimes.... you break people's hearts....\nday... every day I think to myself what could have happened if I never spent that first night with Dante. \nFaerue left me. Dante was dead. Your Aunt Alanna took you from me....... probably for the best because I was depressed, slightly insane, and suicidal.\ngrew close. When Alanna gave you back to me, we all lived together. \nand so in love. We were so happy together.\nMommy and Daddy started fighting... and it grew violent. \nkidnapped you and I do not know what happened or where you are. All I know is that Spencer and I will try our hardest to get you back so we can be happy again.\nDear Mela,\npunched him. And....\nHe's dead, Mela.\nDear Mela,\nAlanna... \nthe right choice to make....\nEveryone I love dies. Everyone I love dies for me... \nMaybe I should die, too.\nDear Mela,\nwhere my heart was broken time and time again by Faerue....\nAnd most of all..... he can support me. If we find you... he can support you too. And he loves you, my dear daughter.\nI don't think I can survive without you, my dear Mela...\nDear Mela,", ""),
        StaticBook("A Proposal", "RossssM", "*a Goblin scribe has written the note and translated it into common;\n\n'Sons the Creator', I -Morakk'Lur- have decided to take pity on you. I make a proposal, bring me a man by the name Vaclav Pascal, alive, and you shall recieve the two-\n-pieces of the thrones I have in my possesion. Be aware that this man will go to extreme lengths to prevent this, and because of this, we will see how much you truly value these pieces of throne.\n*scribbled underneath is the name;\n\"Morakk'Lur\"", ""),
        StaticBook("A Putrid Book", "wardog4445", "Hear my voice and pray, hear my voice and quake, until your bark turns gray, and your branches break,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Feel your leaves become crisp, your roots turn dry as bones, consider these words death's kiss, coming from my raspy drones, \nEmbrace this curse of pestilence, thy name to you is Drudge, as I soak away your last morsel of essence, and fill your innards with sludge,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\nNow shrivel, break and twist, groan, scream and cry, as if being held by my very fist, come to terms with the fact... You will die...\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\nNow you may fall to the ground, to rot here alone, thank you for listening to this wretched sound, and dying to my deathly tone...\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=", ""),
        StaticBook("A Quest Log", "[!]", "yub lord mi kil twitgies fer u an mum", ""),
        StaticBook("A Rambling Note", "Ouity Deathsbane", "I know what you mean about wanting to do this again. I feel like I express myself much better through quill than word of mouth. \nwords, but I'll do my best.\nWhen I didn't have you, each day was something to be angry about. Now each day is better than the last. I go to sleep knowing that more often than not I'll wake up with you right there next to me. Sleeping, beautiful, mine.\nHow did I last without you for so long? I can't imagine it now, after feeling your warm embrace, your little kisses. Your bites, and your witt.\nYou're so beautiful it hurts. You're smart, but sincere, strong yet gentle. When you smile, it lights up my entire world. I live for your smiles.\nAny moment I don't have your hand in mine, or my arm around you, or your head against my shoulder is a moment wasted. You think you're clingy? I yearn for your touch at every waking moment. Crave it.\nyou got that knock to the head. At first I was worried I would let you do something stupid, and you'd be angry at me when you got back your memory. Or worse, that you'd never get it back at all.\nmoments again. The things that defined us. \nLook at me, rambling about sex in a letter meant to express love. You must be reading this shaking your head in disbelief. Or blushing. I like it when you blush, it makes my heart tremble.\nlittle sad, sure, that I'll probably never see those beautiful eyes again, but I'll never stop loving you. Honestly, I won't.\nIf anything, though I'll try to help you get better. Everyone should be able to cry. Someday, I'll be escorting Ilum to an altar, where some charming young man will wait, and you'll cry because he stole her heart, and because he didn't leave with it, and \nbecause we'll be happy. Maybe I'll cry too. \nWind toussles your hair.\nI'm glad you got to see me smile when you got my last letter, I think I'll hand deliver this so I can see your face too.\nI'm sorry for getting drunk, and then trying to kill Vulmir (not that that went very far.) I just get jealous when people go after you in that way. The wolf guards his love with all of the passion of his love, huh?\nI don't think I'll ever stop saying that. Not tomorrow, or in a billion tomorrows.\nIt's my essence itself.\nI love you enough to be the father of a dozen.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A random letter", "Minuscule_Evil", "Whoever recieves this letter please note that you are probably impure, second-rate, extremely stupid and a mistake of nature. Please do us all a favor and dip yourself in acid, you mindless sheep.\n\n-A mali'thill", ""),
        StaticBook("A reply", "CorprlSkyler", "Dear Famine,\n\nAs I have recieved your letter, as should also be returned to you wit this one for reference, it has come to my attention that you wish to purchase property within the city of Kingston, of the Kingdom of Salvus. I am present within the city \nand can guide you through the available housing and shops at almost any time.\n\nSincerely and respectfully, \nJericho Rylin, Godfather of the King, Conte di Sunfall\nDay 1. 14th of the Amber Cold.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Reply", "Sherria Carver", "Aislinn,\n\nI do not know if you will recieve this message. I do not know what is happening with you, and I understand if you cannot tell me.\n\nPlease, Aislinn, be careful. If you cannot see her now, live until you can see her\nagain next time. Know that she will always welcome you back with open arms. Sherria loves you, too.\n\nI will keep your goodbye to her locked away for the time being, as she would be devastated. I wish you luck in whatever you do.\n*the note is signed with 'Carver'.*", ""),
        StaticBook("A Reply", "TheCleaningCrew", "Earl,", ""),
        StaticBook("A Request", "Azoth", "Dear Nienna,\nFirst, you really need to tell your people to not let everyone inside. It was too easy getting in. Second, congragulations on becoming the new leader of the Delvers. I hope this new position of power will benefit us both. Me more so.\nI simply ask that I meet with you soon to discuss something I wish for the Delvers to aid with. Then, I will allow you to take it from there. Until then, I wish you luck in turning this Guild back to its roots.\n                   -Azoth", ""),
        StaticBook("A Request", "Valmir Audane", "Valmir carries with him my blessing to deliver this letter. Though I know not its contents in full, I know Valmir. He is a gentleman and has shown nothing but kindness and sincerity throughout my move to Lenniel. Do let me read it afterwards.\n-Seth'onn\nHello Joe, I write this letter to deliver a request that I have been fighting back asking.  I would like to ask if it would be acceptable to cuddle with Seth'onn.  She has repeatedly shown me kindness when I was in need of whatever kindness and\npleasentries that I was in desperate need of.  She has been an incredible friend to me and I hope that you will have it in your heart to grant me the honor of allowing her to help me so that I may maintain my life even while aspects of it continue to spin\nout of control.\n-Valmir", ""),
        StaticBook("A Request", "Nienna Calm", "Dear Isabella.\n\nI have but one request. Make Avery's life at the druidic grove a living nether from which he cannot escape.\n\nLove, Mom.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Request", "scharfjamie", "Dear Prince Khel,\nI would like to request something-Would I be allowed to copy all of the main signs in Malinor, translate them into certain foreign languages (I have not yet decided-Perhaps Elvish) and put those up near the originals? It would help\nencourage the learning of foreign languages, and increase the culture of Malinor. Also, it would help those who still do not (somehow) speak common.\n-Nordulo Sudo", ""),
        StaticBook("A Request", "princetonlax21", "Mr. Sullas,\n\nThis known as Rasha requests an audiance with yourself. We have had past dealings with each other reguarding science, and this is another question relating to biology. Haelun'or would be considered the most intellectually advance\n-ed city in all of Anthos, and this one would be greatly appreciative for knowledge of a particular study relating to biology. As a fellow member of the Mages College, this one can assure you of his passiveness and peacefullness to your esteemed people. \nThe book is signed -\n\nRasha", ""),
        StaticBook("A Rough Letter", "SapphireShard", "Stranger! I beg you for your aid! I will award you richly in coin if you come immediately!\n\nI am Merchant Lann, and I have been waylaid by creatures on the road to Storm's Crossing! I require urgent aid in finding and recovering\nmy supplies! They are priceless to me and they will be the downfall of me if they are not delivered!\n\nI am currently on the road to Storm's Crossing in the south of Anthos! You can spot my caravan on the road. \n*a rough sketch is drawn onto the letter here*\nhttp://goo.gl/OPFM7B\n((Remember to use\nall capitals!))", ""),
        StaticBook("A Sad Day", "DecoLamb", "\nI.. I truely have no idea how to respond. \nPogo is not the type of pony to run away, so.. the only explination is pony-napping..\n\nThe world is far more cruel than I once perceived, pony-napping and murder runs rampant.\nEver since coming to the mainland it has been nothing but terror, I sleep in the middle of the barn with a blade because I fear losing my children to a callous bastard that thinks them as just supplies to abuse and sell.\nMY only suggestion would be to place up posters calling for a search. Hopefully, someone, anyone out there will know where he is, and who took him away from you.\n\n-Erin", ""),
        StaticBook("A Sealed Letter", "bluestarr", "Vulnir, Vulnir, Vulnir.\n\nIt seems oem has decided to, unfortunately, take residence in -MY- lin. This of course is an eroor that must be corrected as soon as possible as I am now, currently, out of a home. \n~Fern Telrunya, the \nformer occupant of TELRUNYA lin. (( Yaah aha Fern's pissed yo. This time I want to actually follow through with the rp here so we can skype or rp ig or whatever. (y) Yee. On another note, I really don't care about the house, it's all IC! Oh, and lets pre-\ntend error is spelled correctly.. ))", ""),
        StaticBook("A Sealed Note", "Terafir", "*It appears to be a pact, and exact copy. The only thing that is missing is the small N.\nhttp://goo.gl/yCs9Gi", ""),
        StaticBook("A Second Letter", "Mithradites", "To Mr Ambros.\n\nThis is my second choice for magical training, Mr Delonna. I have deemed him to have a reasonable intelligence, though his even-handedness may not be the same as the last student.\n\nShould he prove to\nlack the attributes I have afforded him, do please speak to me about them prior to any possible expulsion, as I take responsibility for any of his actions through this recommendation.\n\nRegards and such,\n\n-L. Sullas\nChicken Egg Log\nWolfs Notes:\nBandage agent:\nJournal One\nmentioned the 'Deeproad' that had some cold presence. Worth a try. Library is leadless.\nnote signed with the name. Book store as well, may have some leads.\ncreature leaves will cure it. I will need verification as this could just as easily kill her. Regardless, I intend to spend more time there.\nNotes On Weapon Smithing:\n-The outside. The whip has 1 barb per each link, designed to maim.The Combat cross a the end of it can be used as a hook to wrap around your enemies. It is effective, yet very loud, and clusmy, however can \n\nThe Spiral Baton:\nslide outward,  to create a long, metal  baton that can be used as a blunt weapon, and is lighter than a club but hurts just as much.\nImpulse one.\nbar and settle down, I felt like a child geting scolded by a parent. I feel terrible for upsetting her, it was going to be a good day too. I probably need another session but I can't talk to her about it now, it's only going to upset her, I can muscle \nthrough for a while longer; I think.\nShopping List\nCloth", ""),
        StaticBook("A short note", "Unknown", "Gravelord: Nimravur, Spreads taint. Target.\nQuity - Mindreader\nBear druid - Torture", ""),
        StaticBook("A Short Story 2", "Oracle", "bit of a massage from your little delicate fingers.”\nThe comment by his friend caused the one standing on Evelyn’s leg to start laughing as he flipped her onto her back, clamping his hands down on her wrists before remarking over his shoulder\n“Well I’ll give those elf folk one thing. They sure can make some fine women for us, even if they fight like spooked rabbits.” Expecting his companion to burst into laughter again at his words the man holding Evelyn down stopped smiling as no reply\ncame and turned to see what was wrong.\nHis friend was unable to answer because he was too preoccupied staring dumbly as his still twitching heart in the hands of a hooded figure next to him. No one seemed to be able to move as the hooded figure\ninspected the bloodied heart, he was taller than both of the knights and leant on a dark metallic staff with 3 prongs on the tip curved so slightly to resemble a mutilated claw, his face was completely hidden within the folds of the pitch black robes\nand his hands were gloved in tight leather. The spell that seemed to hold them all in place broke as the dark figure tossed bloody heart into a sack behind him with a squelch saying almost to himself “Well what do you know. A cruel\nman’s heart beats just the same as everyone elses.”\nThe man holding Evelyn down blinked and rubbed his eyes as his friend fell lifelessly to the ground, snapping to his senses he jumped up drawing his blade and charged at the mysterious man\nscreaming unintelligible words at him as he ran. Sighing to himself, the hooded figure flipped his staff so that he was holding it like a javelin in a almost businesslike manner before launching it with such force as the charging knight. Watching in\nhorror for the second time in the last few days, Evelyn screamed as the staff impacted on the knight’s chest, crumpling the plate mail and bursting out of his back, the shriveled remains of his heart grasped in the points of the staff tip.\n\nShaking his head as if at the stupidity of the two knights the hooded man pulled his staff the whole way through the crumpled body and plucked the heart from its tip “I think that’s a good days work, wouldn’t you agree M’lady?” he said looking at\nEvelyn, who was still rooted to the spot that the knights had stopped her. Unable to answer the horrid question Evelyn shut her eyes, trying to come to the peace that when she also had her heart ripped from her body, she would at least be going to be\nwith Christina. As if reading her mind the man just shook his head “Now now there’s no need to be like that.\nIt would be hardly worth my time to kill you too.” He said as he plopped his newly acquired organ into his sack. Evelyn tried standing several\ntimes but her legs wouldn’t hold so she sat, controlling her mouth enough to ask “Thank you…. But wh-what are you?” her unintentional savior stopped as he started to walk off, turning to face Evelyn directly “Servant of Iblees at your service.” He\nsaid with a mocking bow. The scared look that was in Evelyn’s eyes died as it was replaced with hatred “You… you serve him? If it weren’t for that cursed ‘thing’ you call your master those bloody pigs would never have butchered my sister!” she\nscreamed, trying to stand so she could charge him.\nCocking his head in bemusement, the man just chuckled “If a Guard tripped over and accidentally trampled your carelessly placed fruit that you are selling at the market. Do you blame the\nKing governing the nation for not stopping the guard from falling, the clumsy guard for most likely drinking the night before, or yourself for obviously placing the fruit in harm’s way?” he said, smiling as he watched Evelyn stop and think about his\nwords.\nContinuing before Evelyn could even reply he said “you can’t blame Iblees for not being able to save a girl foolish enough to run in the way of his mindless soldiers. If anything you should be blaming the men who were too busy fighting\namongst themselves to save her. These corrupt men are the reason why we have to fight, to rid the world of their evils.” They both just were motionless in the silence, Evelyn sitting there contemplating his words and the servant of Ibless just standing\nthere with a small smile as he watched Evelyn. Finally he broke the silence, picking up his sack and saying as he turned to leave “You just think about it M’lady. One day you will come to understand it.” And he left, leaving Evelyn sitting on\nthe blood soaked grass with two heartless bodies.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Simple Story", "Unknown Author", "*The old tome is worn and dusty, and the ink is partially faded.*\n\n===================\nA Story\n===================\n\" Two chaste Temple Monks were walking down the road during a heavy downpour of rain. They came across a beautiful woman who was under a tree, taking shelter. She called out to the monks, requesting that they carry her across a small stream nearby.\nThe first monk immediately moved to help the woman while the second silently protested. The first monk scooped the beautiful lady up in his arms, and he carried her across the stream. After crossing it, he promptly set her down and continued on his way. \nThe two began walking down the path once more, and the second monk remained silent for several minutes as the woman disappeared from view. Finally, he spoke to his brother. \n\n'As monks of the Cloud Temple, we are not supposed to have contact with women!\nWhy did you pick that woman up so casually and carry her across the stream?'\n\nThe first monk replied, \n'Brother, I set the woman down long ago. Why is it that you have not?' \"", ""),
        StaticBook("A Sister is...", "Garukumus", "Sister\n\nAs sister is someone who will do anything for family.\n\nEven deck themselves out for cash so her brother can get filthy rich.\n\nThat is why I love my sister.\n\n-Nigel", ""),
        StaticBook("A Small Favor", "Valmir Audane", "Dear Mandru,\n\nI hope all has been well in the nation, I am writting this letter to ask of you a slight favor, I require someone to hold a marriage ceremony in the town of Lenniel sometime in the future, I hope that you will be able to hold it so\nthat the marriage could proceed, if you require more information send a letter to Kinra Stark who runs the tavern in my town.  ((Minst46))\n\nSincerly your ex-apprentice,\nValmir Audane.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Small Note", "Darkdragon274", "I've done as you asked, and I feel better now.\n\nI'm sorry for the outburst. Sometimes it just... comes over me.\n\nI love you.\n-Relbel", ""),
        StaticBook("A Small Note", "theflyingpen", "Dear Dani,\nI appologize for disappearing on you dear, I awoke this morning at the Cloud Temple.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Small Note", "Mithradites", "To the Book-keeper, of emeralds aflame.\n\nI have a secret that I daren't say to you, as it would be improper to embarrass a woman of your high standing with such feelings. But truly, I have begun to greatly admire you, Book-keeper. You, with your head of\nstunning flame, and eyes as green as a crystaline forest. You have confused my senses, madam.\n\nNever, during the time I have known you, have I ever felt anything of the affection that I feel towards yourself. Your grace, intelligence, and \nremarkable beauty astound me so greatly, that I risk falling into a state of shameful incoherence.\n\nI do not wish anything from you, sweet Lelien, without your desiring of it. Know only that I have great admiration for you, but for now,\nfrom afar.\n\n   Yours, \n\nYour ardent admirer.", ""),
        StaticBook("A small note", "Yannirog", "Gooms, I'm low on iron, some noble man wants a large amount so I'll need lots stocked up soon. Thanks\n\n-Your stall worker, Delzio.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Smith's Manual", "Charoodler", "A BLACKSMITH'S HANDBOOK\n\nBy Tyrnal a'Hgraedal, Smith of Barbek Hold\n\n==================\n\n         =-<>-=\n             |\n             |\n            {}\nTable of Contents\n\ni) Foreword\nii) Avoiding Scamsmiths\niii) A note~\n          =====\n1) Tools of the trade\n2) Notes on Metals\n3) The Cast Furnace\n4) Manual Smithing\n5) Types of Swords and Weapons.\n6) An ending note.\n-->A BRIEF FOREWORD\n\nBlacksmithing is an ancient art. It dates back to the beginnings of time, when the races of Anthos scratched out a living in stones. One bright man, good with tools, may have smelted shining stones and found that he had discovered\nsomething entirely anew, the element of Metal.\n\nWith metal, we have been able to create powerful tools; the lumber axe, the pick, and the sword. (And the shovel and some other things). Soon we found more uses, such as weaponry, armor,\nand horseshoes for our cavalry. Metal is the centre of all war and combat. It is at the core of all of our skirmishes. Iron, Bronze, and Steel are the true gods of war, and this you should never forget.\n===================\n--->AVOIDING SCAMSMITHS\n\nAmong the ages, we have accumulated a lot of cheaters, a lot of liars, and a lot of killers. Some of these folks have seeped into the smithing world, and it has caused a mite bit of chaos amongst smiths.\nIf you are not a smith; here's what a scammer looks like.\n\nHe's going to charge a lot of money for a simple item. An iron stiletto with minor detailing may cost you around 700 minas at the very most expensive, but a scammer will not-\n-hesitate to charge well over a thousand minas for it.\n\nHe may claim magical properties or 'enchantments' on his items. Know that only a true Dwarven Runesmith can apply magical runes to a tool. \nMost of all, he will be in it for the money. A good smith takes pleasure in his craft. The sound of hammer to anvil is music to the ears of a true artisan. For a mere merchant or conman, every strike will make him cringe.\n===================\n--->A NOTE TO ALL STARTING BLACKSMITHS\n\nYou are embarking on the path of a truly powerful man. The skill of shaping the fruits of the earth to your will is more powerful than the strongest magics in the world.\nI bid you good luck.\n-Tyrnal.\n() () () () () () () () \n\n     Chapter One\n\n Tools of The Trade\n\n() () () () () () () ()\n\n\nThere are many tools in a blacksmith's shop. From the most essential hammer to\na minor detailing chisel, all implements play a role in the crafting of great tools and armor. \nIn this chapter, I will describe the tools in detail, and how to use each of them. \n\n---> THE HAMMER\n\nMan-made thunder echoes from the forge as the hammer strikes the anvil, forcing the molten iron into shape. \nThe hammer is essential to blacksmithing as water is to life. Without a hammer, one cannot shape metal.\nUsing the hammer is really really self-explanatory. I will not delve into how to use it.\n\n\n--->DETAILING TOOLS\n\nThere is a demand for inscribed 'family swords' that has hung in the air for a few years now. This has led to the abundant use of detailing chisels and knives to inscribe lettering into the fuller of a sword.\nThey have a rather simple usage. Hit the chisel with a hammer in the shape of whatever glyph you want to put on the sword, and you're done.\n\nPlease for the love of Aeriel, don't make any more edgy inscribed katanas. Love, Tyrnal.\n--->THE STEEL FURNACE\n\nSteel is a versatile substance. It creates superior tools than iron or bronze. Steel is more flexible, and more durable. A steel sword is always far more valuable than an iron one, for obvious reasons.\nUsage takes some time to learn, but is otherwise simple:\n\nPlace Iron and a flux into the steelmaking chamber. Lime ((Sandstone)) is the easiest to acquire.\n\n---> ANVILS\nVery self-explanatory.\n() () () () () () () ()\n\n     Chapter Two\n\n   Notes on Metals\n\n() () () () () () () ()\n\nIn my apprenticeship, my master always told me, \"Know your Metals.\" I feel such knowledge is essential. This\nchapter is but a brief guide on the metals of Anthos.\n\nCommon Metals for\nToolsmithing:\n\nIron - The most common, and one of the pillars of the Anthos economy. It is the most common metal used for tools.\nCopper - Copper is useful for things that are not making tools. It is, however, rather soft, and easy to work with. However, it falls flat when used as a tool or weapon used for any heavy stress.\n((Represented by Gold Ingots/Tools, get a GM to name ingots\nUncommon Metals Uncommon in Tools:\n\nGold - Gold is certainly shiny, and it's certainly easy to work with, but it's not good for tools. Hoard your gold or turn it into jewelry. It's more valuable in that form.\n\nTin - Tin is not very\ngood for making tools, however it is necessary alongside copper in bronze production. It's actually sort of valuable in that aspect.\n((Represented by Iron Ingots. Get a GM to name them.))\nLead - It's dense, and very heavy, and a lead mace or a lead hammer is going to do serious damage. \n((Iron/Stone))\n\nGlowstone - It turns to powder when crushed and naturally reflects twice the light fed to it. Useful in detailing, and making lamps.\nRedstone - Redstone is toxic and causes mild delirium when ingested. It seems to conduct some kind of energy as well, as you can get zapped when touching it if not careful. Useful for detailing, but if used in a tool it is likely to shatter into powder.\nSilver - Silver, in folktales, has some special effect against the undead. Whether this is true or not I don't know, but I do know that it's rather heavy and makes terrible swords. It's not half bad for blunt weapons though.\nAlloys:\n\nBronze is a versatile material for tools, but it's not common with the advent of Abresian steel and Dwarven Iron, which make the metal less common nowadays. ((Iron, named))\n\nThere are more alloys to be experimented with, but sadly I don't know a whole lot on the subject that's worth knowing. Such should probably be experimented with.\n\n---> A note on Carbarum:\n\nCarbarum is the goal\nof a foolish smith. The supposed 'ultimate metal' shatters on contact with iron and is only usable for picks and other tools. Even then, if it comes in contact with any refined iron it has the chance to break into unsalvageable shards. \nWeapons-grade or\nnon-shattering Carbarum is nowhere to be found in Anthos. Do not let yourself be fooled.\n===================\n() () () () () () () ()\n\n    Chapter Three\n\n  How to use a Cast       Furnace\n\n  (Also known as 'How I learned to stop hammering and start cheating')\n\n() () () () () () () ()\nA casting furnace really helps in terms of shaping metal. From a simple cylinder of clay to a large, bulky contraption, they all share a simple purpose: To pour molten metal into a mould, that shapes it into something useful.\n\nPlace a mold below \nthe output mechanism, be it a faucet or a tap or a whatever. Let the metal flow into the mold, pray to the Creator that it doesn't stick or fuse, and boom, you have a tool component.\n\nI still recommend hammering things into shape as it gives you more-\n-freedom, however if you have yourself some good moulds, and have to make a lot of tools, I suggest that you take some of the work off your shoulders.\n===================\n() () () () () () () () \n \n    CHAPTER FOUR\n\n    Manual Smithing\n\n  (The ladies like it more than casting things)\n\n() () () () () () () ()\n--->My step-by-step\nguide\n\n1: Get metal\n\n2: Heat metal in furnace\n\n3: Place on anvil\n\n4: Pound into shape\n\n5: ???\n6: Profit\n\n===================\n() () () () () () () ()\n\n    CHAPTER FIVE\n\n  TYPES OF SWORDS\n\n() () () () () () () ()\n\nSwords come in various shapes and sizes with various uses. I am going to bundle in all melee weapons for\nbrevity, however do know that there are a ton of different types of sword and none are generic.\n\nShort-Bladed Weapons: \nDagger: The dagger is to the assassin as the hammer is to the blacksmith. It has proven so versatile\nand so useful that it is used by most as a tool of self-defense or a tool of murder.\n -Subtype: The Stiletto: This type of dagger has a slim blade and is used for self-defense typically.\n -Subtype: The Dirk: This dagger has a larger, longer blade and acts\nlike a shortsword in some situations. It is commonly used in naval combat in lieu of a bulky sword that would hinder swimming.\n\nThe Shortsword:\nThe shortsword is a weapon that is commonly used alongside a shield. It can be used for-\nslashing or thrusting, and is light enough to be carried by untrained soldiers. \n -Subtype: The Gladius: The Gladius has an oddly-shaped handle that makes it more easy to wield with a shield. It is generally avoided in common melees as it is difficult to\nuse at a beginner's level.\n\nMid-Length Swords:\n\nThe Arming Sword: The arming sword is a sword that can be used with or without a shield in hand. It is one-handed but still has good power against mail.\nThe Broadsword: The broadsword is the military variant of the civilian Rapier. It has a protective 'basket hilt' that defends one's hand in combat. It is one-handed and good against unarmored opponents.\nThe Rapier: The rapier is a civilian sword used for proper duels and decoration on dress. It is not typically used by soldiers in open combat.\n\nThe Scimitar: The scimitar is a weapon first used by the Kha, but it's use spread\nto other races as well. It has a curved blade meant for doing extra damage while slashing. It, however, is useless for a stabbing or thrusting attack.\n\nLongswords and True Military Weaponry:\n\nThe Long-Sword:\nThe Long-Sword is \na weapon that has proven to be incredibly versatile in battle. Its length allows it to be used at some range, and it is devastating even at close range due to the raw power of the weapon.\n\nThe Great Sword: The great sword requires\ntraining to use. It is incredibly heavy but can cut through armor, hack off a mailed arm, and split open a helm. It is viciously powerful and boasts a long blade.\n\nThe War Axe: Not a sword, per se, but a weapon that proves worth all around.\nIt can cut through a mailed arm, and split open plate-mail if used correctly. It is however, large and somewhat unwieldy.\n\nBlunt Weaponry:\n\nThe Mace: The mace is a spiky ball on a stick, meant to bash in the helmets of an-\narmored opponent. It is very good against armor.\n\nThe War Hammer: The war hammer is meant to either act as a mace with a long shaft.\n===================I have run out of paper. Oh well. Good luck on your smithing my friend.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Smithing Order", "Dtrik", "What I want smithed and enchanted\nI only want the gauntlet enchanted.", ""),
        StaticBook("A song for Aegis", "lewismanu6", "*******************************************************************************************************************           A Song\n      \n         For Aegis\n********************************************************************************************\nWe fled from what we feared the most,\n\nAs the undead army drew ever close,\n\nDeath indiscriminate to race and rage,\n\nTainted souls blinded with rage,\nWe watched as the fires burned our village,\n\nAnd the black of heart set off to pillage,\n\nWe watched as the blades pierced out flesh,\n\nAnd our ears filled with screams\nof anguish,\n\nShips of all races and nations gathered,\n\nDifferences aside for all that mattered,\n\nDeparture from this lad torn asunder,\n\nWarriors rallied, through rain and\nthunder,\n\nAllies and foes alike sword and shield in hand,\n\nA united Aegis,her final stand,\n\nTo enter the Nether a war with Iblees,\n\n\nClashing swords in a song of symphonies,\n\nA song we'll sing, the might of Aegis,\n\nA song for bards to be sung for ages.\n\nThe seas were wretched, thunder and rain,\nEchoes of men writhing in pain,\n\nTime drifted by like a wandering soul,\n\nAs hunger and illness took its toll,\n\nThe ultimate end we sought to refrain,\n\n\nFruitless endesvors death cometh again,\n\nMany lives were lost upon this voyage,\n\nSo take a moment we pay thee homage,\n\nThe great land we once knew as Aegis,\n\nRaise our glasses a toeast for ages.\n\nThrusting through the roaring waves,\n\nMonths replaced our count of days,\n\nWe would eventually come upon,\n\n\nThe ancient land of Asulon,\n\nWrought with framine, mosters and earth unknown,\n\nWere we settle and call it home?\n\nA hostile strange yet tranquil place,\nOf rivers and mountains filled with grace,\n\nLet us sing our song and turn the pages,\n\nAs life moves on, so fades our Aegis.\n\n\nThis book has been written by Elhadron Mayliff.\n\nThe song was written by Griffith du Mont many moons ago.\n\nI wrote this book because it is one of my favourite songs.\nWe shall remember the people who fell in the great battle against the undead, and we shall never forget them.\n\nSigned,\n\nElhadron Mayliff", ""),
        StaticBook("A Story", "Unknown", "* The writing appears to be slightly faded, the book's pages yellow from age. *\n\n===================The Deer and the Bear\n===================\n\nBy: (The name is too faded to read)\n\" The mountains were beautiful and majestic. Despite all this natural beauty, Khalith never paid any attention to scenery. He and his son spent most of their time hunting in the mountains. \n\nKhalith was an expert marksman with his bow and arrow; he never \nmissed. He was so skilled that he barely had to aim - he simply picked a target, pulled back his bow, and shot down his target. No animal was quick or agile enough to escape his arrows. \n\nKhalith spotted a little fawn wandering in the forest. A fawn must \nbe one of the most adorable animals in nature, but Khalith wasn't in the mountains to admire nature. The moment he spotted the fawn, he slid an arrow out of his quiver and within moments, the fawn fell over - dead.\n\nKhalith noticed the fawn's mother a few\nfeet away, but he couldn't get a good angle to shoot her at. Being a skilled hunter, Khalith waited.\n\nThe fawn's mother was terribly sad about her baby! She let out a pained cry as she started licking her baby's wounds. As she was occupied with \nthat, Khalith's arrow pierced her neck, and she too joined her baby in death.\n\nNot being finished, Khalith explored the area, looking for more animals to hunt. He saw some rustling in the grass, and he pulled out his bow, thinking \"Three deer are \nbetter than two.\"\n\nAs he had done before, he nocked an arrow and pulled back the string. After noticing a noise in the bushes, he located the source of the sound and fired. The arrow sailed through the air, and Khalith was filled with pride as another\ndead body hit the ground. \n\nHis pride melted away and was replaced with anguish, however, when he heard a groan! Deer do not make groaning noises - that sounded like a human voice! \n\nHe rushed over and \ntore back the bush, and to his horror he saw that he had not shot and killed a deer, but his own son who was out hunting with him!\n\nHe was shocked, and he seemed to hear a voice mock him:\n\n'Khalith, now do you\nknow what it is like to see your child shot to death with an arrow? Animals care for their young just as you do. Look at all the anguish you have caused to the animals' parents!'\n\nKhalith stood there, numb; he was too heartbroken to pay attention to a\nrustling sound to the side. In a flash, he realized that the other animal he had heard in the grass was not a deer, but a bear!\n\nBut by then, he was too late...       \n\n                          \"", ""),
        StaticBook("A Tale of Family", "Oracle", "A Tale of Family\n((Written by Kido122 for the Asulon Novella Competition))\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracle Library\n*Strange Numbers\n((9/23/13))\n\n13th of Snows Maiden -1442\nIt was noon in the city of Salvus and a young girl no more than thirteen was standing in a ally next to a bakery, it was a small little bakery with a nice artistic sign\nwaving in the wind and people crowded together in line and at tables, but this girl had no interest in the people, he interest were focused on the nice aroma of the fresh baked bread and how she was going to get it. “Ok, remember don’t get caught this\ntime and I might get something in this stomach of mine tonight’ she said to herself. She sat there for little over an hour watching the movement of the guards and the people, timing was everything when it came to stealing. When the girl saw that\nthe man at the counter was getting bread out for a customer she decided it was her best chance to go for it, she sprang to her feet, grabbed the bread was off, but a guard soon followed. She ran through ally way after ally way but the guard\nstilled followed. She was going around another corner when, as her luck would have it, she ran into another guard. “Hey” the guard shouted as he grabbed the girl by the arm. “What the hurr….Gabby? What did you do this time?”. “Hey Lorantine,\nsorry about running into you an all but I really got to go.” The girl said nervously. “Not so fast Gabby, where’d you get that loaf of bread in your hand there?” Lorantine said with an n humorous nut serious look. “Would you believe me if I said I\nfound it on the street?” Gabby said trying to avoid Lorantine’s stare. “No I wouldn’t. This is the second time this week I caught you stealing, how would your parents feel if they…”. “My parents left me on my own when I was six, If they didn’t care\nenough to keep me then, they wouldn’t care about me taking a bread loaf to keep myself from starving!” Gabby said interrupting Loranantine. “Hey! What did I say before, I talk , then you talk and that’s not the point I was trying to get\nacross, the point is stealing is stealing even if your dirt poor, now give me the bread an run off, if your caught stealing again you are going to be staying in a cell for a while.” Lorantine said letting go off Gabby’s arm. Gabby gave Lorantine a\nsincere look then ran off. Gabby was often in trouble since her parents abandoned her in the old land of Agies, after she came to this new land she lived in area of Salvus and watched the city grow, then she met Lorantine when she was running away from\nthe guard after stealing a apple from one of the merchants, Lorantine saw that she was just a child trying to survive in the world, he helped her out a lot through the years and he was her only real parent figure, he tried his best to be a good parent\nfigure to Gabby, but she was too much of a free spirit. Later that day Gabby was sitting upon a roof watching the sun set as she often did, tying to remember anything about her parents, but there memories slowly died out and vanished through the\nyears.\nThe next morning Gabby awoke to a strange noise below her, she looked down at a boy that just ran into a can of trash. She climbed down the roof and went to the boy, “Are you ok?” she asked. “Um yea, listen I really have to go because….”.\n“HEY, THERE HE IS” a man shouted pointing to the boy, “He’s the one that just stole my chicken!”. Gabby looked at the boy and saw the worry in his eyes and reluctantly said “Listen, Fallow me” and then they ran off. They ran through the market crashing\nthrough stalls like a wild animal trying to find a way of a town. They ran through an open door and into some ones house, they ran to the roof and Gabby jumped to the roof of the house next door and looked behind her to see the boy standing there. “What\nare you doing? Come on they’ll catch us!” she said screaming at the boy. “I’m afraid of heights, I can’t jump that!” he said staring at the gap between the roofs. “You’re either jumping it or coming with me, or you’re going to jail alone!” she shouted\nangered at the boy. The boy backed up, and ran for it just making the jump. “Was that so hard?” Gabby said sarcastically, “now let’s go!” and with those words they were off. They kept running for hours and eventually scaled over the wall and ran into\nthe forest, as they were running off they heard a guard yell “Next time we see you two here it will be your heads!”. They kept wondering through the woods for hours until they finally made camp in a clearing. After a few hours she finally ask they boy\n“What is your name?”. “Eragorn, yours?’ he asked. “I’m Gabby, so where do you come from?” asked Gabby. “I’m not Shure, I lost my parents when I was five or six and just been going where the world takes me, I been fending for myself for quite some\ntime”, “Well I Shure wouldn’t have noticed with what happened in the city” said Gabby in a rude tone. “Hey I didn’t say I was good at fending for myself” Eragorn said jokingly. “Well get some sleep we need to head off in the morning”. In the morning\nwhen Gabby and Eragorn where getting ready to leave Gabby noticed something fall from the neck of Eragorn’s shirt. “Hey what is that?” Gabby asked. “What is what?” replied Eragorn, “That thing dangling from your shirt.” Eragorn looked\ndown and held up a silver necklace inscribed with two large letters G an E. “Oh this, it’s the only thing I have left of my parents, helps me remember them, why?”. “It looks so… never mind, forget about it” said Gabby awkwardly. “Ok. Whatever” said\nEragorn with a little smirk. They spent the next three years together traveling from city to city and town to town, but on the fourth year something happened that changed both their lives. They were in the city of Hanseti, planning on robing a rather\nlarge home. “Ok, you go in through the roof and I’ll go in through back, we get as much as we can and we leave.” Said Eragorn. “Right” replied Gabby. Soon they went on with their plan. Gabby went in through the roof and started to clear out the attic\nwhen suddenly there was a loud bang from downstairs, Gabby went downstairs and hid behind a door looking at a man staring at Eragorn and his wife on the stair well. Eragorn tried to run for it but the man caught him by the arm, “Wait!” he shouted. “Let\ngo off me I’m not planning on going to jail!” Eragorn yelled. “I’ll let you go after you answer my question, agreed?”. “Agreed” said Eragorn hesitantly. “where’d you get that necklace?” asked the man. “Why, what is it to you?” replied Eragorn\nconfused. “Just answer my question and you can go” said the man staring at Eragorn. “It was my parents long ago, I kept it with me ever since they abandoned me” Eragorn said still looking quite confused. “Kasey, we found him” he said\nnearly in tears. “what do you mean?” asked Eragorn. “We gave that to you when you were little, and we gave an identical one to your sister”. Eragorn just looked at the man and women confused. Then Gabby stepped out and said “I knew that was familiar, I\nhad one when I was little but lost it in the ship on was on when it crashed” Gabby said nearly in tears. “My daughter and my son have returned? I can die right know a happy man” said the man with a tear falling from his cheek. “Why did you leave us?”\nasked Gabby. “My daughter, my son, forgive us for not finding you before, but we did not leave you” said the man. “Then what happened” said Eragorn. “It was right before we all moved to this land, Agies was in great turmoil, but you\nwere children and wouldn’t have noticed, I was drafted into the military in the final battle for Agies, so I had to leave with the thought of my death coming soon, I told your mother to bring you two to the ships and to leave without me, When I found\nyour mother again as she could do was weep, there was a crowd rushing aboard the boats and she lost you among the people, I tried searching for you two for two years, spent all my money trying to find you, but I had to give up wondering if you\neven still alive, but as fate would have it you found us instead and now where together” said the man in tears. “and that’s all that matters, that we are together and we shall never leave again” said the women. They all embraced each other, tears\nrunning down their faces, tears of joy and happiness.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Theif v1:book1", "homijoe", "Clerics\n-Theifs guide\n<vol. 1\n\nLenfarthing farms,\nacross to the homes and over the two bridges, one made from Oak and thinned branches, another made from a tree root itself..\nA third, leading past..\nThe Dark forest, spiders amidst and mushrooms and webs of great, holds the trail of which to follow. Mages live here, up the stone hilltop to \ntheir home. Sheep's wool, a farm, and a gatehouse with streaming fountains of crisp water.\nThe second gate, may not always be open, be weary of guards and mages about. The stove rom, on the right... two store cuboards guard chests with simple single padlocks, a trapdoor leading to the great storeroom..\nGuarded by many a locks of steel...\nTo the left, a homely passage with a golden chest without any locks atall... an easy find.\nStraight through past the shrine room, a chest stands in the center... Locked but within holds armor of gleaming iron infused with light abound. Staffs and Axes too\nLastly, the barracks... homes of guards and tennants mustered about carelessly. Doors unlocked and chests unstowed, and easy pick of litter when it comes to fine linen or apparel worth stealing. The masters room is guarded by doors and padlocks.\nDifficult\nOn your travels....\nbe stealthy, speak to noone, if perchance you are caught....\n\"I wish to speak to the master of this establishment on a merchantry business offer...\"\n\"Perhaps I may stay longer?\"\n\n-Spriggar Stormhammer\n\nCompany Owner and servant of his Kingdom of the Dwarves\n\nUntil we stand, we forever hold ourselves as fools, frightened, weak..\nUntil we fight we will not be free.  *1445", ""),
        StaticBook("A threat", "Burz'ver", "Give us the Druid\nDove\n\n\nBy next Elven week\n\nOr face the corruption\n\nAnd lose your homes\n\nGive us\n Elorna\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A Tiny note", "Vangron", "Come and drink some tea with me.\nBring your friend or more.\n\n- Vangron", ""),
        StaticBook("A Tragedy", "Sagwort", "\nWho’s that walking on the moorland?\n\n\nWho’s that moving on the hill?\n\nThey are passing ‘mid the bracken,\n\n\nBut the shadows grow and blacken\n\n\nAnd I cannot see them clearly on the hill.\n\nWho’s that calling on the moorland?\n\n\nWho’s that crying on the hill?\n\nWas it bird or was it human,\n\n\nWas it child, or man, or woman,\n\n\nWho was calling so sadly on the hill?\n\nWho’s that running on the moorland?\n\n\nWho’s that flying on the hill?\n\nHe is there – and there again,\n\n\nBut you cannot see him plain,\n\n\nFor the shadow lies so darkly on the hill.\n\nWhat’s that lying in the heather?\n\n\nWhat’s that lurking on the hill?\n\nMy horse will go no nearer,\n\n\nAnd I cannot see it clearer,\n\n\nBut there’s something that is lying on the hill.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Translation", "lukejes", "An Investiagtion of an Unusual Translation.\n\nThe Translation:\n\"He who dwells below, wreathed in hatred and vengeance.\"\n\nIt was translated by a woman named Toriel who works as an innkeeper in New Abresi.\nInformation:\n  \n1. It was fashioned from iron.\n\n2. The glyphs are similar to that of the undead.\n\n3. It was left behind after the attack on Malinor in 1442.\n4. It is possibly a description of Iblees.\n\n5. It is currently owned by a Mali'ker.", ""),
        StaticBook("A truce.", "Adorellan Kamura", "-a fine, bold set of writing is placed upon the page.-\n\n\"Time for a truce. We'll go our seprate ways. I've changed, Erin has changed me and I shan't hunt nor attack you anymore, aslong as you don't with I. I wish one the best \nin the future, Kaelys Kaden Hightower. Erin has trully changed me, as I've said before, I write the truth upon these pages, Kaelys. She cares for me a lot, she makes me happy and I don't want to upset her. I wish one the best, I don't expect a response,\nhowever, if you wish the same, then we shall come to a halt and go our seprate ways with this truce.\" The note ends.", ""),
        StaticBook("A warning", "[Ranger] Selik", "The people have suffered under your tyranny for too long. Today begins a new dawn, where the people may be free from your wretched shadow. Viva la revolucion.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Warning", "valon487", "Milo Herbwallow, you stand accused of not one, not two, but SEVEN counts of Hobbitism. Punishments may include public humiliation, and time-out. These charges will be dropped if you do the Salm Melontoes Dance.\nI shall even provide a beat on the next page\nDoo doo de doo doo dum dum de dum doo dop bop de boodle doo dee daa DAA DAA DADOODLE DOO DEEDEEDEEDE-DE-DEE\nDEE BOOOOOOOOOOOooooooooooooooooooooooooop\n      - Academia -\nthe building alone.]\n*A gorgeous, photorealistic sketch of a bear and a wolf entwined in a loving nuzzle occupies the first page, the image framed in twisting (drawn) branches and leaves.*", ""),
        StaticBook("A Warning", "everblue2er101", "They are coming. Nothing can stop that.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Wizard Pocket", "Sagwort", "\n\n\n\n\nTen Things Found in a Wizard’s Pocket\n\nA dark night.\n\nSome words that nobody could ever spell.\n\nA glass of water full to the top.\n\nA large elephant.\n\nA vest made from spider’s webs.\nA handkerchief the size of a  forest.\n\nA bill from the wand shop.\n\nA bucket full of stars and planets, to mix with the \ndark night.\n\nA bag of magic mints you can suck for ever.\n\n\nA snoring rabbit...", ""),
        StaticBook("A Wolvengard", "Lord Commander Starke McHaryn", "*The sealed envelope \nbears a snarling black wolf, the stamp pressed into the soft wax, the seal unbroken, it bears the arms of McHaryn, Starke's nameimprinted clearly on the letter*\n22nd of Snow Maidens, 1442.\n\nHail thy most gracious Master Tuv.\n\nI write to ye with a humble proposition. The Wolvengard have always considered themselves to be friends of Abresi and her citizens.\nAt this time the Wolvengard have many fine steeds for sale, in my ventures this passed month to Abresi I noticed her unfortunate lack of horses.\n\nWell my good sir, we have problems that could perhaps solve themselves.\nI have vast amounts of horses I don't need, while Abresi has what appears to be a shortage of steeds.\n\nForgive me if this observation is incorrect.\n\nWith utmost respect, and many well wishes.\n\nSigned: Lord Commander Starke McHaryn.\n\nRuler of Storm Shank, and Crowsfoot, humble leader of the Wolvengard.\n\n*The end of the letter is stamped with the McHaryn crest*\nBuilding Log-Book", ""),
        StaticBook("A Young Shade", "Unknown", "Salamandra\n----------------\n\nA name known to some, abilities envied by many, Salamandra was a world-renowned mage who fell during an unfortunate series of events, and passed away.\nNone but the writer of this tome know his true story, and if one has the time to read it, the reader shall too, learn the truth behind this great Shade, Robe-Weaver, and Father.\nEarly Life\n----------------\n\nSalamandra was raised by his parents in a rather quaint home on a large island in the middle of a vast ocean that lied on the borders of Aegis. How his parents came to\nlive on said island is unknown, and it is unknown what his parents really looked like. After a few years, Salamandra was seperated from his family, and was forced to fend for himself by the age of 7 years old. It should be known\nto the reader of this text that he was sent away from the island for reasons unknown, and landed on a different island. This is where he took care of himself for many years, in the hopes he would see his parents again.\nUnfortunately, his parents never came, nor did anyone. At the age of 50 did Sala have a house of his own, made by his own hands, yet his life felt extraordinarily empty. He had no friends, nobody to talk to, nothing\nto do but hunt to survive using the bow he crafted himself, go to sleep, and repeat the cycle the next day. Finally tired of this, Salamandra created his own boat, a large, sturdy boat with a sail, and set off.\nThough these \nparts of Salamandra's life were not as active and exciting as his later years, nor as \"interesting\", they should still be noted by the reader. Back to our story: Sala continued to sail, passing many islands as he \ncontinued to near Aegis. He would stop at nearly every island to hunt for food and cook it, staying usually for a day or two at a time to collect extra food for the boat ride as he ran low. Eventually, at the age of 55, Sala\nreached the wilds of Aegis, and here he began creating a new life for himself. Unlike on the islands, the creatures of Aegis were different: instead of hunting rabbit and small game, there were plentiful numbers of cow and pig to \nbe found. Here he stayed for nobody knows exactly how long, but when the four races of Aegis finally rose, it was known that Salamandra could be found amongst their ranks. Track of Salamandra's aging was not clearly kept\nas the years passed in Aegis, so they will most likely not be mentioned anymore, though it should be known to the reader that Salamandra died at the approximate age of 1020 years old.\nAegis the new Land ----------------\n\nSalamandra ventured out of the Cloud Temple without much idea of where he should go, but he figured the land of the Elves would be the best. This is where he began his\njourney, venturing through the woods to the city of Laurelin. Being new to the land, he was helped briefly by a figure perched on the noticeboard. Deltaro Black is the name of such a figure, and he'll appear again in the near future.\nSalamandra showed an avid interest in books and learning, though to his disadvantage, he wasn't good at much else besides archery. Growing weary for companionship, he decided to join a group known as the White Ravens.\nThe White Ravens quickly took advantage of his archery skills and gave him the rank of Assassin. Salamandra's first mission swiftly proved his worthiness of his rank by invading the Nical Empire as a spy, and \nsabotaging it from the inside before he helped in the siege that finally ended the Nical, assisting the Teutons in the battle and earning a mitten on the shoulder from Lirinya. Salamandra's time in the White Ravens \nwould come to an end, however, when he is invited to join the Mages Guild by Ambros. He humbly accepted the old man's offer, and began training beneath Guild Master Indelwhen in the Laurelin guild house.\nThe Mages Guild\n----------------\n\nSalamandra began his apprenticeship by spending most of his hours studying in the Mages Guild library, a source of knowledge not many had access to.\nAfter weeks of intense study, he was able to memorize most of the text he found most helpful, including guides to the creatures of Aegis and studies of the void, including scripts by the Arcane Mage, Slayer.\nAfter observing a magic battle between a turned-evil Rilath and Ambros, he decided that he would devote himself to the art of magic, and respect it to it's utmost. Many frustrating months passed as he\nattempted to teach himself magic to no avail. During this time he sought the friendship of druids, and met Danic and Dante Flormai, two people he quickly befriended. After thousands of failed spell attempts, Sala finally learned his\nfirst spell in Earth Evocation. This was Salamandra's first magical subtype, and the one he never lost over the many years he was alive, keeping the art until his death. Many claim he was the greatest Earth Evocationist ever\nto walk the mortal realm, though the Wandering Wizard and Slayer would more than likely take the cake. He continued to practice Earth Evocation within the guild, until he came across a book about golems in a human library.\nEnchanted by the thought of creating a creature of such maginitude, he sought out the greatest dwarven smith known, Arbrek Starbreaker, and undertook the project with him. Together they created the golemn known as \"Raiga\",\nlater known as a near unstoppable machine of war; Raiga was perhaps the fiercest golem there was, standing at 9 feet tall, and perhaps surpassing the Grey Vigil itself. Foolishly falling into a mad desire for more power\nwith his new golem, Salamandra joined a group of two demonic figures, Vor'Kalan and Sheekah the Devourer. Together they stole from and killed many people of Malinor, eventually creating a fortress of the\nonce White Raven merchant tower that was formerly abandoned. A dark elf named Faeyin joined the group not long after it was created, and became it's final member. \nCries of the Soul\n----------------\n\nSalamandra bought a tent within the Nawari Gypsy camp, and used this place to safetly and discreetly store his items. The places was nothing more than his storage place, \nuntil one fateful day, he set his eyes upon a woman with gleaming green eyes in a blood-red robe around a campfire. Much could be said about their relationship, but Salamandra and Serene Bloodcrest found themselves\nfalling for the other, and eventually had a child named Rae'iri.  Legend states Serene practiced a unique form of magic known as \"blood magic\" to keep herself young, though the art has passed from existence.\nSalamandra became a well-known criminal and was forced to change his name to \"Regaki\" during this time, and after long Vor'Kalan and Sheekah passed, or so it was thought. A portal to the Verge was opened near the Cloud Temple,\nand people began flocking to the Verge from the blight of the Undead. During the wars with the Undead, Salamandra killed two: One at Al'Khazzar, and one in Galahar, managing to take the staff of the fallen in Al'Khazzar.\nSalamandra, or Regaki as he was now called, joined another villainous group called the Dark Brotherhood, a vicious guild of assassins that he benefited with his rare magical abilities, as mages were quite a rare sight.\nSalamandra exited to the Verge when the Undead's victory became iminent and the Wandering Wizard fell, and traveled with the rest of the Aegisians towards a new land and a new future, meeting a group called the Battlemages.\nThe Shade Beckons ----------------\n\nThis part of the book has been specifically set aside, for reasons only the author shall know.\nOutside of Laurelin beneath the cover of a large tree, did Regaki meet a robed figure with a passion for magic as strong as his own. Elnir, son of Rilath, openly offered to teach Regaki the ways of his unique magic, and Regaki\naccepted. This is where Regaki began to learn Shade magic, a very dark and feared form of magic that benefited him greatly. Specifics of training he undertook will not be stated.", ""),
        StaticBook("A1 Sale Document", "Toxzero", "This Document is for the Sale of land in the County of Kilburn known as \"A1\". This is for the Sale of the Title of Land Holder.\n\nKzarkus\nBlackburn\nLand Agreement:\nNo Major changes on the outside of the home. This is the sale of land HOLDER not OWNER. As Land Holder you may live, and furnish the house hold as you wish. Changes to the outside is aloud with written permission of Lord green.\nSteward of House Green: Vaclav Pascal\n*The Signature is VERY Neat.* ((Roll 18-20))\n\nLand Holder's:", ""),
        StaticBook("About my eye", "Knyghtfalcon", "I was talking with the rest of the sentinels, and we came about the discussion of having my left, missing eye replaced with an eye from an enderman or spider. If this is possible i would very much like to know. Having my sight restored would be a blessing\nThe note is signed\n-Loche Kindred Faelcyn", ""),
        StaticBook("Ac'Talarah Issue", "connman", "Chapter 1: Food Production.\n\nThe ruin is surrounded on all sides by thick forests and mountains, making over-land farming difficult to construct. This condition leaves two viable options for farming in the region.\nFirstly, Green houses, or walled pits could be fortified on the upper levels of the ruin. These rooms could be warmed and humidified, to allow for the growth of tropical fruits and vegetables. The down-side to these rooms would be their need for constant \nMaintanence, so only a small number of these green houses would be able to function at any given time. Yet another potential problem with these rooms would be the mold problems bound to arise over extended periods of use.\nThe second option would be to carve out small subterrainean chambers beneath the ruin, or flood the lower hallways with rapidly spreading fungi, as I have taken the liberty of preparing in my hall as a testing ground. the results thus far have been \nstaggering. the 'shrooms are spreading spores throughout the hall way, and several neighbours have complained about encroaching plant-life in their personal living space. soon enough they'll be thanking me for taking the liberty of preparing them.\nThis second option appears to be a more viable, quick-fix solution to the problem at hand. the humans and elves of Ac'Talarah may have to get used to a more fungi-dependant diet, but over time I'm sure this will benefit the Delvers as a whole.\nThe only problem with this strategy that arises in my mind would be the issue of worms infesting the fledgeling mushroom groves. Worms would most certainly attract Moles, and while moles may be a protein rich alternative to other animals, I'm worried that\nthey could burrow into the stone work around the fortress, causing all sorts of structural instability, and openings for potential invasions down the road.\nChapter II:\n\nThe Forge-works\n-=-=-===-===-=-=-\n\nThis Chapter is highlighted due to its' Importance to myself, as well as the delving expeditions that the guild regularly partakes in. \nAs Dizzy is currently our only competent smith, he is only able to maintain a small smithy on the surface level of Ac'Talarah. Although this has served the Delvers for the past while, mostly for Dizzy's skill at his proffesion, the weapons and armor \nbeing pumped out of that tapped magma vent are of inferior quality to those hammered in the deep halls of Kal'Azgoth. This is to expected of course, as the Great Smithing Guild under the mountain has spent Centuries carving out the best holdings for\nit's \napparatus's. \n\nTo improve the quality of the Delver weaponry and armor, i propose that The guild finds a way to borrow one of the great Anvils, or atleast delve deeper lodgings for a forge in the bowels of the earth.\nDizzy has agreed to Take me on as an apprentice, which should hypothetically double out production of Armaments and armor. This will not be the case for decades however, as Dizzy is incredibly experienced at his duties, and a young lad would have much \nhardship trying to replicate his works of Metal. One day though, and perhaps I too will be competent enough to suit the Delvers needs. the Brath'Mordakin know that if the guild keeps expanding at the staggering rate which it has for the past while,\nwe'll soon be bunking with room mates as I currently Am!\n\n-=-=-===-===-=-=-\nSincerely,\n\nKairn Stormcaller\n\n[][][][][][][][][][][][][][] [][][]    [][][]    [][][]\n[][]      }{}{       [][]\n[]                      []\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Acaele Leydon", "Spartan5411", "Acaele Leydon you are the most beautiful Lady in all the lands. I would love if we could become more than friends", ""),
        StaticBook("Accomplice #1", "D.", "\n\n\n\n  The Accomplice\n          Vol. 1\n\n\nBy: D.\nTable of Contents:\n\nCriminal News...................1\nBusted!..................................5\nTips 'nd Trix....................7\nCriminal News:\n\nLenniel does not have guards, but rather 'hunting licenses'.\n\nKrugmar is now once again. Outsmart the orcs and you might be able to land yourself something valuable. A rare war trophy perhaps?\nCheckpoints at the krug gate and the following wood bridge have taken recent effect. Be wary, these are usually heavily guarded.\n\nKal'Ithrun remains unlplucked of valuables. Crime runs low but reward gets higher.\nBusted!:\n\nAusar Tarus - Killed and hung on display in Malinor.\n\nConvictions: Necromancer.\n\n'Fyre' - Locked away in Malinor prison.\n\nConvictions: Stabbing  \na guard with a ropedart.\n\n\n\n----\n\nHopefully you or your friends dont end up in next volume's busted section!\nEver find yourself in need a quick reminder of the ancient lang-\n-uage? Impersonating a Lumi'dirm?\n\nQuick Elvish Dictionary:\n\nMali - Elf\nMali'ker - Dark Elf\nMali'ame - Wood Elf\nMali'aheral - High Elf\nKarin'ayla - Hello\nKer'ayla - Hello\nVan'ayla - Farewell\n===================\n\nPlanning a heist? Look for nearby rivers to cross when getting away. You can't have armor but anybody chasing you that does is going to have a hell of a time!\nFencing:\n\nFinding a good fence can be hard. Looking in the right places and knowing who to ask is always helpful. Dwarves tend not to care where the wares come from aslong as they can make a coin, check there.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ad.Rec.Histor[1]", "Amfionas", "Shadow Times \nThe purpose of this book is to document the recent Adunian history and it mainly focuses on the events and actions that ended in their current state. Scattered and divided the Adunians stand as nothing more than a\nshadow of their former selves.\n\nThere was a series of events and errors, bad diplomatical decisions and lust for power that lead to this conclusion. \n\nChapter 1. The Kraltan War\nAt the begining of anthos, the Adunians lived mainly in Ard'Kerrak a city in the northern part of Anthos which was divided by a river with Kralta. \nCurrent leader at the time was Jar Lachlan Mor Elendil. He is considered by many today the reason for Adunias's downfall and on the most part not unjustly.\n\nWhen Jar Lachlan became the leader the Adunians where still very few\nand scattered. After gathering them together, he continued by requesting land from the dwarven Emperor whom graciously granted him such land. Ard'Kerrak was the provided city.\n\nAdunia at said stage was still young and could still\nprove herself. Lachlan's perhaps greatest mistake was made in the selection of people that accompanied him. \n\nA weird sickness of the mind begin to develop to the young Adunians as they would valuate poorly their choices\n and underestimate knowledge and wisdom.  \nAlmost all of them if not all, did not care for trading, proffesions, literature, noble arts and the strength of the body. \nThe Adunians changed from prideful to arrogant and from hard-working to careless.\n Power and meaningless entertainment were their interests while they considered themselves superior to the other races. \n\nBare in mind, as well, that this sickness of the mind was still in its developing stages \nand did not heavily affect adunia these years. Its consequences would appear later on and reveal their significanse shortly before the schism. \n\nIt was at this broad time period between the arrival in Anthos and the Kraltan war\nthat most of the Adunians adopted a new style of fashion the \"kilt\"  which appears to be a fairly long scirt with specific colours for each clan.  The clan members wore their kilts proudly in contrast with the rangers' uniforms and other older \nclothes which faded away for the most part.\n\nA standard Adunian soldier those days would be called a Garda and this unit of militia consisted mainly of Adunians. The gardas would consist the majority of the population\nof the Adunians with the simple civilians being even less.\n\nThe documented clans at the time, were: \nElendil\nArmas\nCampbell\nClaxdon\nDouglas\nMcLeod\nRovyk\nTarus\n\nAn interesting event that occured in that period was the dismissing of the Adunian Court Marshal Rudianos Rovyk due to his poor military skills and foolish choices regarding the military.\nClan Rovyk soon left Adunia and resumed its activities elsewhere.\n\nDespite that, briefly before the Adunian-Kraltan war a sucessful mission in the north was sent after the destruction of a part of the ice wall with many adunians retyrning \nintact under the leadership of prince Derrek Elendil. This proves that they had a fairly strong military since they were able to resist the upcoming black scourge, even if it it was not at the height of its power at the said time. \nUnlike that succesful mision though the Kraltan-Adunian war that was soon to occur did not have any clear ending.\n\nUnlike that succesful mision though the Kraltan-Adunian war that was soon to occur did not have any clear ending.\nSimilar to this ambiguous ending causes od the war are also mostly unknown. Was it a problem with the borders? Did the Kraltan bandits harrased the adunian military or vice versa? \nThere are only two clear facts regarding it.\nWhen the hostilities began Arnorian Elendil suceeded in establishing peace with the Kraltans.\n\nUnfortunately Lachlan rushed in a day later, resulting in an all out war. \n\nArnorian was soon exiled presumably\nbecause he was hungry for power or the belief that he could lead better than Lachlan.\n\nA few facts should be dully noted regarding the relationship of Arnorian and Lachlan. \n\nArnorian at a vague time period before\nLachlan was the leader of the Adunians, but was usurped by Lachlan who exiled him, branding him as a foolish drunkard.\n\nYears later, in Ard'Kerrak, Arnorian returned requesting any sort of potision. \nLachlan asked for him to prove his worth first. The incident with the Kraltans then occured and Arnorian found himself again in exile. \n\nThere is nothing appealing in war, and neither was in the one with the Kraltans.\n The two neighboring cities would send raids to one another with loses from both sides. \n\nThis resulted in the construction of wall around the entirety of Ard'Kerrak, which covered even a part of the Anthosian Highway.\nThe bridge between the two cities was sealed off and curses could be heard between each city's guards.\n\nIn the duration of this war, Lachlan would aquire the nickname \"Macecatcher\" a nickname he \nwould proudly share with others on every ocasion.\n\nThe nikname was created by the following event.\n\nOne Kraltan warrior or lord, challanged Lachlan to a duel. \n When they were in close combat, due to the minimal distance of the two warriors and the speed of the swing, Lachlan managed to grab a Kraltan's mace by the pole that connected the handle and the mace's spike ball.\n\nThis was considered a great display of evil sorcery by the ill-minded Kraltans which began to call the king \"macecatcher\" on every possible scenario.\n\nThe king being ill-minded himself, was proud of his new nickname. \nThe king being ill-minded himself, was proud of his new nickname. \n \nAs mentioned earlier the construction of the wall prevented any travelers from reaching other northern nations such as Malinor and Lenfarthing.\nThis resulted in great annoyance to the local population.\n\nWhen guards were allowed the travellers would be allowed entry to the walled of section and then usually be escorted out of it on its other side, if the traveller so desired.\nYet when there were no guards stationed, the wall would simply stand on the way.\n\nIt should be noted that the architecture of the wall was lesser to the white roses' one. At this point the war had reached its climax.  The dwarven emperor at an attempt\nto prevent a civil war on a small scale, presented Lachlan a choice. To stay in Ard'Kerrak and fight against the invading Kraltans or acquire a large amount of minas and relocate the Adunians to Brom'Kah. \nLachlan chose the second option avoiding the impending attack on Ard'Kerrak and ending a war with unclear outcomes.\n\nChapter 2.The Schism\nFor the following years Adunia began to dissipate.\nAfter many relocations and the royal rebellion, most of the Adunians scattered.\n\nWhen Lachlan departed for reasons unknown, there was much debate on the subject of leadership. Artorous Elendil III being Lachlan's youngest son was the\nrightful heir to the throne, but he stepped down and appointed Kayrin Elendil as the new leader. \n\nBut many Adunians of noble blood protested against Artorous's decision by claiming leadership as well, \nclaiming that Kayrin was nothing more than a Hightower, since one of Kayrin's parents was a Hightower.\n\nAfter much political strife and debate Kayrin claimed leadership and presented himself infront of \nthe Dwarves as the new Adunian leader. \n\nThe Dwarves then appointed him jarl of Brom'Krah and a new edict was written.\n\nThe immediate result was the schism of the Adunians. Most Adunian nobles found a new home in Oren,\nwhere they prospered as nobles, knights, and warriors. \n\nWhile others being mainly followers of Kayrin, decided to stay in Brom'Krah. \n\nIt was at this time that Lachlan reappeared claiming the leadership.\nHe and Kayrin ruled together for a short period of time, gathering most of the scattered Adunians that did not move to Oren. The Adunians moved back to Vaerhaven and Lachlan then left. Three military orders were\nestablished and reborn but none of them lasted for very long since Lachlan decided to depart yet again.\n\nIt was at this time that the two separate Adunian groups were given their names.\nThe orenian Adunians were called Aduniijians and the ones in Urguan were called Anadunai.\n\nThe Elendils of Urguan, changed the family name to \"Earendil\" to further clarify the separation.\n\nDespite the beliefs of many, their major diferences lies in their beliefs and allegiance, as the Aduniijians adopted the faith of the Creator while the Anadunai still follow the Old Faith. ", ""),
        StaticBook("Adelardi Logbook", "Watty_Banker", "Contacts~\n2:\n3:\n4:\n5:\n\n\n\n\n\nTargets~\n2: \"The Leader of the Tuetonic order\"\n3: \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nExtra information on everything~", ""),
        StaticBook("Ado Revisits.", "Wodehouse", "His footsteps echoing on the dark flagstones of the castle, the figure crept through the dark, dank hallways of his former home. As he finished descending the spiral stairs towards the corridor containing within itself his old office, a wave of nostalgia \nwashed over him, and he halted himself. Murmuring softly, he traced his fingers along the walls; He grazed over the cold, stone walls and onto the rough wooden beams supporting the structure. He closed his eyes, letting the memories flood his mind. He\nstood there for a moment, blissfully unaware of the danger of his situation, with nothing but memories filling his mind. The wood too reminded him of his inescapable Elven heritage, and he withdrew his hand, sighing. He pulled up his black and gold\ntrimmed hood as he looked once more behind him, and continued down the hall.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adoption", "Brother Rydel Orlandir MacLachlan Elendil", "~Brother Sergeant Raigeki Kato of the Order of Saint Lucien\n\nI support Rydel adopting a child\n\n\nI, ex-Lord Marshal of Oren, Walter Stafyr support Rydel adopting a child", ""),
        StaticBook("Adorellan Kamura", "__SnowWhite", "Dear Lord Kamura\n\nIt has been a while and for this I appologise. I have kept myself in hiding and away from many people and I am sure you know why. \n\nI wish to meet with you, if I may be so bold as to ask. I will travel to wherever it is you \nseek me to. The matter is of upmost importance. I feel that you and I share the same ideas and this is what must be discussed. \n\nI hope to hear back from you as soon as you are able.\n\n\nYou are my only hope.\n\nSincerely, \nPrincess Sophia \nAlexandra Horen, the first.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adunia Vol. I", "Yopplwasupxxx", "\n         History\n            Of\n           The\n         Adunians\n           Vol. I\n\n\n\n            By,\n      Prince Braen II\n        Author's Note\nMy name is Braen Elendil, second of his name and Prince of the Kingdom of Adunia. This is a combination of work from ex-Lord Thorenir II, Martyr Hanrahan Brae, and myself. This is one of the most complete sets of Adunian history-\n-which I hope will be passed down to our kin and children.\n\n        -Braen Elendil\n\nAge Before The First\n\nA time ago, during the time of the nomadic tribes of the Humans and Elves, there was the tribe of Harren, son of Horen. Harren carried the 'circlet of Horen', as it was believed Harren was the favored son of Horen. The Harenite-\nTribe traveled away from the original lands of the Horenite Tribes. He led past the lands of Elves, where he encountered the tribes of Wood Elves, led by Chieftess Sarai. Battle raged for years as Human and Elven blood clashed, until peace came to the-\ntwo tribes as High Chief Harren and Sarai married. Human and Elven blood mixed, and so a mixed tribe was formed. They settled on the steeps mountains, where they isolated themselves from the outside world. Haren ruled for most of this age, where his son-\nBaren took over for the end of the Age.\n\nThe Age of Ildunians\n\nBaren's reign was short, as he was killed in battle. Olrandir was the son of Baren, and took the title of High Chief for the tribe. Unlike his father, Olrandir moved the tribe away from the mountains and to the coast-\nof the Northern Shore, where they built a city, but instead of a city of sticks and huts, he made a city of stone and iron. He also created the Clan System, the Council of Thanes, and the Earls, which two of the three are still used in Adunia today (the-\n-Earls were dropped after the Adunians moved to Kaedrin). During the end of the Ildunian age, Olrandir's son, Arendil became King of Ildunia. Contrary to his father, Arendil was a poor leader, which caused a rebellion by the pure blooded-\nhumans in Ildunia, causing the Adunians to be cast out of Ildunia. Arendil was slain by the rebel king Owyn Godwinson, having Arendil's son, Elendil, to take his place. Adunians that supported Owyn stayed in Ildunia, which were called Rhodirs.\n(Rhodir-\n-means 'traitor in the ancient Adunian tongue).\nThe Age Of Ildonians\n\nElendil led the remaining Adunian Clans that stayed loyal to the Harren blood line to the Aegis North, were they stayed for only a short time. They built boats of different sizes, where they traveled across the-\nNorthern Sea to an island, where the Adunians started anew. Adunians scouted the island for days, till they came across a small region of hills, where Elendil ordered the Adunians to begin building a city, which became Ildon, the fabled Adunian city.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Adunian Thesis", "daelaris", "Taelu'iheuih's Thesis on the workings of the Adunian people.\n\nIn my findings throughout the years; every path has led me to one final assertion, the Adunians, also known in their bastardized tongue as  Adûnâim or Anadûnê, are the epitome of impurity.\nMy basis for the entirety of this arguement is the simple fact that they have the blood of Malin's children in their veins, an abominable truth. They are impure to the very core, since the days of the 'Binding of Blood' and this taint is still noticable -\n- today.  I diverge in my topic; Another point that I must raise is their primitive, uncouth culture. The barbarity of it sickens me, completely lacking in any form of progress whatsoever. They shamelessly prance about wearing painted rags around their -\n- waists, show no concern for rationality or wisdom and completely disregard any shred of civilized mannerisms. To me, this shows their complete and utter lack of progress; It is simply non-existant! \nNow, with these two topics  tended to, I move on to the 'rich and prestigious' history of the Adunian nation. This graceless excuse for a peoples began with the Binding of Blood, a ghastly perversion against Hiylun, between Haren, the son of Horen, and -\n- the mali, Sarai, whom many Adunians believe to be mali'aheral(Which only fuels the need for the destruction of these impure filth). Their early history was uneventful, impure half-men scouring the lands for resources and pointless bloodshed.\nThis would continue on until the founding of the 'First Kingdom' and the beginning of the House of Elendil; Naught but unclean filth claiming more elven blood than their people. Their insolence brought upon them righteousness, betrayed by the valah they -\n- lorded over and a sect of their own. Driven out of their lands, they were led into banishment by Elendil 'the Exiled'. The namesake for the defilement that is the Adunian Royal House. They refused to succumb to what had been wrought upon them and -\n- established what is known as the 'Second Kingdom'. They prospered on an island north of Aegis until the days of the undead, where countless numbers of the filth were slain in retribution by both orcs and undead alike, a fitting end for the impure.\nThose who did survive the onslaught settled under the rule of the 'Holy Oren Empire' in Asulon, forming the settlement of Ildon. Led by Torrhen II, their people turned to the 'old ways', poisoned by a Hanrahan Brae, him being exemplar for impurity among -\n- the Adunians, his mother being impure filth, Mali'aheral whom participated in copulation with an Adunian. Her name is unknown but she was likely either killed or banished from an enclave in Aegis. Brae convinced the people of Adunia to forsake progress.\nThey began wearing rags around their waists, nothing more than glorified skirts painted in various patterns paying homage to their clan system of yore. Their speech devolved, becoming slurred and unintelligible, comparable to that of the dwarves.\nAt this point, what little 'culture' the Adunians had devolved into nothingness and they became as dwarves, yet impure with the blood of Malin.\n\nAnd I bring part one of my thesis to a halt. Another shall be published once I've broadened by knowledge on -\n- the subject.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adventure Book 1", "Tantaparo", "CREATE YOUR OWN............\nYou check for inhabitants, finding a cave with a lit torch. Do you look inside the cave, or do you run away quickly?\nYou begin to find food, locating two odd herbs: A red one and a blue one. Which do you eat?\nYou look inside the cave, finding ugly orcs and dwarves. Do you try to kill them or do you try to befriend them?\nYou run away from the cave, finding a huge monster. Do you try to fight it or run into the cave?\nYou eat the red herb, slowly beginning to cough up blood, until you die.\nYou eat the blue herb, filling your stomach's hunger. Regaining strength you decide to build a boat or a house.\nYou attempt to kill the orcs and dwarves, dying quickly to their blades.\nYou attempt to befriend the dwarves and orcs. They like you and decide to give you a blue herb.\nYou attempt to kill the monster, hurting it, but netting yourself a short death.\nYou decide to build a boat, riding out into the ocean. Soon, a tidal wave comes, crushing and suffocating you.\nYou decide to build a house, the dwarves and orcs helping you. You stay alive and survive.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adventures: Sea", "kallimar123", "Day one: It started off smooth.\nI got a job as a rigger. I have been rigging the sails since. Nothing intresting has happend yet but a few rough storms\nDay 2: We have been attacked by a large fish, many have been lost or knocked off the boat. The boat has a large whole. We have no clue whats happening or where we are going. Eventually, we can see a large shark looking beast. People start firing at it.\nDay 3: The large shark-like beast has arrived very close to our ship. He starts to rock the boat very hard. People try to kill it, though it still lives. Eventually, another large beast arrives. He arrives on the outher side of the ship. Together they are\ncausing compleet chaos. People are dieing, and the ship is being destoryed. We can see Malinor in the distance. The captain says we have gone too far, though we keep sailing.\nDay 4: People have gotten sea-sick and many have died. I am starting to re-think this trip. The beasts are ramming into us at out side. We have killed one of the beasts. The other is still rambing at our ship. It is charging at us head on. I hopefully wil\nl live to finish this story.\nDay 5: One rough storm has gone by. The large beast is charging at us. If we don't kill it now we will all die. We need alchemy fire, though knowone seems to have it. We are unsure what to do, and how to kill the beast. Night is falling fast, soon enough\nthe beast will ram straight into our ship. \nDay 6: I have been out at sea for six days now. The beast just took a large bite out of our ship. Right now, I am up in a mast trying to stay safe. Hopefully the mast doesn't fall. The boat is tipping to the side, the beast is holding a tight grip onto\nthe boat.  He has open wounds that people are attacking. The beast is sinking. It is taking too many blows, and its brain is frying from a mage's fire. People are cutting the teeth off to remove its grip from the boat.\nDay 7: I have just nearly been killed. The beast is not letting go, the teeth are not being released quickly enough. The ship is being tilted to the side. There are rumors of a krakin. There are many, many holes in the ship and the bottem is beggining to\nsink. \nDay 8: I hope this trip ends soon. The beast is getting out of hand.\nThe beast has just been killed! Though there are still many many leaks. I am still very scared. I have no clue what to do. I have a tooth as a prize, I will go to salvus to rent this \nbook out if I survive. \nDay 9: Many are dead, or suveraly injured from the beast's bite. The are asking for arcanists. I would like to learn it, though I have knowone to teach me.\nDay 10: Things seem to be calming down. We are sailing smoothly now, people are repairing the holes. A storm has picked up. There is lots of deadly lightning. The sails caught fire as long as the front of the boat. I am keeping safe in a storage room.\nThey are trying to make a large pole using a arcanist, they are going to make a pole of fish. Hopefully this will work, I am very scared that the boat will sink. I have found a pretty lady named Alice. She has been very nice. I just hope she is not marrie\nd.\nDay 11: The storm seems to be calming down. It is still raining heavily. I just heard a loud dragon like noise. The weather is nice and there is no beast. I just gave the nice lady, Alice a ripe apple, and some fresh bread. I think she liked it.\nDay 12: So far nothing intresting has happend. I think I will end this book here. Nothing intresting seems to be happening.\nWritten by\nHaudenfox Redensed\n\nCreated During\nA sail exploring the Anthos seas\n\nThis book is 100% true. It contains no lies.\n\nI hope you enjoyed my book. Stay tuned for more adventures.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adventus Adeptus", "gaiusmarius8", "The days of victory has come to an end.\nbegin.\nAnd the agents of the Ultimate Judgement heathens.\nyour own Rapture.\nthe Dominence.\nlay unadorned and empty.\nYou will rest on knee by His will and laws.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aegis BattleMage", "Oracle", "What The Druids Know About The Battle Mages\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracle Library\n*Strange Numbers\n((9/23/13))\n\n13th of Snows Maiden -1442\nPart One Purpose: They protect people using wepons and armour. If they see a person being attacked by bandits or monsters they must try to help unless it would certanly kill them.\nPart Two Ranks So Far: Master:Makes decisions. The master is Mavrick.\nScribe:Writes things regarding the battle mages down.\nApothacary:Is in charge of potions and healing:Apothacary is:Timothy Varius\nBattle Mage: Main", ""),
        StaticBook("Aengul Bloodline", "Mythras Sylvari", "Aengul blood, is built upon being descended from one of the ancient races. . . That of the aengul.\n\nThe aengul, is a creature of great power, striving to manipulate and or use the races in their own way.\nThe aengul blood within the ancient races causes them to become what is a 'unawakened,' Ascended.\n\nOnce the blood manifests, it's the beginning of the process of ascension. \nWritten by The Mystic", ""),
        StaticBook("Aeriels Teaching", "UncleUnicorn", "     The Teachings\nity. We periodically falter in the lines bound within our lives but we are persistent and willful. To understand Aeriel is to understand the world as a whole and the souls that inhabit it. The gift of happiness, of life, of beauty and serenity; All works \nof Aeriel from beyond, and her alone. With so much wonder and awe she conducts, it's no wonder that it shows through every day of the year. I however, have noticed the light diminish day by day. Little by little the torch starts to fade to the point where\nwe can't see it's full potential. Darkness starts to inhabit the torch, to breed and create an everlasting hatred within its flames. I see this torch daily with my own eyes you see. Whether it be war, thievery, or deception, darkness corrupts and does so \nwillingly among those who fall for it's idolized teachings. We can reverse these ideas however by acting more like our guide and teacher, Aeriel herself. Simply by helping those less fortunate land back of their feet or even saying no to taking part in a \n confrontation you don't believe in, we can potentially make this torch re-ignite for the better of humanity and take care of one another again. For we know deep in our hearts that the light will always prevail and display the true fact that darkness\ncould never be able to inhabit our existence. Each of us contain the torch but who will be the one who will keep it lit? \nDay one\nMalinor but that place brings back memories of my parents. They commited suicide thinking I was dead. \ngood way to make a traveling merchant system and hopefully succed.\nDay Two.\nMonster Hunter Acheivments", ""),
        StaticBook("Aeromancy", "Raxxtus99", "Aeromancy\n\n\n\n\nRolen Veryan\nAn arcane mage has the ability to control different elements and allow that element to do as the caster wishes. The elements that are able to be controlled are Air, Water, Earth, Fire, and Lightning. To control these elements requires a strong connection\nto the Void. It takes months, if not years of practice to be able to muster a powerful enough connection to control these elements. However, a mage must choose the path in which he or she wishes to study, being one of the five Elements.\n\nThe abilities of an Aeromancer are plenty. Once the mage has trained and studied much, they are able to summon Air from the Void and will it to do as wanted. Being the least studied element, not much has been discovered of Aeromancy. However, many \nbelieve that Air is the most powerful element of the Elements, as Air surrounds all.\n\nWith this said, it is not the Air that we know that is being manipulated, but rather, Air from the Void. The mage creates the Air in the Void, and wills it into the world in which we live. He or she is then able to control this Air they have summoned. It\nis unknown if Void Air and regular air have the same properties and uses, but further testing will take place.\n\nStaffs are a common tool used by many mages. Staffs are often custom created specific for the mage. They allow for a focus point for the mage. Many mages will use the staff head as a focal point for the element they have summoned to enter our world.\nIt does not enhance the use of magic or its power, but is a personal preference.\n\n*A painting of a staff covers the entire page. The staff is made of a solid white iron, reshaped into that of a tornado. Carvings of clouds and wind run along the shaft*\n\n*At the bottom of this page, smaller text is written*\n\n\n\n\nMore will be written about the subject of Aeromancy once I have advanced my studies to become a more powerful mage.\nDay one,\nDay two,\n*A drawing of one of the Bloodcrystals is here, aswell as the tenticle that seemed to hold it up through levitation*\nFevyyr has found something unnatural just at the gates of Malinor; pure ice. It is a hot day and in the middle of the day, yet the ice does not seem to melt. Something like this cannot exist. Fevyyr assumes it was the northern creatures who did this.\nFevyyr ryc zicd vuiht y haf bmyla du lymm rusa! Dra Druids famlusat ran fedr ubah ynsc. Vehymmo, cra tuach'd ryja du luhdehia nihhehk vnus dra Kharajyr yhosuna! Fevyyr femm cuuh palusa y Druid yc famm, lynehk vun hydina mega cra ryc ymfyoc fyhdat du!\n-This page is empty-\nFevyyr ryt duu silr cikyn oacdantyo... yht yc y nacimd, cra cmabd fedr yh Amv. Dutyo, Fevyyr fyc dymgehk fed dra Amv ykyeh. Rec hysa ec Ulwaen. Yvdan dymgehk fedr res y meddma frema, fa taletat du luhdehia fedr ed... cu huf fa'na dukadran. Fevyyr ec hud \ncina frama ed crymm ku... pid ra ec geht ub lida.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aging Potion", "ilikefooddude", "Aging potion\n===================Still being worked out, this potion increases the aging process by twenty five percent per day, every day.\n1 Cup Savvil, Crushed\n1 Cup Aqua Vitae\n1/4 Cup Swamp Blossom Nectar\n1/3 Cup Tippin's Root, Crushed.\nMethod:\n1. Bring Aqua Vitae to a simmer in a cauldron.\n2. Place Saffvil and Tippin's in a woven spider string pouch, common to those used in tea making.\n3. Infuse into Aqua Vitae until mixture is a sickly pink colour.\n\n4. Slowly add Swamp Blossom Nectar, drop by drop, making sure each is properly infused before adding the next one.\n5. Leave at simmering heat for one to two hours.\n6. Remove from cauldron, bottle quickly.\n\nNote- Adding Elrow Berries, Drake's Tail or Dwarven pumpkin increases how long the effects last, not the potency. \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Aislinn's Report", "Patriotic_Fool", "Aislinn's Report on the Recent Incident in Malinor=============\n\nI will begin with my first encounter with the \"Sentinel Medic\" known as Laila. I encountered Mirlene, a friend I have known for a while, recovering from a stab wound on a bench. She was \nstabbed by Cir'dian on an expedition, from what I gather. We brought her to Laila's room, where she recovered. She was with someone, I believe I heard his name as \"Dante\".\n\n*the writing changes to a different type of cursive*\nI waited there to make sure Mirlene was alright, but she threatened to kill me if I didn't leave. She seemed to enjoy the thought, and I was grabbed by someone from behind. It was Lyweneth, and I stabbed her arm in panic, thinking I was being choked to \ndeath. I don't think she minds; Lywen is quite a tough cookie. \n\nI later found Cir'dian, his knight minion, and Mirlene in a standoff. Cir'dian was hurting Mirlene, punching her and the like, and I attempted to intervene. He ordered his knight to kill me,\nand Mirlene did her best to save me. Cir'dian sadistically said that he wouldn't have Mirlene killed, but that it was completely fine to kill me. In the end, I suffered two wounds and almost died. Nienna and Isabella saved my life. Unfortunately, Laila\n, under some unknown jurisdiction, arrested me and brought me to a jail cell with Mirlene. She tortured me, including dislocating my hand, kicking me in my manhood, and even kissing me with poisons in her mouth. She drank my blood as well, and seemed to\ntake great pleasure in all these acts. I don't know if I could muster the strength to say them, so writing is my only option. \n\nI later found Laila in the forest, and demanded to question her about her horrific actions. In return, she attacked me, using\nher impressive combat skills, resulting in me losing. She pulled a dagger on me which I managed to wrestle out of her hand, nothing but a weak wooden shiv. She moved and was cut by it, then called for the Sentinel's help.\n\nI was beaten close to\ndeath by Azel, then thrown in jail. The Sentinels, in their brilliance, managed to let an armed and armored man enter the prison and enter my cell, where he beat me close to death a second time, as well as stabbed me again. I managed to survive this, \nincluding a man named Kalameet who tried throwing a hammer at me \"because I had weapons\", although I was frisked hours before. \n\nHaving survived all this, I still face banishment. If anything, Cir'dian and Laila should be \nquestioned about their crimes. \n\nThe man who entered my cell was Jex, and he roamed around Malinor, and I believe he harmed Mirlene in his time there.\n\nThe Sentinels have greatly disappointed me, and I don't know if\nI will be able to write about them in a positive light until they prove themselves competent again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alan's Memories", "rittsy", "Precious Memories:\n- Joined the Druids\n- Grew some trees\n- Jumped off a tree and died\n\nBad Memories:\n- Joined the Druids\n- Dropped some Twizzlers\n- Met a Mage\n\nRegrets:\n- Letting Callax live :I\n- (Nothing else is filled in)\n*Please leave the book in the chest when you're done with it, and don't tell anyone where this room is! It's our secret! ;)", ""),
