        StaticBook("Apologize", "[Bandaged] Donald Etburn", "Dear High princess of Malinor\nI wish to speak to you in a peaceful matter and i would like a apologize for a recent action of mine or maybe my horse. I shall be waiting at you're boat for you to arrive\n###################Signed \nDonald Etburn", ""),
        StaticBook("Apology", "Secretary of the Magistrate", "\nOrokana'Shi\nDue to recent investigation, your request for a Magic License has been denied due to suspicion of abusing magic. If you would wish to argue this decision, send a well-worded letter to High Magister Kalameet Izalith.\nIf you would like to resubmit your application for a Magic License, then we encourage a change of behavior, and welcome you to do so.", ""),
        StaticBook("Appointment", "timzuiderveld", "How to Request an \nAppointment.\n\nPlease take an empty \ndocument and fill out the following information.\n\nName\nDate of Birth\nCity of Residence.\nRank.\nRace.\nType of Compplaint:\nplease choose from the following categories:\n-Physical ailment\n-Disease\n-Psychiatric problems\n-Other, please specify\n\nAfter that place the document back in the chest and a staff member will contact\nyou in the near future, emergencies do not require an appointment.\n\n(Also please add your timezone, preferably in GMT.)", ""),
        StaticBook("Aramis' Lineage", "Lucius di Silvari", "Sire: Argent\nDam: Aimee\nSire of Aimee: Argent\nDam of Aimee: Alaine\nSire of Alaine: Argent\nDam of Alaine: Darchelle\n\nOrigins of Argent: First Dalmatian Purebred\nOrigins of Darchelle: Second Dalmatian Purebred\nThis Lineage is affirmed and rendered legitimate by Lucius di Silvari of the Societe d'Argent. *Lucius di Silvari is written beneath in crimson ink.*\n\n*The papers used are high quality, and an S is imprinted on the back of each.*\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Enchantin", "ventios", "Come to Nym Vala to learn about Arcane Enchanting!", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Magic", "Merchant Lann", "Arcane magic has its source in a mysterious and ill-defined realm known as the void. The exact nature of the void is something which has perplexed those of magical inclination for centuries.\nSome would say that the void is both something and nothing at the same time, however more accurately it is a realm of infinite power. It is from this realm that a mage draws from and combines this power with their mana.\nIn this way a mage shapes their spell and brings it into reality from the realm of the void into our own.\n\nHowever, it is to be noted that pulling such power from the void is no easy task.\n For one to be able to control both the amount of power and the form of their desired magic is no easy feat. \n\n Magic is despite this a path followed by more than one. A path of difficulty and power.\nStruggle and triumph. Enlightenment and dissapointment.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Origins", "Eenhoornheid", "\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin'evaral, The Enclave of Haelun'or,\nSince long into the past mages have existed. Pulling their spells and magic into reality. Different mages find themselves specializing in different forms of the arcane. However, the root of this magic throughout those who practice the arcane magic\nis the same. Each arcane mage finds their source of magic from a realm known as the void, to which each living and sentient being is connected.\nThe void itself is a realm of infinte potential, yet almost paradoxically is entirely comprised of nothing. It is from this absolute and undetermined potential which spells and magic is pulled forth from. Connecting only with their minds a mage\nmust take this void and change it into the form which they desire. For an evocationist this is their preferred element; be it earth, wind, water or fire. For other this may be an illusion, pulling forth light and twisting the minds of their targets.\nHowever, it is to be noted that pulling such power from the void is no easy task. For one to be able to control both the amount of power and the form of their desired magic is no easy feat. Indeed, many a novice finds themselves rendered unconscious\nsimply upon their first connection to the void. But, with practice over time balance is achieved and this some of the most potent arcane magic is created.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Shielding", "BrandNewKitten", "     \n    Arcane Shielding\n\n  Discovered by\n  \nIatrilemar Elervathar\n\n*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*\n\n  \nArcane shielding is the act of evoking pure magical energy into a malleable and defensible shield to block physical attacks to yourself or wherever you place your shield. It has been found that the shield takes on many of the same properties as glass.\nWhen starting off on this form of evocation you will find difficulty in pulling it from the void. The main reason for this is the fact that glass is only partially what you are imitating. The act of casting an arcane shield deals with the use of auras.\n          Auras\n-------------------  An aura is more or less a space around all living things that holds mana. Sentient beings are said to have more advanced auras that will take color based on their personality. The color of one's aura directly \ncorrelates to the shield being produced. The reason for this because to cast a shield the magi must use their aura to give shape to the pure arcane energy. Think of the aura as a funnel. Arcane energy goes in and the spell comes out.\n     Basic Shielding\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-\n\nBalance is the dominating factor in Arcane shielding. If one lacks a sense of balance they will not only find sustaining a shield to be difficult but impossible. One must find a sense of balance in their life\ntheir body, their mind and their magic. Once that is achieved and only when that is achieved casting a shield shall be possible. \n\nThe most basic spell to cast and the first one that any mage seeking to shield will learn is the arcane disc, a\nflat circular shaped spell. From this the caster will be able to expand it to create larger walls of shields and with some luck and skill the ability to flex the disc around objects or ones self.\n\nThe first thing one will notice when trying to form a disc\nis a faint colored aura emitting from the focal point. The substance seen is the arcane energy attempting to take shape. With practice a user will be able to give shape to the aura and begin to form the disc from the most center point of the users focus. \nI commonly refer to this as the epicenter of the of disc. Once the disc is mastered the uses of the shield are greatly increased.\n\n       Applications\n       of a Shield\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_- \nTheoretically the shield can expand an\ninfinite amount of space if the caster has an infinite supply of mana. \n\nHowever more common uses involve blocking physical harm dealt to the user via acting as a barrier. Once the shielder is able to flex their magic they will soon be able to \nachieve a full shield or a bubble shield. The bubble is a complete barrier around the user but the amount of mana being drained off the user is increased. The bubble shield is really only viable when the caster is being engaged from multiple directions. \nOtherwise it is simply a waste of mana. \n\nSame with expansion the shield can theoretically take on an infinite thickness however thickening the shield is multiple times more taxing on the caster than epxanding the shield. \nInstead a common use of thickening a shield is to time out an attack and thicken it as the attack is in motion only to lessen it to conserve mana.\n\nAnother common use of thickening a shield and one of the only offensive capabilities to the shield is using\nthe shield to bash an opponent in. While highly ineffective it can still be a viable method in fighting if no other alternative are present. \n\nThe third most common use of a shield is split ones focus to evoke a second shield. The second shield\ncan be used to not only block the user but any other thing or ally. \n\nOne thing that cannot be done with the shield is using it as a projectile. The disc shape simply cannot hold and the user cannot send their shield flying at high\nspeeds. The shield often uses the user as sort of a pivot point and will move around them so because of this the shield cannot fly straight forward into an opponent unless the caster is moving forward as well. As the caster's strength in magic increases\nthey will find themselves able to cast the shield at farther distances without an overwhelming sense of fatigue.\n\n   \nThe shattering effect\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_- \nWhen a shield is put under too much stress it will shatter much like glass before dispersing back to the void. While harmless at a distance the shards of shield produced are  sharp and flying in the immediate viscinity at rapid speeds. A novice in arcane \nshielding who can only cast thier shield in a very close proximity might end up impaling their hands or themselves from the shards. The reason that this happens is because the user who had their shield broken would already be drained of magic and instead \nof their focus being diverted to preventing the shard effect they are focusing on keeping their shield up as long as they can. This of course can easily be prevented and a user reading this book now has the knowledge to prevent self-harm. \n\nThe shard effect can also be useful though. The user can purposefully allow an opponent to shatter their shield in hopes of having the attacker accidently cutting themselves from the shield. While ineffective compared to say a sword the shards can still \ncause severe bleeding.\n\nWhen studying shielding one should seek out a glassmaker to observe the way they meld and shape the glass since it is the only substance in existence that resembles the shield.\nOne would also find it helpful to practice shielding on something that would test one's balance. Acrobatics, gymnastics and other forms of balancing arts are indefinitely helpful to learning how to successfully shield.\n\nOne will find that the substance \nevoked will have a slight glow to it. It is not advised that the caster attempt to sneak up on someone using a shield in the dark. You will find that to be highly inefficient.\n\nShielding is and will always be the most \ndefensible magic but at the cost of \nlacking offensive capabilities. It is recommended that the caster take on a seperate offensive subtype should they wish to use this magic in combat.\n\nUse it defend yourself, your allies, block passageways, deflect projectiles\nprevent the valah's curse.\n\nOne last warning. Attempt to shield mental magic such as illusion and you will soon learn the foolish nature of that decision.\n\n\n\n~Iatrilemar Elervathar,\n\nThe first Arcane Shielder. Inventor of the magic. \n\nThe 12th Arcane Mage.", ""),
        StaticBook("Archery Guide I", "SuperPandaKing", "Content:\nI: Bow and Arrow quality.\nII: Physical tips.\nIII: Corners.\nIV: String power explained.\nV: Useful equipment.\nVI: Why a bow?\nVII: Height of the bow.\nVIII: Situations to use a bow.\nIX: Shooting while moving.\nX: Short summary.\n***********************\n\n\n\n\n\n\n     Written by Arendil Entheos\n              Elf, Malinor\nChapter I: Bow and Arrow quality\n\nThe quality of a bow is probably the most important thing of archery. It decides the power, dubarility, and flexibility. The most useful and powerful wood are the branches of a Oak tree, found at\nMalinorr, the elven land.\nChapter II: Physical Tips\n\nIn order to use a bow correctly, some physical things are required. Such as strong arms, good eye co-ordination, controlled nerves and ofcourse, patience. If you got them all, you're able to use a bow correctly. \nChapter III: Corners\n\nThe position of your bow is decided with the corner-system. You got four corners, Neast, Seast, Wouth, and Nest.\n- Neast: North-East\n- Seast: South-East\n- Wouth: West-South\n- Nest: North-East\n\nThese corners have to be based on the po\n-sition of your target. If your target is on a hill at your right hand, you should use the Neast position in order to take him, without moving your body to him.\n\n\n0\n------\n    |\n    |\n    |                  [0\n=====================\nChapter IV: String power explained\n\nString power decided how far and powerful your arrow will be. there are 3 sections when you pull the string of your bow:\nSection 1: 5 - 9 Meters\nSection 2: 11 - 18 Meters\nSection 3: 18 - 27 Meters\n\nSection 3 is the most\npowerful one. Section 1 is most weak one. Section 3 can be a deadly shot, altough section 1 can only damage someone. Shooting a person, section 3 is the best to use in that case. For animals, section 1 - 2 can be enough. For an evil creature, section 2 is\nstrongly recommended. Ofcourse, arrows will fall by the nature's gravity. This can be controlled by using the corner system and height of your location.\n\ns1: ] - - - - - - - - >\ns2: ] - - - - - - - - - - - >\ns3: ] - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - >\nChapter V: Useful equipment\n\nArchery needs equipment, such as a quiver, gloves, leather clothing and good boots. Also, a cape is good to hide and become one with the environment. The equipment is up to you, but some things are better than others.\nChapter VI: Why a bow?\n\nBefore, swords were the ultimate way to hunt down a target. But, there was one problem. While fighting your target at that range, you could be harmed easily. The bow allows you to hunt down a target at a large range without getting\nhurt. Also, the bow can be alot more effective then the classic sword. Still, the sword is good backup to have. \n\nStep 1: Choose Your Corner.\nStep 2: Shoot with your bow.\nstep 3: Run to your target and finish him with your sword / bow.\nChapter VII: Height of a bow.\n\nThe height of a bow is very important to decide the range of your arrow. If the bow is at a medium height, it'll shoot further then when it's very low or Too high. This is very important to remember while using your bow.\nChapter VIII: Situations to use a bow.\n\nIt's not always needed to use a bow. When you can het your target easily at a good range, that's the first thing you should do. But, if you're at a higher position, the bow is best thing to use.\nChapter IX: Shooting while moving\n\nWhen you're chasing a target, or jumping from building to building, there are a few moments where shooting is has the best effectiveness. While running, shoot when you're near to a tree or obstacle to get cover.\nChapter X: Short summary.\n\nAlthough archery needs alot practising, it's worth it. By using the right tactics and having the requirments, you're able to become a master of the bow...\n\n\nArendil Entheos, 315 yrs.", ""),
        StaticBook("Archive", "SapphireShard", "sewgfwjgepiogjegoegrjelgjergiejgpwkifwfkw[ef[pfkwfowkgpegkepgkmepgrjkeprgbvmepbmerpbgmeprgokerpgkegkeprgokepgkrepgkepgkeprgegergegrergergergerggrgggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggg", ""),
