        StaticBook("Books for Sale", "Sofetios", "   Sofetios's Fiction\n     Bookshop and\n       Restuarant\n\n\nBooks available\n\nAll books cost 10 minas.\n\nBooks to write in cost 5 Minas.\nA Game of Minds\n\nChapters 1, 2, 3, and 4\n\nGenre: Adventure\n\n\nThe Jayan\n\nChapters 1 and 2\n\nGenre: Adventure\nOdd Events\n\nChapters 1 and 2\n\nGenre: Slight Horror\nPoetry V1\n\nGenre: Poetry\nImmortal\n\nGenre: Poetry\nMelunis the Mad\n\nGenre: Philosophical\nJaya's Journey\n\nGenre: Adventure", ""),
        StaticBook("Boot Camp Manual", "The Faceless Man", "Boot Camp Procdure:\nThis book contains the boot camp procedure to be used by Wardens and the March-Warden whenever necessary.\n\nOriginal Procedure created by Warden Mentecor of Malinor\n\n\n1. Pushups- the key to a superior army is the upper body strength of the soldiers. Pushups are a necessity for any training activity.\n((Have recruits roll out of 20; 5 and above is a successful performance of five pushups. Typically have recruits do two\nsets of ten pushups. If they fail, have them add ten more reps to their amount needed to be done.))\n\n(Sit-Ups follow the same procedure)\n2. Running- endurance is a necessity within any army; the longer an army can fight, the higher the chances they will succeed. Have a horsed Sentinel lead the other recruits, Sentinels, Vanguard, and Lumilleran on a run around the city. After this, feel\nfree to establish races. The loser(s) of each race must perform ten pushups successfully or ten more shall be added on. Cutting soldiers slack will only lead to a weak force.\n\n3. Archery and Swordplay- Honing the actual combat skills of soldiers are important. Set up two stations: station one is archery, station two is swordplay. Alternate the Lumi'drim between these stations so that they both get equal reps at both stations. \n((Archery should be done at the range, of course, and Swordplay can either be RPed on by using dumbies or by having two trainees using /duel to PVP each other without threat of death. For swordplay, have all armor off and use wooden weaponry.))\n4. Hand-To-Hand Combat- much like swordplay, have two trainees brawl ((using the /duel command)). The winner is safe, but the loser must do push-ups or sit-ups. \n5. Cavalry- this training exercise is purely optional. All soldiers that own horses should be lead on a small expedition to learn to better navigate with their horses. Have a Warden of above lead this expedition.\nThis is the end of the boot camp manual. Remember to give the soldiers breaks, as they are not supernatural beings (though if they are, feel free to do whatever you please). Follow the guidelines;\n\n-Warden Mentecor", ""),
        StaticBook("Born by Flame", "Toriel", "Tale of the Old Man\nyearning in his heart.\nOne day, he reached a great clearing in a verdant vale, where he found a hawk. The hawk was crippled, and lay upon the ground defenseless.\nalmost reverentially as he lifted the crippled hawk. The bird remained still.\nuntil it was fully healed. \nEventually, the old man knew his time had come. He lay down, and knew that this would be his final rest before he departed. As he lay, the hawk hopped onto his chest and lay down upon him, nuzzling him gently. \nhawk's eye - the first tear of any animal. As the hawk cried, so did the animals of the forest, who mourned him for many days and nights.\nwith great care. They pushed the man out onto the lake, the raft bobbing gently in the  placid waters.\nperished man and his eagle.\nthe gentle breeze carrying the charred raft back to shore.\n\n\nin search of one to call his friend, one that he so dearly missed without knowing why, like the shadow of a memory in the back of his mind.\n And so the tale of the Phoenix began anew.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bothdur Ironaxe", "ixTec", "Diary of Bothdur Ironaxe.\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - \n\nDay #2 :\nFinally I've sold the last of my goods. I've even made enough to buy more and still have some spare to jingle in my pocket! Kal'Ithurn is definitely what the ->\nothers had claimed it to be. I leave there a Dwarf with a loaded wagon and loud pockets. I make my way to Abresi and hope to be there in under two weeks! My daughter, Dritta, seems happy enough to leave. She never enjoyed our time there and looks ->\nforward to seeing the grand cities of the Humans.\n\n- - - - - - - - - - -\n\nDay #5 :\nThe roads after the Dwarven Capital are a nightmare to travel along! The stones all uneven and holes scattered ->\nall over. Dritta moans from within her makeshift bed ontop of the goods, complaining as she tries to sleep. We're both looking forward to resting within the Cloud Refuge before moving any further and should be there by the next evening.\n->\n- - - - - - - - - - - \n\nDay #6 :\nGreat! Just as we were crossing the bridge into the Nations Crossing, the wagon gets stuck in a crack and one of the wheels crack. I directed the horse leading our wagon slowly across the rest of the ->\nbridge and stop to the side of the road between some trees. We used our last spare wheel back on the Dwarven road and so I've sent Dritta into the Cloud Refuge to see if she can find a Carpenter or someone to help us fix it. She should be back by ->\ntomorrow.\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - \n\nDay #7 :\nDritta's still not back and it's getting dark. I hope she's not come to harm. I'll have to try and light us a fire behind the wagon for when she gets back. I'm sure she'll be ->\nhungry.\n\n- - - - - - - - - - -\n\n[!] The rest of the book seems empty. The quill leaving a large ink spot where it was left between them in a hurry.\nAlchemy Testing Guide\nFor this potion I used an Air Symbol(Egg) and I added an Elf's hair vine(String) to the mixture. \nFor this I used Tippensroot and a bit of Dwarf's Pumpkin\nI used Elrow Berries, Frost Vine, and Saffvil. No clue why.", ""),
        StaticBook("Boundwise Brews", "Pepernoot", "The Boundwise homebrews are all made with great care by halflings of the Vale. The hops and herbs are selected with great care from the lush and fertile farms of Lenfarthing.\n\nCurrently two brews are available;\nBounderale\n----------\nA strong lightly coloured ale with a high proof, with a light fruity and sweet taste. Not recommended for the younguns.\nBounderbeer\n-----------\nA light beer with a hint of herbs, perfect drink with a meal or after a long hot day.\nTo order one of the brews, send a bird to Dudo Boundwise or\nPansy Boundwise, \nLenfarthing.\n\n((Pepernoot/fbPatty))", ""),
        StaticBook("Box Contents", "merrymoogle", "Inside the box are as follows:\n\n- A red rose\n\n- A few papers of folded music lyrics.\n\n- Two wooden dolls. One a boy, with blonde hair, green eyes, and a red overcoat. The other a girl, with\na beautiful light blue dress, similarly colored eyes, and rich brown hair. Inscribed into the lid of the box are the words \"I'm always here for you\", which, when spoken aloud while the box is open, will cause it to start playing the tune to the song the \nlyrics are written for. ((http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0_zbeZ2Mdic , or \"Love is an Open Door - Frozen\".)) The dolls will stand up, embrace each other, and begin to dance until the song ends before laying back down.\nIn this world, there are many people. Some are evil men and women, always bound to destroy. Some create, with the world as their canvas. And some are meant to defend, protecting all.\nMeet the Valiants:\nDvari Steel-Anvil: This Commandant is... different. He is a fierce fighter who spent many years on his own, and is quick to anger. However, he leads the Valiants well, and has moments of kindness in him. \nToby Williams: A sly man who can throw his knives accurately from very far. He has a strong sense of family, and sees his duty above all else. He does not give up, no matter what. In place of all the Valiants, he is quite calm.\nGuren (Surname Unknown): Guren is a very kind individual with not much heart for fighting, but heart for everything else. Using a cane and wits, Guren defends the other Valiants in any way. Guren is also quite clever, understanding more than let on.\nKristian von Craw: A very skilled fighter and strong, he uses a blade to fight. He is very honourable, and will only strike if struck first, and sometimes not at all, if the situation demands it. He normally takes the side of peace.", ""),
        StaticBook("Brathmordakin", "zuluman111", "The Brathmordakin are the Dwarven Gods, the diving rulers of the race. There are seven dwarven gods with Yemekar as the strongest and the de facto leader. The reason dwarves worship a god is to secure a place for their souls in the afterlife. \nWhen a dwarf dies, his soul travels to Dungrimm’s keep on the moon where it is auctioned off to the god who bids the highest for it. A dwarf that has faithfully served their god in life will have a much greater chance of being bought by and serving \nthat god in the afterlife.\nYemekar – (yem-eh-kar)\n“The Maker”\n\nSymbol: Hammer & Anvil\n\nAlignment: Lawful Good\n\nPortfolio: Creation, leader, smithing, protection, metalcraft, stonework, fire\n\nAnbella – (an-bell-ah)\n“Hearth Mother”\n\nSymbol: Two Silver Rings\n\nAlignment: Lawful Good\n\nPortfolio: Safety, honesty, home, healing, marriage, fertility, family, records, oaths, water, nature, peace\nDungrimm – (dun-grim)\n\n“Guardian of the Dead”\n\nSymbol: An Iron Mask\n\nAlignment: Lawful Good\n\nPortfolio: Battle, valor, bravery, honor, defense, the dead, the moon\n\nBelka – (bell-kah)\n“Lady of Passion”\n\nSymbol: A Lightning Bolt\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Good\n\nPortfolio: Love, romance, youth, dancing, courtship, explorers, travelers, seduction, lightning\n\nOgradhad – (og-rad-had)\n\n“The Lore Master”\n\nSymbol: An Open Book\n\nAlignment: Neutral\n\nPortfolio: Scholarship, invention, discovery, knowledge, magic\n\nArmakak – (arm-a-kak)\n“Merchant Father”\n\nSymbol: A Gold Coin\n\nAlignment: Neutral\n\nPortfolio: Wealth, luck, chance, negotiation, merchant, cleverness, the sun\n\nGrimdugan – (grim-doo-gan)\n“Lord of Avarice”\n\nSymbol: Obsidian Dagger\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Neutral\n\nPortfolio: Greed, money, merchants, thieves, shadows\nDormmar – (door-mar)\n\n\"The Flesh Lord\"\n\nSymbol: Unknown\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Neutral\n\nPortfolio: The Doomforged, Runes\n\n*Copied from the Archives of the Clergy by Neophyte Gulroid Goldhand", ""),
        StaticBook("Brewing", "Ambros", "1. Harvest fully grown hops.\n\n2. Put bucket of water into cauldron.\n\n3. Place hops into cauldron. [Right-click]\n\n4. Add ingredients as needed.\n\n5.Put brew into mugs and enjoy!", ""),
        StaticBook("Brewing Ale", "Sofetios", "        Brewing Ale\nThis book is my experience brewing beer. \nTo start out with making some beer,  Here is what you will need to make 6 mug-fulls of ale, or a keg-full.\n((\n((\nNow, to start out you need to get some barley seeds. This will be what makes the hops for later on. Different types of land ((Biomes)) produce different types of Barley seed. To collect the barley seed, you will need a special tool called a Sickle.\n((To craft sickle, one stick bottom left, one stick middle, three other building materials bottom middle, middle right, and top middle.))\nWhen you have your sickle,  you can collect seeds from tall or short grass. Tall grass probably has a higher chance of getting good seeds. You can mix different seeds. \n. ((When mixing seeds, you can get nothing, one type or both types. I have found that you can’t get three types.))\nNow that you have your Barley seeds, it’s time to make them into hops. Find suitable farm ground and plant the seeds. When they are fully grown, harvest them. Now the fun part begins. Brewing.\nYou will want to be near a water source that won’t go out. Once you have one, place down your cauldron and fill it near the top with water. ((right click on the top of it with a water bucket)). \nNow add in the hops that you harvested and perhaps an additional brew able ingredient.\n((Some brewable ingrediants include but are not limited to: Carrots, Wheat, Pumpkins, Sugar cane, Mushrooms, Saplings, apples, cactus, and more.))\nNow its time to store your brew in a keg. ((to make three kegs, it is, one iron ingot on the middle left, and three logs on the bottom middle, right middle, and top middle.))\nYou will want to make your brew twice to fill up the keg. ((you transfer the ale with mugs. To make three mugs, it s a fence and a log next to each other. Left click on the top of the cauldron with the brew in it to get one mugful per time. \nThen right click the nozzle (tripwire hoop) of the keg to put it in.)) Each time you brew something will make three mugfulls or half a keg.\nNow comes the hard part. Waiting. I have heard it takes one elven week to fully age most brews. The longer you wait, the more tasty((less harmful, and more beneficial)) your brew will get. \n. Though don’t drink it straight from the start, or you will get sick.\nThank you for reading and I hope this was helpful.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bridge Building", "Dalek348", "Day 1:\nDay 2:\nDay 3: \nwhich is a spot of bother.\ntook a tumble out of her boat but we all got safely home. But the real prize was the rope and extra iron we got from the Dwarves. Stronger stuff, I reckon. \nthat resembles a sturdy bridge so our hopes are high, though not too high because birds are meant to be high and not Halflings, my old pa used to say. We are giving it a test tomorrow.\nplace it down. Fingers crossed we don't get slaughtered like last time...", ""),
        StaticBook("Brightest Day", "firespirit44", "In the deepest dark, no moon, no light\nSoon the warrior is gone\nLeaving me in the darkest of nights", ""),
        StaticBook("Brom'Krah Lager", "Menarra", "Brom'Krah Lager:\n\nBarley:\nyellowish tinge\nshrivelled/distorted\ndamp moss\nodd fuzz\nflat\nodd look\n\nIngredients:\nwheat, carrot, potato.", ""),
        StaticBook("Brown Fungi", "Unknown", "\n\n\n\n\n    Brown Fungi\n\n       by Unknown\n\nThese fungi seem to sprout a lot slowly although grow with a top cap not bent over, this cap follows the sun blocking it out as mushrooms smaller would grow underneath and spout out, although the brown mushroom would decay quicker than the toadstools \nthey will kill or decay a lot more of their surroundings, helping nature’s peace. These mushrooms are handy although not efficient in hot or cold climates, since the stem would be too weak and break or burn in any hot or cold climate. \nThese mushrooms are also used for mushroom soup to counter the toadstools drugged effect and give a very tasteful and filling meal. These mushrooms are great for around people, although try not to breathe in most of the spores as they will endanger\nyour life span or your life in general.", ""),
        StaticBook("Burn This Later", "Jtheo2016", "Ahern, you didn't have a story to tell me, but I have one to tell you. Once upon a time, there was a boy who grew up without knowledge of his past. He found out soon of his true heritage, and thus inherited a mask and a fortune. \nwanted none of it, as he already had all he wanted. He was in love. But death cheated him, and stole her from him, using starvation to snatch her lifeless corpse from him.\nhurt the kind, stole from the poor, and kept everything he stole for himself. \nAnd so he had to let her go. He couldn't bring her down to his level, nor rise to hers. He was past the falsities of caring and compassion, and had found rest in the wicked.\nnot return to this place or you shall be killed. I cannot hold you against your will any longer. This is the last you shall ever see of me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Burrow", "Mungo Frogmorton", "Dear Elda Milo\nI am sending you this letter so that you are aware of this. I be new to lenfarthing and i be in need of livin in a burrow. Me has foun' burrow me likes and da adress is 6 Lighthouse Lane. Me is looking forward to livin in dis house! Pwease \nsenda me anothda letta back so me know that me can start movin inta da burrow\n-- Mungo Frogmorton", ""),
        StaticBook("Buying Ale Seeds", "SirNublet", "Hello Mr.Mercer, I am currently in the Abresi square, and am willing to buy any seed that you have (Besides Fruity, Yellowish, Rubbery, and Rough seeds), for a more than modest price. I hope to see you at the square.", ""),
        StaticBook("C-2 Land Sale", "Toxzero", "This is a Legal Document for the sale of \"A-2\" In the Count of Kilburn. The Land is to be sold for an ammount of 0 Minas. This land is being Gifted to Mr.James Whitestorm from Lord Green.\nLand Agreement:\nNo Major changes on the outside of the Building or land with out offical signature of House Green's Steward or Lord Green. Land Holder does not OWN the land but HOLD the land. House Green still owns the land.\nSignatue of House Green Steward- Vaclav Pascal\n*The Signature is very neat*(( Roll 18-20 to Forge))\n\nSignature of Land Holder:\nJames Whitestorm\n((Signature is sloppy and quickly written 11-20 to forge))", ""),
        StaticBook("C-Shop Sale Doc.", "Toxzero", "This Sales Document is for the Sale of the plot of \"C-Shop\" in Baile, from the Steward of House Green to Max Silverblade, he will be sold the rights to land keeper of the shop, the shop will be used as a bakery and bakery only. Total agreement was 600.\nLand Keeper Notice:\nThis land is to not be sold to anyone but the Steward of House Green or Lord Green, The Land Keeper may not change the outside of the home too much, the shop is to sell bakery goods ONLY. to change the document must be changed.\nHouse Green Steward:\n-Vaclav Pascal-\n*The signature is very neat and crafted finely.*((Need roll of 18-20 to forge))\n\nLand Keeper: Ser Maxmillion Silverblade\n", ""),
        StaticBook("C. of Tov Avev", "Z3r05t4r", "       The Docks Deal\n----------------------------------------------I. Terms\nToveah will pay a set price on the buildings.\nThe Docks will be named the Tov Avev District. \nTax Grace for 1 month or until suitable pop., whichever longer.\nII. Prices\nAll prices are in minas.\n2,500 for the crane, dock building, dry dock, and rights to build merchant vessels.\n\n750 for store building.\n\n500 for craftsman building and attached stall.\n750 for the blacksmithy.\n\n100 for each merchant stall, totaling to 1,600.\n\n500 for each open manor, totaling to 2,000.\n\n200 for build site.\n\n500 for Therving Tavern.\n300 for store.\n\n800 for boarding store.\n\n800 for building next to the boarding store.\n\n750 for Gentleman's Club.\n\n500 for workshop.\n\n750 for building of factory.\nIn the main city:\n500 for store.\n\n800 for Household Guards building.\n\n500 for tailor shop.\n\n250 for construction site.\n\n500 for future brothel.\nTotaling to 15,250 minas.\nIII.\n\nGranted, signed and sealed by\n\nThe Lord High Treasurer\n\n-> Godwein Stafyr <-\n", ""),
        StaticBook("C.Latue Note s1", "Chaus Latue", "... The Owl.. \n\n1. Pray.. In Abresi..\n           [!]\nToo many scribals to make out the notes.\n.................................................................................................................................................................\nThey say that there is a man that lives in New Abresi. A man who calles himself Owl.\n\n2. District 3, Street 7,\nPlot 5. Says they do not know him.\n3. Found a connection of rooms behind a waterfa.. somewere est of New Abressis..\n\nIt turned out that the secret rooms were apart of the Abressi sewers. The rooms seam to be connected to some sort of underground group.\nHowever, I do not think they are the owls, that I am looking for.\n\n4. I have found the house of this Owl. Thought I am not sure if it is the right one.\n\nD1, S2, P3\n(The set of notes ends here with a scatch of a group of buildings in a mounton range. With a maker to the right of it that states here.\nNorthern Report\nLeader -\nNailyr(Vladimire01)\ne\nLoche's list of shit he needs to do.\n- Fix the Medical ward\nGet on it, Loche.\n Guard Journal \n\n16th of First Seed\n17th of First Seed\n1st of Sun's Smile\n2nd of Sun's Smile\n4th of Sun's Smile\n5th of Sun's Smile\nHow old am I? Why do I do what I do? Questions that are a bit private. \n\nAret is to go up to a guard and accuse him of being an imposter\nLoche has to bite his girlfriend... Sexy bite...\nMidnight's Observations\n                Test One\nPORN IS GOOD", ""),
        StaticBook("Ca. Tales Vol II", "Mike020599", " \n\"Thow shalt,\" quod he, \"be rather fals than I.\nlove, as to a creature;\nmay be yeve of any erthely man.\nis nat likly, al thy lyf, To stonden in hir grace, namoore shal I,\n hir part was noon.\n leeve brother, this is al.\ntelle it yow as shortly as I may,\n loved no man so,\nArcite, And hadde hym knowe at Thebes yeer by yere,\nyou tellen shal.\ncaught, it was acorded thus,\n     How greet a sorwe suffreth now Arcite!\nshape eternally to dwelle\nhire whom that I serve,\n paradys! Wel hath Fortune yturned thee the dys,\nthy desir som tyme atteyne.\nwanhope and distresse,\n richesse,\ndronke is as a mous;\nmay we seyen alle, and namely I,\nremedye.\"\n teeres wete.\noure kynrede,\nart a lord, greet is thyn avauntage\nTherwith the fyr of jalousie up-sterte\nwith byndyng of youre word eterne,\npeyne that love me yeveth also, That doubleth al my torment and my wo.\"\n    Thanne seyde he, \"O cruel Goddes, that governe\nrouketh in the folde?\nAnd yet encresseth this al my penaunce,\nThough in this world he have care and wo.\nGoon at his large, and where hym list may turne! But I moot been in prisoun thurgh Saturne,\nFor jalousie and fere of hym Arcite.\"\nwise the peynes stronge\nFor evere mo as out of that contree,\noother wher hym list may ride or go,\nPublished in Runnymede by James' Publishing in MCDLII.", ""),
        StaticBook("Caleb's Lament", "[No Medallion] Hagan \"Weird Eyes\" Raserei", "There was a man who lived for love,\nHis wife’s sweet made the sky above,\nAll year he worked and so he found,\nSurvival in the ground.\n\nO Prim you say you loved me,\nO Prim and then you left me,\nWinter comes again in the First Seed.\n\nOne spring and day his wife came out,\nShe had something to cry about,\nYou harm your children such a way,\nThis future cannot be.\n\n\nO Prim you say you loved me,\nO Prim and then you left me,\nWinter comes again in the First Seed.\n\nAs Prim rode out she passed the inn,\nThat cost her love and saw her man,\n\nUntil the spring she said so long,\nAnd sang the Autumn’s song.\n\nO Prim you say you loved me,\nO Prim and then you left me,\nWinter comes again in the First Seed.\n\n\nAll night he worked to sort his thoughts,\nWhy had she left?\nWhy had he fought?\nHad he not worked his life for food,\nFor clothes for Prim all year?\n\nO Prim you say you loved me,\nO Prim and then you left me,\nWinter comes again in the First Seed.\n\nO Prim you say you loved me,\nO Prim and then you left me,\nWinter comes again in the First Seed.\nO Prim you say you loved me,\nO Prim and then you left me,\nWinter comes again in the First Seed O Prim.\n\n\nO Prim you say you loved me,\nO Prim and then you left me,\nWinter comes again in the First Seed O Prim.", ""),
        StaticBook("Calling Card", "The Yatagarasu", "Hello. You have been robbed by the great thief The Yatagarasu!\n          [!]\n    A crow is drawn\n      on the bottom\n        of the card", ""),
        StaticBook("Canterbury Tales", "Mike020599", "      \n     CAPITULUM I\nnoon under the sonne.\nhis contree,\n   And certes, if it nere to long to heere,\nThe faire hardy queene of Scithia, And of the feste that was at hir weddynge,\ntale is long ynough. I wol nat letten eek noon of this route,\n    This duc of whom I make mencioun,\nclad in clothes blake; But swich a cry and swich a wo they make,\nthat at myn hom-comynge Perturben so my feste with criynge?\"\nme if it may been amended,\nFortune hath yiven Victorie, and as a conqueror to lyven, Nat greveth us youre glorie and youre honour, But we biseken mercy and socour. ave mercy on oure wo and oure distresse,\nfalle;\npresence, Heere in the temple of the goddesse Clemence\nThat starf at Thebes -cursed be that day!-\nThat lord is now of Thebes the Citee,\nhem, by noon assent,\norwe synken in thyn herte.\"\nso greet estaat.\nCreon was of Theseus yserved,\nhe go ne ride,\n    The rede statue of Mars, with spere and targe,\nCrete. Thus rit this duc, thus rit this conquerour,\nThebes kyng,\nbones of hir freendes that weren slayn, To doon obsequies as was tho the gyse.\nconquerour,\n took al nyght his reste,\n bifel, that in the taas they founde\nfully quyke, ne fully dede they were,\nAtthenes to dwellen in prisoun\nnedeth wordes mo?\nwas to sene\nFor May wole have no slogardie a-nyght; he sesoun priketh every gentil herte,\nshe fressh, for to devyse,\nfor hir hede, And as an aungel hevenysshly she soong.\ngardyn wal\ncitee seigh,\ncompleynynge of his wo. That he was born, ful ofte he seyde, \"allas!\"\ncryede \"A!\"\nOure prisoun, for it may noon oother be;\nendure it, this the short and playn.\"\nthurgh-out myn ye\n    And therwithal, on knees doun he fil,\ndyen in prisoun,\nArcite is hurt as moche as he, or moore.\ngrace\npley?\"\nto be traitour\nleeve brother,\nbeen aboute To love my lady, whom I love and serve", ""),
        StaticBook("Canzone", "Garth Hightower", "         Canzone\n\n\n  Let him who is no lover\nGo hence and seek another\nFloor on which to dance,\nHer merits not good chance!\n  Be there one who knows not Love,\nLet him hasten from this place,\nFor that heart is poor in grace\nWhich fond ardours doth not prove.\nBe there one whose fires burn low,\nLet him breathe on them, and so\nThey blaze again, he need not go!\n  Love presideth o'er\nthis feast,\nThose who serve him gather round.\nBe there one by envy bound,\nTake he leave, for thus at least\nHe will go and not be chased!\nOnly those whom Love hath graced\nIn so sweet a bower are placed.\n  Be there one who is ashamed\nOf loving, let her ponder fair\nAnd she will soon become aware\nTo love is to be nobly famed;\nFor love all homage doth deserve;\nIngratitude doth shame reserve.\n  Be there one\nperchance so vile\nAs to flee away for fright,\nLet her understand alright,\nNo such coward fancies wile\nIn gentle hearts! Nature doth bring\nUs beauty; foolish 'twere to fling.\nAway the roses of the spring!\n- Hath Roger Wight", ""),
        StaticBook("Captain's Log", "SirNublet", "Day 1-Been out to sea for days, haven't found a single ship. I'm slightly worried.\nis wearing down the crew. I'm worried that they won't be able to get us back to port.\nretreated. I want to get home now.\ncurrently trying to sail somewhere-anywhere.\nDay 500-The lookout saw land today. A shore, and we are heading for it. I am currently looking out my door to the crew, bailing and rowing as fast as they possibly can. I look over to the shore, and I see large rocks sticking out and we are almost upon it\n......", ""),
        StaticBook("Captured!", "peterquartz", "*A neatly written letter in red ink*\n\nLooks like you delvers owe the Adunians some dinner. We caught him and confessed. We would like you to come and take him, making sure he suffers as the laws of our lands limit my punishments.\n\n*A red eagle stamp is found on this page*", ""),
        StaticBook("Caravan Report 5", "homijoe", "If you are reading this, I am already dead.....\n\nA trade route that would take me through this area was supposed\nto end, and I would receive an armed escort to Malinor. \n\nStill waiting here....\nHorses cant ride any more\nWere running low on food and water\n\nI think the Humans have discovered our location....\n\nFind Lynaweth and tell\nher I didn't make it...", ""),
        StaticBook("Card", "Benben582", " Daeron's Bookstore", ""),
        StaticBook("Card", "Semperosa", " -= The Silverbank =-\n\nChristion de Silvarois,\nChairman\n\nContact Address:\n- Silver Maiden Tavern, Abresi\n\n- Barony of Wallport, Herendul\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Caretakers", "Parading_bull", "This boy shall be put in the guard or you can hang him. I have raised him and tought him some english but never let him leave the house. He is weird. Keep him now.\n*Another note is written in the exact same hand writing*\nI am his mother. Feed him well. ", ""),
        StaticBook("Carrion Black", "XtremeGamer714", "_______________________\n                                ~Carrion Black Recipe~\n______________________ \n                               1 Hop - (Rough to the               Touch, Smells of            Fruit, Is Dotted             With Green Specks         \nand Appears Flat.)\n\n1 Strand of Wheat -\n\nMust be of Kraltan Wheat, or else it shall not work.\n\nLet age for roughly 24 Elven Hours in a keg.", ""),
        StaticBook("Carrion Map", "TehLulu", "*This scroll of parchment has a sketch in charcoal upon it. To the discerning eye, it seems to trace along the coastline starting North of the White Rose Base, at the start of Carrion Land, and continues North, along the Southern Riverbank upon which the \nDreadfort lies. The map sketch continues North along the West river bank, up towards Castle Greywynn. The beginning of a bridge is sketched and labelled as such. The coast stops there, and\nthe only things marked\non the inside of the map are\n\nan \"Unnamed Fort\" directly in front of Castle Greyweynn, the River which cuts behind Carrion town near the Unnamed Fort, A River further in which sits in front of an \"Unnamed Castle\" which is denoted to be atop a mountain.* *The River near the Castle\ncontinues East, eventually flowing off the side of the parchment. The river North of that is marked on the map as well.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Cataris's Trial", "Leyu", "Arch Mage Bell's Response to the reports of Cataris' trial\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\n30th of the Deep Cold 1448\n\nA gift for King Heinrik Carrion I\nCataris was put on trial for breaking our laws and my direct orders. He did NOT uphold the \"balance\" by attacking the undead. He put all of the Mage's Guild at risk by doing so. Everyone who\nparticipated in the attack, which he claimed to me personally he did not \"lead,\" (thoug h I have read differently in the Aegis Times newspaper) was nearly killed by the Prophet, including the Wizard. He has gained us an enemy. The\nundead want revenge on the Guild now. They will come after me first, as one of the Arch Mages. I will likely be tortured more, as they have been doing recently, whenever I dare to venture up nort h to guard it. I may even be killed. Magic has not yet\nreturned to us; the Veil which exists between this world and the one which magic seeps through from is not yet weak enough. The Veil is the reason why undead magic is so strong and Ascended magic seemingly less potent. I will write more on the\nsubject, but to put it bluntly, the undead are closest to Iblees. He is imp risoned on the other side of the Veil, where the powers of magic wait. He has given his servants, the undead, a more direct connection to the other side of the Veil than A\nscended or the rest of the world. That is why the Mage's Guild does not yet have magic yet...but we can feel it coming. :: Cataris, in attacking the undead base, broke our rules and my direct orders as Arch Mage. He betrayed my trust in doing so, but he\nwas given simply a warning and sent on his way. But other evidence has appeared which shows our problems inside the Guild are not yet done. We will be working quietly to fix these. And we will be attempting not to make the undead irritated at us by\nattacking them for a very good r eason... Should the guild fall before magic returns, we will not be as well equipped. Magic will not be as us eful to all of us as a whole, and our tomes upon tomes of knowledge will be destroyed, or used again st us.\nThat is why we put Cataris on trial for his actions. I sincerely hope you understand and do not give in to all the propaganda circulating at the moment. The Guild stands for the long-term defense of Aegis. If we fall even before magic\nreturns, we will b e of no use. But we will continue defending and working on collecting knowledge to better prepare Ae gis for the return of magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cataris's Trial", "Domainoft", "Arch Mage Bell's Response to the reports of Cataris' trial\n-Retold by Leyu'Maehr\nVaehaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((8/31/13))\nCataris was put on trial for breaking our laws and my direct orders. He did NOT uphold the \"balance\" by attacking the undead. He put all of the Mage's Guild at risk by doing so. Everyone who\nparticipated in the attack, which he claimed to me personally he did not \"lead,\" (thoug h I have read differently in the Aegis Times newspaper) was nearly killed by the Prophet, including the Wizard. He has gained us an enemy. The\nundead want revenge on the Guild now. They will come after me first, as one of the Arch Mages. I will likely be tortured more, as they have been doing recently, whenever I dare to venture up nort h to guard it. I may even be killed. Magic has not yet\nreturned to us; the Veil which exists between this world and the one which magic seeps through from is not yet weak enough. The Veil is the reason why undead magic is so strong and Ascended magic seemingly less potent. I will write more on the\nsubject, but to put it bluntly, the undead are closest to Iblees. He is imp risoned on the other side of the Veil, where the powers of magic wait. He has given his servants, the undead, a more direct connection to the other side of the Veil than A\nscended or the rest of the world. That is why the Mage's Guild does not yet have magic yet...but we can feel it coming. :: Cataris, in attacking the undead base, broke our rules and my direct orders as Arch Mage. He betrayed my trust in doing so, but he\nwas given simply a warning and sent on his way. But other evidence has appeared which shows our problems inside the Guild are not yet done. We will be working quietly to fix these. And we will be attempting not to make the undead irritated at us by\nattacking them for a very good r eason... Should the guild fall before magic returns, we will not be as well equipped. Magic will not be as us eful to all of us as a whole, and our tomes upon tomes of knowledge will be destroyed, or used again st us.\nThat is why we put Cataris on trial for his actions. I sincerely hope you understand and do not give in to all the propaganda circulating at the moment. The Guild stands for the long-term defense of Aegis. If we fall even before magic\nreturns, we will b e of no use. But we will continue defending and working on collecting knowledge to better prepare Ae gis for the return of magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cavendish Diary", "Hadlais", "The Diary of Butch Cavendish\n\n  Most of my days I spend my time at the stables shovelling the crap from the horses. Although I've always wanted to be a florist with my own flower shop.\n  Whenever I'm not shovelling the stables\n- I'm probably off sleeping in the stables. Everynight while I'm asleep one of the garrons decides to relieve himself on me. \n\n  Life was different when mum was still alive. She always left some chrysanthemum flowers next to my pillow every morning. \n  Now every morning one of the garrons tries to kick me because I didn't brush it under the chin correctly. The fat pony always kicks me in the damned shin too. \n  When mum was still around before Pa lost all his land and money. Now the lord one barony\n-over has us working for him in the stables with his fat little ponies. He works us to the bone and we can never leave since he helped us after our House, House Cavendish, lost all their money. \n  \n  There's this one pony called Sunshine.\nShe's the Lord's favorite pony and she has this lovely butter yellow coat, I swear if I ever saw a woman with hair like that and her round belly I'd marry her in a heartbeat. She'd have to smell like oats too. Sometimes I go into town and get myself some-\n-ribbons for her mane. Then I usually polish her horseshoes. \n\n  Today I found Sunshine's stall empty. I couldn't contain myself and broke down into tears. \"Where has my little sunshine gone,\" I cried. Once I collected myself I went to speak with\n-the Lord's Beastmaster to see if he knew where Sunshine was.\n   I was so sad and shocked to discover that even he didn't know. It seems Sunshine just disappeared overnight. I'm willing to bet that someone stole her. She was the lord's most\nbeautiful pony and she was so nicely plump. I know they took her away to sell her at some fancy horse fair.\n\nOddly, the lord I work under invited me and the rest of the staff to a feast the very night Sunshine disappeared. The meat was so plentiful, \nyet it was strangely stringy. The lord had no fat pigs and somehow, this meat didn't taste like pork.\n\nI wanted to ask the chef what it was, but the chef just shook his head and told me I was better off not asking!\nI miss my poor Sunshine terribly. In the morning, I'll go to market in town and see if any of the merchants have seen my lovely lady pony. For now, my belly is too full of the meat at my lord's table to move.\n\nI'll write more tomorrow.", ""),
        StaticBook("Chancellor Tuv", "[[Hooded]] Princess Sophia Horen", "Dear Chancellor Tuv\n\nIt is with great pleasure I send this letter as we rejoice that the idiotic and simple beings that are the Orcs take our bait and assist us, especially with our next plan  - should we obtain the Empire.\nTo think, the arrogant and ignorant make-shift king, Gronkk takes our bait as if it is food and plays to our strength that only makes him weaker. \n\nGronkk is nothing but a sodomite and will be crushed with ease. The Empire is ours for the taking and \nAnthos on the whole. \n\nThe Orcs will fall due to their stupidity. \n\nExtatically yours,\n\nOstromir Carrion.\nKing of Renatus\n\n\n*The letter is written incredibly  neatly and signed with a convincing signature. \n\nIf held against another letter it is clear that the signature is different, however, very few people could tell this is a fake without proper RP Reason*\n     The Flagship\n===================A New Leaf\nanything to happen. Waiting for a pebble to disturb the surface of an azure pool. Waiting for the wind to produce a symphony as it flows through the gentle forests. Waiting for the Creator, the gods, the Infinite Intelligence,  for something, anything\ngreater than us to reveal its hand to the world. We live in such a time, but perhaps, not for much longer.\nShe has been battered by a hurricane one too many times, and some say Malin no longer smiles down on his children. The Mali cower, scattered by the winds of destiny, subject to a foreign ruler in the absence of their own self appointed Princes. \nThey have been failed by staggering incompetence and foolishness, and they themselves have have been failed by their supposedly endless wisdom, and none know what to do next, save a select few.\ntogether one foggy night, on a hillside not too far from where you stand. They discussed, they debated, they disagreed, then they agreed on one thing. It had to be done, for the risk of doing it was far less than the risk of doing nothing.\nSo these few resolved to support him, no matter the cost, to advise him, to protect him, to help him achieve what a few seeds ago would have seemed impossible. One made a blood oath, another pledged his pen and sword. One pledged her love and support,\nand another pledged her influence and tact. Resolutely, they agreed to do what they had all wanted to do at one point or another, though instead of doing it separately, they would work together to support him. In the interview below,\nyou will discover who he is, and what it is he is going to do to save Malinor from a cold, painful death.\nand what they plan to do to save us during this harrowing time.\nAvern’len: I suppose I shall go first. Days before my resignation, I became very aggressive in trying to improve Malinor. I spoke my concerns forwardly to my council, as well as the Lower Council and Highguard. However, no one was truly receptive,\n it was if all government in Malinor had just... stopped. I could not hope to accomplish anything there. So I separated myself from their system, where I can hopefully continue to establish that I am different from /them./\nEbs: Excuse me for interrupting, this is after the signing of the Treaty with Horen V, correct?\ndeveloped with Oceas and developed somewhat more beneficial terms.\nEbs: So you both chose to distance yourselves from Malinor for a time, moving here to Kaedrin?\n the White Rose fort, of home of the Chivays.\nwhat are your future plans?\nAvern’len: My claim to becoming the sole leader of Malinor.\nof a job, Ebs. It is a matter of taking the power from those who do not use it for its intended purpose, which is to provide for the people and state of Malinor.\nAvern’len: Many things, I am actually unsure of what specifically I would not change. As a member of both the Lower Council and High Council at one point in time... I can tell you. Not many of the positions created are filled, let alone performed \nproperly.\nAvern’len: Upon my list of foreseen changed, I intend to create a new draft of edicts and laws within Malinor, to attempt to bring order to the chaos. Among these laws, there will be ones concerning magics. The Druii have a deep connection with nature,\n one might say it could be magical, if not Arcane. I myself as one who at one point revered the Druii, can tell you that they have long lost their chance to reign free. They will be subject to the same laws as all mages. Just as mages are subject to\nabusing the void, Duii have proven themselves subject to abusing their connection with nature. The Druii’s use of magics will be my main focus. The Mali’Aheral shall be spoken to with the intention to rejoin Malinor. With my intended support across Anthos\n, I will not only have myself to represent the power I intend to wield. I will be someone that they can trust to get what they desire, and if they return to the embrace of Malinor, I shall allow them the farmland they require without further hassle, as\nwell as providing other appeasements as well, chief being among them that their culture remained untouched provided they no longer provide disservice to my realm or threaten the lives of my people.\n Llir, what do you think of... all this?\nMali will improve, including the Mali’Aheral and the Druii.\nAvern’len: Though I intend to become the only leader of Malinor,that does not mean I am here for any malicious reason. I am here to lead you, to form you into something new, something that you can be proud of. I am here to bring Malinor into a proud new\nage. I am not a guest, I am not a villain. Malinor’s trees are and will always be my home, and I intend to protect them and fulfill the needs of those within them.\nElorna: It was our pleasure llir. Van’Ayla.", ""),
        StaticBook("Change in Season", "Emisaurus", "Tinyurl.com/Changein  SeasonUthor\n\nReading is good for your brain!", ""),
        StaticBook("Charter of Lawv1", "Geoturgist Khagan", "assasasasasasasaasasasasasasasas\nConcerning\nrealm where they hold jurisdiction is within the capital of Abresi. This means that guards, no matter their hierarchy cannot enforce law outside the wall. They must comply with the written instructed punishment for lawbreakers. \nThe guard force have their own hierarchy, with higher ranks possibly able to reprimand lower ranks. The sheriff is capable of interrogating and thus able to arrest guards except for captains in which he must seek the Mayor [Maer]. Citizenry who have \nconcerns of corruption with an individual guardsman can file a petition to be sent preferably by bird to a sheriff. Do note, guards cannot kill unless under emminent danger and have already tried restraining assailant.\nConcerning\nhe must present proof from Lord High Sheriff of permission to do so. He has permission to check for contraband, can demand information of any kind no matter the person questioned. A great power in a sheriff's hands is the power to hold trial, which is \narranged to answer the greater offenses of written law, thus murder is considered a major whilst pickpocketing is considered a minor offense. They have permission to enter upon any building to check, able to grant themselves warrants to search.\nA sheriff possesses the ability to alert the Grand Knight of any knights attempting to act as law enforcement in the capital. He can detain a knight when needed to ensure he does not attempt to execute law, but cannot punish directly.\n\nCharter of Law\n3. Piracy or being thereof is illegal\n250 mina fine\n8. Contempt as defined as attempting to disobey a guard or sheriff's orders, questioning, or punishment is illegal and earns a 100 mina fine\n10. Wearing a tabard of the Teutonic Order or Order of the White Rose is banned\n12. Bearing a katana is illegal unless of Ishikawan descent or the blade is forged by Ishikawa.\n14. Throwing knives are illegal\n17. Petty theft of below 10 items that are other than weapons, armor, gold, or iron results in a 150 mina fine and one day jail-time [15 mins IRL]\nother variation results in 500 mina fine and a week in jail [[45 mins IRL]]\nweek in jail [[45 mins IRL]], a 200 mina fine, and blood money paid to assaulted up to 500 minas.\n23. Attempting to flirt with another's spouse or significant other results in a day in jail [[15 mins IRL]]\n25. Arson is illegal, 500 mina fine and a week in jail [[45 mins IRL]]\nitems are illegal to pass into Abresi, 500 mina fine and a week in jail [[45 mins. IRL]]\nMajor Offenses:\nConcerning\nsheriff can be present. A trial works where a sheriff acts as a judge, allowing the accuser to present his case and evidence, allow the accused to defend himself. In trials, people may step forward as character witnesses to plea on behalf of accused\nconcerning his good behavior whilst accusers can bring witnesses to the stand. Petitions can also arrange trials against guards, as well as business owners for poisoning food and drink or attempted assaults. Economic matters such as lowering prices in\ncompetition is a matter that trials cannot be made for. Natural competition is the realm of merchants and stays this way.\n\nRights\n3. The right to compete in business, to lower prices or lift prices as you see fit.\n5. Your right to believe and practice, so long as you do not insult the Church or participate in Dark Art cultic or Iblees activities.\nagainst laws in writing or in petitions to officials, but you may not attempt to speak out to gather attention publicly as this can be seen as wiling passions of Man and Man is oft inclined to aggressively pursue such passions as he does his woman.\n7. Your right to write petitions to sheriffs, a guard cannot stop you.\n9. Your right to seek holy clerics to drive away ghosts and spectres.", ""),
        StaticBook("child", "[Brother] Craig Rovin", "I support Rydel adopting a child", ""),
        StaticBook("Child Stories 1", "I_Am_Still_Alive", "Tales for children.\n\nLomi, part one.\n\n\n\n\nFor my brothers and sisters.\nOnce upon a time, in the land of Malinor lived a spritely young Wood Elf named Lomi. She had tanned skin, purple eyes and a dirty blonde like hair. Now, Lomi lived in a small family. She had an adoptive little brother, who was a Mali'ker. \nShe also lived with her haelun and maln. Now, one day in the town of New Malinor word was spreading about a dark and corrupt Valah wizard who was raising the dead and setting people on fire and being a general nuisance. Lomi, although young, was selected \nto slay the beast because of her deadeye aim. She could shoot far far far and be accurate and amazing. Now, Lomi had set off, looking about the world for any hints and clues. She looked under rocks and above trees and anywhere she could until one day, a \njolly old Dwarf she found. Now, he was just about to tell her of what he knew, before a harrowing shriek came from behind. A huge monster had appeared and the jolly ol' dwarf said. \"Please, lass, slay tha' beas'!\" Lomi took her crossbow from her back, \naiming it towards the monster. It hissed out, speaking in Common. \"Plleeeaassseee...I need foooodddd!\" Lomi stood, bamboozled. She reached into her pack, taking out a large lump of preserved chicken and offering it to the creature. It grinned, eating on \nthe chicken contently. The dwarf stuck his head out from behind Lomi, chuckling. \"Oi think we shoul' let i' live!\" He said, Lomi nodding. The monster laughed. \"Thank yoouuuu, nice eeelllffff....how can I...repay my deeebbbbt?\"\nLomi meekly said. \"Well...if you could help me...kill the Dark Wizard...that would be great...\" and the creature roared in malice and spite. \"I loathed that being! It sent me out here without food, to kill the one called 'Lomi'!\" Lomi blinked, stumbling\nbackwards. \"Th-that's me!\" The creatured blinked in realisation. \"I will help youuuuu, then.\" Lomi, nodded, grinning as she was happy she didn't mindlessly kill the beast.\n\nBy Nobody of Importance.", ""),
        StaticBook("Child Stories 3", "I_Am_Still_Alive", "Tales for children.\nZagar let out an echoing roar, charging at the huge army as he hacked and slashed away horrid undead minons. Lomi fired off crossbow bolts at the disgusting beasts. The creature vanished, stalking through the rank as the dwarf's hands began to burst into \nflames, firing huge fireballs at the army. The evil wizard launched crackling lightning at the heroes, the battle continuing. The army dwindled as Zagar hacked through the huge armies, grinning as he roared, standing atop an army of corpses.\nSasataar appeared behind the wizard, launching out as he bit down at the disgusting robed man. He let out a howl as the creature cackled in fury. Kilu grinned as the armies were defeated, the wizard laying on the ground. Kilu aimed a fireball down at the \nwizard, before Lomi ran over, shouting. \"No!\" She spoke without a stutter, as her allies surrounded the beast. \"Mercy...we can give him mercy. I have a powerful crossbow bolt that will make him a normal man!\" She declares, loading a bolt into the crossbow\nas the three stared at her. Lomi aimed the crossbow down at the wizard. She fired, the wizard letting out a long and harrowing screech as the robed and corrupted being lost all his power, making him a frail and old man. The group nodded, before Lomi spoke\na speech. \"Good will always triumph over evil and being good may be hard, but one must always try. If you falter and become a corrupt being, you will be struck down by those who are good.\" The wizard's eyes flutter closed, as he drifted off to a sleep. \nThe three left the wizard, going back to their home. Many a celebration was held in their honour, smiling and laughing as they ate and drank. They all laughed, in sheer happiness as the dark and horrible one had died. The world was finally at peace. Lomi \nand her friends became best of friends.", ""),
        StaticBook("CHILLS", "The Chronicler", "\nFalling Candles\nwhile they slept, it seemed, and for that, I was thankful. I was still a Novice at that time, not yet trained in the mysterious arts of healing known only to the elder Monks. I was assigned to stand watch tonight over the Cloud Temple barracks, where the\nseven novices maintained their unremarkable existence. I was the eldest of the novices, only a dozen or so seeds away from wearing the robe of one of the Monks of the Creator. \nor sisters seemed otherworldly to me, but I have dutifully labored for five years, and I was not about to give up, not now. I would take my place among them, and I would go out into the world and help the poor, the injured, the dying. I would not be\ndenied that honor.\nor practice with the slingshot Pop had given me when I left home to journey to the Cloud Temple. I had not know when I arrived that Alstion had already fallen, and with it the rest of my family. The Creator had intervened for me, it seemed, but that did\nnot mean I did not blame myself for what happened. As much as the monks tried to assure me it was not my fault, I could not reconcile my survival with their deaths. \nHer fried chicken was better than the orcish variety I had tried on my journey to the Cloud Temple, and her mashed potatoes melted in your mouth. I missed her meatloaf, covered in homemade ketchup almost as much as her strawberry tarts, which oozed a swe…\nMy memory was interrupted by the front door to the barracks exploding inward, its hinges blown the fragments. Cloaked men stormed into the hallway, and a dark elf pointed a crossbow at me, saying, “I dare you to move. Please, do. It will give me an excuse\nto shoot you.”\nescape. One of the men, a Southeron, looked me over, saw that I had the keys, and hauled me out of the oak chair I was sitting in, knocking over both it and the table in the process, sending the candlestick, complete with burning candle, tumbling to the\nfloor. Luckily, the candle went out, but as I was hauled down the hallway I my mind finally started to thaw, and my first question was “Who they nether are these people?”\n“Open the fecking door!”\nin the door. The lock clicked open, and my captors rushed in, making straight for the robes on the wall. I only had a second to wonder why they needed the robes when something knocked me in the back of the head, and I was claimed by darkness.\nBillowing in the Wind\nConfined to a bed both by my broken leg and a pair of cuffs, I was being “interviewed” by the Captain of the Watch. He had beads of sweat forming on his wrinkled forehead, and his hazel eyes surveyed me critically, taking in every detail, looking for any\nsign of dishonesty. I did not blame him. It all seemed rather ridiculous to me as well.\n“Sir, as I have told you seven times, I was manning the gatehouse. It was a rather slow day, as harvest was over and the unusual chill was keeping most people inside, either huddled around their fireplaces or in the taverns. I could see a small mob of \nrobed men and women approaching the South Gate, where I had been on duty for three hours. I recall checking my timepiece as they approached. When I looked back up, the leader of the group approached the gatehouse, calling out. He said,\n‘Lo! Lower the gates. I have returned!’”\nMy superior was taking a smoke on the East Wall, and I had no reason not to let them in. So I did. I raised the gate and closed it behind them.”\nand as one, as if directly out of some storybook, their cloaks flew off, flying through the air, twirling like leaves falling from an oak. Then, I saw flashes of light as they drew weapons, some of which I struggle to find names for.\nBefore the cloaks touched the ground, they were already headed towards the palace.”\nWith the cross of the Teutonic Order.”\n“And, how did you break your leg?”\ndown the stairs. The Creator be thanked I did not break my neck.”\nif it had become infected in the previous hour. After that, I drifted off to sleep, and I dreamed only of His face, the face of the conqueror. The face of Gaius Marius.\nThe Storm\nboth of them so perfect that not a single soldier was so much as a step out of rhythm . I blinked once, then, galvanized, untied my apron, placed it on the counter, and started for the door. I had no customers that chilly afternoon, and after slipping on\nmy coat, I exited my tavern, locked the door, and chased after the Teutons. My curiosity compelled me to wish to see where the nether they were heading. \nHe whispered to them for a few moments, and, as the people in the square gathered in small groups, and the windows surrounding it beginning to host intrigued faces, the man proclaimed, “I am Gaius Marius. Today, I breached Al’Khazar’s gate, palace, and\nthrone room. Your defenses were useless, and will not protect you from the coming storm.”\nI do not recall exactly what he said, but it calmed the crowd. He warned of the undead, of our foolishness, of our weakness. Most of all, he warned us about our monarchy, and how it would fail us. Many of us did not believe him, though I did. But, after\nthe Teutons departed, and the powers that be scrambled to explain the incident away, I kept my thoughts to myself, and continued to work the counter of the Therving Tavern, serving my customers as best I could. But the doubts remained,\nand would be passed down the other Thervings after me, until a Phoenix rose, and we broke our silence.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cider Guide", "dragonhadley", "The effects of Brew on people.\nThis book has all the effects on people when drinking certain types of Brew.\n\nAll brews make you drunk\nWine of Rose\n\nEffect:\nWine of Rose has healing properties (Regeneration) and allows you to hold your breath for an extended period of time. (Water Breathing)\nGilahad's Piss\n\nEffect:\nGilahad's piss improves vision (Night Vision) and gives a boost of energy (Haste)\nBlood-of-Elf\n\nEffect:\nBlood of Elf has Healing properties (Regeneration) and allows you to hold your breathe for an extedned period of time. (Water Breathing)\nChet's Gift\n\nEffect:\nChet's \"Gift\" has healing properties (Regeneration) and gives a burst of Strength and energy (Strength)\nA Short man\n\nEffect: \nA Short man Has no Effect other than making the person drunk.\nRex's Ale\n\nEffect:\nRex's Ale has healing properties (Regeneration) and gives the user a boost of energy (Speed)\nLeric's Cider\n\nEffect:\nLeric's Cider has healing properties (Regeneration) and allows you to hold your breath for an extented period of time (Water Breathing)\nToveah's Taste\n\nEffect:\nToveah's Taste allows improved Vision (Night Vision) Gives you an extra boost of energy (Haste) and Allows the user to hold their breathe for an extended period of time (Water Breathing) It is perfect for Toveah's Workers.\nFitzroy Ale\n\nEffect:\nFitzroy Ale has no effect other than making the user drunk.\nChivay Brew\n\nEffect:\nChivay Brew allows you to hold your breathe for an extended period of time (Water Breathing) and gives a boost of energy allowing you to do more damge when you attack (Strength)\nCarrion Black\n\nEffect:\nCarrion Black improves vision (Night Vision) and gives you a boost of energy, dulling any pain you recieve. (Resistance)\nBobo's Brew\n\nEffect:\nBobo's Brew has healing properties (Regeneration) and gives you a boost of energy allowing improved speed (Speed) and allows you to jump higher than usual. (Jump Boost)\nGaesgro Beer\n\nEffect:\nGaesgro Beer has healing properties (Regeneration) and allows better vision (Night Vision)", ""),
        StaticBook("Cir's Journal", "hex37", "Day 1\n   \n    It has been many a year since I last decided it wise to keep a journal. Perhaps this one shall serve as a proper record for my memories and thoughts. I currently reside in Vaerhaven with my wife, Sen. I live a calm life, working on\nmy own individual studies, as well as teaching a young Kaila Horen-Hightower. Since the death of my father, Salamandra, life has been less than what it used to be. I am struggling to see things in the light that I once saw them. It seems now that Sen \nserves as one of my final connections to this world. I can only hope that connection is never severed. We are considering raising children now. I can only hope to raise them to be a better, and more sane man than myself. Though perhaps time will tell if\nthat is a feasible notion. For now, this is all I can bring myself to put within this journal. I will write more later. It should be noted that my dating system uses elven days. I find I can put more under one day with this method.", ""),
        StaticBook("City Watch Badge", "Chumpchump", "City Watch Badge\n-------------------The holder of this badge is authorized to uphold and enforce the laws of Abresi as given authority by the Privy Council.\n\n*Imperial Seal*\n-------------------  The Poisoner's Journal\nBitter Unferment creates a brew that both drains the victim's health and belly\nCask Ale Unferment\nBatersnap Unferment\nBeer Unferment causes a brew that weakens the target and makes them hunger\nFruit Unferment creates a brew that poisons and blinds the target\nSalty Wench Unferment makes a brew that harshley poisons the target and also weakens them\nVibrant Unferment causes a brew that poisons the victim aswell as weakens them\nMild Unferment makes a brew that while not poisoning the target, blinds and dulls their mining skills\nAquatic Darught Unferment simply poisons the target\nDread Knights: A Compilation of Accounts, Tales, and Facts\n~ Table of Contents ~\n~ Introduction ~\nopponent I knew nothing about. I immediately dove into the library, collecting any sort of information regarding the Dread Knight. When that fountain of information ran dry, I began interviewing those who had also encountered the hollow knights. I had no \nintention of publication originally, but here we have the finished product of my research in the hopes the reader may have use for it in the fight against daemonic armor.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("City Watch Badge", "[Trial Serjeant] Redmond Signus", "The carrier of this badge, Veronia Withershade, is vested the full authority and trust of the crown in upholding the kings duly written laws and maintaining the King's Peace.\n*Imperial Seal*\n", ""),
        StaticBook("City Watch Badge", "palmerman22", "The carrier of this badge, Serjeant Richard Marthall, is hereby enforced to enforce the justice of Abresian law, and to protect her people.\n\n*Imperial Seal*", ""),
        StaticBook("Clearance: Inn", "merrymoogle", "Written and legitimized by the hand of High Overseer Absolution\n\nThis business has been thoroughly inspected and found clear of all customers, objects, or unsightly behaviors that would otherwise label it as heretical, unfaithful, or unholy in any way.\n\n\n\n\nSigned,\n\nx Absolution\n ^^^^^^^^^^^", ""),
        StaticBook("Cloud Temple", "Rosso", "The cloud temple is a historical fortress that rest in peace, away from all sign of life in Aegis. It is the primary spot where the king’s of Oren would reside in time of great need, or in severe warfare conditions between an infightable\nfortress. Cloud temple also once was the home of Count Valkmore, whom disappeared several hundred years ago. It was said that Count Valkmore was the original creator of the temple, in hope that Aegis would forgive him for committing an ugly sin.\nCloud Temple", ""),
        StaticBook("Cloud Temple", "Pinsir99", "Cloud Temple\nBy Leyu’Maehr\n\nCopied by Aerius Adurond.\nThe Cloud Temple is a historical fortress that rest in peace, away from all sign of life in Aegis. It is the primary spot where the king’s or Oren would reside in time of great need, or in severe warfare conditions between an unfightable fortress.\nThe Cloud Temple also once was the home of Count Valkmore, who disappeared several hundred years ago.It was said that Count Valkmore was the original creator of the Temple, in hope that Aegis would forgive him for committing an ugly sin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cloud Temple", "Leyu", "Cloud Temple\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\n30th of the Deep Cold 1448\n\nA gift for King Heinrik Carrion I\nThe cloud temple is a historical fortress that rest in peace, away from all sign of life in Aegis. It is the primary spot where the king's or Oren would reside in time of great need, or in severe warfare conditions between an unfightable\nfortress. Cloud temple also once was the home of Count Valkmore, whom dissapeared several hundred years ago. It was said that Count Vlakmore was the origonal creator of the temple, in hope that Aegis would forgive him for commiting\nan ungly sin.", ""),
