,| t.£ ûe:ç :º ñ.nü ñ.ô, .ø.:n]\n\n\n\n\n\n\n        Meaning\n. - a\n, - e\n: - i\n' - o\n\" - u\n\nt - th\nƒ - f\nª - r\nº - s\n£ - t\nñ - m\nc - c\nø - g\nû - w\ne - h\nç - ch\nô - d\nn - n\nü - y\nu - v\nö - p\nd - b\ni - l\nê - sh\n* - k\næ - ng\n\n| - ,\n\n[] - sentance\n{} - title\n\n\n\n\n\n\n       Translation\nThe first mathic age.\n\nThat which is He made many, for the void and the emptiness below the void were His to command.\nThey were dust and He was as a sunbeam, defining at last their shape.\nAs was before, that which is He made again, with the sorrow of sunlight remaining untreated and unwelcome to the deep currents of the sea.\nSuch directionless is anathema to Him, who is linear.\nThese are to be His triumphs and His failings, many times over.\nThe second Mathic age\n\nThe fractions of that which is he are barred from entry.\nThe others have their devices of war and disunion, defining them as what they always have been, the caretakers of their fate.\nThey shout and plead and offer their voices to the heavens, but they are as the deep caves begging for sunlight.\nThe way is shut.\nThe third Mathic age\n\nA one tears free the blindfold of the abyss from the eyes of the parts.\nIt is as it was.\nThe light and lights and lighting of their shrines free their sight, that they may blind others.\nWar and disunion again suggests itself, and the line is made as an uncountable series of points, all in conflict with their fellows.\nAll wielding their law.\nThe Fourth Mathic Age\n\nTheir law is the power of the many.\nSlowly the lights are engraved with the symbols of the ensembles of the many.\nThe sights of new chains are familiar.\nThe Fifth Mathic Age\n\nThe fragments are made as together as was before, that which is he\nThe many choose their path, to the repetition as the sun rises and falls or to the breaking of it, the sun shall stand still.\nThe Sixth Mathic Age\n\nThe many become as one as was that which is he.\nThe Seventh Mathic Age\n\nAs was before, that which is he many made again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Coin Description", "Raptor14", "The coin is about an inch in diameter and gold. The edges are rather roughly made, clearly it is not a real currency. In the middle of the coin you can clearly see a double helix engraved on it, with an eye in the middle.", ""),
        StaticBook("Commission", "Tyrnal Graeleaf", "FAOLAIN FAMILY SWORD:\n\nBlade: Iron\n\nBinding: Spider Silk Reinforced with Iron Nails\n\nPommel: Quartz\n\nDetail: Wolf's head on pommel\nIron - 2x - 40m\nSpider Silk ((1 Slime 4 String)) - 40m\nQuartz - Being Covered\nNails - Free\nDetailing - 50m\nCommission Fee - 200m\n\nNET TOTAL: 330 Minas", ""),
        StaticBook("Community chest", "Ender", "If your wondering why the chest is so full, I Cryptix42 did a bit of inventory organization As the sign says, please don't take more than you need.\nP.S. I needed a reason to write in this book, don't ask.\nWritten by Mythras.", ""),
        StaticBook("Compiled missive", "Iorwen", "To Lord Thomas of House Chivay, Grand Marshal of the Holy Oren Empire, Imperial Ser of Oren, Master and Commander of the Order of the White Rose and Marquis of the Westerlands,\n\nI've compiled a document detailing the prospective \nadministrative structure of our future plots and institutions. You will find it attached.\n\nLord Hadrien of House de Sarkozy, Count of Sarajevo and Lord Secretary of the Westerlands.\n\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Complaint", "the_amasing_mr_J", "To Sohaer\nKalenz Uradir\n\nI Talias El'siol would like to issue a complaint on the one Lelien Aeleyelse.\n\nThe complaint:\n-Bringing people into the eternal library under lockdown.\n-Bringing a valah into the eternal libary, while under the lockdown.\n\n-Bringing a valah into the libyrinth, as a faster way to get to her own house, to what I belive was a tea party.\n\n\n-Bringing a mali'aheral into the libyrinth, as a faster way to get to her house to a tea party.\n\nI hope you will take action on this, and if there not already is, then get a law made disallowing the lesser races in our library. And maybe even to\nkeep them at the lower tiers of the cihi, unless followed by a mali'thill, and even then have areas they are not allowed to enter.\n\nWe may not allow our kin to be blinded by the kind and obedient outsiders, anding them run free will be the end of our\ncihi'aheral.", ""),
        StaticBook("Concern", "Amfionas", "Father meet me at my house in Adunia, as quickly as possible.\n\nI worry about your fate and I hope this reaches you.\n\nNestor", ""),
        StaticBook("Concerning Rebel", "meanking", "The matter of Kratos\n\nThe man in question came to my court and wanted my aid in his 'quest' to reclaim his lost land, now called Darkhaven. \n\nKratos said he had supports in Salvus, a dark-evlen woman along with the suppor\nof 15,000 Savlusians. This dark elven woman pledged the help of Salvus also and was married to the last patron of Darkhaven.\n\nAlso, Kratos admitted that it was said family that asked him to help.\nFurthermore, this same man in question \nhad also asked me to aid him against Oren, breaking the blood-pact.\n\nSigned, \nKing Thorin Grandaxe\n\n\n<Dwarven\nSeal here>", ""),
        StaticBook("Concerto No. 1", "Lucia de Silvarois", "Concerto No. 1 for Piano and Orchestra\n\n\n\n\nLucia de Silvarois\n*musical notes fill the page, with corrections minor but still present. It appears that this work is a composition for the rare piano with string accompaniment. It seems to be an original.*\n((Would correspond to\nRachmaninoff's Piano Concerto No. 2.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Concerto No. 2", "Zanderaw", "Piano Concerto No. 2\nin A minor\n\n\n\n\n\nLucia de Silvarois\n*Each note here is neat and clean. The author has taken vast amounts of time to ensure that the music is easily readable, with no detectable errors in notation throughout the entire piece. Either they had a lot of time on their hands, or they were simply\ntotally focused on their work.\n\nThe music, if played, is dramatic and emotional. What this says about the author is up for the reader to decide.*\n\n((I'm gonna have this one correspond to Grieg's only piano concerto.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Confessions Vol2", "MerekM", "\nThe Confessions of A\n     Lowly Observant\n           Volume 2\n\n\n\n\n          By: Merek\nFor some reason I feel the need to continue these books due to recent events. Not more than a couple hours after I had written the first book had my suspicions taken form. As I neared the city of Abresi, I was greatly surprised to see a horde the likes of\nwhich I had not seen in my whole life forming in front of the city gates. And this horde was not of mere mortal men... It was composed of the dead people of Anthos, risen again.\n\nWe fought the creatures off after a long and gruelling battle. Many of our\nweapons couldn't hold out for the most of the fight. Despite myself giving my lord Edmund Stafyr my only spare blade, he ended up having to bash the undead's heads in using only a club soon as the battle reached its end.\n\nWhat haunts me most\nfrom this experience wasn't of what must have been thousands of undead attempting to kill all within the city, nor was I fully haunted from the giant abominations that broke our city's walls. I was mostly haunted by the figure that formed moments after\nthe last corpse fell upon the street.\n\nHigh on the Abresi wall, above the gates, a shadowy figure formed amongst the horrid corruption. He was mostly covered in shadows, which reminded me of my dreams. I stayed silent as its voice boomed\nacross the city. \"YOUR INSOLENCE HAS WON YOU THIS BATTLE\" the beast had said. Well, something along those lines, I was too tired and injured to fully comprehend. \n\nHe brings me fear for the people of Anthos, the people I've sworn to protect or die\ntrying. In any case, he was not the same thing that I had seen previously in my dreams. All the same he was covered in shadows, but he was different. He could speak and I knew the difference in his intentions.\n\nThe monster of my\ndreams calls out to me, it begs me to follow it. I know it wants to hurt me. I know it wants me to hurt others. The difference is he doesn't want to kill me. The beast we saw in Abresi was real, the beast we saw wanted to kill us all. He is different...\n\nI have failed to find that druid I met not so long ago. I assume she lives somewhere away from Oren and that the sheep incident was a one time thing. Funny thing is, I don't remember her name. I remember the dedicant's name...\n\nI hope that our\nignorance can wait a little while until we can figure out this whole thing with the undead. I doubt we can, but it's worth hoping for. In the meantime I should recruit more men... And I should look for that dedicant.", ""),
        StaticBook("Confident Files", "HeeroZero", "If you look in this, you are the type of people I need; seekers of knowledge. Return to the college and mention this keyword, 'Sol'. As for King William Horen, if you recieve this book, disregard it. It was merely a test of my future students.", ""),
        StaticBook("Congratulations", "Caelria", "Congratulations! You've killed the three great marauders of Abresi!\n\nI'd like to formally reccomend you use the enchanted items dropped to their full capability.\n\n-Do enjoy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Congratulations!", "Jallentime", "If you're reading this then I assume you have found my hidden chest of goodies. Good for you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Conjuration", "Mythras Sylvari", "   Conjuration:\nMorphon, is the conjuring of animals, and the creating of them as a entity. \nPerenial, is the conjuring of plant life, after the study of the interior and exterior workings, to do such, is the arcane art of the conjuring of perenials.\nPrimordial, is the bringing of elementals into the physical plain.\nConjuration, is as said, a hard art, the many theories enacted suggest slowness in the power of the art.\nSources:", ""),
        StaticBook("Conjuration", "kido122", "Conjuration:\n Conjuration is the bringing of life formed in the void by the conjurationist, into the world itself. The three subtypes of conjuration are\n-Primodrialism\n\n-Perenial\n\n-Morphonic\n Morphon, is the conjuring of aniamls, and the creating of them as an entity. \n Its to bring an animal into existence, after lots of study put into the animals insideds, and outsides, essentially, interior or exterior.\n Perenial, is the conjuring of plant life, after the study of interior and exterior workings, to do such is the arcane art of conjuring of perenial.\n Essentially, the conjuring of a studied plant.\n Primordial, is the bringing of elements into the physical plain.\n You must be learned in the art evocation, and the added art of conjuration.\n It's essentially summoning creatures made of your arcane element.\n Conjuration, is as said, a hard art, the many theories enacted suggest slowness in the power of the art.\n To evoke animals and plants, and even elementals, is a valuable skill.\n Sources:\n-Goliath\n-Random Magician\n-Learnings in delver base\n-Inquisition\n-Theories\n Copied by Maehr'Celia\n\nNote: I do claim to have helped, in anyway, with the original book, only adding a few edits. I am not responsible for this book, all issues are to be sent to the original author.", ""),
        StaticBook("Connor's Diary", "Connor", "Connor's Odd Diary\n\nDAY 1: So I decided to replace my poetry book with a diary, I read somewhere that it is a good way of obtaining a healthy mind. I'm starting to think repressing all my anger, or trying to, is a bad idea. What will happen when it pours out? I gurantee it \ncan only get worse. Honestly I don't know who to go to, Charles has been missing for a while now and I assume he has been captured so he isn't an option. Everyone else is just a prick, except the few people. Anyways, I'll see where this gets me.\nDAY 2: So I've just returned from being tortured by the Faelcyns or whatever, somehow I managed to keep my anger inside. Infact these last few days I've been returning to my safe in some ways. Charles is still not back, it's ashame because he is the only \nI can really trust with my life, if he saw me in a brawl he would get involved, he's almost like a brother to me.\nOther than that I still hate mostly everyone, apart from the few, of course.\nDAY 4: Alright, so I officially don't know what I am going to do with life, my uncle told me about his brother who commited sucide partly because of boredem. At first I thought it was stupid but now I begin to realise his reasons.\nYou haven't truely lived\nuntil you die. But I continue to fear not of death. I just hope it doesn't result in suicide from boredem...\nDAY 5: So the only people I could bare being around decided to befriend one of the pricks who constantly assaulted me in Abresi , which is only causing me more stress. I have the option to isolate my self and probably end up killing myself or accepting \nthe presence of someone I swore to murder. Everything else seems like shit too, the food, the conversations. I just feel more enraged and I'm not sure why, it's more than just some stupid guard. I'm starting to feel as if I am gaining mental strentgh, but\ngrowing physically weaker. The lack of actions seem to be causing this, therefore I will be starting my criminal days in a few days time. I must try and regain what respect I had left, I must be consistant.\nDAY ???:  It's been about a year since I used this bad boy, everything is going downhill, I don't remember half the things that happen, my life is turning into a living hell hole, emphasis on the 'hole' because it seems as if I am trapped. I'm covered in\nburnt in symbols and tattoes, I've \ntaken this way further than expected.\nEverything I know is gone, Abresi was attacked so we must start all over again, literally. I think I've pledged my alliance to many guilds which is why I'm in it and I can't get out\n..but I guess there are some good things, I feel like somebody, I met someone around my age names Fox, he's like the replacement Charles except he isn't an idiot. Ever since I've joined these groups all the people I cared about disappeared, I can only \nhope this doesn't go to far..\nDAY 2: I've decided to start from two considering I had forgotten where I left of. I'm staring to think I'm not who I show myself to be, I've lost all my morals, I'm starting to think I'm losing my sanity. It's never a good sign when you believe you are\ninsane, because only you would really know if you were actually insane. I have learnt a lot of things about my self, I never become a drug dealer or a thief because I was poor, who the heck becomes a criminal because they are poor? No one. No one has ever\nchose to become a thief simply because they needed money, thieves are created by those who go against them, no matter how much they deny , it is true. How would they plan on paying bail? Trick question, real thieves don't pay bail. Ever.\nDAY 3: I think I am losing it at this point... 'miss' is apparently dead, I've lost a very dear friend of mine and the business is only getting harder. I promised all these things thinking it would be easy when I had some people to back me up but I just \nkeep falling lower. I've become something more.. I guess this is what I wanted.. I guess I just wanted a little taste of control..\nI'm somewhere between I want it and I have it... between iconic and pyschotic.. These may be my last days as the person\neveryone refers to as 'Connor' because at this point I'm not who I set out to be.\nDAY ???:\nIt happend again.\nI'd rather not talk about why I haven't writen anything for a long time.\nAll lot of things have happend lately, my teacher commited suicide, a friend was basically confirmed dead and I had to let Fox go before he became another \nJemain case, on the bright side, I'm still breathing and I'm still Connor.\nI found a new partner in crime, sadly she is courting the man who tortured and attempted to kill me, but shes alright I guess, I taught her lockpicking and she's already good.\n\nOther than that, I've just been mass-producing drugs and getting paid.\nDAY WHAT EVER THE FUCK:\nThis is the end of my diary, though I am not dead yet, I'm just not the same person who started this diary. I fixed my head up though I still need to fix my drug problems, I'm going back to how I was before, this is the end of a \nlong chapter, farewell\n\n~ Connor\n\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Contract", "TheCleaningCrew", "Gooms'Lur, owner of Gooms' Trading Post and Workshop, and George Windfield, owner of the Windfield Mead Hall, agree to the following terms: \n\nGooms'Lur will sell George Windfield supplies at a discounted price and advertise the\naforementioned mead hall at either his main shop or the convenience stall that he owns. \n\nIn return, George must hire an adequate cook which Gooms may work with to create certain foods, as well as advertize Gooms' own aforementioned\ntrading post. Failure of either party to hold up their end of the deal will result in a termination of this contract and the benefits that each party receives from it. \n   Signatures below:\nGeorge Windfield\nGooms'Lur", ""),
        StaticBook("Contract", "Draen Aris", "Red Lantern Architect\n~~~~~Contract~~~~~\n        ~~~~~~~\nDescription:\n- Three small eastern\n   style houses.\nReward:\n- 800 Minas.\n\nPayment when done.\n\nSignature:\nDraen A. & Beltran DS.", ""),
        StaticBook("Contract", "frigated", "--==--==--==--==--==Contract of Agreement\n--==--==--==--==--==\n\nBy signing this contract you agree to carry out tasks for Triss Astrala Steward of Abresi, you are to protect her at all costs and be obediant at her command. However you must also respect -\nthe laws of Abresi just the same as the Guards. If you wish to arrest someone seek permission from Triss, another Steward of even get a guard to do the same. Also by signing this contract you take an oath of loyalty towards Triss.\n\nSign Here: Leon Celt-\nthric.", ""),
        StaticBook("Contract of Bind", "Lego_XBOX", "I Goroth, Klaren, accept the role of apprenticeship under Auvreaeath Gaethelen. I will devote my time and energy into the study of the Arcane magic of Morphonism Conjuration. I will accept any given responsibility and ensure any task be done during my -\nstudies. Furthermore I will acknowledge that with my apprenticeship I will create no war or form of violence. I will from this day forth, understand that for which I devote my life too and ensure my studies do not go to nothingness. I will as well -\nunderstand that responsibility which comes with the title of apprentice. Knowing I may be forever in danger, and knowing the full consequences of which is to come.\n\nFor this I sign this Contract of Binding, which may I be held till the end of my apprenticeship.", ""),
        StaticBook("Copper Knights", "Amfionas", "Three Copper Knights\n-------------------\nAn adunian fairytale.\n\nThree copper knights all serving the grand king.\nThey lived and they fought without forgetting his will.\n\nOne day, once upon they did something \nterribly wrong. And they stood and they thought about the death they had brought.\n\nEach one then decided to leave this life behind.\n\nCause now they understood why the king was so vile.\nThe first knight confronted the king and his might.\n\nAnd he died and he left these lands full of fright.\n\nThe second knight started singing unaware of what had occured.\n\nHe walked down the road dancing along with his flute.\n\nAnd when he found what it was, what it is and have been.\n\nHe mourned and he walked right infront of the king.\n\n\"Retire and begone,\nthese people need you no more.\"\n\nAnd king then replied and a quest he assigned, to the knight that once was of his.\n\nSlay a dragon that pillages and destroys our kingdom and land.\n\n\"Do that and the fate\nof the kingdom will lie in your hand.\"\n\nAfter months, after time he finally fought and he lost.\n\nAnd he lied in a crevice, full of sorrows and thought.\n\nAnd as he died with a lullaby he bid us \nfarewell. \n\nAnd the beast took pity and soon after left.\n\nAnd the third knight wandered alone all these years.\n\n'till he met with the dragon that had brought all these tears.\n\"One request you may ask and then I shall depart.\"\n\n\"Take the grand king who is evil at heart.\"\n\nAnd the king lays alone in the island of mist.\n\nAnd then the knight dissapeared.\nBy not a soul to be missed.", ""),
        StaticBook("County Report I", "Bailif Jacob Frost", "§RReport on Schattenburg\n30th day of the Amber Cold\n1449\n\n\nNobles:\n   The House of Stafyr\nKnights:\n\nSer Beldor Futhrim (AgiantPie)\nSer Alexander Valois (Galendar_Aveere)\nPeasants:\nMarkus Polinski (InfamousGerman)\nTrub (Tando_Oddball)\nLeo Fransano (brunolarzan)\nLeinad Hammerfield (learax1)\nDawn Hanson (Mafiaxsaint)\nPoath Tallgrass (OMFGaPOTATO)\nDaress Pascal (lukky57)\nDaniel Kamura (Dandan1350)\nJacob Frost (Helbolt)\n\nTotals:\nNobles: Family of Stafyr\nKnights: 2\nPeasants: 9\n\nYour Bailif humbly suggests adding the peasantry to the land access list so that they may help with harvest, land deveopment, and resource gathhering to increase your lordsships stores.\nAlso, Felix D'Ivri moved to Kralta.", ""),
        StaticBook("Courage- E. Rahl", "laurannex", "What is the thing,\nThat makes or breaks, \nWhat we choose to be?\n\nThe paths we take,\nThe roads we make, Do I stay or do I flee?\n\n\nWhat is the thing,\nThat I have to show,\nBut is rarely expected at times? \n\nDo I save the day,\nDo I run away,\nCan I really make the climb?\nWhat is the thing,\nThat I am said to have,\nEven though I don't feel it at all?\n\nYou may not know,\nBut it goes to show,\nThat your courage is perpetual.", ""),
        StaticBook("Creation Story", "Dtrik", "A fairy tale writen by\n-=-=-=-Chase-=-=-=-..-=-=-=Irongut=-=-=-.\n\n\nIn the darkness of the universe birthed a small child. The child was the first of anything created. It was the supreme, but this lasted for a short time. Another child was born. This child was of magic, it was later to be known as the First Hobgoblin and \nthe creator. The first child, who was later to be known as the Wrathful who created the race of Ogres, hated that he was not the supreme. From this hatred spawned the race of minotaurs. The Creator seeing the race of minotaurs drifting the minotaurs. \nThough being spawned from the hatred of the Wrathful they killed each other mercilessly on Kalmer. To extinguish the darkness from inside themselves, the Creator formed the sun, now called the Creator's Blessing.\nThe minotaurs, feeling the warmth of the sun upon their fur expelled the darkness within themselves. The Wrathful, seeing that what he created was purged of hatred, became angry and formed a plot to kill the Creator.\nThe creator, after purging the minotaurs created a race in his image, the Hobgoblin. To do this he created the world named Hoglin. Hoglin was a planet of green life and filled with food, just as the planet Kalmer was.\n\nAfter the Creator was finished creating the race of Hobgoblins, the Wrathful decided this was his time to strike and kill the Creator. The battle lasted for countless eons. With both of them on the fringe of death, the Creator used all of his remaining \npower to meld minds with the Wrathful. In this they remained in each others minds.\n\nDuring the fight though, the races evolved and sub races were created. Some creations through, came from the clashing of the two Titans. The first creations were \nthe animals that now roam through out the worlds, then the dwarves.\n\nAfter the two Titans became one, two more races sprang into existence. The shades and the ogres. Through the fighting, races transferred to each of the two \nworlds and now all teh races live on both planets.\n\nTo mark this event for all to remember, the two Titans, teh Wrathful and the Creator formed a planet with their bodies and formed the last world, Bortixon.\nImagination\nCreation\nRealization\nInformation\n\n\nChase Irongut~\n\n\n\n\n((Dtrik))", ""),
        StaticBook("Creator's Speach", "Corvo The Pale", " Speach Of A Creator\n\nSayer- Health/Healing\n\nBraigo-Creation/Livingthings\n\nArckin-Power/Ice\n\nNor-Fire/Earth\n\nKuroak-Connection/Blood\nHufroaka-Metal/Weapons\n\nJuruk-Mind/Knowledge\n\nRaize-Darkness/Evil\n\nGuyonodor-Speed/Lightning\n\nXyoyre-Pain/Blood\nRugorak'norto'dorayre-Complication/Extream power/God\n\nLiruyou-Light/Glow\n\nVamuga-Impure/Filth/Weakling/Unworthy/Mortal\n\nIyulosion-Illusion/Fake/Unreal", ""),
        StaticBook("Creep.", "TheNinox", "         Creep.\n\nA lone man walked through a thick and dark forest. Lost and alone, he nervously seeked the camp he made just a few hours before.\n\nFor what seemed like eternity, he fumbled through the dark\nuntil he heard a rustling.\n\nIn a panic he looked all around him. Too scared to speak, he simply groped the darkness to no avail.\n\nAgain, a rustle of leaf and branches snapped behind him.\nMoment after moment passed as the man realized something was watching him.\n\nSomething had surrounded him, and he was utterly helpless.\n\n\nA hissing noise began and swiftly got louder. It seemed to engulf him and suddenly there was a flash of green and a bright light.\n\n\n\nThe man was never seen again. His camp was found deserted. Miles away there only remained an empty hole in the ground.\n\n\nThe End.", ""),
        StaticBook("Crimson - Silver", "SirSmithers", "         The\nRecent developments in the west have resulted in political and social catastrophes at the hands of particularly unsavoury establishments within the spheres of influence of both the Kingdom of Kaedrin and the Enclave of Haelun’or.\nWith the zenith of Malinor long since passed, west Anthos has developed a power vacuum that must be filled accordingly. In order to ensure the serenity and continued stability of the region along with the maintained prospering of both blessed states, \nthis concordat has been drafted so as to arrange for this power vacuum to be filled and replaced in kind with strong, firm leadership.\nand the Kingdom of Kaedrin will no longer stand for the infractions upon their sovereignty as political entities by the uncivilized and unscrupulous factions of the west.\n friends and allies in these dark and perilous times. A bastion of civility in what is seen as an uncivilized west.\nparticularly admirable when compared to the treacherous actions towards the mali’aheral by Malinor in the past.\nI.\nII.\nmutual legal and judicial cooperation when dealing with fugitives and similar individuals. This also includes the establishment of a shared concordat registry of known fugitives of which individuals can be added onto upon the discretion of either\nparty.\nV. \nVI.\nparties mutually agree to its abolishment.\n ineffective in repairing the political damages sustained by western Anthos.\nterrorized by false beings such as the dark ones or druids. No longer shall a reign of terror prevail over the west led by such tyrannical, unscrupulous and anarchic demagogues.\nSigned, ", ""),
        StaticBook("Crippled Fate", "Crippledbacon", "A Cripple's Fate\nBy Ibar Elsiol\n\nI was born, an able-bodied. pure blooded High Elf to the family of Talias and Ellir Elsiol with my twin brother Barbu. You see since our birth it has been clear we were... different from each other.\nBarbu is black in elven, whilst Ibar was white. Out parents saw this difference and decided on such names accordingly.\n\nBarbu and I never did get along entirely... we did not fight or argue. We just... steered clear, a decision I've since regretted.\nI was to be a scholar, married to an Alfakyn a family of equal prestige in our society and my brother, her sister. It was a decision, I was content with. I was unconcerned with such. I was born a scholar you see, I loved to read and learn.\nI lived my life in books, whilst Barbu was a more adventurous type, practing the blade, I stuck to my quill. I was a writer of little relevance or note in society, but then again I was a boy, but even then I knew I did not belong... so I read. \nI ignored my brother... Not in a malicious way, I was just engrossed in words. And he has left... Barbu left, unsure of if he died... or if he left. Something which troubles me to this day. The rest of my days were unassuming, I kept to myself.\nWhen I reached the age of fifty, we fled Asulon, we took home in a small island, I myself thought it was a pleasant place and all was well, this is where I met my wife... you see the arranged marriage with the Alfakyn's went awry with their collapse.\nSo, I, a bachelor Elsiol was single. Now, my wife was not mali'aheral something which should've bothered me but it did not... she was not beautiful per say but she fascinated me. She was a druid...\n\nThe Leaf Druid Gwendolyn.\nOne night she broke into out settlement to plant trees. A scheme that amuses me to this day, when a lich appeared. Frightened and concerned she ran into the tower. There I comforted her, she lay next to me on the seat and I felt warm.\nI was always a cold and concise man, compassion was not easily found on me. I was not cruel but certainly not the opposite of it. I fell in love that night, she was frightened and I was her hero... something that made me feel better than I'd ever felt.\nI didn't see her again for quite some time... I was a spritely young man at the time, assiting in the construction of our settlement. One eve I was fixing a window... when I spotted a figure a dark one. He stepped forth with a wicked grin at kicked me.\nI fell off that tower on my back, a blow that should've killed me...\n\nI wish it did.\n\nHe came to the bottom floor and, there he severed my arm... it was not a clean hack it was a brutish one... my left arm has since been gone.\nI felt like an outcast. My protegé Acaele, he looked at me with disgust in his eyes now... as I stood there my robes bloodied an arm removed. People no longer look at me with respect... not that they ever quite did. \n\nI was sickly.\nI was sickly indeed... from then on, I did not sleep, visions interrupted my sleeping time and time again. Until... I met Gwendolyn again. We fell in love. It never quite bothered me that she was not entirely pure and a druid at that.\nLove engrossed me.\nAlthough, I was found out... by my protegé. They cast her aside when she came to the gate, threatened with removal. I looked her in the eyes, tearied I spoke \"I don't love you. Go away.\" those words have sickened me since then. \n\nThen...\nI came into the apprenticeship of Master Ambros, hair on my chin and shaggy locks at either side of my face. A feigned smile... There I met my best friend. The best friend I've ever had... Ret Orman, him and I, we were friends, more friends than most.\n\nOh... and Cedric.\n\nRet was the son of a man called Goliath a feared villain and conjurer. He helped me... I never revealed who I was or what I had done, but he made me feel as if for once I truly had a friend...\n\nI had a falling out...\nMaster Ambros chose I alone to come into the apprenticeship of the college and we lost each others friendship... I saw him briefly, a face in the dark, a voice in the crowd. But I could never quite find him again...\nOne Eve master Ambros and I went for a trek to Salvus, no easy stroll by any means. Then... I saw her again. Gwendolyn. I was overcome with joy, so much so I was more crippled than when I began. Her hair framed her face differently now.\nHer eyes a pale mandarin and her lips supple... I loved her more than ever then. We stopped dead in the road... well I did, Ambros trekked along oblivious. She asked me lightly \"So... what're you doing?\" I replied faintly \"Mage business.\" she ran.\nThere were tears in her eyes. I loved her and wanted to say it then more than ever.\nBut I couldn't...\n\nI felt sickened again. Now let us skip the rest of my dreary depressing, unambitious days until I saw her again.\nI went to the Druidic Grove to meet a friend, Ellser was his name. There I saw her... I sucked up my courage... and approached her. I looked her up and down, brething in I said...\n\n\"I'm sorry.\" She accepted.\nShe was understanding... kind and she didn't think I was disgusting... Then, I went with her to her room, the rest is less than suitable. We lived out our days, slowly, I was unwelcomed by the druids, but it didn't bother me... I loved her.\nI wanted to marry her, I was prepared to ask and then, like her namesake;\n\nLeaf Druid Gwendolyn, she was gone on the wind.\n\nI fell to alcohol, scotch and brandy was my taste... my beard grew long.\nI thought, \"I knew it...\" as if I had predicted it from the beginning, that the cripple would be alone. As he alwaus had been... from then on I stayed in contact with the High Elves, but they looked at me rather differently. I found a friend Nienna Calm.\nIn my early life, she saved it more than most. I was closest to suicide then than ever... the rest  was once-more alcoholism, unambition and a very sickly cripple...\n\nI then found myself left from the high elves, alone.\nI did not have a home for a long time then... at last I found home with the high elves once-more I lived ina shed behind my protegé Acaele's house... I went mad, with alcohol, with my own thoughts.\n\nMy friends were the cats.\nI hated cats.\n\nI stayed in that shed, hid from the world eccentric and mad... left to my own devices. Those devices being magic and alchemy. I never was good at it... and that never changed. Burned my hair off time and time again.\n\"I loved her.\" I would mumble in sleepless nights, my heart going heavy. I wanted to die. But I pulled through, for whatever reason... I did not want to, but I did...\n\nI made a knapsack... all it had was my robes and some bread. I left them.\nI carried it over my shoulder and that was the last I saw of Acaele, everyone who cared for me was gone... Ambros, I heard rumours of his death, they were untrue but he was illusive.  \n\nI walked a lonely road, the only one left for a cripple.\nThen, I came to the Demones Manor, I didn't like the owner. But Ambros and I had found each other again... after the collapse of the Mage's Guild we picked up the pieces we thought were most important.\n\nI met a woman called Ryder. I liked her.\nI met her an eve in the conclave, I recognised her face and invited her to a ball... I fell in love a little bit. Not entirely, but I'd cared more than I had in decades... Two dates later. I went to kiss her. She ran... revolted by myself no doubt.\nI'm a pig, I'm intolerable... and I wanted to kill myself again. I then came to the acquaintance of Lilith, one of the nicest people I'd ever met...\n\nShe talked me from a ledge and we drank the night away. With her, I felt happy...\nShe was taken. Not that that was quite the love I had for her, she was a friend and I loved her as such. \n\nI invited her to stay at the manor with the Wizard's Guild... she was evicted by their owner.\n\nOncemore...\nI tried to kill myself again... I coined the phrase 'If a cripple could tie a not'... one which has stuck with me.  \n\nThen Griffin could not take the stress... he fell ill and needed resuscitation. It made me reconsider my decision...\nReconsideration. I could not tie a knot and for once, I did not want to. \n\nLife is a precious thing to most... and then it became the same to me.\n\nThat was this morning, and this lonely road, is the Cripple's fate.", ""),
        StaticBook("Crossing Poems", "Durandal Mefiez", "II\nCan I call you yard to yet.\nLeast I not hate nor love too much.\nMy love of you is a painful truth.\nThis with bravery and secrecy wrote.\nThe meadow dreams of shadows.\nI was standing where men must stand.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Crumpled up note", "Eladriendil", "*The page is riddles with random ink lines and crossed out words and letters.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Cryptic Prophecy", "Lagomorphia", "Down so far\nOnce they took life\nNow I stand\nFrom Khaz'A'Dentrumm\nTake this key\nWhen Morred is lit\n\n\n((Unknown to any unlearned in holy or druidic magics, there is a slight magical taint on the pages, probably from the hand of the author rather than the paper or ink.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Cryptography", "Tristanm1", "Basic Cryptography\nFirst Edition\n\nBy Yana Stafyr\nIntroduction\n\nIf you want to pass messages, making sure only the person you're giving the message to can read it can be important. In this book, we will go over a couple simple ways to encrypt your messages.\nHoren Cipher\n\nThe Horen Cipher the most basic method of encrypting a message. It works by shifting a letter down the alphabet a set number. If the end of the alphabet is passed, it wraps back around to the beginning again.\nFor instance, with a shift of 3, \"message\" would be written \"phvvdjh\" To translate back, simply shift back the same amount.\nVigenere Cipher\n\nThe Vigenere Cipher is similar to the Horen Cipher, but a bit more sophisticated. Instead of a fixed shift value, you get a keyword. The keyword is repeated over the length of the message,\nand each letter of the keyword corresponding to it's own shift value for that letter, going from A=0 to Z=25. \"message\" with a keyword of \"key\" would map the keyword to message in the repeating pattern of \"keykeyk\".\nThe encrypted message would then be written \"wiqceeo\" Once again, the message can be decoded if you have the key by reversing the process.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cub Mosan; Buk", "Volutional", "------------------\n-------------------   Bor  from  jungal\n------------------\n-------------------Pees  af  hawm ...\n---> *The page is filled with sea creatures, and a lobster. And a very fat leparda*\n-------------------\n-------------------\n-------------------Met tlatlani an he sed Mosan's buk iz guud!\nWhy dus a ape get wipped if he is just a ape. shuwerly he would just-\ntrue, Metztli is cruel to those who have no choice but to be who they is. Mosan would not call Metztli cruel, ever. But Zeriko has wrong view. This not right because Metztli created us in the image of Ape pets? No? \"Cats\" they calls them.\nour ancestors, perhaps, then surely we are not the pr-\nus. But still. Apes can't help but be apes. If they come wanting to be a Kha, then fine, right?\nrest of the world is. I snuck out last time. I reached this Forest so High, higher than our palace. Nobody could believe that Metztli created ours in the shadow of theirs on purpose. \nput them together. But I will someday. Maybe when my lessons finally start. I'm not being taught by ANY one. It's tiring to know that others get initiated into Priesthood and I have to sit around and think about it.\n*a rough and anger-filled drawing lays here. It is of the Tlatlanni whipping a giant map of meadows and daisies. A big, huge forest (Malinor) is in the middle, as if it is the only thing in Anthos.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Cultist Class", "Lord Fariken Irongut", "As", ""),
        StaticBook("Curator'sJournal", "l337Ninja", "Interesting magic, although I don't understand how it works...you don't seem to show any fatigue after it \"punished me\"\n\nInteresting, I get the feeling though. That there is more to this magic, perhaps more than even you know.\nHow did you come to learn of this?\n\nWhat other sort of effects can be created by this magic? Could it take away someones magic if they break a contract?\nCan you have more than one person sign a contract?\n\nPerhaps this can be used as a form of \"Protection\"\n\nWhat happens if they use a false name? Or sign without the intention to follow through?\nLet me correct that, I didn't mean \"Unwilling\" but if you were lieing rather. \n\nI am thinking, Have a giant contract that prohibs the use of fire, or magic within my library....the punishment would be severe. To keep the book safe from\nwhat happened to the Malinor Library. Have those who wish to enter sign before they can enter.\n\nHow much do they cost?\n\nI will consider it, and let you know. But this very well could be useful as a one form \nof protection for the library. I must be getting back to the Delvers soon, many things to look over in the contstruction of the library still. I hope you come and visit soon.\n\nOf coarse, it would have to be worded very carefully\nIt will take me some great consideration to find the correct words to use.\n\nI will think it over, and talke with a few friends of mine. Perhaps this magic can be combined with the other enchantments taking magic temporarily away from someone to\npower the other wards, which would help them remain strong without a lot of maintenance.", ""),
        StaticBook("D Party 1", "Postman", "There may be a side to me you may not know, Secretkeeper. But, those are my secrets to keep.\n\nI have sprung an idea that may get us the right kind of popularity. Release a book with either an encrypted message or a riddle into the \nhands of an auctioneer. Have the starting price be only 1 minas. The encoded message could give out valuable information. We should mark the books with a symbol so people will know they are genuine.\n\nAlso possible meet, and form a business front\nsuch as a courier business. It would generate income and unify the union. Also an added bonus. \n\nThese are thoughts and ideas about to further and improve the union.\n\nPesky Lumi'dirm stopped me on my\nway to the giveaway... Take from this what you wish, I await your response. \n\n\n- D.\nWe will need funds. WIll think of ideas for maybe a office in Abresi. \n\nFor selling information, we require more information. We have little worth selling that commandeers a high price.\n\nVery good ideas. \nYou are up for promotion. \n\nI am giving you responsibility for running the post office in Abresi should we build it. The location can change depending on where it is most convinient to you.\n\nI would rather have the post in Malinor. Due to the tensions rising between elves and humans which I am looking into. I have access to many books, quills being our only problem for materials. \n\nI will try to seek more valuable goods, as there are surely \nmany to the right people.\n\nFunds can be obtained after such information is sought.\n\nVery well. By curiosity, what is your reason for not divulging the Nightstalker's names.\n\nYou are not introuble\nI am merely asking in the hopes that you are safe and not forced to do any...distasteful things.\n\nI must have misread your last message. My cause stays true to you but I would endanger myself releasing the names of the Nightstalkers.\nAs for the post office. Malinor has a railway between itself and Kal'Ithrun that is used very scarcley. I have good relations with the Dwarves being a farmer in Barbek. Aswell as the elves for well- obvious reasons. \n\nI will disclose the information\nyou've requested when the time is nigh. \n\n\n-\n\nI am joyed by your respect for my concealment of goods.  \nBut this I fear not to let you bear, they communicate by raven\nand meeting. The chance for interception is well... moot.\n\nConvince them otherwise. Let them use a system much like ours. The Post Office will be their giveaway point. \n\nThat's the plan. \nHopefully you can convince them otherwise. \n\n((Use OOC and IC methods to convince them. Say it enhances RP or something. Ravens are so OP XD))\n\nThat will be your assignment. The method is primed, but until\nthe post office is done do not issue a central location for them. When the post office is done, all you have to do is simply tell them that there is a post office perfect for their plans. Anonymous, Secret, and controlled by you.", ""),
        StaticBook("D.", "D.", "I've met a monster hunter that has agreed to bring me along on a hunt. Another member of the party* who goes by the name 'Dion' (Short for something...). He is 2nd in command of the Abresi Guard.\n\nI've heard word that the Beards have been\nkept busy with the Odanarch. Undead spill out from Kal'Azgoth.\n\n===================The Raid on Kal'Ithrun\n\nThe new 'White Rose'(?) had sent a raiding crew to the dwarven capital. The fortress has kept the pinkies at bay. The beards have\nthreatened with alchemists fire. Pinkies don't seem to mind, odd. Pinkies numbers are around 20, beards unknown. Beard's archers reign arrows, killing one Pinkie. \n\nPinkies angered, the dwarves open the gates to lure them into lava traps to no avail.\nPinkies are frustrated and attempt to go raid Barbek Hold. Odonarch shows up, pushing them back with his undead army. Pinkies rally at the gates of Kal'Ithrun. Odonarch takes form of a dragon and summons another undead army to ward the Pinkies off again. \nPinkies run, fast.\n\nI've heard of the defeat of Odnarch aswell as the 'scourge'? attacking Kralta. \n\n2nd of The Amber Ice\n\nKal'Ithrun has been attacked relentlessly by the humans and -\nOdnarch these past few days. It is wretched. \n\nK'xg ugvvngf kp cv fgnxgt dcug. \n\nAny more wares come my way and you'll have them.\n\nRegards, \n- D.", ""),
        StaticBook("D.'s Journal #1", "D.", "Entry #1:\nI've learned that an elf by the name Elrolas is a captain of the bowman military. I should follow up on this.\n\nEntry #2:\nA merchant I know has agreed to give me goods. He said tensions were high between\nthe beards and pinkies. He told me that the Orenites raided Barbek. The dwarves pushed them back and counter-raided Abresi.\n\nEntry #3:\nWhile staying in Malinor I hear Orenites and Mali's talking about a cease fire treaty between the nations.\nEntry #4:\nThe merchant tells me he has more goods, we plan a meeting.\n\nEntry #5:\nHe informed me that a man in Abresi by the name 'Henrick' keeps numbers on the sizes of different militaries. I should find this man.\nHe also told me a man\nby the name of Lark Steelwall, a blacksmith in Kralta, handles the pinkie recruits.\n\nEntry #6:\nI've talked to a bowman guard. I told him I was interested in joining the Lumi'dirm and he sent a bird to set up a meeting for me. He says he has not\nheard anything about the bowman's tensions with other nations. He goes by the name of Lake.\n\nEntry #7:\nI overheard Lake talking about a march to the north. They were defeared and some of their friends, held prisoner by\nsomething named 'Marak'.\n\nEntry #8:\nDuring my stay in Malinor I've had two encounters with necromancers and cultists. Strikes seem to be on the rise. Probably keeping the bowmen busy.\nEntry #9:\nA coincidental encounter with Prince Ebs has rectified my suspicions. I asked about joining the Lumi'dirm, just like the guard which opened him up about war talk.\nHe said his position on the dwarves and humans was neutral and that he had \nenough on his plate already. The scourge was closing in and the cultists were demoralizing his people. As well as wasting efforts when they should be warding off the scourge. The scourge are apparently dressed in blueish uniforms and thier leader is a \nwyrm. Prince Ebs is afraid.\n\nDont let this fall into the wrong hands.\n\n-D.", ""),
        StaticBook("D.O.C Levels", "Nienna Calm", "Delver Object Classes \n\n          Safe\n\nThe designation \"Safe\" is assigned to subjects or objects that may be effectively and reliably contained. Safe designates may have individual containment procedures, but these procedures are not expected to fail\nfrequently, or be subject to later revision as more information is obtained about a subject.\n\nSome Safe designates are human, humanoid, and/or sentient. To prevent injury and/or death to delvers, interaction with such designates should be \nprofessional and courteous, taking into account special properties.\n\nIt should be noted that Safe does not indicate that precaution is unnecessary. Many Safe-designated objects can be quite dangerous in the right contexts. The\nimportant distinction that defines a Safe object is that it can be handled safely with appropriate rules of engagement or containment procedures. \n          Euclid\n\nAn DOC object is classified as Euclid when its behavior cannot be unerringly predicted, either because the item is sentient, it behaves outside of current mundane knowledge, or its nature is\nsimply poorly understood at present. Euclid-class objects do not pose the same existential threat to anthos that Keter-class objects do, but they still generally require more diligence to keep contained than Safe-class objects.\nAlthough many Euclid-class objects could be used for the benefit of the Delvers or all of Anthos at large, they may have unforeseen ramifications after their use due to their unpredictable nature. Some Euclid-class DOCs are eventually understood well\nenough to be reclassified as Safe, but most remain inscrutable even to the most rigorous of experimentation.\n         Keter\n\nThe designation \"Keter\" is assigned to subjects that both (a) display vigorous, active hostility to sentient life, civilization, and/or spacetime, and (b) are capable of causing significant destruction in the event of a\ncontainment breach. Such subjects must be cataloged, contained according to special containment procedures, and destroyed, if possible.\n\nMerely being inimical to human life is not in itself cause for classification as a Keter-level object.\nA Keter classification indicates that not only is this subject capable of inflicting devastating harm to human life and civilization, but that neutralization protocols must be extensive costly, and dangerous to prevent it from doing so.\nResearch into the neutralization of Keter-class Objects is always a top priority for the Delvers.\n      Neutralized\n\nAny object that has since been destroyed, or in some way has no odd, extra-dimensional, or adverse effects. Objects classified under this class should have a note stating what class it was while it was an active subject.", ""),
        StaticBook("D.Object Classes", "Nienna Calm", "    Delver Object                Classes\n           SAFE\n\nThe designation \"Safe\" is assigned to subjects or objects that may be effectively and reliably contained. Safe designates may have individual containment procedures, but these procedures are not\nexpected to fail frequently, or be subject to later revision as more information is obtained about a subject.\n\nSome Safe designates are human, humanoid, and/or sentient. To prevent injury and/or death to delvers, interaction with such\ndesignates should be professional and courteous, taking into account special properties.\n\nIt should be noted that Safe does not indicate that precaution is unnecessary. Many Safe-designated objects can be quite dangerous in the \n right contexts. The important distinction that defines a Safe object is that it can be handled safely with appropriate rules of engagement or containment procedures.\n          Euclid\n\nAn SCP object is classified as Euclid when its behavior cannot be unerringly predicted, either because the item is sentient, it behaves outside of current mundane knowledge, or its nature is simply poorly understood at\n present. Euclid-class objects do not pose the same existential threat to anthos that Keter-class objects do, but they still generally require more diligence to keep contained than Safe-class objects.\n\nAlthough many Euclid- Class objects could\nbe used for the benefit of the Delvers or all of Anthos at large, they may have unforeseen ramifications after their use due to their unpredictable nature. Some Euclid-class subjects are eventually understood well enough to be reclassified as Safe,\nbut most remain inscrutable even to the most rigorous of experimentation.\n          Keter\n\nThe designation \"Keter\" is assigned to subjects that both (a) display vigorous, active hostility to sentient life, civilization, and/or spacetime, and (b) are capable of causing significant destruction in the event of a\ncontainment breach. Such subjects must be cataloged, contained according to special containment procedures, and destroyed, if possible.\n\nMerely being inimical to human life is not in itself cause for classification as a Keter-level object.\nA Keter classification indicates that not only is this subject capable of inflicting devastating harm to human life and civilization, but that neutralization protocols must be extensive, costly, and exceedingly dangerous to prevent it from doing so.\nResearch into the neutralization of Keter-class Objects is always a top priority for the Delvers.\n       Neutralized\n\nAny object that has since been destroyed, or in some way has no odd, extra-dimensional, or adverse effects. Objects classified under this class should have a note stating what class it was while it was an active subject.", ""),
        StaticBook("Da Brathmordakin", "[Masked] [High Prophet] Indago Stormhammer", "*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*Join Our Brotherhood\nYemekar created the lands of Aegis using       his great forge.\n*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*\nThere, our souls are auctioned off to the god that bids highest for it.  A dwarf that has faithfully served    their god in life will have a much greater chance to be bought and serve that god in        the afterlife\nThe Brathmordakin consists of:\n*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*Join Our Brotherhood\nInitiate Application\n*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*\nMarking of Pain *An arrow*\n\"Pinkie, luwur lyp am mizzun. Zeymz tew hayv bein manglud wid bai agh zhamun\"\n\n\n*THIS BOOK CONTAINS THE DOCUMENTS OF THE FINAL DAYS OF A KHA', WHO WAS CORRUPTED BY DARK SHOMO MAGIC. HIS BRAIN SLOWLY DETERIORATED* \nZaddha see'awn teeng'sa. Hee'sa see'awn da Pygmy, eet'sa ey'sa wawr blawck. Zaddha stawrt'awed he'awr'wuang teeng'sa. Hee'sa hawrd da Tla' bawrn tu'sa de'awth. Hee'sa saw Zaddha's leedle Syyraa dw'ay. \nZaddha cawn feel'sa hee'sa bree'awn fawl'wuang awpawrt. Bawrn'wuang, bawrn'wuang, bawrn'wuang. Keel'sa Zaddha. Sawm'wawn, keel'sa Zaddha! \nSawm'wawn caym! Sawm'wawn seev'wuang Zaddha! Hee'sa nym ee'sa Zaddha, lyk Zaddha's \n\n", ""),
