        StaticBook("Enchanted Letter", "RHcrow", "*The letter's ink glows with a faint hue of orange*\nArzota old friend! How are you?\nboosting our tourism in our small Republic.  I have opened up the \"Wizard and Biscuit\" a tavern suited more for the likes of traveling magi and scholars.  My old friend Varstivus and Mandru help me run it.  Perhaps you should stop by some time for a drink\non the house. \nWe are stumped on design ideas but would also like more perspectives on designs and layouts.", ""),
        StaticBook("EnchantingBasics", "Roxforbraynz", "Upon these pages I write information given to me by my friend, Ambros, so that I may not forget these facts and reference these as I learn.\n\n((Proof of conversation:\n\nimgur.com/a/eN1jF ))\n  Enchantment is the art of empowering an object with super- -natural abilities. To enchant the object, you must be able to touch and see it, otherwise you cannot enchant it. You must then imagine the object in your mind and then imagine the powers you\nwish to imbue upon the object. The limits of the enchant are your imagination, however you must fully understand the nature of the abilities you are bestowing upon the object as well as having enough mana to power the enchantment.\nYou must then imagine the object and the enchantment together and allow them to fuse in your mind to form one new creation. You then allow your mind to open and then your mana will flow into the object and empower it. However, the enchantment will\nonly last for as long as your mana remains within the object. After that, the enchantment is gone and then you must reapply it.\n\nThe book ends here.", ""),
        StaticBook("Enchantment List", "patu97", "List of Enchantments\nBy Daren Bonehill.\n\nHere are the Enchantments that I know. \n_______________________\n\nBane Of Arthropods I:\nA square of four emeralds.\n\nUnbreaking I:\nAn X of five emeralds\n5 emerlads in a line seems to do both unbreaking and looting?\n\nInfinity I:\n EE  EE\nE  EE  E\nE  EE  E\n EE  EE\n\nThat's all I have for you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Enchantment Note", "Sagwort", "Death! \n\nPlop.\n\nThe barges down in the river flop.\n\nFlop, plop.\n\nAbove, beneath.\nFrom the slimy branches the grey drips drop,\n\nAs they scraggle black on the thin grey sky,\n\nWhere the black cloud rack-hackles drizzle and fly\nTo the oozy waters, that lounge and flop\n\nOn the black scrag piles, where the loose cords plop,\n\nAs the raw wind whines in the thin tree-top.\nPlop, plop.\n\nAnd scudding by\n\nThe boatmen call out hoy! and hey!\n\nAll is running water and sky,\n\nAnd my head shrieks -- \"Stop,\"\nAnd my heart shrieks -- \"Die.\"\nA curse on him.\n\nUgh! yet I knew -- I knew --\n\nIf a woman is false can a friend be true?\n\nIt was only a lie from beginning to end --\nMy Devil -- My \"Friend\"\n\nI had trusted the whole of my living to!\n\nUgh; and I knew!\n\nUgh!\n\nSo what do I care,\n\nAnd my head is empty as air --\nI can do,\n\nI can dare,\n\n(Plop, plop\n\nThe barges flop\n\nDrip drop.)\n\nI can dare! I can dare!\nAnd let myself all run away with my head\n\nAnd stop.\nDrop.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDead.\nPlop, flop.\nPlop.", ""),
        StaticBook("Enclave Journal", "Bakerismaxamis", "I have noticed that the shade creatures have ceased to exist around the outpost.\n\nAlso the activity of the boardering town is quite abysmal and really offers no form of protection. If Malinor wanted they could easily take the town. They could use\nthe hills to their advantage. I wouldn't mind the town being wiped. The architecture is quite bland. \n\n-Iatrilemar", ""),
        StaticBook("Encrypted Book", "xXxDemolishxXx", "Felix d'Ivri\n\nNecromancy:\nI've been praying to Setherin alot more now that I've bought my own house. Blood is upstairs from the rituals I've been performing. My skills in Dark Magic have greatly increased. A few days ago, my \nbody began to release a dark essence of some sort, and my eyes being engorged with blood, giving them a dark red tint. This seems to occur everytime I become angry, or slightly mad. The essence makes me feel of having two souls and bodys, one being stored\nin me, like a capsul. Dark resin seems to only enchance it quite a bit... Can this power be used to raize dead? I must try.\nThe north, I've visited, with me freind, Zorak. We went on a mapping quest and for looting.\nThe Harbingers dont phase me either.\nSetherin's Harbingers are ones of fright, but not to me. Me and Zorak ran into one about a moons back. We fought a rizen Frost Troll, and won. In return the Harbinger gave us a Bloodshard. One item that can corrupt a whole city or even you.\nMy times have been good, some good wealth has came upon Zorak and I. I've sold about 7 assorted gems so far. Lets hope prosperity continues.\n\n22nd of the Suns Smile\n\n1449'\n\nFelix", ""),
        StaticBook("Enemies of Brath", "zuluman111", "\n\n\nEnemies of the Brathmordakin\nKhorvad – (koor-vad)\n\n\"Lord of Darkness\"\n\nSymbol: An Eye\nAlignment: Chaotic Evil\nPortfolio: Undead, chaos, disease, hatred, anger, temptation\n\nThe lord of the Undead, also called Iblees. He is a fallen Daemon who once sat among the Brathmordakin. Khorvad is an enemy to the Brathmordakin and to all creation. \n\n\nChaos spread across the land, the temptation of souls; unholy anger and burning, uncontrolled hatred are his agents. Disease spreads from him and the Undead serve under him.\nOndnarch – (onn-narrrh)\n\n\"Bringer of the Silent Cold\"\n\nSymbol: An Ice Crystal\nAlignment: Chaotic Evil\nPortfolio: Cold, frost, ice, consumption, possession, corrupted beings\n\nOnce a force of good when known as Wyrvun, this ancient enemy of the dwarves aligned with Khorvad and became a sinister evil, capable of possessing the living and corrupting them to his will. Consuming the souls of those who forfeit them, \nin his wake came a cold unmatched by all. He once led a vast army of these creatures but having been banished by the ancient dwarves, he has lost much of his original power\n*A small inscription can be seen here*\n\nThe spread of knowledge and awareness of the enemies of the Brathmordakin ensures that they will not rise in power.\n\n*Copied from the Clergy archives by Priest of Armakak, Gulroid Goldhand", ""),
        StaticBook("Enkavma", "Delilah", "------Enkavma------\n\n*The pages appear to be yellowed and torn, the ink faded. the book appears to be hundred of years old*\n\n47 years it took me. 47 years to build the most powerful weapon Asulon has ever seen. A weapon that burns i\nwith the intensity of the sun; able to burn through iron, even steel! It is called Enkavma!\n\nI will begin  my recount of the development of Enkavma in the early days of Asulon. It was the 3rd year since the races arrived in Asulon. I was a \nsoldier, no a warrior of the Uruk nation. I served the loyaly, as their Sakromn, strategist of war. But I was no ordinary member of the Krughai. I was a Kheshig, an elite fighter and spy. What made me most useful was my race. I was no uruk, but i was\n\nan elf. the first to become accepted as a bruhda. I proved my worth and my loyalty, I was one of them. This made me valuable, the most valuable as a spy.\n\nMogroka, Rex of the uruks gave me a mission on that 3rd year. to learn as much\nas I could about the human nations. To take their technology and knowledge and bring it to the uruk nation.\n\nIt did not take long to gain the trust of the humans. I became a member of the Oren Navy. It was in the navy that I learned \nof cannons. A weapon that launches spheres of stone and iron which could rip through walls of wood and stone, annihilating anyting in its path.\n\nIt was then that i made it my mission to understand how these weapons work. I began with a sketch of the\ncannons. I took note of the barrel, the gunpowder and the ammunition. I spent many years studying the cannon, every two years heading to the uruk sands, testing the designs. I did this for nearly 23 years and yet, i could not seem to build a cannon \nOne night, while sitting at my desk in my home, writing gunpowder formulas down, I became angry. In a sweep of my arm I knocked all of my materials off from my desk. In those materials that fell were my prototype gunpowder, a mixture\nof redstone dust and finely crushed coal as well as my inkwell. In a strike of luck the ink and gunpowder muxed together creating a red goop.\n\nI was, of course curious of this goop, such as its properties. Was it still, flammable? If so, how hot does it\nburn? I quickly went to testing and found out this goop burned extremely hot and retained its sticky propeties even when bruning. The flames burned quite long as well, approximately 2 minutes.\n\nI continued tests on the goop for the\nnext 3 years. It took me such a long time as I conducted these tests in my own home in Oren, careful to not let them find my great discovery.\n\nIn these tests I discovered that the goops floats in water, even when it is burning. Also the goop \nwas difficult to put out as it kept burning even when I threw water on it. It seemed the only was to put out the burning goop was by snuffing it out with a large amount of gravel.\n\nI decided to name the goop \"Enkavma\" meaning burning: due\nto its properties.\n\nBelow is the material ratio for Enkavma:\n\nRedstone:Coal\n1:1\n\nInk:Redstone/Coal\n2:1\nI knew that alone, the Enkavma on its own was not a weapon, it needed a delivery system.\n\nI looked back onto my notes on cannons and took inspiration from such.\n\nThe Enkavma would be mixed within clay pots.\nThe pots would need to be almost perfectly cicular, so when launched, they are not broken early.\n\nOnce the Enkavma is mixed in the pot, the pot must be sealed.\n\nTo launch the waepon, I desinged some sort of cannon. It is no\noridnary cannon though. The cannon is forged of ion rather than obsidian, as the obsidian cracks unde the pressure of the gunpowder against the interior of the barrel. \n\nWithin the barel is six pressure lines, these pressure lines are carved into the\nsides in a hexagonal shape which abruptly comes to a shallow divet 3 inches from the end of the barrel.\n\nThese pressure lines crack open the pot of Enkavma and cause the Enkavma to spray from the barrel, whilst being ignited by the still burning\ngunpowde.\n\nThe range of the Enkavma cannon, simply called Enkavma as well, is approximately 30 meters, short but deadly.\n\n*Below are sketches of the cannon, intricate, but easily understood*\nI have decided to burn the original notes on Enkavma, because I fear Oren will be too dangerous with such an instument. I leave this copy of my journal in Ager's library with Throdo therving, in hopes the secret remain with him and those he trust.\nMay Enkavma never enter the wrong hands.\n\n Sakromn Nroca'Azog\n\n    Year 62, Asulon\n\nI, Abdul Mudbee, have found this book in the Agerian Library amongst dusty books which seem to have not been looked at in a long time.\n\nI understand this book and intend on not sharing its secrets, except only with my brother, Taheem and\nhis son Tahjeet in hopes they will know the proper thing to do with such a powerful weapon. \n\nLet this book and the secrets it contains be used properly,\n\n    Abdul Mubdee\nCopied and distributed by\n Delilah Eshing Vethisil\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Ent Legend", "birdwhisperer", "        Foreword\nThe Ents are mysterious creatures that were found within the forests of Aegis, and now in Asulon. Little is known about them, but they are often found near sacred groves or ancient trees, keeping them protected and free of disruption. But the tale of the \nfirst Ent is interesting in itself.\nfrom within the confines of his roots. So, he waited for the stars to align, and produced a seed of gold, and let it fall to the foot of his gargantuan trunk to sprout.\ntree half as large as its father. However, it found that its roots were not bound in the soil, and so it walked. It roamed the forest, finding purpose under the gentle guidance of the Eldertree. The Ent soon found humans attempting to fell an ancient oak,\nwhich cried out in agony. Letting out a roar, the great being assumed its role as guardian of the forest, and tore through the men with unforgiving vengeance. And such is the story of the first Ent.", ""),
        StaticBook("EPIC BREW BOOK", "\"Willhelm Strife\"", "Ale House Brews:\nRubbery Hop: Water Breathing\nRough Hop: Haste\nBlue/Prickly Hop: Resistance\nMossy Hop: Resistance\nYellow Hop: Swiftness\nFlat Hop: Haste\nShriveled: Resistance\nFruity: Regeneration\n§i\nOdd: Nothing\nUnnatural: Bad Effects (Not Harmful)\nFuzzy: Invisibility\n\nAle House Brews:\n\nBeer Drinks:\nBubbly Beer: Flat\nBloatin' Beer: Flat W/ Sugar Canes\nFuzzy Beer: Fuzzy W/ Saplings\nSmall Beer: Shriveled\n\nCider Drinks:\n\"Excited\" Cider: Yellow And Fruity\nApple Cider: Fruity W/ Apples\nBerry Cider: Fruity & Odd\nBlackberry Cider: Fruity & Prickly\nBoysenberry Cider: Fruity & Flat\nCarrot Cider: Fruity W/ Carrots\nKiwi Cider: Fruity & Fuzzy\nMeaty Cider: Fruity & Dotted W/ Flesh\nPeach Cider: Fruity & Mossy\nPear Cider: Fruity & Rough\nSweet Cider: Fruity & Rubbery W/ Wheat\nWalnut Cider: Fruity & Shriveled\n\nWhiskey Drinks:\nWhiskey Slug: Unnatural\nRotten Whiskey: Unnatural W/ Rotten Flesh\n§LLeering Whiskey: Unnatural W/ Spider Eye\nWine Drinks:\nAging Wine: Rubbery & Shriveled & Odd\nBlack Wine: Rubbery & Prickly W/ Spider Eyes\nBlueberry Wine: Rubbery & Prickly\nCherry Wine: § Rubbery & Fruity\nGreen Grape Wine: Rubbery & Mossy & Spotted\nHoney Wine: Rubbery & Rubbery W/ Wheat\nPeppermint Wine: Rubbery & Rough W/ Apples\nPomegranate Wine: Rubbery & Yellow W/ Wheat\nRed Grape Wine: Rubbery & Mossy W/ Apples\nSmooth Wine: Rubbery & Fruity\nSour Wine: Rubbery & Odd\nStrawberry Wine: Rubbery & Prickly & Fruity\nWhite Grape Wine: Rubbery W/ Apples\n\nAle Drinks:\nWIP\n\nBattle Brew Drinks:\nWIP", ""),
        StaticBook("EPIC BREW BOOK 2", "\"Willhelm Strife\"", "V.B.'s Brew Recipes:\n\"Excited\" Cider: Yellow & Rubbery Hop With Carrots\nWhen Ready: Swiftness & Regen.\nCarrot Cider: §F§ Fuzzy § Hop With Carrots\nWhen Ready: Night Vision\nBerry Cider: Fruity Hop\n\nWhen Ready: Regen\nHoppin' Hobbits Cider: Spotted hop\nWhen Ready: Jump Boost\nWalnut Cider: Blue, Prickly Hop\nWhen Ready: Resistence\nBubbly Beer: Flat Hop\nWhen Ready: Haste\nBloatin' Beer: Flat Hop With Sugar Canes\nWhen Ready: When 3 Squiggly #'s appear\nFuzzy Beer: Flat Hop With Saplings\nWhen Ready: When 3 Squiggly #'s Appear\nSmall Beer: Shriveled Hop\nWhen Ready: Resistence\nWhiskey Slug: Unnatural Hop\nWhen Ready: When 3 Squiggly #'s Appear\nRotten Whiskey: Unnatural Hop With Rotten Flesh\nWhen Ready: When 3 Squiggly #'s Appear\nLeering Whiskey: Unnatural Hop With Spider Eye\n\nWhen Ready: When 3 Squiggly #'s Appear\nGoatsMilk: Odd Hop\nWhen Ready: when 3 Squiggly #'s Appear\n\nAll Drinks will be sold at 15 Mina except GoatsMilk which will be sold at 5 Mina. Ye are welcome to make any brew at any time from this \n§§list. Of course I will be on Skype if needed any help or questions and if allowed will pop in from time to time to check in.\n\nI am building a tavern which will be built by time I come back hopefully if all goes to plans. Also ye mates\nare welcome to buy wood from BurntToast74 if needed to make more mugs, just record what ye buy and I will pay later.\n\nContact me if someone want to order brews or asks for anything.\nSee ye later mates, I will be back soon and thanks fer all yer help and hard work...the future brings greatness to ye both if all goes to plan ;D", ""),
        StaticBook("Epic of Hilan", "firespirit44", "My gift was my curse\n\nOh my patron Xan, why hast thou forsaken us!\nI weave the tales of my bretherns\nWhat started as 10, only I remain\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Eren's Contract", "leon8555", "Amador Servant\nContract:\n===================I promise to server House Amador well until being dismissed, or until death.\n\nEren Kawazaki", ""),
        StaticBook("Esperanto", "Nordulo Sudo", "Esperanto Workbook, I:\\r\\rThe Esperanto language is a unique one, easier to learn than most languages, and related to nearly all other languages. Why, you might ask? Esperanto is the mother language of English; as Blah has an earlier version of Blah, \nand there is modern-day Dwarvish and Old Dwarvish, there must be a mother tongue of English. That is Esperanto. Due to this, many old papers are written in Esperanto.Vocabulary: The vocabulary of Esperanto is easy to understand, and formulate on \nthe fly when speaking it due to how closely related it is to English. Dictionaries, while currently a little difficult to get, are being re-manufactured.\\rGrammer: The grammar of Esperanto is somewhat of a fusion of English grammar,\nplus a couple of switches (for plurals, instead of adding an “S”, you and a “j” at the end of a sentence. Also of notable addition is verb endings. These verb endings must be memorized:\nIndicitive past, -is.\\rIndicative Present, -as.\\rIndicitave Future, -os\\rInfinite (for everything), -i.\\rYou will see how to use them.\\rArticles in Esperanto: There is one article in Esperanto,, La, which could either be ‘The’ or ‘a’,\nNow, some example sentences:\\rNecessary vocabulary: \\rLa-The, Dog-hundo, runs-kuras.\\rLa hundo kuras. = The dog runs.\\rLa hundo kuros. = The dog will run.\\rLa hundo kuris. = The dog ran.\\rLa hundoj kuras. = The dogs run.\\rLa hundoj kuros. = The dogs will run.\nLa hundoj kuris. = The dogs will have ran.\n\n\nLook for the book, “Esperanto II”, for more sentences and a smoother and less rough introduction to Esperanto for the common person. Also look for, “Esperanto Sentences, I” for entirely workbook sentences. \n-By Nordulo Sudo", ""),
        StaticBook("Esperanto I", "scharfjamie", "Esperanto Workbook, I:\\r\\rThe Esperanto language is a unique one, easier to learn than most languages, and related to nearly all other languages. Why, you might ask? Esperanto is the mother language of English; as Blah has an earlier version of Blah, \\r\nand there is modern-day Dwarvish and Old Dwarvish, there must be a mother tongue of English. That is Esperanto. Due to this, many old papers are written in Esperanto.\\rVocabulary: The vocabulary of Esperanto is easy to understand, and formulate on \\r\\r\nthe fly when speaking it due to how closely related it is to English. Dictionaries, while currently a little difficult to get, are being re-manufactured.Grammer: The grammar of Esperanto is somewhat of a fusion of English grammar, \nplus a couple of switches (for plurals, instead of adding an “S”, you and a “j” at the end of a sentence. Also of notable addition is verb endings. These verb endings must be memorized:\nIndicitive past, -is.\\rIndicative Present, -as.\\rIndicitave Future, -os\\rInfinite (for everything), -i.\\r\\r\\rYou will see how to use them.\\rArticles in Esperanto: There is one article in Esperanto, La, which could either be ‘The’ or ‘a’.\\r\nNow, some example sentences:\\rNecessary vocabulary: \\rLa-The, Dog-hundo, runs-kuras.\\rLa hundo kuras. = The dog runs.\\rLa hundo kuros. = The dog will run.\\rLa hundo kuris. = The dog ran.\\rLa hundoj kuras. = The dogs run.\\r\nLa hundoj kuris. = The dogs will have ran.\n\n\nLook for the book, “Esperanto II”, for more sentences and a smoother and less rough introduction to Esperanto for the common person. Also look for, “Esperanto Sentences, I” for entirely workbook sentences. \\r-By Nordulo Sudo\\r", ""),
        StaticBook("Ettiquette", "Katalion", "          A young\n       Female Aheral's\n   Guide to Ettiquette\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ By Ariana Desourir\nTranscribed by Amras Yavelti\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~1. Alaways be trustfull and trustworthy to all High Elves.\n\n2.Never place a light estimate on the art of reading and good expression.\n\n3. Study to keep verse in all Mali'aheral events and studies and, above all, scandals.\n\n4. Keep good posture whilst walking: Head \ntall but never rigid. Sgoulders back. No unnecesary motion around the thighs.\n\n5. Whilst walking, arms should swing yet the arc limited, remaining graceful .\n\n6. Whilst speaking in public,as a rule, dont point elsewhere.\n7. Look at the person to whom you are speaking in the eye.\n \n8. Never ask another male aheral to walk with. It should be vice versa.\n\n9. Never keep your hands behind your back. Nails must be always cleaned.\n10.  Pay utmost respect to your elders.", ""),
        StaticBook("Eva", "TaylorStriffe", "Eva,\n     If your reading this, then I've probably already left. I don't know when, or if I will be coming back. I don't know if I'll find Oslo, or wether he'll be alive or not if I do find him. If I don't return, I'm probably dead. The journey will last \na few months at the least. I'm bringing some Flays along with me, so I won't be /completely/ alone.\n\nIf I do come back with Oslo, chances are I won't be able to say these next words, without getting the crap beaten out of me.\n*a few ink marks and scribbles can be seen here, as if the writer was deciding wether or not to write them.*\n\nI care for you, Eva. A lot. Both you and Ariela. I'm doing this because I want to bring Oslo back to you: I want you to be happy.\n*the pages smell strongly of whiskey, and are signed at the bottom.*\n\n-Abner", ""),
        StaticBook("Everal", "Oracle", "The History of Everal, the First City of the Elves\nA long time ago the First Race crossed one of the Great Oceans of Aegis to arrive on a beach. This beach was bestowed with a Magikal power from a long gone time. It let all plant grow abundantely there and in the surrounding\nareas. The sand there made glass as hard as steel and that which would never break. So when the First Race, later known as Elves, planted their magikal seeds... great towering trees grew in their place. Ordinary Fyre could not scorch these\ntrees, for the magik embeded in them was still new. The Elves thrived in the new land along with the trees, spreading its seeds wherever they went, creating an Empire that Dwarfed all others previousely known. The Elves lived inside the trunks of\nthese towering trees, singing to them to help them grow. And all was peaceful. Then one day many centuries later, a Astronomical Strom swept across the land, Felling the Magikal Trees where they stood. Lightning stroke the exposed Earth, melting the\ngound and forming pools of lava. Great Fyre, fueled by the dark energys of the storm, burnt all of the remaining trees. Only a few kilometers remained. This is where the Elves sheltered during the storm. They named this area Evaral, meaning\nProtected in their lost language. They tried to spread the seeds of the Magikal trees once more, but the Earth still remembered the horrors of the storm and wouldn't let them grow. And when this area became overpopulated, the Elves started to\nreach for the sky! They trees grew until they touched the highest planes of the Atmosphere! And all was at peace one again. The Elves built walls of enchanted wood around Evaral, to protect the city from new predators and spirits that rose with the\nStorm. And then a terrible thing happened. Some of the Elves dissented from this way of life, as wonderful as it was. They became greedy and wanted more land, ores, and resources. One by one the Dissenters left Evaral, preferring the\nnew forests beyond its border. They spread out far accross the land, struggling to cope with their new homes. Eventually even they settled down and formed small villages, under no ruler. Some even evolved into other races, forgetting\nwhat they left behind. By this time only a few families remained in Evaral, and they did not know what to do. They missed the kinship of the other Elves, so they decided to leave too. But before they left each family took with them a seed from the\nfirst tree, which happened to reside in Evaral. This tree was very old and wrought with homes. And its spirit was sad too, for it missed the Elves that left. It shed its bark to help the remaining Elves in their journeys, forming impenetrable armor to\nhelp the remaining elves in their journeys. This armor now resides in the Tomb of Evaral, as the First Tree's spirit reclaimed it. And then none were left in Evaral. However over the centuries the seed still could grow, but the land never accepted them.\nUntil one day, many centuries later, it came in the hands of a young druid. The great city of Evaral's location is hidden from the world, but many believe it is still ou t there. Perhaps one day, a great hero will stumble upon it. And bring it to power\nonce again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Everal", "Domainoft", "The History of Everal, the First City of the Elves\n-Retold by Leyu'Maehr\nVaehaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((3/3/13))\nA long time ago the First Race crossed one of the Great Oceans of Aegis to arrive on a beach. This beach was bestowed with a Magikal power from a long gone time. It let all plant grow abundantely there and in the surrounding\nareas. The sand there made glass as hard as steel and that which would never break. So when the First Race, later known as Elves, planted their magikal seeds... great towering trees grew in their place. Ordinary Fyre could not scorch these\ntrees, for the magik embeded in them was still new. The Elves thrived in the new land along with the trees, spreading its seeds wherever they went, creating an Empire that Dwarfed all others previousely known. The Elves lived inside the trunks of\nthese towering trees, singing to them to help them grow. And all was peaceful. Then one day many centuries later, a Astronomical Strom swept across the land, Felling the Magikal Trees where they stood. Lightning stroke the exposed Earth, melting the\ngound and forming pools of lava. Great Fyre, fueled by the dark energys of the storm, burnt all of the remaining trees. Only a few kilometers remained. This is where the Elves sheltered during the storm. They named this area Evaral, meaning\nProtected in their lost language. They tried to spread the seeds of the Magikal trees once more, but the Earth still remembered the horrors of the storm and wouldn't let them grow. And when this area became overpopulated, the Elves started to\nreach for the sky! They trees grew until they touched the highest planes of the Atmosphere! And all was at peace one again. The Elves built walls of enchanted wood around Evaral, to protect the city from new predators and spirits that rose with the\nStorm. And then a terrible thing happened. Some of the Elves dissented from this way of life, as wonderful as it was. They became greedy and