        StaticBook("JayasJourney C1", "Sofetios", "         Jaya's\n      Chapter One\n“Sure Mom!” I answered. I put on my sword, closed the back door, and headed out. Knowing exactly where I was going as I ventured more into the woods. As I walked I couldn’t help but notice how nice everything was today.\nFrom the glistening emerald green leaves leaving a slight greenish tint on the ground, to the random scuttles and noises coming from the woods, it just seemed like it was going to be a good day. I approached the usual spot I hung out at near dusk.\nA small opening with a flat rock and a small clear pool in the middle. It wasn’t much but I always thought better here. I laid down on the rock looking up into the trees and begin to wander off in my head.\nI was about to dose off when I heard something. I sat up quickly. It wasn’t a normal sound. It sounded like the song that Linink played on the piano at the Festival, only it was on a flute. Cautiously, I got up and went in the direction of the sound.\nIt got louder and louder as I went along through the trees and bushes until I reached another larger clearing. I looked amazingly at what I saw. There was a Statue in the middle of the clearing with multiple statues around the clearing.\nThey all looked just like the one in the middle of town, except in different poses. The one in the middle had his arms outstretched in front of him.\nI went closer and saw that in it’s his hands outstretched was a Bow, Arrows, A sword, a dagger, and a scroll. Cautiously I went up closer to the statue and was about to take the scroll when suddenly the music stopped and a voice said,\n“Hey! Boy! What are you doing here” Startled I jumped back and turned to face an old man.\n“Well why didn’t you say so? Go ahead and take a look.”\n“Um… ok…” I said confused, turning to face the statue. I slowly took the scroll and opened it. Written on it was… nothing.  I frowned and looked back but the old man was gone. Only in his place was a flute.\nI scratched my head, went to it, and picked it up. As I touched it I heard the music start again but this time, it was in my head. Shocked again I dropped the flute, the scroll, and the music stopped. \nCuriously I picked up the flute and tried to play the notes I had heard. I had played the flute many times before but this time felt different somehow. As I finished playing the notes nothing seemed to happen. \nI wondered what I was expecting to happen. Once I waited about a minute I bent down and picked up the scroll. Only this time there was something written on it. Curiously I examined the scroll. \nIt had a few lines of music notes on it and the title of it was called “Song of the Rain”. The music notes where different from the ones I had just played, so I began to play these ones. \nAs I played it sounded like a stormy night at sea. When I completed it, nothing seemed to happen. After a minute I walked to the statue, wondering if it would be a good idea to take the sword. Suddenly a Voice behind me said,\n“Would you look at that! You’re a natural at the flute.”\nSeeming to ignore the question the old man looked at the weapons the statue had.\nThen looked at the face and said,” But… where they his?”\nBut he was gone. I turned back to the statue that had the weapons but they were gone. Suddenly I saw something on myself. I looked down and there was a sword on my belt, but it wasn’t my sword, it was the statues.\nI looked to the other side of my belt and there was the dagger. I slowly reached up and touched my shoulder. As I did I felt the feathers of an arrow and the string of a bow. \nI then realized it was dusk, my mom would be annoyed if I wasn’t home soon. I took off the weapons, put them back on the statues hands, and began to walk home.\nAs I walked home I noticed the air began to feel denser and the wind began to pick up a little bit. Suddenly. I felt a raindrop. I looked up and one hit me on my forehead. I started running as fast as I could toward the house. \nAs I got in the back door my mom was standing there with her arms crossed. \n“Jaya.” Said my mom in a warning voice. \n“Are you alright?” I said. She walked slowly to a kitchen chair and sat down.\nLinink was the best doctor around and also the leader of the adventurer’s guild, a guild that helps people and goes on quests. My friends Sofetios and Sofia go there.\n“Wait, why?” I said concerned. “Do you think I’m sick?”\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\nRedmond's notes on magic:\nsat down and tried, but it only ended in a small, but loud explosion. So I went and ate and then it kind of worked. I sat down, took a deep breath and started to cast the magic, but it then ended in another explosion. \nSun's Smile 17th\nenvironment. The spark I did ended with a small, but loud explosion.  The sound was horrible and almost made me deaf.  I almost died last time I did this. I was so nervous. I need to continue to work on my magic skills though. As they are horrible and \nneed more practice.  I think I will be done in about a year or so.  So far I haven't hit anybody with my electricity. So I must be doing something right. Back to electricity, I am learning the new ways of it and have been progressing.  I will try again.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("JayasJourney C2", "Sofetios", "         Jaya's\n        Journey\n\n            ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n      Chapter Two\n\n         Linink\n\nAs I woke up the next morning I couldn’t help but feel a bit afraid. Linink was one of the most important people in town and he was never really free.\nAlso, why was my Mom so worried last night? I stepped out of bed. Instead of the usual hardwood floor I was used to I was stepped on something lumpy and cold. I looked down and jumped back on my bed. \nThe weapons from last night where on the floor right next to my bed. \n\n“Jaya what’s all the racket?” Said my mom’s voice. It sounded like she was coming to my room. Quickly, I covered the weapons with my blanket.\nLike that would do anything, but it was worth a shot. My mom came in the door and said,\n\n“Jaya why is your blanket on the floor?” \n\n“Bad dream.” I Lied.\nMy mom frowned, bent over, and was about to pick up the blanket. I closed my eyes and cringed from what was about to happen. \n\n“Jaya are you ok?” Said my Mom concerned.\nOpening my eyes I saw my mom had folded the blanket and on the floor was nothing.\n\n“Uh, yea.” I said scratching my head. “I think I just must have hit my head.”\n“Well it’s a good thing your going to see Linink today.” My mom said. “Come on, breakfast is ready.”\nI ate very little breakfast this morning. The taste of it as usual was great, but the stress of what I thought was to come overcame my hunger. After breakfast my mom took me straight to The Adventurers Guild.\nAs I approached the massive building I started to get nervous. My mom opened the doors, led me past staring students, rooms that where full of weapons, and many more things. \n Finally we reached Linink’s Office. The large green door looked inviting enough but as to what was to happen behind it still worried me. \nWithout knocking a voice said, “Come in.” My mom and I entered the triangle shaped room. I saw Linink sitting a table in the middle, but beside the table on both sides where my friends Sofetios and Sofia.\nI relaxed a little. At least they would be here with me. “Jaya, would you please take a seat.” Said Linink coolly.  I took a seat, looked back at my mom, and Linink then said,  “I need to speak to Jaya and his friends alone Madam.” \nMy mom nodded and left the room quietly. Everyone was quite for a bit until I said, \n\n“What am I here for?” \n\n“I’d like to know that too.” Sofetios added.\n\n“Same here.” Said Sofia. After a moment Linink said,\n“We are here to discuss a recent series of events.”\n\n“Like what?” said Sofia. “Other then the Melonko Festival being today all that’s really happened was that Rainstorm last night. \n“Exactly my point” said Linink. “A rainstorm now? In the middle of summer? I just don’t really see that as natural. There is also the Prophecy.”\n\n“You mean that old tale everyone listens to at the festival?” Said Sofetios inquiringly. \n“Just that.” Said Linink seriously. “From what I’ve seen happening in the last two days I’m inferring that it may be coming true.” At this Sofia laughed and said,\n“Like that would happen now. I mean the rain was probably coincidence and it’s not like the weapons have been found.” At this I felt the blood drain from my face. \n“Well from what I heard from Jaya’s Mother last night, I think they may have been found.” Said Linink. Sofia and Sofetios look right at me and Sofetios said, “You didn’t really… I mean you couldn’t have…” \n“He probably didn’t” Said Sofia, Otherwise he would be wearing them right now. It’s not like he would leave them at his house or something if he found them. Right?” I looked slightly down at this comment.\n“The weapons only appear if the owner wants them to.” Said Linink. Sofetios turns to me and said. “Well Jaya? Did you actually find the weapons?” I tell them the whole story of what happened last night and this morning. \nWhen I finish, Sofia is staring at me in disbelief, Sofetios is too, and Linink looks the same as he did before. No one said anything for a while until Linink said,\n\n“Well I guess the prophecy is coming true.” \n“Should we tell everyone?” Said Sofia.\n\n“No.” said Linink. “That would only raise panic. We should just tell whoever really needs to be told then you three set off after the festival.”\n\n“Us three?” I said.\n“Yes.” Said Linink “You know both Sofia and Sofetios pretty well. Except for what each they specialize in.” I didn’t actually know what Linink taught Sofetios and Sofia in the Guild and they had never shown me.\nI gave an odd face to all three of them then Linink said, “To put it bluntly Sofetios is a magician and Sofia is a fighter, in class terms that is.” \n\n“A magician?” I repeated while looking at Sofetios. \n“Intermediate magician.” Said Sofetios. “Sorry but Linink said we couldn’t tell anyone outside the guild.” \n\n“Wait so what can you do?” I said. “Levitate stuff or something?” Sofetios looked at Linink and Linink nodded.\nAll of the sudden everything small in the room started to slowly floated upwards.  I froze and looked around.  Then the things in the air floated down to their original places.\n“You see Jaya, Everything we teach at this guild more or less has to do with Lin.”  Said Linink.\n\n“Lin?” I said curiously.\n“Yes, it is something that is in everything around us.” Said Linink. “Kind of like a fifth element so to speak. Sofetios will be teaching you about this on your travels.”\n“Wait.” I said. “There’s a whole Fifth element?”\n\n“Yes.” Said Linink simply. “Sofetios, Sofia, please get ready for your departure.”\n\n“But sir.” Said Sofetios. “We still-“\n“Come on Sofetios.” Said Sofia as he grabbed Sofetios on the shoulder and had him follow her. When they closed the door, Linink turned to me and Said. \n\n“You have a long journey ahead of you.”\n“Yes sir…” I said tentatively.\n\n“I just need to make sure you really have the weapons.” Said Linink concerned.\n\n“I would sir but I don’t know how to get them to appear.” I said.\n“Just hold your hand as you would your sword and try to will them there.” Said Linink. I did so and in a second a white sword materialized there. It felt warm in my hand. Linink seemed was taken aback a little, so I asked, \n“Sir, why me?” Linink seemed back as himself and said after a moment,\n\n“Because He chose you. At least that’s what the Prophecy sais.” Linink got up and went to his bookshelf. \nHe picked up two books and put them both on the desk. He opened one and the inside of it was hollowed out. All there was, was a semi-clear sphere about an inch long. \nHe handed it to me and said. “This is something I’ve been working on for a long time. Use it well.”  I sheathed the sword and took the sphere and said,\n\n“Sir, what is this?”\n“Don’t you recognize it?” Linink said surprised. “It is object from part of the lore they tell at the Melonko festival. Well, my version of it anyway.”\n\n“I’m sorry sir, I don’t really listen to the tales they tell.” I said a little embaraced.\n“Well then I should probably tell you.” Said Linink. “It is my version of a water sphere. This one I would say holds about 1 week worth of water for 3 people.” Unbelieving, I stared at the sphere.\n“All you need to do is heat it in something and water will come out.”\n\n“Sir?” I said. “What did you mean by ‘your version’?”\n\n“You’ll find out soon enough.” Said Linink. Suddenly there was music outside. “The festival is starting.”\n“Sir, what now?” I said.\n\n“Now, you go enjoy the festival.” Said Linink. “But before you go,” Linink picked up the other book and handed it to me. “This is a book on lore of Edrot. You may want to study it.” \n I turned to leave when Linink said, “and Jaya, two words of advice. First, with the powers you will soon possess, Make sure you use them the right way. \nSecondly, I need you to will away that sword for now. The people in town don’t need to see it.”\n\n“Is that all sir?” I said.\n\n“That’s all” Said Linink.\n\nEnd of Chapter Two\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayko's Journal", "MinimanTheFirst", "Guard Activities - Jayko Lokomo Azura II\n2/24/2014\nSemper tresspassed into the Keep after quitting, then resisted arrest, broke out of jail, and then resisted arrest again. He was charged with Disturbance of Peace and paid the fine.\n3/08/2014\n\nDaily Patrol.\n\nFound \"The Scarecrow\" on the rooftops. Told him to get off and he responed with hostility. Wounded my pride.\nFought off minions of the Crooked only to have the Devourer temporarily take over Abresi. I was one of 7 survivors. Reinforcements came consisting of Humans and Dwarves. They purged the city of the Scourge. During this, Scarecrow attacked me again.\nThis time, he threw a tomahawk at me, left me to die in fire, looted me, and shattered my pride. He sided with the Crooked. He's officially wanted for Heresy and 2 attempted murders.\n\n3/09/2014\n\nDaily Patrol around what's left of Abresi.\nNote: I'm not going to run away from the city I call home. This is a war on our home. As a wise man once said, \"Fighting a war tests your courage. Defending your home tests your heart.\" I will not leave until either I die or the being resposible is killed\n(I prefer the second option) - Jayko Lokomo Azura II\n\n*Will Help Rebuild Gatehouse*", ""),
        StaticBook("Jean's Diary, I", "[Stolistes Enforcer] Jean Havok", "Dawn of a new day,\nI did, the people I hurt... I don't why I haven't killed myself, I don't know why I carry on living. Why am I alive? All I know is I have to keep going, I've come so far... I don't want to end up like Jemain. I need to find a new purpose in life. Connor's\nLast words to me were \"Shave that beard, find a lass, and never look me in the eyes again\" He was my best friend, and he never wants to see me again. He's going to kill a king, we both knew from the start that is a suicide mission, but... I was all he\nHad, I was the one that kept him going. He sacrificed his last reason to live so that /I/ could live a better life. I'm still looking for a purpose to live, at the moment I just wander... Maybe the Delvers? I have a whole new world to discover, and I wont\nwaste this chance at life that has been given to me. I'm a new man, atleast, I hope.\nThe Delvers,\nwas trying to change. I couldn't bring myself to tell him about they things I did. He said the Delvers would find out soon enough, and if they do... Well, then I guess i'll have to find a purpose somewhere else, then.\nBlue,\nIt's not all bad,\nthieve and such, I said no of course, too young to be doing that sort of thing. Though then again, so was I.\nHonest day's work, \nmade collecting logs, so I stoped by Abresi steel and bought a genuine dwarven felling axe, for 70 mina. It's nearly as sharp as my cutlass for God's sake, and it's only for cutting down trees...\nBranching out,\nsomething. But no, there pretty just like me. I was kind of rascist in my youth, I'm starting to see. I told them about the magic pipe story, they don't buy it like everyone else. That Uruk thought he could drink me under the table? Ha, please...\nAttacked,\nluckily, I got to it first. I left the knife in her right knee cap, I don't know why I spared her. Maybe it's because I can see myself in her? Anyway, I survived with minor inguries, so thats good. I guess all that training did me some good after all.\nQuite the day,\nas young as me. I talked to Draen, and he said if I want to study hydomancy I should go to the oracle libary, but first i'll need permission from Nienna and the little bitch Crineas...\nFucking Glowstone,\nWillow,\nso I bought eight, 960 mina. She was skeptical at first, but I also threw the magic pipe into the offer, and after  showing what it can do she couldn't resist. We went back to her place and made the trade, I was about to leave when she offered me a drink.\nI said \"Sure\" with my generic smile, and she poured me and her a glass of whiskey. We spent the entire night drinking and talking, though I ended up doing alot of talking. I brought my past up my mistake, and she inquired about it. I told her about what I\nused to do for a living, and that I was trying to change. She didn't seem to bothered, and I asked her about her past. She was pretty drunk at this point, and I was getting there. She crawled over the table, and sat next to me and started to tell me about\nher past life as a assassin. She broke down into tears talking about it, and ended up crying on my shoulder. I know what it's like, to have the memory's of killing burnt into your skull, those are things you can never forget. After comforting her for \nawhile, I brought her face up to mine and kissed her. Nothing too deep, just a peck on the lips. I think she liked it by the way she was blushing, and she kissed me back. We stayed in this embrace for awhile, kissing more deeply all the while. Then, my \ntie came off, then my shirt... then her robes, and well... I'm not going to go in detail what it was like here, but i'll just say it was /really/ good.\nGodanistan, or whatever his name is. We got our clothes back on and headed over to the door, and saw some scruffy looking guy with his nose pressed against the door. He said all he wanted was love, from Willow probably. I said he would never get it, cos' \nhe isn't a dashing rogue like me.This made the man angry, and Willow giggle. Willow also pointed out there was something else this man probably doesn't have... Just sayin'\nkilled the unarmored man nearly staright away after he begged for mercy. There was this other guy in golden armor, charged at me like a manic. He obviously didn't know how to handle a sword, because I easily evaded his attack, and killed him. \nWe dragged the bodies into Willows basement, and she patched my shoulder wound I got off the guys sword after he flung it foward when I stabbed him. I ended up asking if me and her were together. I want to be with her, I just wasn't sure if she felt the\nsame way about me. She does, thank God. Jean and Willow, then. Sounds good, poetic even... Anyway, I also got some hellstone off the guy I killed, and the delvers just happen to be looking for Hellstone.\nGood bad luck,\nOracle Libary,\n/free/ I have had a streak of good luck recently, honestly.\nUseless,\nfor you. Kill yourself Jean.\n...\nIt's over,\nSlade?\nwasn't supposed to be like this...\nEverything's going to shit...\ncity, putting up poster to join the one true faith or some bollocks like that. Not to mention the fact they think they can just execute people they consider heretics in the street. Luckilty, I managed to get Tuv to move their executions outside the walls,\nbut as an Enforcer their still breaking my balls. And in the midst of all this, Slade is starting to rear his ugly head again, great. Fuckin' great...\ni'm getting over Willow, maybe I should try and hit it off with Mirai.", ""),
        StaticBook("Job Application", "timzuiderveld", "To the most Exalted Treasurer of Renatus \"Tuv\"\n\nGreetings my lord,\n\nRecently I have found that you were the one to be contacted for a job in the greatest Empire Anthos has ever known. So I, Gregory Brooks\nWish to meet with you to discuss my possible employment in the great Human Empire.\n\nMy preference lies with working for the treasury, I feel I could be of more use there than swing a sword or haul goods.\nI assure you that I am well versed in the arts of Finance and that I have plenty of experience.\n\nI hope to see your reply soon\n\nKind Regards,\n\nGregory Brooks.", ""),
        StaticBook("Job request.", "Asher Flamecloak", "Dear Golrodir Eritaf,\nThis message is coming from a wood elf in the Hall of labor. I am requesting work as a hunter. My name is Asher Flamecloak. I have experience with a bow and currently own one myself. However I do not own any arrows. I grew up in the \nwoods and had to hunt for food. I know how to skin an animal and get the right meat from the right places. Please send me a bird if an arrangment can be made to get me off my arse and start working. \nKind regards.\n-Asher Flamecloak", ""),
        StaticBook("Joke Book", "Tantaparo", "Funny miscellaneous quotes, and jokes.\n\nPart one : \nFunny last words of anonymous people.\n((Real people in real ife!))\n\n\"This is no time to make new enemies.\"\n\n\nOne last drink, please.\nPart two :\nAnti-jokes\n\nWhats white with four legs that will kill you if it fell on you?\n\nanswer : A bath tub\n\nWhats out of this world that you see everyday?\n\nanswer : the moon.\n\nWhats red and bad for your teeth?\n\nanswer : a brick.\n\n((OOC part three\nyomama's))\n((\nYomama is so fat, that she broke the stairs to heaven!\nYomama is so stupid, that she tried to drown a fish in water.\n\nYomama is so stupid, that she stayed up all night trying to litteraly catch some sleep.\n\nYomama is so hairy, that when you were born you got carpet burn!   ))\n((RP))\nPart three :\nNormal jokes\n\nWhy was the skeleton sad at the party?\n\nawsner : he had no-body.\n\nWhy is a tomato red?\nawsner : it saw the salad dressing.\n\nTheEnd.\n\nAwsner : the restart.\n\n((Legit end))", ""),
        StaticBook("Joke book 2", "WearsomeKarma", "Rigal's Joke book number two :\ntoo short\"\ndiabetes\nAwsner : someone threw a book at him.\nPart four : Poem jokes\n((Moar anti jokes))\nA man walks into a bar, except its a metal bar, like a pole and gets hurt.\nThe final joke :\nThanks for reading my book, all jokes that are lore acceptable are in RP thouse that arn't are ooc.", ""),
        StaticBook("Jon's Tale", "BloodstainBlade", "        Chapter 1\nup something from the city?\" He asks. The boy nods and the man takes off.\n   \"Momma, Daddy!\" He calls. He runs over to his exhausted parents, who had just returned from work.\n   Fire, screams, a man bursts in the house. \"Oi, we need to go.\" He yells. Jon is roughly picked up by his father as he runs out. He screams, seeing the burning remains of his village.\nground, panting.\n   Jon sits on the ground between his parents. He lays on his mother's lap, silently crying.\n   A few days later, a tired Jon and his family arrive in the capitol. His father goes to the docks. \"The Undead have destroyed Riven,\" he says. \"Is there an evacuation location?\" The man shakes his head. \n    \"Three tickets on that boat.\" His father says. The man nods and hands him the tickets then closes the pay slot.\nbe, they didn't know.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Mellanius Veran", "   Mellanius Veran's\n        Journal on \n  The Hallowing Halls\nIf my theories are correct, then I, Mellanius Veran, could potentially become one of the most well known people of the world! Even more known than The Wandering Wizard!\n\nSomewhere, deep down in the earth of Anthos, a rift in the Void exists. I know, I \nknow, all of the 'scientific mages' believe a rift to the Void cannot exist, for it shall 'destroy the world'. True, perhaps it isn't possible, but what if there was some sort of containment field around it? A 'wall', so to say, to keep its destructing \npower away from the mortal world! Truly magnificent, just think what would be possible with it! The power that one could have by using a rift to The Void! Think about it! Now, where was I? Oh yes! Deep down in the earth, one of these contained rifts \nexists, oh yes yes, opened and contained by whoever lived before us in Anthos. I do infact wonder how such a magnificent race that is able to do such a thing became extinct. Well, enough talki- I mean writing, I am going to find the Hallowing Halls!", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "An Unknown Valiant", "I'm growing tired of his constent torture of us. It's all he fawking does. He calls them drills, but he is lieing to us, to the House and to himself. Dvari is a horrible leader and should not be the Sargent of us. He couldn't lead a sheep across the road,\nbut he is trusted to train the Valiants. I'm surprised he hasn't drunk himself to death, that fawking bastard. \n\n-unsigned", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Alex Bedevere", "Day 1\nThe Pentagram:\n-*drawing of pentagram*\n-Large\n-Made of stone\n-Dead body in the center.\n-Seems to be corrupted.\n-It is a human skeleton.\n-Naked\nDay 4\nThe Bloodied Wall\n-Cave wall.\n-Patches of crimson rock\n-The rock seems to contain blood and oozes from it's surface.\n-The rock doesn't seem to be as solid as others.\nDay 8 \nThe Red Crystal\n-Red\n-Large\n-Floating\n-Corrupts anyone who's near. Physically and mentally.\n-Very sturdy and hard to break.\nNote: I attempted to crack it with a stone pick. It shake.\nThe Body in the ice\n-Human body frozen in ice.\n-Under archway.\n-Clothes in peasant clothes.\n-Slit in the throat then frozen.\n\nArea:\n-Ice/stone spikes\n-Canyon\n-Caves\n-Snowy\n\nPhysical Corruption Effects\n-Pale skin\n-Spiders are attracted to you\n-Flesh begins to slowly decay.\n-Illness\n-Nose bleeds\nMental Corruption Effects\n-Hallucination\n-Insanity\n-Violent Urges\n-Nightmares\n\nNote: These take about a month in order to have full effect.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal 1", "Katalion", "Inspection of DarkHaven\nTrip With Kalenz #3\nAdditional Notes\nExplosion at the gates\nAttack on Malinor 1\nSecond Political Visit of Malinor\nAttack in Haelun'or\nAttack on Haelun'or\nAdditional Notes", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal 1", "Deece94", "3rd of The Grand Harvest 1454\nsee that it is returned to health. \nthe wild. I shall miss her dearly, it is sad but this bird has been the only source of companionship i have had in months. \nto leave in no time at all. The Alabaster Seabird is a truely beautiful and magnificant creature indeed. The rate at which she has gotten stronger is astonishing, i wish i was as strong as this bird has proven to be. \n20th of The Grand Harvest 1454", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Entry", "Alexander_Wh", ":::Journal of Aengoth:::\ndwarves, but by myself. I hope that by following and meeting Farren's standards I will once again be able to honestly call the dwarf lands home. Yet, at the same time I feel the pull of Salvus. If I could I would attempt to help it, yet no longer can I.\nThe reason being is I don't want to serve in a military force, and I don't think there is anything else I could offer to Salvus. I have made the attempt to, but with each attempt I grow more and more... distant and dissapointed. My most recent effort in \nlight of Grand King Thorin Grandaxe weighs heavily, for I know I cannot meet the task he requires of me, yet another task I wanted to do yet failure showed itself in my path. I've sought many fresh starts, even recently I joined the Delvers hoping it \nwould bring some of the joy and happiness I am sorely missing in my life. Yet I cannot forget my past ambitions and failures. I don't know what to do, no path seems possible. I can't find myself a home with the Dwarves, Salvians, or a new group. Perhaps\nI was meant to be one who wanders aimlessly. How sad is it, that even now I write in a journal confessing my depression. Oh the younger me would laugh and jeer at my weakness of spirit. Maybe.. maybe I am a relic of Asulon, which was meant to die with it.\n((09/07/2013))", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal II", "birdwhisperer", "I have run out of space in my old journal... it is fitting that I would begin a new one at this time of my life. I can feel my baby preparing to be born. It should be any day now.\ndangerous and unpredictable world. While I yet carry him, or her, he's safe from that.\n*rather clumsy drawings of tiny hands, dispersed with a few butterflies and designs for baby clothes fill the page.*\nGavin may be taking over as my guide... I've already cut a branch from our birch to make a staff.\nbecause he still has feelings for me. I don't know what I'm supposed to do about that, it's not as though I've done anything to encourage him. And he has done nothing aside from being a pleasant friend.\nIt would seem I've been robbed. I'm not sure when, exactly, I only just now noticed. I found a note in one of the drawers about a donation to the guild, and locks, and another one of those gold coins.\nThe opal ones, at least, were left alone, which I'm thankful for because those were my favorite. But the ruby one, and the white crystal necklace have both been stolen. None of the books seem to have been bothered, at least...\nI learned a bit about healing from Gavin. It seems most of it just has to do with common sense and being prepared. He also said I may be attuned soon. And I need to work on my staff.\nAvern'len returned some time ago, and Lenniel'onn is walking now.\nCallax has given me the task of finding objects in the forest that represent Ceridwen and Cernunnos.\n*a few sketched birch leaves float across the page, accompanied by a single apple, a badly-drawn horse, and varying patterns for what appear to be stuffed toys in the shapes of small animals.*\nThere has been a strange attack... the same creatures that Avery was having visions of all those years ago. And this time I don't know where he is.\nSo now I'm waiting for Callax...\nthat might be the problem. I certainly hope Oz has gotten past things, it's been several years after all. But lately it's been hard to tell.\nsimply ease out of each others lives.\nLenniel to regard Oz as more of a father than Avery. I'm not sure if he does.\nLast night was odd.\nthat, there was a loud explosion and something fell from the sky and landed near the bridge to Lin'everal. It was mostly stone, but also ice, and was somehow on fire. We put the fires out, and took some pieces of the stone. The Valah said it must have\nlaunched as an attack from somewhere, but I believe it is a fallen star of some kind.\nBrother Shadow suggested I name my staff. I've no idea where to even start.\nviolence... anyway, so I am considering growing a sort of cemetary. Though this would be more like a small grove where people can remember their loved ones. Perhaps burry them, if they wish. But a place of remembering and honoring the dead.\nThings I'll need:\nAvern'len is showing up less frequently... I'm worried about him.\nLenniel'onn is nearly three now, and running around more than ever. Today has been a long day, though. I don't remember ever being so frightened before, except perhaps during Oceas's wedding...\nwent with Lenniel to the Delver's base. I knew it was a terrible idea at the time, yet there we were. He and Nienna's daughter started playing a game, and I lost sight of him. I must of searched around those tunnels for hours. It felt as though I was \ngoing to lose my mind, I was so sick with worry.\n*a few small sketches of roses and flowers fill the page, appearing to have been rather half-heartedly.*\nThe druid's grove is gone. The creatures from the north overtook it. I'm not sure where they've gone, but I can't have Lenniel so close.\nno other choice. Our room is very close to the entrance, though, so it's not so bad. And Lenniel seems to enjoy playing with Nienna's daughter, Eventa. He wanted to come here.\n\nI spent most of the day waiting by the shores near the Mali'aheral with the druids. Lenniel has gotten it into his head that Gavin is his Maln. This is exactly what I feared would happen with Oz, and it seems that through Gavin's meddling and Lenniel's...\nneed for a father, it's happened despite anything I may have tried.\n*the outline of a beach and small hill, covered in trees fills the page.*\nI have been attuned with nature and am now a full druid! Saviticus oversaw, and my totem is the Dove. It isn't quite what I was expecting, though I'm not sure what I did expect. But it seems fitting.\nAvery is back!\nThe past few days have been rather interesting...\nthough Gavin would be removed from his seat as Arch Druid, but he was not. Instead, Kefi was made a second Arch Druid.\n*wheat sheaves, birch leaves, owls, sparrows, and simple, curling flowers are sketched on this page*\nI don't remember how long it's been since I picked this up last...\nSome time ago, I met two strange men just outside the gate of Malinor. They were both wearing hoods, but one said his name was Torian, and the other may have been a mali'ker. They told me a man had been watching Lenniel'onn, and was probably a danger to \nhim. They wanted me to come with them to Adunia to confront this man. Then one of the Delver mages, Richard Tarus, walked past and said they were wearing undead robes, with the eye of Iblees. So I left to check on Lenniel, who was asleep on Samuel. Meta \nfollowed me, apparently, and warned me of the men.\nour home in the Delver's village.\nfor Avern'len. I thought I'd lost between moving all my things so often.\nthem, and went running over Malinor and Samuel looking for him.\nand I took him to the monks to heal.\nhired by some knightly order in Oren to be their personal bard. He seems very happy being in Abresi...\nquite different from what he's used to.\nHe was taken from the middle of the city\nwe have gone is ever safe. There is no home for the three of us that is both safe, and happy...", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of B.H.D", "[WrongSkin] [Youth] Tiz Arrior", "3rd of The Deep Cold, 1447.\nI have been staying in Abresi for quite some time, and everything seems so enchanting. I'm downstairs from Abner's Clinic, after giving them quite a show, and something peculiar is happening. I don't want to press him on it.\n28th of the Grand Harvest, 1449.\nThe issue so far has been resolved, and everything is as it should be. Krugsmas has passed, with all the lovely celebrations. Merry Krugsmas to all, and to all a good night!\n-Santy Bart\n17th of The Amber Cold, 1449.\nI had made a Krugsmas present for the three children of Abner and Eva, but....recently, I discovered that there are only two. There is a great shroud of mystery surrounding this child, but I will not press them on it.\n2nd of Snow's Maiden, 1449.\nAbner has been getting into bad drinking habits lately. It appears that this isn't the first time he has done this. Eva also has a shroud of mystery about her, with those golden eyes, flashing. It's only when she's angered.\n3rd of The Deep Cold, 1449.\nI've been debating on buying a house near Eva's and Abner's, so that we could stay in touch. But they seem so small....will it be enough? Perhaps I'll consult them for insight on this matter.\n*The date is not given* I've been investigating Abner on his drinking addiction, and I'm getting myself into danger. If anyone finds this, please give this to Evangeline Rahl, she will make good use of it, by fuel or by journalism. I need- *abrupt end*", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal: W. Imp", "Meet2012", "Fauna Manuscript: Water Imp\n\nRecorded by Ev Ar'ahern\n\n- - - - - - - - - - -\n\n     Upon an expedition to a secluded cavern hidden behind a waterfall, the group discovered what\nseemed to be an abandoned house.  It's location was not exactly ideal, as the humidity within the cavern was not kind to the paining and books within the home.  Water dripped through the wooden ceiling, and the place smelled of rotting wood.\n     The group entered the house while exploring the cavern, looking around for clues as to who resided there, or why the house was built there at all.  Solid evidence was never discovered.\n     \n     When every member of the\nexcursion was within the home, the door slammed shut, seemingly on its own accord.  There was no light generated in the house, so the pyromancer Richard Tarus created a source.\n\n     Shrill laughter was echoing around the\ncavern outside of the house, and the sound of cracking ice was produced near the door.  We attempted to pull the door open, and were greeted by a thick wall of pure ice.  Such ice could not have formed naturally in the time that we were in the house.\n     It took some time, but Tarus melted through the ice, confirming that it was magically created.  We crawled through the hole that was created for us, and the hole sealed itself after us.\n\n     We scrambled up to the entrance of the cavern, and were \ngreeted by a small, blue being standing on a ledge.  He cackled again, and then proceeded to shoot bursts of water at us.  When I shot water  back at it, the shot did not seem to phase it, despite being a direct hit to the chest.\n\n     The imp dove into\nthe water that flowed in from the mouth of the cavern, and seemed to disappear.  We ventured closer to the entrance, and the cavern suddenly shook.  The water began to swirl around where we were standing, forming a large wall of rushing water on all\nsides.  Thinking quickly, I created several large pillars in the middle of the raging whirlpool, which disrupted the water's flow.  As the water died down, the imp lept from it back onto the ledge above us.  Artemic quickly notched and shot the imp, which\nmelted into a liquid state and drained back into the water.\n\n     We finally exited the cave, climbing across an ice bridge that I created back to land.  We witnessed one final glance of the imp as he jumped from the waterfall onto a ledge beside it.\n     In summary, it appeared that the imp was both made of and able to control water.  It's origin is unknown, as is its intentions.  This encounter begs the question of whether or not other elemental imps exist, and if so, where?", ""),
        StaticBook("JournalOfWar", "ski_king3", "\n\n\n*Within the scroll, rips, smudges and wear have led to some of the words being impossible to read. It is clearly extremely old*\n\n\n    Journal of War\n\n\n      By duh High\n     Shaman Gobo\n\n\n\nDay 201 - Lur and Rex still be fightin’ ‘bout who……….. be duh strongest. Krug hurt, but still fightin’ the Iblees.\n\n\n\nDay 539 - Duh flames o’ green has spread. More and more brudduhs becoming green. Healer twig comes, but taint doesn’t stop. Orcsy shamans don’t know, but duh babes still shrivel like squeali…..\n\n\n\n\nDay 1008 - Duh stouts try to go klomp Krug, but Gorkil and Dom klomp back. Stouts g……………………..when duh humies come to battle. Twiggies no want leave tree land.\n\n\n\n\nDay 1500 - Green flames duhn’t be shrivelin’ da babes, but most brudduhs have been touched. Ancestor of duh sky help contain duh taint. He say those who perish with honor be\n\n\nfree o’duh taint. Wounds of Krug worsen every day. All brudduhs hope Krug strengthens so ‘e may perish with honor………………………………………………….\n\n\n\n1788 - Krug has passed in duh mid…….of b……………………………………………….ur and Dom be quarrelin’ about who be duh leader. Da humies be crazy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Jungle Barley", "Menarra", "Jungle Barley.", ""),
        StaticBook("Kar'Lani", "Kalesta", "Kar'Lani\n\nRetold by Kalesta\n\nOracle's Library\n\n19th of Sun's Smile\n-1446\nIt is believed that the Undead had found an artifact of an old clan called \"Kar'Lani\". The only known clue to its current whereabouts is the old tombs of Winterfell. We've sent searching parties, but none have returned. I fear this Artifact may be cursed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Keep Walking", "Oracle", "Keep Walking: A Tale of Truth by Silion Luthias\nHail friend, I am Silion Luthias, and I'm going to tell you a story. This particular story, happens to be one of great importance to me me, for it is the story\nof me, and my brothers. We've all been scarred, vruised, and crushed by the harshness of reality but, we've also all come together under odd circumstances, and have become traveling companions, and friends to the\nend. As I sit underground in my study, I look towards the future, for it's bright, and full of promise, and untold stories filled with adventure and hope. But, to look towards the future, you must keep the past in sight, so, to learn of our current\nadventures, you must know our pasts. :: There are 5 of us, Caden, Guraim, Gruol, Qwert, and I, Sillion. Each of us have tragedy in our past, but it has turned us into better people. First, we shall start with Qwert, one of two Dwarves in our party. ::\nQwert was born in the Farlands, a place I've yet to see His mother died during childbirth, and his father died in a fire, trying to save Qwert. From there, he was raised by a wolf mother, and her cubs, so, he was illeterate when he came to us. From\nthere, he moved onwards the Oren, and eventually was brought into our party via Caden, and here he resides still. :: Next, is Gruol, our Orc friend. Gruol was raised in the LOrcish fashion, but joined the Orcish Guard as a adult. But, during a routine\nsweep of the lands, the unit Gruol was placed in encountered a group of bandits looking for food amongst a group of homes. During the battle, most were slaughtered but, one of the humans in his teens started running. Gruol's captain ordered\nhim to hunt the boy down, and kill him. But, Gruol refused. :: Gruol was reported to The Rex, and was discharged immediatley . GRuol was shamed by his people, family, and country. So, he set off into the wilds, looking redemption, and riches.\nHowever, I found him, befriended him, and he travels with us as the group powerhouse, and is still looking to return his honor everyday. :: Now, we move on to my dear friend, Caden. Caden was the second member to join our party, and is our swordman.\nBut, his past is the most horrendous of all of ours, and it's time I document it for the world to know. Caden was raised in the Cathaldus Family, one of the most prestigous famlilies in Laurelin. He was taught sword fighting, archery, and perfect\nEnglish to name a few of the many privelges he had in his childhood. :: But, when he was quite young, he family adopted a young Orc child, I'Shaak. Caden was raised with him, learning from I'Shaak brutish capabilities, Caden became a force to\nreckoned with on the battlefield. However, I'Shaak caught a illness in his teen years, and died. THis gave Caden a respect for orcs, adn a hole in his heart, that has been left unfilled for too long. Then, in his first years of adulthood, a hit was\nordered upon his family. Caden was away, training with his blade, when his family was murdered in cold blood in their sleep. When Caden returned that night, exhausted from practice, he found his parents corpses strewn with blood and bile sliced open in\nplaces along their throats, chest, and stomach. But, to their dismay, a hred of clothing adorned the bedpost, plastered with blood. But, the true color still showed, purple tinged along the edges with green. It was the flag of a local mercenary company,\nand only their captain wore the colors. Sillion marched to the local fort his blade sharpened to a razor edge, and nothing but primal fury, and the lust for revenge swarming amongst his consicous. He trudged in, busting open the doors,\nand listened to the sounds of men rowdily drinking, laughing, and reveling in a well earned payment, most likley a very large one. Caden walked into the Main dininig hall, and stood, ready to charge. He ran his eye across the\nrows of fighters, and then steadied his gaze upon the only man standing, the captain, adorned with a flowing shirt, with a ripped sleeve. Caden drew in a breath, and screamed, \"YOU TOOK MY FAMILIES LIVES, I REQUIRE YOUR IN PAYMENT! YOU PATHETIC\nBLEMISHES BARELY MAKE THE PAYMENT!\" Caden then pulled out a bottle of spirits, plugged with a hankerchief. He dipped the flailing hankerchief end into a torch, and hurled it onto the table, fire and glass flew around, men instantly went up in flames,\nsomefrom the initial explosion, some from the sparks touching their alcohol drenched garb. amonsgt the chaos, most fled, or perished, but, the captain stood eyelocked with Caden. The captain brandished a beautiful gilded\naxe, imbuded with diamonds. The pair began stalking towards one another, and the captain swung the massive chunk of metal towards Caden's throat, but he deftly sropped, and instantaneously drove his blade into the captains right\nstomach, ripped the blade left, and stepped back to let his guts splatter on the masonry. As his innards tasted air, he dropped to his knees and feebly tried to return his organs to their rightful place. He looked up to Caden, blood seeping\nthrough his teeth, and whispered, \"Your father died in his sleep, but your mother was awoke by our footfalls. She looked up at us in her nightgown, eyes full of fear, and she screamed. She squealed like a swine. I imagine the sound would be like music\nto you, dagger-ear.\" Caden stared at him with pure fury, then raised his blade, and dropped it through the captains spinal cord. His head rolled across the floor. and landed amongst the pile of burnt bodies. Caden walked back to Laurelin, drenched in\nblood, dragging his blade, and staring into the distance, eyes blank. AS he entered, he prepared for a heros embrace, but was gripped by guards right away. They then began dragging him through town, preparing to throw him into\nprison for the murder of a entire company of mercenaries. As the men brought him through a cluster of homes for the richer members of town, a politician whos face was lightly covered, looked to be chuckling lightly. Caden was jailed\nbut escaped after a small sentence. I found him in the wilds, crouching near a tree, holding a makeshift stabbing weapon. I coaxed him to me with a loaf of bread. Once I got him eating, he told me this story, and I vowed I would help him find the\nmonster who hired the hit upon his family, and so he stays with us now.", ""),
        StaticBook("Keep Walking", "Domainoft", "Keep Walking: A Tale of Truth by Silion Luthias\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\nVaehaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((8/28/13))\nHail friend, I am Silion Luthias, and I'm going to tell you a story. This particular story, happens to be one of great importance to me me, for it is the story\nof me, and my brothers. We've all been scarred, vruised, and crushed by the harshness of reality but, we've also all come together under odd circumstances, and have become traveling companions, and friends to the\nend. As I sit underground in my study, I look towards the future, for it's bright, and full of promise, and untold stories filled with adventure and hope. But, to look towards the future, you must keep the past in sight, so, to learn of our current\nadventures, you must know our pasts. :: There are 5 of us, Caden, Guraim, Gruol, Qwert, and I, Sillion. Each of us have tragedy in our past, but it has turned us into better people. First, we shall start with Qwert, one of two Dwarves in our party. ::\nQwert was born in the Farlands, a place I've yet to see His mother died during childbirth, and his father died in a fire, trying to save Qwert. From there, he was raised by a wolf mother, and her cubs, so, he was illeterate when he came to us. From\nthere, he moved onwards the Oren, and eventually was brought into our party via Caden, and here he resides still. :: Next, is Gruol, our Orc friend. Gruol was raised in the LOrcish fashion, but joined the Orcish Guard as a adult. But, during a routine\nsweep of the lands, the unit Gruol was placed in encountered a group of bandits looking for food amongst a group of homes. During the battle, most were slaughtered but, one of the humans in his teens started running. Gruol's captain ordered\nhim to hunt the boy down, and kill him. But, Gruol refused. :: Gruol was reported to The Rex, and was discharged immediatley . GRuol was shamed by his people, family, and country. So, he set off into the wilds, looking redemption, and riches.\nHowever, I found him, befriended him, and he travels with us as the group powerhouse, and is still looking to return his honor everyday. :: Now, we move on to my dear friend, Caden. Caden was the second member to join our party, and is our swordman.\nBut, his past is the most horrendous of all of ours, and it's time I document it for the world to know. Caden was raised in the Cathaldus Family, one of the most prestigous famlilies in Laurelin. He was taught sword fighting, archery, and perfect\nEnglish to name a few of the many privelges he had in his childhood. :: But, when he was quite young, he family adopted a young Orc child, I'Shaak. Caden was raised with him, learning from I'Shaak brutish capabilities, Caden became a force to\nreckoned with on the battlefield. However, I'Shaak caught a illness in his teen years, and died. THis gave Caden a respect for orcs, adn a hole in his heart, that has been left unfilled for too long. Then, in his first years of adulthood, a hit was\nordered upon his family. Caden was away, training with his blade, when his family was murdered in cold blood in their sleep. When Caden returned that night, exhausted from practice, he found his parents corpses strewn with blood and bile sliced open in\nplaces along their throats, chest, and stomach. But, to their dismay, a hred of clothing adorned the bedpost, plastered with blood. But, the true color still showed, purple tinged along the edges with green. It was the flag of a local mercenary company,\nand only their captain wore the colors. Sillion marched to the local fort his blade sharpened to a razor edge, and nothing but primal fury, and the lust for revenge swarming amongst his consicous. He trudged in, busting open the doors,\nand listened to the sounds of men rowdily drinking, laughing, and reveling in a well earned payment, most likley a very large one. Caden walked into the Main dininig hall, and stood, ready to charge. He ran his eye across the\nrows of fighters, and then steadied his gaze upon the only man standing, the captain, adorned with a flowing shirt, with a ripped sleeve. Caden drew in a breath, and screamed, \"YOU TOOK MY FAMILIES LIVES, I REQUIRE YOUR IN PAYMENT! YOU PATHETIC\nBLEMISHES BARELY MAKE THE PAYMENT!\" Caden then pulled out a bottle of spirits, plugged with a hankerchief. He dipped the flailing hankerchief end into a torch, and hurled it onto the table, fire and glass flew around, men instantly went up in flames,\nsomefrom the initial explosion, some from the sparks touching their alcohol drenched garb. amonsgt the chaos, most fled, or perished, but, the captain stood eyelocked with Caden. The captain brandished a beautiful gilded\naxe, imbuded with diamonds. The pair began stalking towards one another, and the captain swung the massive chunk of metal towards Caden's throat, but he deftly sropped, and instantaneously drove his blade into the captains right\nstomach, ripped the blade left, and stepped back to let his guts splatter on the masonry. As his innards tasted air, he dropped to his knees and feebly tried to return his organs to their rightful place. He looked up to Caden, blood seeping\nthrough his teeth, and whispered, \"Your father died in his sleep, but your mother was awoke by our footfalls. She looked up at us in her nightgown, eyes full of fear, and she screamed. She squealed like a swine. I imagine the sound would be like music\nto you, dagger-ear.\" Caden stared at him with pure fury, then raised his blade, and dropped it through the captains spinal cord. His head rolled across the floor. and landed amongst the pile of burnt bodies. Caden walked back to Laurelin, drenched in\nblood, dragging his blade, and staring into the distance, eyes blank. AS he entered, he prepared for a heros embrace, but was gripped by guards right away. They then began dragging him through town, preparing to throw him into\nprison for the murder of a entire company of mercenaries. As the men brought him through a cluster of homes for the richer members of town, a politician whos face was lightly covered, looked to be chuckling lightly. Caden was jailed\nbut escaped after a small sentence. I found him in the wilds, crouching near a tree, holding a makeshift stabbing weapon. I coaxed him to me with a loaf of bread. Once I got him eating, he told me this story, and I vowed I would help him find the\nmonster who hired the hit upon his family, and so he stays with us now.", ""),
