 eye across the\nrows of fighters, and then steadied his gaze upon the only man standing, the captain, adorned with a flowing shirt, with a ripped sleeve. Caden drew in a breath, and screamed, \"YOU TOOK MY FAMILIES LIVES, I REQUIRE YOUR IN PAYMENT! YOU PATHETIC\nBLEMISHES BARELY MAKE THE PAYMENT!\" Caden then pulled out a bottle of spirits, plugged with a hankerchief. He dipped the flailing hankerchief end into a torch, and hurled it onto the table, fire and glass flew around, men instantly went up in flames,\nsomefrom the initial explosion, some from the sparks touching their alcohol drenched garb. amonsgt the chaos, most fled, or perished, but, the captain stood eyelocked with Caden. The captain brandished a beautiful gilded\naxe, imbuded with diamonds. The pair began stalking towards one another, and the captain swung the massive chunk of metal towards Caden's throat, but he deftly sropped, and instantaneously drove his blade into the captains right\nstomach, ripped the blade left, and stepped back to let his guts splatter on the masonry. As his innards tasted air, he dropped to his knees and feebly tried to return his organs to their rightful place. He looked up to Caden, blood seeping\nthrough his teeth, and whispered, \"Your father died in his sleep, but your mother was awoke by our footfalls. She looked up at us in her nightgown, eyes full of fear, and she screamed. She squealed like a swine. I imagine the sound would be like music\nto you, dagger-ear.\" Caden stared at him with pure fury, then raised his blade, and dropped it through the captains spinal cord. His head rolled across the floor. and landed amongst the pile of burnt bodies. Caden walked back to Laurelin, drenched in\nblood, dragging his blade, and staring into the distance, eyes blank. AS he entered, he prepared for a heros embrace, but was gripped by guards right away. They then began dragging him through town, preparing to throw him into\nprison for the murder of a entire company of mercenaries. As the men brought him through a cluster of homes for the richer members of town, a politician whos face was lightly covered, looked to be chuckling lightly. Caden was jailed\nbut escaped after a small sentence. I found him in the wilds, crouching near a tree, holding a makeshift stabbing weapon. I coaxed him to me with a loaf of bread. Once I got him eating, he told me this story, and I vowed I would help him find the\nmonster who hired the hit upon his family, and so he stays with us now.", ""),
        StaticBook("Keira", "[Sentinel] Cillion Chase", "Cillion,\n\nI have no place in this world anymore, So I am leaving the Princedom \n\nRecently my youngest sister, Keira, has joined the Princedom.\nI wish for you to take care of her while I am gone\nDo not tell her the things I have done and my sexuality.\n\nI wish for her to remember me as a good Brother.\n\nI am giving you acess to my house, please replace whatever you take\nPlease remember to make Pancakes for Keira from time to time and also make sure she doesnt get hold of the cookie chest\n\nThank you\n\n\n--Solenoden ", ""),
        StaticBook("Keira's Journal", "l337Ninja", "24 Amber Cold\n1448\n\nDear Diary,\n\nI seem to have lost my my previous diary, so I am starting a new one\n\nI caught some fish today and fed it to a cat, she seems to trust me!\nI dont know what I am going to call her yet.\n\nI made Dad and Alana\neach a chocolate cake and I was asking them some stuff and they just ignored, then I went upstairs and they were having sex!\n\nI couldnt handle this\nanymore so I \ndecided to 'experiment' with alchol, it tasted great, only problem was that when I woke up I vomited alot, although I think Alana shoved something down my throat while I was sleeping to get the alchol out of my 'system'\n6 Snow Maiden \n1448\n\nI bought 3 more bottles of Absinthe at the Tavern today and Im putting one of them on my desk, so they think that is the only bottle I have, and 2 are hidden under my bed! I doubt they will \nfind them!\nI went on a trip into the jungle again and there seemed to have been no zombies or spiders.\n\nI came back home and the bottles under my bed have been taken.\n\nDear Keira, I hope you know that me and Alana are very sorry for what we did. We are now married and Alana is pregnant. When you read this I hope you can forgive me and Alana, I'm still feeling bad about it.\nLove,\nCillion\n21 Deep Cold\n1448\n\nI have returned from my 6 month training trip and I havent seen Father or Alana, I wonder where they are\n\nAlso, I am geussing Ryan is either dead or hasnt been returned to us.\nOn my travels I bought this glowing sword, the man who sold it to me said that it was more duriable and that it 'knocks' enemies further backwards\n\nI havent tried it out yet though, It better last long, It costed 200 minas\nTommorow is my first birthday!\n\nI dont know if I should tell Father or Alana\n\nI wish my Brother was here to celebrate my birthday\n\nI gave the enchanted sword to Cillion and Alana gave me a \nwater evocation tome!\n25th Grand Harvest\n1448\n\nIm sorry I havent kept my diary up to date,\n\nYesturday our house was taken by a man who calls himself the Shadow, after we moved out he gave us his previous house\nLuckily the gaurds took-\n\n*The journal seems to stop abruptly here, as if something interuptted the author mid-sentence*", ""),
        StaticBook("Key To Farming", "sean_desed", "Key Tips to Farming.\n\nHere you will learn the skill of farming, types of crops, soil's health, and a fun hobby. Also, don't worry if you feel that farming isn't for you. Anyone can do it as long as they follow these simple rules and steps.\nChapter One-\n\nFirst thing's first, safety and equipment.\nGloves aren't necessary, but they are a good help. Wearing old ragged shoes is always a good idea when farming. (Get dirty easily) Wear something comfortable while you're at it.\nSince you're around dirt and on your hands and knees often, it is a good choice to wear older clothing. Although it is not required, it is a messy job. Last thing, make sure you keep yourself warm in the winter and hydrated and cool in the heat.\nChapter Two-\n\nTools.\nFor one thing, it is very hard to farm without proper tools. A decent hoe and sickle are the main tools you need for farming. Your hoe shouldn't be used as a weapon, same goes for your sickle. They can be delicate\ntools and require lots of care and responsibility. Make sure that everything you use is properly cleaned after use. Make sure that your hoe of sickle doesn't rust if it's made of metal material. Rusted tools can break easily.\nChapter Three-\n\nUsage of Tools.\nUnless you plan on growing hops than your sickle doesn't have much use. Your hoe is very important though. It is used to till the land into nice, neat and orderly lines, in which your seeds go. Sadly, the question is,\nhow do I use a hoe? Well it is very simple. Grasp it almost as if it were a rake. One hand towards the top of the handle and the other towards the middle to lower section of the handle. You simple dig it to the ground and move it back and forth until the\ndirt spreads away from itself. Your sickle, on the other hand, is used for finding hop's seeds. Basically what you do with your sickle, is you just grab a handful of tall grass (Or grass in general) and slice away with your sickle. \nChapter Four-\n\nHow to Find and use Seeds.\nFinding seeds is fairly easy. Just go out and look for tall grown grass and break it down until you find seeds. Most likely they will be for wheat. With hop's seeds, you use your sickle against \ngrass until you manage to find hop's seeds. If you can find a pumpkin or a melon the seeds for those are inside the items. To grow seeds is a simple concept though. After you till the land with your hoe you just sprinkle the seeds in the lines.\nChapter Five-\n\nSoil Condition.\nThis is always an issue for large farmers. Your soil has a great effect upon how healthy your crops are. Nutrients are needed in the soil, which most soil does, and water. Without a lot of water your crops\nwon't grow quickly, and if it's bad enough they won't grow at all! To fix these problems, it is best to keep patches of water near your crops, or perhaps small streams of conserved water to flow through. \nChapter Six-\n\nDifferent Foods.\nWheat items today are one of the few most consumed items. A big example is Bread. Wheat also is found in cake and cookies. Of course, those aren't found as often, they are still widely seen amoungst the people.\nClosing-\nFarming is a widely done activity throughout the lands. It is constantly needed by the vastly growing population. It's as if there isn't enough food to go around anymore. After reading this farming can only get easier. So now I ask. Go out and\nfarm. Grow crops, have fun, and help the hungry with any spare food or extra crops you have.\nHappy Farming\n\n-Ayton Falo", ""),
        StaticBook("Kilburn Tavern", "Toxzero", "This Document is for the Legal Sale of the Tavern in Baile. This has been sold for 0 Minas. The land has been Gifted to Mr.James Whitestorm. The land is still Owned by House Green but the land owner will be James Whitestorm.\nLand Agreement:\nNo major construction of the land with out the Steward or Lord Green's signed permission. Land Holder does not officaly OWN the land but HOLDS the land.\n\nNo taxes are to be payed, but a 5% Sales Tax in return.\nSignature of House Green Steward- Vaclav Pascal\n*The Signture is very neat*((Roll 18-20 to Forge))\n\nSignatue of Land Holder:\nJames Whitestorm ((Signature is sloopy and quickly written 11-20 to forge))", ""),
