    private fun _ANTHOS_7(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Note", "Goldie_Fishe", "Going out for some \nsupplies. Stay warm.\n\n-J\n\n------------------\n\n*some wheat is missing*\n*there is a scrawled note on top of the chest*\n\nSorry, \nwas really hungry.\n- Celia'Len\n\n\nAm heading out for Salvus, hope to see you again some time.\nThanks for everything.\n\n-Celia'Len\n\n*tiny blood stain at the bottom of the page*", ""),
        StaticBook("Note", "Aislinn", "*The note is written in blood.*\n\n\" Hello. I apologize for my lack of activity. I am pleased to say that (one) of my personalities has regained most of his memories.\n\nI will be able to resume normal duties and\ncontinue serving Him. Should you require anything, contact me. \"\n\n-Aislinn\n                      ( o )\n12th of the Deep Cold, 1444\n13th of the Deep Cold, 1444\n13th of the Deep Cold, 1444\n14th of the Deep Cold, 1444\nChronicles of the\nRetold from the best of my memories, I shall try to inscribe my doings during this most holy of wars and analyse political and militaristic factors in contemporary wars\nFrom recent memory and accounts, I can recall the sacking of Malinor. We pillaged the city, holding the gate for several days before moving deeper into Luminaire. After raiding the Druid's grove, we pulled back.\nLater that month, we attempted the same thing. Resistance was weak at first, then a joint effort of humans and dwarves managed to dislocate us. I blame the mismanagment of our forces, who went rampant in the city, allowing the enemy to pick us off, one by\none.\nNorthern nation. We captured a prince, and the part of our group that I had sent around the long way were able to ambush the main army. They were crushed and routed. We took the castle that same day, laid waste to it, and left.\nAnother sally against the Herendulians. Taking up position atop a church, we were able to defeat yet another group of barbarians.\nRebellion is brewing in Oren. As those who remain loyal to the Horen blood mass for an attack, the levies of Carrion sharpen their blades. \ninterfere, success is almost as well guaranteed for both sides. With mercenaries out of the picture, I shall examine this war.\ntroops are veterans of raids and numerous battles. Amongst them, we can count the Flays, or Blackmonts, or whatever the call themselves now. Experience does these troops well.\nthey always do. If only I could drill them, discipline them into a an actual fighting force. Then, there would be a chance. As it stands, taking the initiative is the best hope for these troops, who currently hold Baile.\ntraining is quickly performed, victory stands in certain of the current monarchs. \ncompany I used to lead before being granted Master's gift.\n1. Lack of Experience\n2. Weakness\nMalinor would stand a better chance at winning wars.\nrisking to hit allies, and it is hard to concentrate on the void when arrows fly. If these magers were trained and armed in conventional warfare, they would prove to be a most beneficial addition to an Elven war machine.\n4. Supplies\ncurrent and previous human wars is due to the fact that there economy can be geared into one that supplies their soldiers, rather than remain in a civil type economy.\nresults in them losing the initiative, and forcing them to fight on their enemies terms and battleground. If they grew spines and took action, a devasting blow could be delivered upon their enemies.\nToday, our glorious Lieutenant Shae'Tan took down three dwarven veterans. As they charged him, our heroic leader opened a rift. As valiant Kambasors fought the Dwarves, our Commadner moved through the smoke, and ended up behind the filthy dwarves. \nKambasors killed one, and our master took care of the other two. Much praise upon him, and Setherien guide his sword.\nunhonorable act, using their Teutons in a surpise attack. They were no might for us, and we slew them in great numbers. Victory for the master.\nA joint dwarven/ human scouting party was sent to the North. I happened to be stationed under the gateway at the time. Arrows flew as they approached, striking several Kambasors. I used the Master's Boon to strike many of them down, and the Glurztfolk \nfinished the rest. I was wounded and knocked out, before being taken inside for treatment.\non why the elves could not be an effective and forceful military. During this battle, I saw each of these points work against the pointy elves and their allies. In the end, it was simply because of large numbers and for our amusement that we allowed them \nto retake the island.\nToday was a dead full of bloodshed and woe, for today was the day we would corrupt the outside of Herendul.\n-orthy opposistion, but they soon fell by the combined efforts of blades and His boon.\nThe fight, overall, was very lackluster. Their forces were well numbered and well equiped, but they were felled easily by our horde.", ""),
        StaticBook("Note", "Jimacat", "Untill next time, love.\nSend word when the child is returned.\n       With Love,\n           -Alexander               Bedevere", ""),
        StaticBook("Note", "[Fake Left-arm] Tybalt Smith", "George, Here is the stuff for the stables. Please finish it in less than an elven day. \n\n- Tybalt", ""),
        StaticBook("Note 1", "Jack", "Smelting:\nThe process which turns metal ores into liquid, seperating them from pure iron and impurities, called slag. \n\nOne must use charcoal when smelting in a proper bloomery, to ensnare the pieces of slags. Coal too will work, but any other \nform of fuel will not create slag, leaving a undesired metal. ", ""),
        StaticBook("Note 1.5", "firespirit44", "Smelting \n\nOnce done, pour the liquid into a cast, and skim slag off the surface. This will ensure the iron will be as pure as possible when it comes to making steel or can be hammered straight to wrought iron.\nTo make steel, only coal and charcoal can be used once again. The carbon content from them will infuse the metal, turning it a dark, grayish color. \n\nThere is only a little bit of carbon in steel, anymore and it will become brittle and break.\n-12th of Snow Maiden's, 1337\n\nJared", ""),
        StaticBook("Note 2", "Jack", "Forging\n\nThe first use of the anvil and ring. Heat the iron or steel in the forge, once it has glowed red yellow, pull it out carefully with tongs, and quickly grab your hammer to create the shape in what you want. A longsword is roughly \n35 to 43 inches long.\n\nWhilst forging, black slag will start to come off the hot blade. And this process needs to be done repeatedly in order to clear any impurities still hidden. \n\nIf working on iron and low heat, one can make cast iron or wrought\niron, to which we derived the name blacksmith from. Black refering to the color of wrought iron. Heat to orange yellow, and hammer for 10 minutes. Repeat for 6 hours.\n-Jared\n\nEnas dont you dare burn my notes ever again or I swear to Xan he wont save you from my wrath. ", ""),
        StaticBook("Note 3", "Jack", "Tempering\n\nTempering can change the colour and hardiness of the metal. \nBlue is the lowest, followed by purple, orange, yellow, light yellow, then hottest is white. \n\nRemember to use a \nflux when tempering to protect it from the elements(air).\n\nIf anyone asks for a red sword, give them a blade made of glass.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Note 4", "Jack", "Sharpening\nit is their lake that produces the finest stones.", ""),
        StaticBook("Note for Austin", "[Masked] Davkas", "Dear Austin,\n\nI have gone away on a trip do not leave the city and let no-one in the house.\n\nTake care,\n\nDavkas\n-------------------        The Golden                           Dragon\nBrew (Carrot)\n\nFood\nPotato\n1. Note adress #\nhouses", ""),
        StaticBook("Note for the Kin", "sprintindwarf", "*The note is written in fine ink*\n\nDearest William,\n\nI would like to speak with you privately in the palace.\n\n                    -Augustus\n                        Vincrute\n\n\n\n\nhmm just got back from recovery from my smithing accident, ended up looseing my eyes and on top learn how to write blind, things will be a bit hecktic trying to learn smithing, not to mention father dosent know yet, though ferren is nice about it.\nthe new king, Forrin i belive, reconized me, though only because i couldnt talk, but it is nice that someone remembers. i hope father, dosent hate me for my burns.\n\nking started a tournament, a king and queen from the humans apparently came, they\nseem decent enough but who knows. only humans iv met have tried to kill or kidnap me. only races iv meet that seem nice are elves.\n\n[entry 3] \niv been wondering around anthos, iv came to a human settlement though im not shure \nwhat it is called or even where i am, right now im just following the scent of humans and elves to find sha, she usually hangs around humans so i should find her with them.\n\n[entry 4]\njust found another human settlement dont\nknow what it is called but im pretty shure many races have been here, i smell diffrent smells so sha might have been here. almost got robed in the same city, i guess the humans dont know restraint, or at least he smelled human, not shure what he was.\n*The writing is pressed into the paper, as if written under stress.*\nFailures abound.\nRegression.\nEnough for one day.\nWorry\nAll has been well so far, though. I'm just paranoid...\nClose Call.\nOn the plus side, the staff saved me. It is also apparently a better cleric than Mirlene or Mandru.\nFootnote.\nCalmness.\nRel, \nSecurity\nThe Mushroom\nand have fixed the glass. Maybe it will grow to a degree similar to that of Ivan. Maybe.\nDisease?\nI just hope she never catches it.\n*Written in eloquent writing*\n*The dark, stressed writing of the first day has returned.*\ntimes, and Art gone. I will need to be carefull. I kept a brotherhood of serial killers and rebels together, I can keep a few stubborn mages in line.\nFurther Worries.\nIf it isn't...\n*The writing takes on a slightly more relaxed tone*\nsupport for Polgrath was... fairly unwavering. I cannot be sure, but I have a suspicion he may have planned to kill me.\nI need to be carefull.\nCouncil.\ngiven the second mana regent seat? He cannot function as our total leader, but making him equal to Art and Nienna may both allow him to help us, and keep his followers in line.\nI certainly have the most experience...\n* The writing is light, as if written with a wounded arm. *\nI lost the spare key, but my others remain hidden in this room. I've closed the room's gate and crudely bandaged myself. I need to find Nienna. There's no telling if they will hurt her or not.\nHuwel.\nBlack Man.\nDizzy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Note from Above", "Telanir", "*the book is bound in rugged leather with thick, good-quality pages. The writing contained inside is cursive and neat, the one who wrote the book must have taken their time*\nGreetings.\n\nI am sure that you are aware of a certain problem that has arisen as of late.\nAn odd 'necromancer' of sorts seems to be on your tails, and I'm sure you are dieing to find out why.\n\nKeep reading.\nThere are numerous things that may be happening, but I am sure that these events are no coincidence.\n\nBecause the mage plagues your minds, your physical state.\nHe tries to bend your will, to earn cooperation. Interesting?\nAs of late, something that has not happened for decades, a certain cave has opened up after being sealed.\n\nThis event coincides with the beginnings of torment from the necromancer.\n\nYet the cave isn't simply a dug out rock.\nIf you are still curious... I invite you to participate in a search.\n\nA search, to discover what is going on, and more importantly, why.\n\nI cannot be sure if the fate of Anthos is concerned here... but keep on your toes.\nYou must choose five people.\n\nOnce you have chosen these five, strong, and brave participants, I will get you prepared.\n\nMake sure that you hurry, much is at stake.\n-T", ""),
        StaticBook("Note from Below", "Telanir", "Stay safe.\n\nI will handle the necromancer for now.\n\nWhen I give the signal... today, or not today, be ready.", ""),
        StaticBook("Note in Chest.", "Jistuma", "The Blue Mustache goes to one and all. He doesn't care if you are farmer or nobility, he will steal from you, and make your life like the nether. You had nothing but food in this chest, I leave you with some, but my kindness is not always like this.\n  Always Remeber\nThe Blue Mustache\n\n\n\n*A Drawing of a big Mustache, colored blue, is on the rest of the note.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Note to Delonna", "kalanthe", "Greetings Delonna.\n\nMy brothers and I ave recently arrived in the city and are wishing to establish ourselves here as we've grown tired of travelling about. We were told to speak to you insofar as to seek housing and hopefully jobs within the city.\nOur skills are varied, with myself having field profiecent alchemy skills, my borther Anameous is a historian, and my borther Adormil is an artist. Hopefully we can come to an arrangement. Currently, my brothers and I are staying at the inn. I hope to\nhear from you soon. \n\nMaehr’sae Hiylun’ehya\n\nKalanthe Aralis\nJus' sittin' in teh gate'ouse waiting for people to ye know... ask fer teh gate teh be lif'ed.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Note to Elrolas", "emberhard", "*An Albino Raven comes bareing a note and an shined brass key within its tallons*\ndruid's grove gate) it would be up the tree to your right. There's a way up behind some small trees))", ""),
        StaticBook("Note to Healer", "Random Shopkeeper", "I hope the letter reaches a healer capable of perhaps creating a medicine that may heal my boy.\n\nAt the moment he is sicken and in bed, with fever and coughing. He appears fairly weak and sleeps a lot. \nI hope that something can be done, I am oh so worried.\n\nThank you.\n\n((If you didn't realise, it's the common cold. I think a good healer could make something for it.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Note to Kaelys", "Ministry Student", "Greetings O' Kaelys-\n\nIt is with much pleasure that we announce to you the finding of a Hightower relic. Knowing you to be a possible interested party, we would like to give it to you. Our point of residing with relic in hand is the Abresi\nstables outside the Old Large Walls.\n\n- Ministry Student Aquilas", ""),
        StaticBook("Note to Mirtok", "x_Vinny_x", "  Hello Mirtok. I have matured some in the last time we met. I currently work at a farm for House Valois. I am making enough mina per week to support myself. I wrote this note to request that I hop in a Sariant training session. I will not be a-\nliability! I have my own housing and if I get injured or something you don't have to worry about that. I'm sure the people at Valois farms can fix me up. Please consider this, just training. I will be working at the farm for the Valois if you wish to \nrespond. I will be out in the fields so I will most likely get a bird if you send one.\n\nSincerely,\nVincent Olo II", ""),
        StaticBook("Note to mother", "Elerra Isttel", "Im sorry mother for whatever I said I swear I had no clue im sorry about all of this its just so hard with you and dad I just don't know what to do anymore I still love you mother. I love you. YOu never failed me I failed myself Im sorry. I Love you.\n*A picture is drawn when she was a kid of her and her mother into this page*\nRoger's Logbook~\nHow LogBook Works:\nNow it may be hard to do this while taking many orders so the best thing to do is just write:\n*It is required that you format your logbook like this or you will get 10% less of your full pay. This helps Spike log his sellings and profits, also helps receive your pay faster!*\nWeek Four Logs~:\n\nanus - butt\nass-pirate - homosexual\nasscock - idiot\nbampot - idiot\nbullshit - poop\ncock - penis\ndamn - darn\nfag - homosexual\nfuckass - idiot", ""),
        StaticBook("Note to Nienna", "Art Camoryn", "Nienna, ", ""),
        StaticBook("Notebook Vol. 2", "Zanderaw", "General Compositions for Solo Piano and Cello\n\n\n\n\nLucia de Silvarois\n*Even thicker than the first notebook, this contains a wide range of compositions. One can almost tell which mood Lucia was in when she wrote them: in some parts the notes are thickly written and sharp, while in others they seem to flow across the page.\nThe margins are in many places once again filled with general notes to herself, and even the occasional poem in Auvergnian, most of which are mediocre at best: simply ways for the author to release stress and think. It's clear that none of this was\nintended to be shown to others.\n\nAround the halfway point in the notebook marks when she got her hands on a cello, for these pages are suddenly filled with experimentation with the instrument, mixed in with further piano.*\n((More Bach! Hope you aren't completely over it by now. This one corresponds to both the second book of \"Well Tempered Clavier\" and his solo suites for cello, the first of which in particular is excellent.))\n\nSun's Smile\nsiblings are doing. ", ""),
        StaticBook("Notebook: Vol 1", "Zanderaw", "General Compositions for Solo Piano\n\nVolume 1\n\n\n\nLucia de Silvarois\n*This book is unusually thick. It is a binding together of many pages which are almost universally slightly crumpled from being handled often. Each page is filled to the brim with musical notes, corrections, and the occasional bit of handwriting, not just\nin the common tongue but sometimes in Auvergnian as well. If played, the music is highly variable as far as tempo and tone, but is generally orderly and comforting.*\n\n((This is a large collection of hundreds of pages of Lucia's own compositions,\nwritten alone in her free time. This particular book would correspond to book 1 of Bach's \"Well Tempered Clavier.\" I highly recommend listening to the first two pieces, if only to get a feel for what the music is like.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Notes", "Patriotic_Fool", "My Personal Notes==\n\nTo begin, I will have to identify what I am aware of currently. Given various negative events in my past, combined with a possible mental disorder that I have been afflicted with for an unknown amount of time, an alternate\npersonality was created. This personality was either a manifestation of my actual nature, or a byproduct, partition of the mind so to speak. \n\nRegardless, this alternate self had a few interesting characteristics. Firstly, he was\nextremely intelligent, crafty, and calculating. He seemed to operate on a higher level of thinking than I was previously, and could allocate memories and actions in a mechanical way. I find it extremely intriguing, almost fascinating in a way.\n\n\nThis inherent craftiness was offset by a primal urge that overcame him. He needed to feel pain, perhaps even inflict it upon others. From what I recall, it was one of the few ways he found entertainment. This was an almost 'animalistic'\ndesire, a stark\ncontrast to the cunning, cold persona he would sport most of the time.\n\nAdditionally, the worst obstacle he faced was 'boredom'. He did many things to occupy himself, including games, some.. unsavory sexual activity, even allowing himself to be \ntortured.\n\nAfter I recovered, I believe that the alternate personality was never 'destroyed'. Whatever it was, it simply merged with me and became a part of me, which is a problem in itself. I do not know whether I am the person who I was\nbefore. Perhaps both.\n\nAn interesting observation I have made is that I can use the skills and mindset of the alternate personality at will, if I simply concentrate on it. For example, everything I have written here has been done so using help\nfrom the calculating, logical side. I have noticed that I can read at an alarmingly fast rate and process things very fast, as well as do mathematics and similar activies with ease. \n\nA drawback is that I still feel the urges that the alternate\npersonality felt. I have tried various things to stifle the urges. Alcohol did nothing, nor did various herbs. Poison had no noticable effect either, aside from almost killing me. There's only two things that have seemed to help. The first is doing things\nthat the other personality indulged in, such as getting tortured, cut, or other such mutilations. \n\nWhile not the most pleasant of activites, it at least helps. Another thing I have noticed is that doing things I liked to do before helps as well.\nBeing around Aenor and Isabella especially, it seems to relieve alot of tension, even if we talk about serious matters. That is all that seems to be discussed nowadays.   ", ""),
        StaticBook("Notes on Alchemy", "Triplewing", "--Notes on Alchemy--\n-------------------\n         IIIIIIIII\n           II II\n           II II\n          II   II\n          II   II\n         II     II\n        II       II\n        II       II\n       II         II\n        IIIIIIIIIII\n     -Ein  Sarard-\nDistilling water is one of the most simple tasks in alchemy, but quite trivial in the end,\nunless you know what to do with it.\n\nFirstly, you must set\nup the alembic. You are to put /coal/ under the minor vessel, connected to the major by a tube.\nThen you must add some /water/ in the minor vessel, and heat the coal under it. As it heats up, water will vaporize, and it will turn to vapor, and eventually slide down the tube into the major vessel, thus producing distilled water, pure and drinkable.\n            [!]\nA well-drawn picture of an alembic is here, seemingly random arrows show where to put water, and where to put coal. The whole explanation simplified in the picture.\n-------------------\nBrewing a potion requires patience, as everything might not go as planned. The brew might become thin, it might be smooth.. but it needs to be just right for an effect.\n\nThe simplest potion one can brew needs only a single ingredient; Tippen's Root.\nAs starting with a fresh and clean set is obvious, you should consider starting by grinding some Tippen's Root in your mortar & pestle, the finer, the better. Make sure you don't eat any Tippen's Root raw though, the effects aren't good.\nAfter grinding, \nthe root, you must toss it into boiling water. It will dissolve in the water, producing a smooth, a bit jelly-like liquid as you let it stand there for some minutes. Eventually, you are to pour it into vials, and then wave the vials around a bit, as the \nsemi-transparent liquid is quite hot. You\ncan use this as an ointment for a rash or a minor wound. It's good for keeping your teeth shiny aswell.\n-------------------             [!]\n    A small illustration\n    of Tippen's root is\n    on the bottom.\n-------------------It's fairly easy to make something else from the same ingredient; if you were to boil the Tippen's Root until it dissolved in the brew, you would make a different brew\naltogether.\n\nThe potion that is the outcome from water\nmixed with Tippen's Root makes a potion that's almost blinding to look at. This potion, however, isn't used for making your teeth literally shiny, but makes you drowsy. It can therefore be used as a sleeping draught.\n\n-------------------\n       IIIIIIIIIIIIII\n     IIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIII\n    III    IIIIII    III\n    II      IIII      II\n     II    IIIIII    II\n      IIIIII II IIIIII\n    II IIII IIII IIII II\n     II IIIIIIIIIIII II\n      II III II III II\n        II II  II II\n         IIIIIIIIII\n            [!]\nThe page has a big illustration of a skull, titled \"WARNING\" just below.\n------------------- The following brew is\nnot a potion, but has a harmful effect instead.\nBe careful not to drink it or try to pull any unwise stunt with it.\nThis is most likely the most simple poison one can make. As all you must do is grind some spider eyes into a.. purple mush and then add it into the water in your alembic. Then you are to heat the minor vessel, distilling it into a poison in the major.\nYou know you have succeeded, if you can see small roots slowly\ngrowing out of the brew. Then you simply change it to a better vial or a bottle, be careful though, not to\nget into touch with the poison, as the roots will keep growing even if digested..\n\n            [!]\nPicture of some roots\ngrowing inside a bottle\nis illustrated here.\nBeside the picture, is another illustration; it seems to be the same bottle, but the roots are a bit bigger.\n-------------------\nThe following potion on the other hand has both good, and bad effects. This potion is great for heavy workers, as it gives you a slight advantage\nwhen mining or chopping wood and the\nlike..\n\nTo make this potion, you must first find\nsome Swamp Blossom.\nThis is quite a trivial task, but it's a bit harder to find.. I still wouldn't call it rare though. When you have the swamp blossom, you must cut it up to small pieces instead of grinding it. You need the juices of the swamp, you know?\n..Then, you just add them in to the alembic\njust like with the purple mush and wait for it to vaporize in the major vessel for use. You can feel the energy of the potion if you have done it correctly, as the whole bottle should be shaking.\n\n            [!]\nThere's an illustration\nof a vial here, some \nrandom lines about as to depict its shaking.\n-------------------\n  / IIII\n /   II  \\\n \\  IIII /\n    II II\n   IIIIIII /\n  \\        \\\n  /\n-------------------     End of Volume I\n-------------------  23rd of Amber Cold\n          1453\n-------------------        Ein Sarard\n-------------------Afterwords: \n     Alchemy has really\n     been a blast for\n     me, special mention\n     for Nithradien", ""),
        StaticBook("Notes on Blah", "Aspirant Fevyyr", "Notes on the Orcish language, the 'Blah'.\n\nWritten by Aspirant Fevyyr.\nOrcs, due to their tusks, are unable to speak perfectly common, so they have made their own little language. It mostly consists of mispronouncations of normal words, but there are a few custom words.\nUg - Greeting, hello\n\nThrom'ka - Formal, honorific greeting\n\nYub - Yes\n\nNub - No\n\nHosh - Good, one can add 'bub' infront of it to create 'super good', or \none can add 'nub' to it, to create bad or not good.\n\nLat - You, lats is plural\n\nMi - I/Me\n\nRulg - Thanks\n\nBlah - Speak, also used as the name\nfor the Orcish language\n\nGruk - Understand\n\nSkah - Insult\n\nDabu - Honorific form for 'yes'.\n\nAgh - And\n\n\nThis is as much as Fevyyr could understand of their speech that were clearly distinct words. There is probaply a lot more, but Fevyyr shall find that out another day.\nIm going to find him. Im going to do to him what he did to me. Ill be careful", ""),
        StaticBook("Notes on F.H.T.", "Athri", "Fi'hiiran'seth the void based sub-division of Fi'hiiran'tanya has two spell procedures.\n1: Direct Spell Re-direction.\nStep 1: Focus on the spell and clear your mind of all distractions and thoughts. \n2: Re-directing spells full circles.\nStep 1: Focus on the caster and clear your mind.\nCurrent realm origin: Caster", ""),
        StaticBook("Notes: Malinor", "picklesickel", "\"New\" Malinor was created recently. On my travels there I have seen a sprawling new town. \"Old\" Malinor appears to have been abandoned because of some sort of taint. The town is small but is growing quite rapidly. It is located very close to the...\n\nHigh Elven city. In between them is a sprawling coast which is being converted into a dock for ships going in and out of new Malinor. In the middle of the coast is a small island where a strange red crystal lays completely desimated.\nMalinors guard force appears to be missing. People are attacked in the street daily however little to no help ever comes.", ""),
