        StaticBook("Odd Events C1", "Sofetios Jayamen", "       Odd Events\n\nA Fictional book series with a bit of Horror\n\n           ~By Sofetios\n                Jayamen\nPrologue\n\nMy name is James Geedin. My family recently settled in a new land without a name, so I call it Genway.  We were lucky enough to stumble upon an old house. \nWhoever built it, I don’t know. Some odd stuff seems to happen here, but I’m determined to stay at my new home. This is my story.\n      Chapter One\n        The Light\n\nI woke up in the middle of the night with chills running down my spine. I was around 13 at the time. I went downstairs to get something to drink. \n That’s when I noticed it. I looked out the window and noticed a light in the distance at the woods. Though it wasn’t yellow like a fire, it was white. I thought about checking it out, but decided I should go to bed instead.\nThe next day in the morning, I went downstairs to have breakfast, but the thing was, my parents weren’t awake. That was unusual, so I went upstairs to their room and knocked on the door. \nWhen I knocked on the door it simply opened slowly from the force of my knock. I looked in, but no one was there. I spent the rest of the day looking for them, but to no avail. \nSoon it became nighttime and I was in the kitchen. That’s when I noticed it again, the same light as before. This time I went out towards the light. I came to the forest clearing where the light was coming from.\nThere was a small mirror in the center, angled towards my house. Then I noticed something, the white light wasn’t coming from the mirror, It was coming from the attic window of my house being reflected by the mirror. \nI saw a word carved into the mirror. It said “Truth”. I looked back towards the house. Could my parents be were that light is? I took the mirror and made my way back the house. \nI got to the house and made my way upstairs to look for a way up into the attic. I looked different places until I got to my parents room. I walked in and there was a small white light coming from the bookcase in there, going around the books. \nI walked up to the bookcase and looked through the cracks between the books. There was a white stairway that lead upwards.  I shifted the bookcase over and started walking up the white stairs. Until I got to a white trapdoor above me.\n cautiously, I lifted it up a crack and looked in the attic room.  There were two statues that looked just like…  I then opened the trapdoor fully and rushed into the white room towards the two statues. \n They were exact replicas of my parent, but they had faces looked like they were scared of something. Suddenly there was the sound of the trapdoor shutting behind me. \nI looked back to see something in white robes that covered its whole body and a light coming from under its hood. \n\n“Who are you?” I said scared. It simply stood there. I looked back towards my parents for a second and back again.  \n Then it was right in front of me. Startled I fell back and the mirror dropped on the floor face up but didn’t break. I got up and backed up. It didn’t move. \n Then I noticed something. In the reflection on the mirror on the ground, where the thing was supposed to be was a person. The person in the reflection had light coming from its eyes. \nI took out my short sword. Getting ready to fight whatever this was. I lunged at its chest, but as it made contact with the light coming fromit, the blade turned white. I dropped my sword from it happening. \nI was about to panic when I remembered the mirror, then got an idea. Keeping my eyes on the person, I picked up the mirror, careful not to get in the light. \nThen with one hand, I slid it under the light coming from the person’s hood, trying to aim it back at it. Suddenly the light coming from under the hood disappeared. Then the person in the robes simply fell over, solid as a stone. \nI turned to the statues of my parents. I wasn’t sure what to do. I talked, I yelled, but there was no response. I had never felt so alone before. My parents turned into stone, not knowing how to turn them back to normal. \nBut then that made me realize something. Something I should have thought from the start. \n\nWho had left the mirror in the woods?\n\nEnd of Chapter One\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this! I'll be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing send me a bird or tell me in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("Odd Events C2", "Sofetios Jayamen", "        Odd Events\n\nA fictional book series with a bit of horror\n\n          ~By Sofetios\n                Jayamen\n      Chapter Two\n        The Music\n\nI stayed awake for two days, fearing to go to sleep in case something else like that person with the light coming from their eyes was here. What was I going to do? \nMy parents turned to stone and I had no Idea of how to turn them back. It was starting to turn to night again. I went to my parents room and sat down on the bed. \nhough when I sat down, I sat on something that felt like paper. I jumped back off the bed and looked where I had sat. There was an Envelope. Carefully I took the envelope off the bed and opened it. Inside was... A key. \nI examined the key and noticed four letters. They read B. E. D. A. I was more then tired, I was exausted. I simply sat down and stared at the staircase with the key and the mirror in my hands, not sure what to expect.\nI felt my head dropping but caught myself. I couldn't let myself fall asleep now, not when things like the thing in the attic might exist.\nMy head was drooping again and I was about to give in to sleep when I heard something. The slight tinkling of what sounded like a piano. \nThat was odd, I had examined everywhere in the house in the last three days looking for any rooms like the attic, and found no piano in any of them.\nCarefully, I got off the bed and out into the hallway, the mirrors face pointed outward from me in my hands. O followed the sound until I got to the end of the hallway. The music was four notes playing continuously in a pattern. \nThe music was coming from the wall, yet there was no door. Confused, I looked to the mirror. It had shown me things that weren't there before, maybe it would work again. I turned away from the wall and put the mirror face facing me.\nIn the reflection I saw myself, but I also saw a door behind me that wasn't there when I looked before. I turned around and jumped back. There was now a door right where the music was coming from.\nCarefully I turned the knob, but it seemed to be stuck, or... Locked. I looked down to the key in my other hand and tried fitting it into the keyhole. It fit, so I turned it, and right as it clicked, the music stopped. \nI froze. Did whatever was in there now know I was there? I slowly took the key out and put it in my pocket. Then Held the mirror in front of me with one hand and opened the door with my other one. \nIn the room was a piano and some music sheets on the floor. I didn't see anyone or anything else in the room though.\nI slowly walked up to the piano. I saw that it had the names of the white keys imbedded into them. I hesitated, then played C, D, E, F, G, A, B, then C again. \nNothing seemed to happen.  I began to think coming here was a bad idea, so I turned and went to the door. I twisted the handle, but it was locked again. So I quickly took out the key and was about to put it in the lock, when I noticed the letters again. \nB. E. D. A... I went back to the piano and played the same notes, B. E. D. A. nothing again seemed to happen, But then the keys I just played repeated themselves without me touching them. \nIt started getting faster, faster, and louder. Suddenly I felt a strong breeze, but there was no window. The sheets blew off the ground and started swirling around me. I looked to the door but it wasn't there anymore.\nThe sound was now deafening. I yelled for help and then... I woke up.\nI sat straight up in my parents bed, holding the mirror. I walked over to the place in the hallway where the door was supposed to be and looked in the mirror to see if the door would appear, but it didnt.\nI walked back to my parents room and sat on the bed, sunlight coming in through the window. But as I sat down, I felt something small and lumpy under me.\nI sat up and there was a key, with the letters B. E. D. A. on it.\n\nEnd of Chapter Two\n\n“Fear mainly occurs in the absence of knowledge.” ~Sofetios Jayamen\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I'll be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know in person or by bird!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Odd Events V.I", "Elwin", "A blue haired elf, whose name is unknown stands with a figure clad in black. The two chat nonchalantly of death, lack of feeling, and the horrors of simply existing. They seem to have some in common, and yet... they remain still far apart in personality. \n\"I cannot help you sir, or you cannot help me?\" the blue haired elf asks, a female looking to be in her twenties, if one would compare to a human.\n\"I lack the answer for.\"\n\"At least you are not so anxious anymore.\"\nHe hesitates.\nHer ears flick and turn red, her voice sounding hasty. \"I should... I should go... I should leave you b-\" \nback then?\" he asks.\nand he looks slightly hurt. \"I made everyone think that... including the ones I needed...\" he says with a defeated tone.\nHe adjusts the straps on his right gauntlet unconsciously, and her ears wilt a bit.\nwords tasted like... having been away from civilization for so long...\"\nare there?\"\nme, and he is long gone... immortal, he is.\"\n\"I can't die, by principle.\" he says.\n\"Yet, if one elf dies,\" he says, \"plenty more will remain, and live on.\"\n\"Vanish, but not be forgotten.\" she responds. \"Mourned over greatly, but remembered with pride... with justice... with light... honor...\" she pauses. \"With wyn.\"\n\"But existed and will never be forgotten.\" she says.\n\"Then you will have cursed me for as long as you live.\"\nI perish... I will be bound to this realm by a chain of memory.\"\n\"... As long as you wish it.\"\n\"Precisely... but it wouldn't be just you... those who've walked out of the inn earlier... those who are present now... they'd all have to die as well.\"\nevents... so many would have to die... I am now more trapped than I ever was...\"\n\"It is the inevitable.\" she almost hisses, \"Does it show you nothing that I face it without fear for you?\"\n\"Because... because I still heard them... and I still taste wyn...\"\nguidelines in this 'twisted' dream that has started since I saw you... dare I follow anything else... I would stop dreaming.\"\nweakly, breaking the silence.", ""),
        StaticBook("Odds and Ends", "Ko'Da'Ri", "Store Prices\n------------------------1. Minerals\n2. Earthly Materials\n3. Maps\n4. Cloth\n5. Food\n6. Wood\n7. Instruments\n8. Staffs\n9. Special Requests\n10. Other\nMinerals\nIron = 20 Minas\nChain Mail Link = 3 Minas\nGold = 30 Minas\nGold Nugget = 4 Minas\nRedstone = 15 Minas\nDiamond = 250 Minas\nLapis Lazuli = 25 Minas\nFlint = 5 Minas\nEnder Pearl = 300 Minas\nEarthly Materials\nStone = 50 Minas\nCobble Stone = 30 Minas\nStone Bricks = 40 Minas\nStone Bricks* = 45 Minas\nNetherrack = 50 Minas\nSand = 40 Minas\nDirt = 10 Minas\nCoal = 3 Minas\nCharcoal = 2 Minas\n(Per stack, except Coal & Charcoal)\nMaps\nCustom Map = 25 Minas\n+ distance in meters*0.5\nMap = 25 Minas\n\nCloth\nWhite = 100 Minas\nDyed = 175 Minas\n\n(Per stack)\nFood\nBread = 5 Minas\nCarrots = 3 Minas\nPotatoes = 3 Minas\nCooked Potatoe = 10 Minas\nApple = 3 Minas\nCheese = 10 Minas\nCake = 15 Minas\nSoup = 8 Minas\nMeat = 9 Minas\nSpices = 4 Minas\nTea = 20 Minas\nWood\nLogs = 50/Stack\nPlanks = 13 Minas/Stack\nSigns = 5 Minas\nFence Posts = 5 Minas\nDoor = 10 Minas + extra for installation\nChest = 5 Minas\nTable = 3 Minas\nInstruments\nString = 50 Minas\nAir = 40 Minas\n\nDesigns = 25 Minas-100 Minas\nStaffs\nBasic Wood Staff = 50 Minas\nCarvings = 25 Minas\nIron Decor = 50 Minas\nDiamond Decor = 250 Minas\nGold Decor = 125 Minas\n\nSpecial Requests\n\nDifficulty = 10 Minas-500 Minas\nMaterials = 10 Minas-1000 Minas\nTime Frame =  Free for no time limit\n1 Day Need= 100 Minas\n1 Month Need = 20 Minas\n\nOther\nAncient Artifacts = 200 Minas\nBooks = 10 Minas\nWriting Materials = 5 Minas\nOdd Objects = 10-500 Minas\nMisc. = Judge Based on object and your best judgement.", ""),
        StaticBook("Official Pardon", "Italian_Assassin", "The wielder of this may be granted ONE free pass from arrest of the following crimes:\n\n1) Theft of no more than 500 Minas\n2) Assault\n3) Arson of no more than 500 Minas\n4) Public Drunkeness\n5) Public Urination\n6) Impersonation", ""),
        StaticBook("Okar Contracts", "Teerz", "Okar Magic\nOh today do I have a tale to please the eyes!  Oh yes!  I shall inform you of the studies I did of a Woman and her Okar, it was delightful!\nbut eventually that wasn't enough, Tulatha found the book on Okars and decided to do a ritual.  Since she was already a mage she was able to do this!  No non mages where able to use this magic.  Isn't that amazing?\nnormally, she had Lan fetch a live wolf and skin it.  A dead wolf skinned just didn't do anything.  After the skin was tanned it was carved deeply with a sybool, using a dull bone.\nAfter that Tulatha had to mix her blood and Lan's as well as keeping a bowl of his and hers seperate.  \nA Bond of Lovers \nA bond of Friends\nThe bond Transfer.\nThe symbol must be writen in the blood of both the Okar and the Mage.  Once this is done Tulatha channeled her mana into it and passed out.\nAfter Effects.  \nspeed, and smell increased alot.  \nthings.  One can not bond more than one Okar.\nIf one or the other dies the other always feels it, and tends to go crazy till they are brought back....if they are brought back.", ""),
        StaticBook("Okars", "Teerz", "Okar Magic\n\n\nWriten by Tulatha\nA note to everyone, what I have written in here is documentation of what I went through.\n\n*A scribbled message lays here*  \n\nDo not read this....It wasn't worth it.\nMy name is Tulatha, I am a mage from the mage wars, long before even the creator was a popular religion, and what I found today was amazing, it was a tome on a type of magic.  I will attempt this magic with my beloved husband.  The following will be what \nwe have to go through.\n\nWish us both luck!\nIn this tomb we found there were several strange symbols\n\n*Symbols are drawn along with a circle*\n\nHowever the instructions go we must use a wolf pelt...however WE must skin it alive, it is the only way.  \nWe had the idea of trying to do it with a dead wolf, however nothing happened, it seems to do this we must follow exactly.\n\nWe had to mix our blood, and create the circle, once that was done we both signed our names in our own blood.  Then with the \nblood mixed we had to create our symbol, we choose love as it suits us.  \n\nAfter I channeled my energy into the parchement i collapsed, it seems to have been a great strain, but now my lover can sense me....its amazing!\nIt actually worked, my friends tried it, each used a different symbol, however they where never able to bond  more than one.  Lucy tried to bond Philip to another person, and it worked as well!  However she was depressed afterwords....maybe it was a bad\nidea, however she cheered up when she got a new okar.\n*A new entry is a few months later*  \n\nMy husband went insane....he kept keeping me behind him in fights, however I am a strong firemage, why would he try to protect me?  He can't seem to sense where I am however it doesn't matter, he still knows\nthat I'm alive.  We'll do a few tests later.\n*A later date*\n\nThis magic is a curse...he died...he killed himself!  Where did I put the tea....\n\nI need to find the tea, I will return to writing this later...however I will state....what did I want to write I don't know.  I should sleep.\n*A few months later is a new entry*\n\nTo those who try this magic, be ware....it is dangerous.  Much more dangerous than any thought.", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Adunian V.1", "Jistuma", "   -Ancient Adunian-\n\n           OOC:\nThis is an IC book teaching the reader how to read and speak the Ancient Adunian tongue. The book only teaches the very basics: Nouns, verbs, sentence structure and the like. The book\n\nlacks information on descriptive words and some adjectives. For a character to learn what this book offers would take 6-12 months as it is a complicated language. ((That’s 1-2 RL weeks))\n\nActually typing in Adunian is simple. You go into\nGoogle Translate and select Irish. You simply type in what you want to say, and copy-paste the translation into MC text. It’s courtesy to also put the English translation in OOC, making it easier for others to RP.\n\nHave fun learning Adunian!~\n            IC:\n\nWritten by Monk Argyll\n          ~=~\n      *200 pages\n       of writing\n       on Adunian\n       is here*\n\nOld Adunian V.1\n\nWritten by Monk Argyll\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerHaven\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Adunian V.1", "Rosso", "   -Ancient Adunian-\n\n           OOC:\nThis is an IC book teaching the reader how to read and speak the Ancient Adunian tongue. The book only teaches the very basics: Nouns, verbs, sentence structure and the like. The book\n\nlacks information on descriptive words and some adjectives. For a character to learn what this book offers would take 6-12 months as it is a complicated language. ((That’s 1-2 RL weeks))\n\nActually typing in Adunian is simple. You go into\nGoogle Translate and select Irish. You simply type in what you want to say, and copy-paste the translation into MC text. It’s courtesy to also put the English translation in OOC, making it easier for others to RP.\n\nHave fun learning Adunian!~\n            IC:\n\nWritten by Monk Argyll\n          ~=~\n      *200 pages\n       of writing\n       on Adunian\n       is here*\n\nOld Adunian V.1\n\nWritten by Monk Argyll\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerHaven\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Adunian Vol1", "SortedJarhead", "   -Ancient Adunian-\n\n            OOC:\n\nThis is an IC book teaching the reader how to read and speak the Ancient Adunian tounge. The book only teaches the very basics: Nouns, verbs, sentance structure and the like. The book\nlacks information on descriptive words and some adjectives. For a character to learn what this book offers would take 6-12 months as it is a complicated language. ((That's 1-2 RL weeks))\n\nActualy typing in Adunian is simple. You go into\nGoogle Translate and select Irish. You simply type in what you want to say, and copy-paste the translation into MC text. It's courtesy to also put the English translation in OOC, making it easier for others to RP.\n\nHave fun learning Adunian!~\n            IC:\n\nWritten by Monk Argyll             ~=~\n     *200 pages \n      of writing\n      on Adunian\n      is here*\nJob Name: \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Book", "arockstar28", "-As you begin to read the book, an enigmatic force begins to trap you, making you unable to move until you put the book down.-\ntongue, some sharp, some smooth, some rough.  Dragon tongue is not usually used for recipes for cooking, or for alchemy. \ninside the core. Some have no soul, but are electrically bound.\nbring people back to llife. This is a weird force that barely any magic could do.\nto actually make a spell. The connecting of the void is not simple, nor hard. You empty your mind and you study it. This takes a while for you to do so. \nAnthos:\n\n\n\n-The water seems to have not gotten to this page-\ntowns were burned down. Few people are here, but they have all died.  They got...the disease...\nup by the people from the new land. Two other people are on this land, as I saw them. I have no one to talk to. -The rest of the page is torn-\n-A bear seems to have clawed this page out.-", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Diary", "laurannex", "I have traveled to the northern lands of Oren in a region known as \"Hanseti\".  Most people of these lands eschew the arcane of all sorts but this region seems different.  Not different in a way that they may be more accepting. But different in that there \nmay be less watchful eyes.  \nMoving on,  There is a large estate here, it seems larglely unoccupuied.  I detected a very strong arcane power emminating from the mountain it sits on.  Looking about the estate I found a large Library, I will wish to \ngain access to it at some point.\n---------------------\nEntry 2\nI have settled myself into my new abode.  It seems a race of halflings live south of here.  \nToday a bird addressed to a man named \"Saul\" came to \nme. I do not know for what purpose.\n\nI shall make my first foray into town to track down signs of misuse.\n--------------\nI made a trip to the region known as Salvus and its capital.  There I made contact with a woman who \nturned out to be more useful than expected.\n\nI will hear from her further.\n=================", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Journal", "Jistuma", "I did not know what it was, I did not know what it wanted...\n\nThe sounds, the whispers, they overcame my head, I shouldn't have followed them... Why did I follow them...\n\nIt became dark, it wasn't suppose to be dark... I couldn't see far, like black mist covering my eyes... It spoke from nearby, I couldn't trace from where... When I turned my head it was already on my back...\n\nI fell to the screech, that awful screech! I couldn't bare it, my ears felt like bleeding... I covered my ears I couldn't hear the forest anymore, but the whispers... they wouldn't stop... they were all around me...\nI closed my eyes, I didn't want to see... I wanted to leave I was on my knees praying for salvation... I don't know how it happened, I could start to see him with my eyes closed...\nI remembered my wife, I was finding safety in her thoughts... She appeared to me with a smile, I didn't know how she got next to me, I fell to it's tricks... I hugged her tightly, I felt blood on her back... I heard her scream, that awful screech...\nMy son, please not my son... I tried running I triped... I looked back to the corpse of my son... I couldn't deal with it's hollow eyes as the screech had come...\nI couldn't move... my body couldn't stop shaking... A dark voice spoke, full of anger... It asked if I feared, it asked if I regreeted stealing from them... I didn't know, I didn't steal anything...\nMy cries were met only in pain through my body, I couldn't do anything...\n\nI don't want to see them... I don't want to be near them... I felt cold... so cold...\n\n\nThey have me... my lord they have me... I don't know what to do... those beings...\n\nThey were like boars... dead boars... Parts of armor were inside them... they shouldn't be alive... Why did I travel alone, I shouldn't have ran away...\nThey were many, they took me to the north... They didn't find my book... I can hear the screams of more... I don't know what they are doing... why did they take us... why would they want us...\nWe're going to die, I don't want to die... I saw it... I saw the one they took from this cage... He's back... He's burnt... his armor has melted inside him... Why is he smiling... why!?\nThey're coming for me,\n\n\n     NO\n\n               Save me\n\n\n\n        Help\n\n\n\n\n\n                  HELP", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Paper", "Gwindor Twiele", "Hints for the puzzecubes:\n\nIron: You have attained my secret already!\nGold: Those who fly eventually fear these,\nEmerald: Each face needs one of each symbol!\nRuby: Sail away\nDiamond: Complex, Like one of these___\nPearl:\nIf you make it to this one, Good LUCK.\n19th of the Amber Cold, 1444.\neveryone's sake.  I truly wished that something could have happened but it is clear now that I have always been wishing and not once has a wish been truly granted.  I thought life could have more to it, but as a man told me while I was defending my friend\nLife is about survival.\nwelding:\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Record Book", "PandaC0mmander", "Expenses\n--------\n\n+30 mina, 1 Iron.\n+60 mina, 2 Iron.\n-130 mina, 41 Books.\n+140 mina, 5 Iron.\n+Mined, 28 Iron.\n+Mined, 11 Iron.\n+Mined, 16 Coal.\n-Used, 8 Coal.\n-Used, 1 Iron.\n+Mined, 2 Iron.\n+Mined, 11 Iron.\n-Used, 3 Iron.\n+120 minas, Hatchet.\n (Ask Igni for minas)\n-Used, 2 Iron.\n+1,200 minas, 40 iron\n (Ask Igni for minas)\n-Sold, 40 iron.\n-Bought, 7 iron , 140.\n-Bought, 7 iron, 127.75.\n-Bought, 1 iron, 15\n+60 mina, sold 2 Iron.\n+120 mina, Cane blade.\n+500 mina, Rings\n+70 mina, Halberd\n+60 mina, chest piece\n+60 mina, iron hoe.\n+120 mina, chain armor\n+60 mina, iron sword\n-2 iron, iron sword", ""),
        StaticBook("Omgnuh", "[Bruised][Facial Burn] Erin", "The one who threw the flaming rags is here.\n\nWhat do I do?", ""),
        StaticBook("On Mali'Aheral", "Rosso", "The Mali’Aheral, the blessed elves. Or as others call them: High elves.\n\nThis elven people is one of the most hated by their own race. People see them as racists and don’t think they’ll do any good. They kill members of their own race, for\nthey are ‘impure’. However is this true?\n\nI say not.\n\nThe culture of the Mali’Aheral goes back to a specific elf known as Larihei lomahnih. She was one of elven kind who bathed in water that contained enchanted golden\nParticles, which had changed their appearance. Her elven kind had a paler skin and longer ears than the other elven kinds. They were also taller and their hair had become fiarer. \nThe change that these particles had made to them also was psychological,\nthese early Mali’aheral had shifted away from their original beliefs and thought more logical.\nThey became scolars, one of which was Larihei.\nAs a child of her kin she learned their traditions and ideals. And soon she appeared to be a\nmaster in all subjects a Mali’Aheral was expected to learn. She grew up to become the leader of the Mali’Aheral and to be their support in the council of princes in Malinor.\nHowever she promoted the Mali’Aheral’s believes in the council: That elves were\nthe superior race of Aegis and that they should also rule the other races.\nHowever the other princes and princesses said that she was only promoting war and was a danger to the elves. Larihei was banished from Malinor.\nHalf of the Mali’Aheral followed Larihei when she went to find a new home for their race. The other half remained with Malinor, slowly losing their culture.\nHowever when those high elves found the ruins of their kin in Asulon, the old culture was revived.\nMaehr’sae Hiylun’ehya That is the core of the Mali’Aheral culture. It can be translated as “Progress and Heath”.\nBreaking that sentence down, you can split it up in two parts: Maehr’sae, or Progress and Hiylun’ehya, or Heath. Maehr’sae refers to\nthe development of knowledge and the value of it. It is the base of the position of science in their society, as scientist stand in a high position die to their ability to recover truth and knowledge.\nHiylun’ehya stands for the heath and purity of the\nMali’Aheral race. They wish to keep their race from mixing blood, because they believe that their body is the perfect design. A Mali’Aheral is not to ruin his body, he shall not damage it in any way.This means that he or she will not tattoo nor scar their\nBody out of free will. They are also not to mix blood with other races, because they produce children who are not ‘perfect’ anymore. This includes intimate contact with other races, because they would risk creating a ‘failure’, a child of mixed blood.\nAnother important part of their culture is that they believe to be superior to other races, die to them able to think clear because they do not follow any god.\nThey frown down upon the religions of other races, however they respect those who show to be\nwise and able to think logical.\n\nCombat is another thing that is frowned down upon, as it is an action that does not require thinking and will only cause the loss of people. That last one is very important: The Mali’Aheral are, of\ncourse also subject to the curse of Malin’s children, therefor all lives are valued high and loss of one is a waste. It is therefore also expected of all Mali’Aheral to create children at some point in their life.\n\nThe Mali’Aheral frown down upon those of\nmixed blood, they moght discriminate them, they are not violent however.\nTheir only violent people are the sillumir, the mourning blades, they are the Mali who give their sacrifice to the race by taking up the sword. Their name comes from the need\nfor them to fight, a sad thing to do in their society. They are respected for their sacrifice and remain few in number, due to the morals of their race.\nA Mali’Aheral does not fight unless necessary\n\nI hope this has\nenlighted you about the Mali’Aheral.\nThink about this next time you see them, and try to understand their actions.\n\nMaehr’sae Hiylin’eyha\n\n -Vallel’Yuln Aeléyèlsa\n\nOn Mali’Aheral\n\nWritten by Vallel’Yuln\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerHaven\n", ""),
        StaticBook("On Mali'Aheral", "Jistuma", "\nThis elven people is one of the most hated by their own race. People see them as racists and don’t think they’ll do any good. They kill members of their own race, for they are ‘impure’. However is this true?\nI say not.\nParticles, which had changed their appearance. Her elven kind had a paler skin and longer ears than the other elven kinds. They were also taller and their hair had become fiarer.\nThe change that these particles had made to them also was psychological, these early Mali’aheral had shifted away from their original beliefs and thought more logical.\nThey became scolars, one of which was Larihei.\nthe leader  of the Mali’Aheral and to be their support in the council of princes in Malinor. However she promoted the Mali’Aheral’s believes in the council: That elves were the superior race of Aegis and that they should also rule the other races.\nHowever the other princes and princesses said that she was only promoting war and was a danger to the elves. Larihei was banished from Malinor.\nHalf of the Mali’Aheral followed Larihei when she went to find a new home for their race. The other half remained with Malinor, slowly losing their culture. However when those high elves found the ruins of their kin in Asulon, the old culture was revived.\nMaehr’sae Hiylun’ehya That is the core of the Mali’Aheral culture. It can be translated as “Progress and Heath”.\nMaehr’sae refers to the development of knowledge and the value of it. It is the base of the position of science in their society, as scientist stand in a high position die to their ability to recover truth and knowledge.\nHiylun’ehya stands for the heath and purity of the Mali’Aheral race. They wish to keep their race from mixing blood, because they believe that their body is the perfect design. A Mali’Aheral is not to ruin his body, he shall not damage it in any way.\nThis means that he or she will not tattoo nor scar their Body out of free will. They are also not to mix blood with other races, because they produce children who are not ‘perfect’ anymore. This includes intimate contact with other races, because they\nthey would risk creating a ‘failure’, a child of mixed blood.\nThey frown down upon the religions of other races, however they respect those who show to be wise and able to think logical.\nCombat is another thing that is frowned down upon, as it is an action that does not require thinking and will only cause the loss of people. That last one is very important: The Mali’Aheral are, of course also subject to the curse of Malin's children,\ntherefor all lives are valued high and loss of one is a waste. It is therefore also expected of all Mali’Aheral to create children at some point in their life.\nThe Mali’Aheral frown down upon those of mixed blood, they moght discriminate them, they are not violent however. Their only violent people are the sillumir, the mourning blades, they are the Mali who give their sacrifice to the race by taking up the\nsword. Their name comes from the need for them to fight, a sad thing to do in their society. They are respected for their sacrifice and remain few in number, due to the morals of their race. A Mali’Aheral does not fight unless necessary.\nI hope this has enlighted you about the Mali’Aheral.\nOn Mali’Aheral", ""),
        StaticBook("On Mali'Aheral", "Godness_Aurea", "The Mali'Aheral, the blessed elves. Or as others call them: High elves.\n\nThis elven people is one of the most hated by their own race. People see them as racists and don't think they'll do any good. They kill members of their own race, for\nthey are 'impure'.\nHowever is this true?\n\nI say not.\n\nThe culture of the Mali'Aheral goes back to a specific elf known as Larihei lomahnih. She was one of elven kind who bathed in water that contained enchanted golden\nparticles, which had changed their appearance. Her elven kind had a paler skin and longer ears than the other elven kinds. They were also taller and their hair had become fairer.\nThe change that these particles had made to them also was psycological, \nthese early Mali'aheral had shifted away from their original beliefs and thought more logical.\nThey became scolars, one of which was Larihei.\nAs a child of her kin she learned their traditions and ideals. And soon she appeared to be a\nmaster in all subjects a Mali'Aheral was expected to learn. She grew up to become the leader of the Mali'Aheral and to be their support in the council of princes in Malinor.\nHowever she promoted the Mali'Aheral's believes in the council: That elves were\nthe superior race of Aegis and that they should also rule the other races.\nHowever the other princes and princesses said that she was only promoting war and was a danger to the elves. Larihei was banished from Malinor.\n\nHalf of the Mali'Aheral followed Larihei when she went to find a new home for their race. The other half remained with Malinor, slowly losing their culture.\nHowever when those high elves found the ruins of their kin in Asulon, the old culture was revived.\nMaehr'sae Hiylun'ehya\nThat is the core of the Mali'Aheral culture. It can be translated as \"Progress and Health\".\nBreaking that sentence down, you can split it up in two parts: Maehr'sae, or Progress and Hiylun'ehya, or Health.\nMaehr'sae refers to \nthe development of knowledge and the value of it. It is the base of the position of science in their society, as scientist stand in a high position due to their ability to recover truth and knowledge.\nHiylun'ehya stands for the health and purity of the\nMali'Aheral race. They wish to keep their race from mixing blood, because they believe that their body is the perfect design. A Mali'Aheral is not to ruin his body, he shall not damage it in any way. This means that he or she will not tatoo nor scar their\nbody out of free will. They are also not to mix blood with other races, because they produce children who are not 'perfect' anymore. This includes intimate contact with other races, because they would risk creating a 'failure', a child of mixed blood.\n\nAnother important part of their culture is that they believe to be superior to other races, due to them able to think clear because they do not follow any god.\nThey frown down upon the religions of other races, however they respect those who show to be \nwise and able to think logical.\n\nCombat is another thing that is frowned down upon, as it is an action that does not require thinking and will only cause the loss of people. That last one is very important: The Mali'Aheral are, of\ncourse also subject to the curse of Malin's children, therefor all lives are valued high and loss of one is a waste. It is therefore also expected of all Mali'Aheral to create children at some point in their life.\n\nThe Mali'Aheral frown down upon those of\nmixed blood, they might discriminate them, they are not violent however.\nTheir only violent people are the sillumir, the mourning blades, they are the Mali who give their sarcifice to the race by taking up the sword. Their name comes from the need\nfor them to fight, a sad thing to do in their society. They are respected for their sarcifice and remain few in number, due to the morals of their race.\nA Mali'Aheral does not fight unless necessary.\n\nI hope this has\nenlighted you about the Mali'Aheral.\nThink about this next time you see them, and try to understand their actions.\n\nMaerh'sae Hiylun'eyha\n\n -Vallel'Yuln Aeléyèlsa\n", ""),
        StaticBook("On Mali'Aheral", "Leyu", "On Mali'Aheral\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\n11th of Malins Welcome 1449\nThe Mali'Aheral, the blessed elves. Or as others call them: High Elves.\nThese Elven people are one of the most hated by their own race. People see them as racists and don't think they'll do any good. They kill members of thier\nown race, for they are 'impure'. However is this true?\nI say not. The culture of the Mali'Aheral goes back to a specific elf known as Larihei Lomahnih. She was one of Elven kind who bathed in water that contained\nenchanted golden particles, which had changed their appearance. Her Elven kind had a paler skin and longer ears than the other elven kinds. They were also taller and their hair had become fairer. The change that\nthese particles had made to them also was psycological. These early Mali'Aheral had shifted away from their original beliefs and thought more logical. They became scholars, one of which was Larihei.\nAs a child of her kin she learned their\ntraditions and ideals. And soon she appeared to be a master in all subjects a Mali'Aheral was expected to learn. She grew up to become the leader of the council of Princes in Malinor. However she prmoted the Mali'Aheral's\nbelif in the council: That Elves were the superior race of Aegis and that they should also rule the other races. However the other Princes and Princesses said that she was only promoting war and was a danger to the Elves. Larihei was\nbanished from Malinor. Half of the Mali'Aheral followed Larihei when she went to find a new home for their race. The other half remained with Malinor, slowly losing their culture. However when those High Elves found the ruins of their kin\nin Asulon, the old culture was revived. Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya That is the core of the Mali'Aheral culture. It can be translated as \"Progress and Health\".\nBreaking that sentence down, you can split it up two parts: Maehr'sae,\nor Progress and Hiylun'ehya, or Health. Maehr'sae refers to the development of knowledge and the value of it. It is the base of the position of science in their society, as scientist stand in a high position due\nto their ability to recover truth and knowledge. Hiylun'ehya stands for the health and purity of the Mali'Aheral race. They wish to keep their race from mixing blood, because they believe that their body is the perfect design. A\nMali'Aheral is not to ruin his body, he shall not damage it in any way. This means that he or she will not tatoo nor scar their body out of free will. They are also not to mix blood with other races, because they produce children who are not 'perfect'\nanymore. This includes intimate contact with other races, because they woudl risk creating a 'failure' a child of mixed blood. Another important part of their culture is that they believe to be superior to other races, due to them able to think\nclear because they do not follow any god. They frown down upon the religions of other races, however they respect those who show to be wise and able to think logical. Combat is another thing that is frowned down upon. as it is an action that does\nnot require thinking and will only cause the loss of people that last one is very important: The mali'Aheral are, of course also subject to the curse of Malin's children, therefor all lives are valued high and loss of one is the waste. It is therefore\nalso expected of all Mali'Aheral to create children at some point in their life.\nThe Mali'Aheral frown down upon those of mixed blood, they might discriminate\nthem, they are not violent however. Their only violent people are sillumir, the Mourning\nBlades, they are the Mali who give their sacrifice to the race by taking up the sword. Thier name comes from the need for them to fight, a sad thing to do in their society, They are respected for their sacrifice and\nremain few in number, due to the morals of their race. A Mali'Aheral does not fight unless necessary. I hope this has enlighted you about the Mali'Aheral.\nThink about this next time you see them. and try to understand their actions.\nMaerh'sae Hiylun'eyha\n-Vallel'Yuln Aeleyelsa", ""),
