        StaticBook("Quacktopia", "Oracle", "Quacktopia\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracle Library\n*Strange Numbers\n((9/23/13))\n\n13th of Snows Maiden -1442\nThere once was a man named Jack, he was the most coolest and best person in alllll of Aegis . He was the kings most trusted advisor and warrior, one day the king told him to go on A adventure to Quackatopia, the\nduck ruled kingdom of the sea, Jack eagarly accepted. : He traveled through the blazing deserts, the freezing forests, and the mean ocean fianlly making it to Quacktopia, he celebrated, drinking till drunk then flirting with allll the pret ty duck\nladies. When he awoke he got to business and was tasked with eliminating the meany head wolf people to the south of Quacktopia. Jack arrived at wolftopia and beat up alllll the wolves . After arriving back at Quacktopia he found out he\nimpregnated the duckling, later he was killed by the ducklings dad, THE END Quacktopia", ""),
        StaticBook("Quota", "Grundi Ashmail", "         Quota             \nIron: 20                  Coal: 16                   Gold: 16                    Pay: 125 Minas per week\nWatch your back tree", ""),
        StaticBook("R.Plants Vol. I", "Amfionas", "Rare Plants and their Properties\n------------------\nby Larky\n\nThere are numerous peculiar plants and vegitation that can be found in any realm.\n \nThis is but a small effort to document their properties.\n1.SilverLine\nThis plant is named silverline due to its unique silver lines that mark its leaves.\n\nIts height is equal to that of the tall grass and it usually grows in cold climates where its covered in snow.\n\nThe most remarkable\nthink regarding this plant is that when lit on fire it emits a silver light. The fire with this color (silverfire) can retain this state for a couple of minutes to a few hours depending on the number of leaves used. \n\nThe fire created despite its differe-\n-nce in colour, has no other peculiar properties.\n\nTemperature and size remain relatively the same.\n\nIf the leaves are left to dry under the hot sun, one will observe that they have longer effects.\n2.Dablaora\nThis plant is easily distinguisable due to its vivid orange colour. It grows mostly in the deserts.\n\nShould the dark red fruit it forms be consumed one would be able to mimic perfectly the sound of a squirel.\nThe reason the dabblefruit causes that is unknown. It is also unknown why the person still retains its ability to speak properly.\n\n3.Velteleafy\nVelteleafy is a mostly normal plant. What distinguishes from other is its fruit.\nThe plant forms fruits the size of a small melon.\n\nThe fruit is coloured purple with blue dots and is quite nutritious and filling.\n\nThe problem is that the saliva of the user becomes quite thick and sticky.\nHe soon begins to form large violet and blue bubbles that fly off whenever he tries to speak or breath with his mouth open.\n\nThe veltefruit does not appear to have any long term impacts on the health of an individual that consumes it.\nIt is also quite entertaining.\n\n4.Treledelti\nThis plant is distinguishable by its pale yellow leaves with red sybols that resemble flames.\n\nIt does not grow in a particular region set aside deserts and \ntundras. \n\nIt does not create any fruits and when its leaves are consumed the user is overwhelmed by a sense of hunger.\n\nHe is able to consume twice as much food than the normal ratio and the effect wares\noff only after an hour. \n\nOnly to be eaten at a party where there is an abundance of food and beverages.\n\nWritten by Larky at the 16th of Malin's Welcome, 1451\n\nVaerhaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Raak's Journal", "Benben582", "\nI'm not too sure where to start. I have just found a home in Vaer'Haven and am currently employed as a guard. Well the Jarl calls it 'Auxillary to the Legion' or 'Town Police'. But, I like the sound of guard better.\n\nAnyways I do like the \narmor and sword they have provided me. I have only slain monsters with the sword and it has not seen battle but it is a good blade, it will stay true in battle, that I am sure of. \n\nI am currently thinking of quitting this whole guard business and \ntake up a new occupation. It is really dull work. I want something that stimulates my mind. I'm fairly interested in the arts of alchemy and engineering. I know there is already an apotheracy in Vaer'Haven so I might have some luck as an apprentice.\nFor now, I remain a dull guard. Dont get me wrong I like order and protection. But I'm not sure the life is for me.\n\n((7/7/13))\n~Raak Stormbeard\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Raak's Notes", "Benben582", "         -======-\n            Notes\n              On\n           Alchemy\n         -======-\n\n~ Raak Stormbeard\nAlchemy has four rudementary elements that are the basis of all potionmaking. \n\n- Fire\n- Earth\n- Water\n- Air\n\nThese each have their own unique uses.\nFire:\nUsed for potions of:\nDestruction, anger, hatred, aswell as bravery, courage, and gusto.\n\nEarth:\nUsed for potions of:\nStrength, solidity, firmness, fiora, animals, healing and many other subjects.\nWater:\nUsed for potions of:\nLiquids, peace, balance, life, and rebirth.\n\nAir:\nUsed for potions of:\nAgility, perception, travel, quickness, and even flight.\nReagents are used in every potion. They can be found everywhere in common plantlife to to swamp fungi.\n\nReagents each symbolise one of the four rudementary elements. Sometimes perhaps they symbolise more than one at the same time.\nReagents also have different tiers of quality, some are weak and some are more potent.\nI heard a man speak something of a thing called a Panacea? Surely he must've been joking they are a myth! No potion can cure all disease and injury to perfection!\nAlas, I shall not dwell on these fables...\nElf's Hair Vine: Strong Symbol of Air\n\nCrouching Feather: Strong Symbol of Air\n\nZawabate: Moderate Sybol of Water\nPotion of Acuitiy:\n\nMinor:\nBase - Water\nAir x2 (Perception)\n\nLesser:\nBase - Distilled Water\nAir x3 (Perception)\n\nGreater:\nBase - Aqua Vitae\nAir x4 (Perception)\nForward\nConjurities \nmagical \"left overs\".  The symptoms range from strange boils on the skin to odd colored rashes, such as blue, red, brown and white.  The best treatment for this seems to be rest and the casting of more magic!", ""),
        StaticBook("Raaks Journal v2", "Benben582", "Journal #2\nEntry #1:\nVaer'Haven's new Jarl Lachlan put a stop to the Dread Knight influence upon his town. He confronted them at their tower, I was right behind him, weapon drawn. Tensions were high but there was no bloodshed.\nEntry #2:\nI met a Lad named Drahak, he was also apart of Vaer'Havens Marcra. We went on an adventure, but were bested by the elves elusiveness. We were journeying to their capital but got lost. Oh but a journey it t'was. Hordes of monsters and slips -\ninto a river, 50 foot fall from a ravine right int' it. I had to jump down there to help the lad. I couldn just let him drown. After that I decided to call it quits as there was no sign of the path, even at high grounds.\nEntry #3:\nI need to work up the courage to tell the Marshall that I dont want to be apart of the Marcra. I've also looked over the form to join the Dwarven Engineering Guild and have decided that I would rather not become an engineer. \nEntry #4:\nI met a fair elf by the name of Vul'ker Ayal'ame. He was on his way to Kal'Azgoth in search of a bow. I had a spare and traded him a bow and arrows for a book and quill. He was very friendly, I wish him safe travels.\n\n~Raak Stormbeard", ""),
        StaticBook("Raevir Tougn", "friar7", "        The Raevir\n           tongue\n   By Domnik Dogislav\n-------------------Yes-Da\nNo-Niet\nNever-Neh\nOi-Ey\nHello-Ej\nHello (formal)-Eja\nGoodbye-Dravo\nBye-Dra\nInsult (cunt)-Vlag\nConfidence-Khrum\nBrother/friend-Borsahomosexual-homosex\ninsult-chok\nidiot/fool-zhenya\nwhore-damen\nAnnoyance-cetnik\nAdunian-macecatcher\nCreator-Godanistan\nCreator-god/godan\ntroublemaker-rascal\ncurse-sved/sveda\npolearm-bardi\nPenis(insult)-Pednik\nDark Elf-Plagus\nOrc-Kebab\nScourge-Spookam\nCrossbow-Blet\nArmour-Bron\nTo equip-Don \nPeople-Folk\nWorking man of the main hub-Sovet\nWorking man of rural area-Strelt/Strelesy\n------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Raglin's Journal", "gaiusmarius8", "Raglin's Journal\nDay 1\nhelp. Recently there were bandits that slipped into the area, I shooed them off, severely injuring one of them. Walls need to be reinforced. Currently we're working on the second floor of the keep, and the ravine down under. Hopes are up about it.\nDay 2\nbrought up, doubling it in size. We've a whole new floor dedicated to residents, including children. Aye, Tanith made quite the childrens' room. Perhaps one of these days, I'll have a wee lad of my own.\nwell! We've started brewing in the keep, and I'll be honest, it's not bad! I call it, Edgehand Delight. Tanith is bein' a dear with helpin' me. So nice to have such a helpful lass around th' place. Wee Geralt beh growin' well! He'll be bigger than me!\nDay 4\nbecause it soothes me. I've been delving into the history of Runesmithing. Perhaps something will come of it, eventually.\nmuch without Tanith and Baldir's approval. I hope that they don't respect me any less. \nWow, things are so different than they used to be. I've acquired quite the promising lad as a bodyguard. He's doing well. The Clan Hall is looking grand as ever, as well. Hopes are up that Tanith will set to work soon. I'll not rush her. The poor lass has\nso much to take care of, as it is. I really do love the Toovs. I hope my stay shan't be cut short by anything. \nit'll stop a strike or two decently enough. Baldir and the Rose seem to be amidst something crucial. Something partaining to the Wilds.... I'll not pry. It's the Rose's business, and however buddy-buddy I may be, I'm no true lad of theirs. Perhaps, if I \nhaven't already, I'll earn my permanent keep amongst the tales of the Roses. But for now, my clan is my soul priority.\nher back. I don't believe I've cried such as I did for many a year. This is twice I've lost my love. Athani before, now Kalra? It seems me love life is cursed. I buried her in the dwarvish mountains, where she belongs...\noutside the Teutonic Order's base the other day. Held firm in trenches, awaiting their approach. They never came, so we pulled out. \nDay 10\npass again....\nI've been reading deeply into runesmithing, I've been scouring the dwarven library, as well as my own. The art's inner workings are starting to form in my mind, but I've a ways to go, yet. \ncertain magics. The workings of flame seem to draw me in close, but not so much as electricity.\nserves as an intimidating piece. And quite stylish, at that.\nrelatives, who will be moving in soon. It's so good to find more of my kin. \nDay 30\nlads a memento; a bear claw. Yeah, yeah. Bjorginar and all that. But that was years ago. Besides, I have quite the collection of other, more interesting items.\n315 years old. Hiebe is what, 800? I've got a ways to go.\nDay 34\nPain. So much. I can't remember when I last branded myself with the markings of runes. I'll reveal them, soon. ", ""),
        StaticBook("Raglin's Journey", "Alexander_Wh", "The Adventures of Raglin\n\nIn this book, I shall share with you some of my many tales and adventures I've gone through over the years, starting with the beginning. \nChapter 1: Kal'Karik's Demise\n\nMany years ago, the city of Kal'Karik was a prosperous and wonderful place for dwarves and people in general to live, grow, and become prosperous in. Its streets bustled with busy dwarves, happy families, and a generally \npopulation. I lived there with my wife, Moira, and my son, Talgrin; Tally for short. We lived happily, enjoying an average life of a dwarf. I worked in the mines, as well as the woods, as a hunter. My son was an aspiring bowman, himself. He would often \njoin me on my excursions, and we'd have a grand time. On one fateful day, I denied him when he asked to join me in the woods. I had been having trouble finding prey, and began venturing farther. I didn't want to risk him getting hurt. So I went alone, \nleaving he and my wife in Karik. Many hours passed, I sat crouched in a treetop, scanning the woods for any sign of movement, or life, when the sound came. It was thunderous, but yet rhythmatic. I froze, listening. It seemed like beats of...wings. I \nlooked into the sky, and the sight came to my eyes. It was a dragon. Something I had not seen in my time, but read of. It came like a black cloud, the sun being blotched out. The air grew dry. I watched as the massive beast loomed over, before it dove for\nthe gates of Karik. I threw myself from the tree, rolling as I hit the ground. I began to ran, panting and pumping my arms. I had to get my family out of there. But the screams came before I even neared the edge of the woods. Flames erupted over the \ninnards of the city, and the sounds of hundreds of dwarves, burnt to a crisp, echoed through the mountains. I fell to my knees, sobbing, as I witnessed the flames engulfing the city within, smoke pouring from the gate. Dwarves were evacuating, and I made\nmy way closer, scanning the faces for my kin. But, to no avail. I waited, hours later, not daring to venture into the fallen city, for it had collapsed within, lava pouring over the streets. My kin...They were gone. My bloodline, gone. And since that day,\nI've never been the same.", ""),
        StaticBook("Rainbow-Coat I", "JJKoshane", "Hello there, my name is Von... At least I THINK it is. You see, I awoke in D'hara which was a part of a nation called Empyreal. I had no memory of anything before that, the only reason why I use the name \"Von\" is because that was sewn on the interior of-\nthe coat I was wearing, which at the time I was sporting a purple and yellow velvet coat, I later found my current glorious Rainbow Coat in some ruins on the Island I called home for my first few months in Empyreal. That very coat has become my passion.\nWhile I was in D'hara I lived with a young fellow named \"Shatter\", me and Shatter were living together during my stay in Empyreal. Everything was fine until a couple of the nation's members decided to make their own little town outside of D'hara.\nThe owners of this town were none other than the Greene Twins. At first I was friendly with them, but one day we had an argument and the younger brother hated me from that day on, Eventually after a large amount of his rude behavior I've had enough.\nI went to Arethor and bought a very weak paralyzation toxin from a local alchemist. The next day I walked into their village and asked a little girl if she could sneak some of this very weak toxin into some of her cookies that she was baking for him.\nIt turns out that the Younger Brother of the twins had heard me and called the guards on me, my first reaction was to run. And ran I did, I eventually reached my home and descended into what was more of a dungeon rather than a basement in our home.\nI ran through the re-inforced doors of the cellars and as I did, I locked them behind me, after I did so I crept into a dark corner of the lowest part of the basement. Somehow the guard who was pursuing me had broke through the doors and captured me.\nHe had dragged me for what seemed like hours and eventually threw me into the prison of that town. After a couple days of solitary confinement, they had let me out. I cursed the men and ran away to Arethor. In the course of time I dwelled in Oren land-\nI've had jumped from job to job and then eventually decided to revisit Empyreal... Only to find out that a native volcano had erupted and destroyed the land I had once called home. \nI saw some ruined wanted posters that depict a crude drawing of myself performing a dark ritual in front of the volcano, under that drawing was text that had said:\n\"WANTED: RAINBOW-COAT\nREASON: PERFORMING DARK RITUALS THAT CAUSED THE VOLCANO TO ERUPT\"\nAfter seeing that poster I ran as fast as I could to the boat I sailed to there with and sailed back to Arethor... Ever since then I have been drifting faction to faction while recieving the same amount of hatred...", ""),
        StaticBook("Ralof's Diary", "georgemeywes", "*The pages seem old. some stained*\n\nDay 1: Father came home today, Injured and burnt, he wouldn' speak but only mumble to himself, I didnt know what was happening,\nMother came down with the herbs from a druid she knew but Father refused. I asked what\nhad happened but was sent to bed, supper never came and now I am sleepy.\n\nDay 2: Father.............\n*the page seems to be slightly ripped*\nDied.\n\nDay 347: Mother Has Left now leaving me, her grief was to much\nfor her, I have not been able to write, for time passed so quickly.\n\nDay 532: There Coming, The wilderness is harsh and life isnt easy, I must flee, how lese will I survive!\nI hear them they are close I must run! \n*A little blood lies on the page*\nDay 533:\nThey, hurt me I have been hurt and beaten and left here, in the Witch Woods, I sit by a Muashroom next to thee river shivering\nits starting to get dark and spiders are near.\n\nDay 545: A druid lives here with an Ent Toad\nhe's wonderful\nhe looks after me, feeds me but  I know soon I must leave, I will travel To Lenfarthing.\n\nDay 600: I found a cave here In Lenfarthing my, my mothers body lays at the bottom! I pick up her gem and store it in my pocket, its all\nthat I now have left of her, A large Dwarfs body lay next to her bloodtstained like the mark on her Chest, it was him, I bet he killed her! *He didn't write as he was very angry at this moment*\nDay 683: I travel to the dwarven lands to meet them, to know who did this! \n\nDay 745: They beat me, I will not return there, EVER, I am scarred down my chest on the right side now I will travel to adunia.\nDay 2348: I forget I have this! I have done much in the time, but now I travel to Old Adunia.\n\nDay 2389: No one is near? I now travel to Clodu Temple I will find directions there!\n\nDay 2467: They tell me there is a new Adunia \nin the dwarven Lands, I will travel there, but no where near the Capital shall I cross\nI will not harm the Dwarves but I will not Protect them either,\n\nDay 2587: A home a Job! I 'ave a nice life here, time to stop my diary, I will move on to a new life!\n*Ralofs Signature Lies Here*\n           Ralof\n\n\n\nMy Diary", ""),
        StaticBook("Ramblings, Pt. 1", "Patriotic_Fool", "Aislinn's Ramblings===\n\n-Good and Evil-\n\nThese two concepts seem to divide our society clean in half. On one hand, there are those who are \"good\", on the other, the \"bad\". I will begin by defining each of these. \nGood is the concept of purity, positive things, and happy things. Pleasure, joy, laughing, smiling, and friendship are all good things. Beauty is a positive concept, and many beautiful things invoke happiness. When one is happy, one tends to do more good \nactions, in order to further that happiness. Good also comes in the forms of helping others, even at a cost to oneself. Being selfless, or putting someone else before you, is the key to furthering good. A man who helps a beggar both provides a positive\naction by relieving the suffering of another life, and he betters himself by helping those around him. Even if he doesn't see an immediate return from his actions, Fate tends to smile upon those who are kind. \n\nThe opposite of good is evil. This is the \nconcept of negative things, feelings, emotions, and actions. While a frown might not necessarily be evil, nor sadness or other negative emotions, the results of those emotions are what causes evil to take place. A man may be overcome in grief over the\nloss of his wife, and may harm others in order to gain an outlet of his feelings. Being sad isn't a bad thing, but rarely does happiness cause one to harm others. Such instances will be covered shortly. Those who are evil tend to be selfish, short sighted\ngreedy, and animalistic. They strive to gain for themselves, whether by harming or killing others for the gaining of material wealth, or for sick and twisted pleasure. Pleasure, as said, is not a bad thing /unless/ it is gained at the expense of another. \nAn important distinction is that one may be evil but have an excuse, such as a mental disorder, a \"need\" or \"fetish\" to cause harm to others. The person may be motivated through religious means, or logically convince themselves that their actions are \nnecessary. There is no gray room, however.\n\nKilling is killing. Torture is torture. Harm is harm. Negative actions are negative, regardless of intent. \n\nThe question then arises. Are those who are evil merely under a temporary\nlapse of judgement? Perhaps they had problems in their lives that they struggled with, and that caused them to do evil things. One is either good, or evil. There is no middle ground, for such a \nmiddle ground /cannot/ exist. How can one be both male and \nfemale? Both tall and short? How can a distance be both short and long? One is either good or evil, the extent varying from person to person. A shopkeeper may simple cheat his customers, occassionally. Are his actions wrong? Yes. Does that make him\nan evil person? It depends. \n\nI believe that good and evil sit like great mountains, each atop the peak. On one peak is the epitome of good, the purest and most selfless, kind, and strong \"good\". On the other is the most corrupt, twisted, \nand horrendous evil. We are all on different positions between the mountains, seperated by a massive chasm. Some may be at the bottom of the \"good\" hill, another may be mid-way up the \"evil\" mountainside. A psychopathic murderer is certainly closer to the\n\"evil peak\" than a petty thief. For these reasons, laws are established to punish those who have committed crimes, or done evil actions. Murder is much more serious than theft. \n\nThere is only one question that remains, however.\nIf good and evil are two mountains, with a chasm in between, is neutrality even possible? \n\nCan one be both good and evil simultaneously? Can one be neither?\n\nI can only use myself as an example. \nI have committed evil actions, and I have committed good actions. I have no Deity to guide my ways, and have had to figure out what is morally acceptable on my own. I feel that I am at the bottom of this chasm, trying to climb up on one side or the other.\nAs I make progress, I fall back down into the pitch black abyss, and the process repeats itself. \n\nI believe, sometime in the future, I will become either good or evil. The natural inclination is to tend towards good, as that is the accepted \nalignment, but how can I be good if I am naturally evil? Additionally, how can I be evil if I am naturally good? \n\n*the writing changes in style slightly*\n\nInteresting read, Aislinn. I wish I could help out more, but\nsadly that's not my job. You may be able to change who you are through your actions, or such things may have been decided long ago. \n\nIt's up to you to find out.", ""),
        StaticBook("Raserei's Ballad", "Hagan \"Weird Eyes\" Raserei", "In the merry Autumn’s Cold, From me home I started,\nLeft the house of home, Nearly broken hearted,\nSaluted knowledge dear, Grabbed me darlin' notebook,\nDrank a pint of beer, Me grief and tears to smother,\n\nThen off to reap the scorn, Leave where I was born,\nGet a stack paper, To banish bounty hunters,\nA brand new pair of brogues, rattlin' o'er the bogs,\nFrightenin' all the dogs, On the mountain path to Malin’\nOne, two, three, four five,\nGrab the miss and help her\nDown the mountain path\nAll the way to Malin’,\nWhack-fol-lul-lee-ra.\nIn Lenniel that night, I rested limbs so weary,\nStarted by daylight, Me spirits bright and airy,\nTook a drop of the pure, Keep me heart from sinkin',\nThat's the Weird Eyes cure, Whenever he's on for drinking.\nTo see the lassies smile, Laughing all the while,\nAt my curious style, 'Twould set your heart a-bubblin'.\nAnd asked if I was hired, Wages I required,\nTill I was nearly tired, Of the mountain path to Malin’.\nOne, two, three, four five,\n\nGrab the miss and help her\nDown the mountain path\nAll the way to Malin’,\nWhack-fol-lul-lee-ra.\nIn Malinor arrived, I thought it such a pity,\nTo be so soon deprived, A view of that fine city.\nWell then I took a stroll, All among the quality,\nBundle it was stole, All in the neat locality;\nSomething crossed my mind - When I looked behind,\nNo bundle could I find, Upon me stick a wobblin'.\n\nEnquirin' for the rogue, Said me small town brogue,\nWasn't much in vogue, On the mountain path to Malin’.\nOne, two, three, four five,\nGrab the miss and help her\nDown the mountain path\nAll the way to Malin’,\nWhack-fol-lul-lee-ra.\nFrom there I got away, me spirits never failin'\nLanded on the stead, Just as the elf was watchin';\nThe darky at me roared, Said that minas had me,\n\nWhen I grabbed about, A sentence found for Weird Eyes,\nIt was with the dame, played some sadist games,\nDanced some hearty jigs, The water round me bubblin',\nWhen off the job, Wished meself was dead,\nOr better far instead, On the mountain path to Malin’.\nOne, two, three, four five,\nGrab the miss and help her\nDown the mountain path\nAll the way to Malin’,\nWhack-fol-lul-lee-ra~.\nThe knights of Mistress here, When we safely landed,\nCalled meself a fool; I could no longer stand it;\nBlood began to boil, Temper I was losin',\nPoor old Stenar card’nal, They began abusin',\n\"Hurrah my soul,\" says I, My limbs that I let fly;\nWolfy boys were nigh, An' saw I was a hobblin,\nWith a loud hurray, They joined in the affray.\nWe quickly cleared the way, For the mountain path to Malin’.\nOne, two, three, four five,\nGrab the miss and help her\nDown the mountain path\nAll the way to Malin’,\nWhack-fol-lul-lee-ra.\nGrab the miss and help her\nDown the mountain path\nAll the way to Malin’,\nWhack-fol-lul-lee-ra.\nWhack-fol-lul-lee-ra.\nWhack-fol-lul-lee-ra~.", ""),
        StaticBook("Raven and Cat", "Moose_M", "The Story of the Raven and the Cat\n\nBy Veghim Carter\n-29th of Sun Smile-\n\nRaven swooped and rested down/ On a muddy pole./ He looked to the ground and frowned/ for he saw a cat at his toes./\n\n\"Come down here, nice old bird,/ Your age is has reached its peak./ Now is my time to devour you up.\" He purred./ \"Your meat, feathers, brain and beak.\"?\n\n\"O don't eat me,\" The old bird cried/\" for my meat is no good at all.\"/\"at the little mice.\nhe pried./\"So I won't have to fall.\n\nThe mice are to fast,/ and I am to old./ But your time has passed/ so let me eat you intead of the bugs and the mold./\n\n\nThe raven screeched and choked/\nattracting a big dog that was evoked/\nThe mutt rushed over and ate the old cat/\nand the old raven laughed at the dingbat/\n\nMoral: Brains will always beat age.", ""),
