        StaticBook("A Nobody Like Me", "zach211w", "Nobody\n \n        First book\n           \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n   By: Mirlan Fartingo\n\n Life ain't easy for us    kind of people.\n We're basicly just \n nobodys. \n Nobodys, roamin' the\n streets in search of\n somethin' to do. \n Friends to meet but,\n theres no one who \n likes a nobody like\n you.\n\n You should try it but\n you'll probaly give \n up. You'll cry for\n help with no talent, no    skills. Oh you'll moan\n you'll groan, no \n group wants you.\n Can't get no happiness  in you life except \n when you get a new \n book, a new house.\n You can't make\n\n parents proud, not \n even smile. Oh yes \n indeed a nobody is\n harder then you \n think, tryin' its best,\n but it fails. This is my \n buddy, my pal\n writin' a book is my \n vacation to paradise.\n Oh you'll see what I \n mean some say \n humans are easy to\n\n grow up as. But I think   you'll find another \n word for it. 'cause \n it ain't sugar, it ain't \n spice, it ain't even \n really nice. Lonely, \n Oh lonely you'll be.\n Day dreamin' when \n you finally find a girl.\n But that won't 'appen. \n Cause its not\n\n sugar, ain't spice its \n not even nice. \n Oh ye you'll see what I   mean! They throw you    out 'cause you don't \n fit in, no skills, no\n talents, not even any \n friends. Oh ya, you got\n no skills, no talents,\n and more.\n\n          \n        Hope you enjoy\n    It's my first book,\n    it probaly won't be  \n    that enjoyable, \n    but I would like \n    to tell you about a \n    life of a nobody, \n    like me.\n  \n    -Mirlan Fartingo", ""),
