        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§l   The Craft of \n   Metalworking \n         & \n    The Art of\n    Forgework \n\n       ~ ~ ~ \n\n§r§oBy Silir'ilume,\n\n Forgemaster of the \n     Blessed City\n     of Lin'everal\n\nBefore one seeks entry into the domain of those who call themselves metalworkers, one must first master the understanding of the concepts and principles, both vital and not, of one's intended craft. The author of this title must indeed\n\nlay stress upon the fact that a mere tome cannot act as a basis of instruction in the place of a master of the craft. A tome can relay requirements, concept and technique, but no more. True mastery comes only with instruction from one with proper\n\nexperience, for this craft is not merely one of striking ceaselessly upon metal. Metalworking, in concept and practice, is design, arrangement, organization, cutting, uniting, drilling, finishing, tempering, welding, brazing and\n\ntoolmaking. It is an elegant dance, of which the end product is grace and beauty in its purest form. A blacksmith's tools are his trade, modified to his fit his own style of craftsmanship. One cannot generalize the craft of metalworking, for one cannot\n\ngeneralize art.\n\nThus, having fully comprehended the complexity of metalwork, one must first begin by embracing blacksmithing's intrinsic properties. Before one can proceed, one must first\n\nobtain the tools necessary to weave one's art out of base metals.\n\n§l       Tools\n§rTools are to a blacksmith as a sword is to a swordsman, or a brush to an artist. Without one's tools, one cannot shape the metal to form the\n\nimage in the mind's eye. A blacksmith's tools are numerous, but certain tools in particular are what one might consider 'vital'.\n\nThe most obvious and most distinct tool that a blacksmith will utilize is that of the\n\nforge itself. To work properly with the metal, the material must first be stimulated through the process of heating. A forge requires two distinct sources of energy to run properly; fuel and air. The most proper and common material utilized as a fuel\n\nsource is that of 'black powder'; a distinct, finely grown substance made through the burning of coal and removal of impurities. The second required material, air, is obtained through the proper usage of a certain object known as a 'bellows'. A bellows\n\ngenerally takes form as a leather bag with two handles and a narrow nozzle for placing in the forge. When one pumps said bellows, air is likewise pumped into the flames, thus causing them to grow in both size and temperature. If one were to visit various\n\nsmithies across the expanse of Anthos, one would take note that the bellows used varies greatly depending on the ability and success of the resident smith. Smaller smithies may utilize a comparably smaller, handheld bellows whilst larger smithies may\n\ndabble in technology such as pulleys and gears to keep their forges running properly.\n\nWith these two materials considered, one would note that the size of one's forges also plays a relatively large and important\n\npart in the method at which one goes about their craft. Many start with smaller forges; they use less energy and heat more quickly. Larger forges, in stark contrast, use much more energy and heat much less quickly. Such forges, however, also maintain heat\n\nmuch better and their temperature can be controlled to a finer degree.", ""),
        StaticBook("3rd riddle", "§bA Riddler", "Another clue, haha, I got you, where the magical tome will be, is up to you, at an auction in Lenniel, perhaps ? Go and check the clue !", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "12/22/13 Prices:\n\n(First Opened)\n\nDiamond/Emerald: 75 mina minimum, no engraving. \n\nGold: 50 mina minimum, no engraving.\n\nSilver/Iron: 25 mina min., no engraving.\n\nSmall and easy engravings cost and extra 5.\n\nSmall and difficult engravings cost an extra 10.\n\nBig and easy engravings cost an extra 20\n\nBig and hard engravings cost an extra 25-30.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "((12/23/13))\nOliver Blackwell: Gold/Emerald ring, 85 mina. Given to owner.\n\n((12/23/13))\nBartholomew (John):\nIron framed fans (2),\n60 mina. Sold to buyer\n\n((12/24/13))\nIllylis Orway (RabidAnimal):\nDiamond Ring, engraved. Price cut in half since ore was provided. 30 mina (small discount)\n\n((12/26/13))\nMarcus Constantine\n(Sarkly):\n14 Carrot gold w/ diamond inset. 80 mina.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "\"New Malinor\" has been created after the original Malinor became \"tainted\". The people here are happy and actually find this new version of Malinor more open and free. A wall is being built around the town, and full houses are being constructed.\n\nNew Malinor is very close to the High elven city, which I has been dubbed the \"Silver City\" by many. The walls are made of a strong stone. The people there are known for the racist tendencies and were quick to give me a helping of it.\n\nThere is a small island inbetween new Malinor and the Silver city. A strange ruined crystal lays there. After further inquiring I have discovered this crystal was created by \"The Black Scourge\". An apparent malicious group of people attacking Anthos.\n\nMany say they come from the north, I shall be heading there soon to see what there is to see. I will soon be taking a sample of this crimson crystal to study and test on my own.\n\nI have been traveling to northern Anthos only to find scattered dead land everywhere. Blood, death, and worst of all the never ending chill of the northern parts of Anthos. Strange dark black skeletons roam the area, my frail body cant deal with them, so\n\nI will cotinue to avoid them the best I can.\n\nI have just left the north. A strange being threatened me I have to give him a \"book\" an elven day about my travels through Anthos or I will face death. I do not know what to do.. or what to think...\n\nI am horrifyed yet intriqued.. what an awful thing to pen down.. I will give them what they want as long as I stay alive. I am traveling to Lenfarthing home of the halflings in an elven day.. Maybe I can just forget about this whole situation.\n\nStaying at an Inn, the owner is quite a kind orc. I also spoke with a few kind people and showed them a bit of my \"Magic\" abilities. It brought a smile on my face to see others so happy because of something so little. Lastly I visted the cloud temple.\n\nThe library is filled to the brim with great books I might just stay here and assist with there growing collection. \n\nI have woken up in a cold sweat... The northern reaches call to me in my dreams. I fear them, I fear death but why, why am I...\n\nStill so interested in traveling there? I need some real rest and maybe a bit of food this idea is getting the better of me.\n\nI am heading to the north, today I will give them that information. I.. I feel so horrid about this... I met a man.. he was\n\nattacked by them. I dont know what I seek anymore.. Am I greedy for information? what is wrong with me.. I am to old for all of this.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Dwarves \nN/A", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Many years ago there lived a small family called \"Donagon\". They lived deep into the dwarven lands. Harkmold Donagon and Elizebeth Donagon had a child by the name of Davlin. His father trained him in the art of axe wielding. Davlin trained hard every day,\n\nfor many weeks.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Ariana's Diary\n\n\n\nIvan, if you read this\nyour eyeballs will\nfall out.\n\nEntry 1:\n\nIt's been three years since Father died. It was hard at first, and it still is, but I'm trying to come to terms with it. Even though I know Alester is right, it's hard to let go of the past. Even though I still miss her, it wasn't as hard with\n\nmother. Maybe it's because I knew Father longer. Maybe I don't feel as safe without him. I don't know. What I do know is that even if I live longer than any elf, a piece of me died that day.\n\nEntry 2:\n\nAlester has become very ill. I've had to take on his duties in his place. It's quite stressful, knowing that everyone is watching you. It feels like they're just waiting for you to slip up. Luckily, William is helping me make\n\ndecisions. I was attacked in Abresi, also. I can't believe it, but Ivan actually saved me. It was quite heroic (even for him). He even got a sword from a man who was there. Perhaps he's more brave than I once thought.\n\nEntry 3:\n\nArion began acting strange today. He passed out on the floor of the throne room. When he woke up, he didn't remember anything about us or where he was. He kept talking about needing his staff and needing to help the dwarves\n\nfight off Iblees. I don't know what he was talking about, but it scared me. I hope he returns to normal soon.\n\nEntry 4:\n\nIvan told me he saw Alester and Kalina kissing. I don't approve of their relationship, but I'm just not going to speak of it. Like I told Ivan: We can't choose for him. Alester is changing. Whether for the good or for the bad, I don't know.\n\nEntry 5:\n\nToday I spoke with a nice man named Segavex Egrotus. He's a soldier who has gone on many adventures. When I'm old enough, I want to go explore the world just like he did. A man also talked of one of bannermen being a criminal.\n\nI'm not sure whether to believe him or not. I'll have to ask Alester later. Speaking of which, Alester just left. He only left a note telling us he isn't sure when he'd be back. He left me in charge. It puts a lot of pressure on me, but I think I can\n\nhandle it. I have lots of people to help advise me if I need it. I do hope he comes back though. If he doesn't, I might be stuck here forever.\n\nEntry 6:\n\nI take back what I said before. If Alester comes back, I'm sure he won't approve. The thing is, I'm getting married! Pretty soon I'm going to be Mrs. Westfall. That's right, William proposed to me. That's the problem... Alester wanted me to\n\nmarry a noble, but instead I chose William. If it comes to it, I'm prepared to run away from Gren. I don't know where I'll go, but I don't care as long as I'm with Will.\n\nEntry 7:\n\nI've just come back from my wedding. It was held at the Oren Chapel. Many people attended, and I had a wonderful time. I am now known as Ariana Westfall! Alester still hasn't returned from his journey. Even though I don't want\n\nhim to come back and be angry, I do hope he's safe wherever he is. Even if he wanted to marry me to someone unknown, he's still my brother. And I still love him.\n\nEntry 8:\n\nI've just told Will that I'm going to have a child. Isn't that exciting! He seems to be even more worried about me. We also told Ivan that we're married. He was shocked, but I think he's alright with it. Construction is\n\ncontinuing on the new storage room. I can't wait until it's finished.\n\nEntry 9:\n\nConstruction is done on the storage room, but it's a small happiness. A sign has been posted outside the barony. All Westfalls are banned from entering. I wonder if this means Alester has returned, or if it's just a\n\nbannerman. But since I am no longer welcome here, I suppose I should leave. Will is receiving land for a barony and once construction is complete on the house, I'll move there. Until then, I'll stay in Gren and hope no one sees me.\n\n*A page seems to have been ripped out*\n\n*A page seems to have been ripped out*\n\nEntry 11:\n\nI've officially moved to Verglass (Will's barony). The manor is huge and the view is great. I can't wait until more people move here. Our baby is due in a few months. I can't wait to name it. Will was talking with Alester and Alester called\n\nour child a 'daemon spawn'. It saddens me that he thinks so, but I won't let him get me down. Our child is going to be amazing, and nothing will convince me otherwise.\n\nEntry 12:\n\n*The pages are covered in tear stains* I've just learned something terrible. I can barely believe it, but at the same time I know that it is true. Ivan told me that he is a cannibal. He even has nightmares about\n\neating me. He's changed. It scares me to think of what he has done. I'm not sure if I can trust him anymore. I'm afraid for my child, and I'm afraid for everyone else. He wanted me to kill him, but I couldn't bring myself to do it. I can't bring myself to\n\nend a human life. Not like he has. But I know one thing for certain: he's not the Ivan I once knew. And he certainly isn't my brother.\n\nEntry 13:\n\nI've come to terms with Ivan's 'problem'. It still scares me a bit, but deep down I knew I still loved him. Recently, a pair of twins was born to me and Will. A boy and a girl. Their names are Terryn Nathan Westfall and\n\nLeyna Ellyn Westfall. They're the cutest little things in the world and I love them very much. It makes me miss my own mother...\n\nEntry 14:\n\nOur barony is growing larger by the minute. We have so many new people living here. Many new buildings are being made as well. Will and I were recently invited to a ball in Gren. I hadn't been to Gren since I left. I went out to my\n\nfavorite balcony. The windows had been closed off. I left the ball early...\n\n*A note is tucked inbetween the pages here*\n\nHoney, I love you. If I don't see you again, I just want you to raise the children, be safe, be strong.\n\nWilliam Westfall\n\nEntry 15:\n\nSince I was kidnapped (I would rather not talk about it, if you don't mind.), nothing much has happened. We've lived happily, watching our children and barony grow. So much time has passed since my childhood. So many things turned\n\nout differently from what I imagined them to be. I still haven't seen the world. I've only been as far as Nation Crossing, but I didn't get to explore much because of the war. I think it is time...\n\nEntry 16:\n\nI've done it. I've wrote a note to Will and I'm leaving Verglass. I'm actually kind of scared now that I'm doing it.... but I'm determined to stay on the path I've layed out for myself. I've always wanted to see the world. It's such a big\n\nplace. I hope maybe while I'm on my journey, I can find whatever it is I'm looking for out there. I'll be leaving my diary here for safekeeping. This may be my last entry. I'll always cherish the memories I've made here in the North. Farewell.\n\nEntry 17:\n\nI recently got a job, so I stole back into Verglass and got my diary back. I'm very glad I didn't get caught, because I wasn't able to wear my hood. The people who employed me (The Di Silvari's) asked me not to wear it. I'm taking\n\ncare to be cautious, however. Verglass and Gren are a little too close for comfort, but I'll have to make do. I'm still worried about them notifying Will. Lucia seems nice enough. I hope we can become good friends. I'm still not sure about Lucius and\n\nGathius, though. I'm not sure if I can trust them... Also, Ivan and I have been fighting. He recently was killed (yet saved by the monks) for murder. I cast him out of my life, but somehow I still feel empty. He's not the little brother I remember though.\n\nEntry 18:\n\nI just came back from a walk where the most horrible thing imaginable happened. I had sat down by the lakeside in greymarsh when I heard a sound. There was a man standing behind me. I drew my knife on him, but he had clawed\n\ngauntlets and looked so frightening that I dropped my knife. As soon as I did, he kicked it in the lake. He cornered me and was asking why I was walking about. When I reluctantly told him about Ivan, he seemed not surprised. I wonder who he was... his\n\nface was hooded so I couldn't tell. He was also asking where I lived. I think he's trying to stalk me. I hope he goes away soon...\n\nEntry 19:\n\nThe same thing happened to me today. The man caught me on the road and eventually forced me onto the ground. His clawed gauntlets dug into my head. He removed his mask eventually, and I thought I recognized\n\nhim. He said that I did know him, but he wouldn't say his name. He said he was going to kill me, so I tried to stop him by saying Ivan wouldn't be happy about it. I know I went on a limb about the 'knowing Ivan' thing, but I had my suspicions. Soon after\n\nI mentioned that, however, he ran off. He said he would be back another time. Maybe I shouldn't go on the roads anymore...\n\nEntry 20:\n\nIvan and I made up at a dwarven festival, but it was soon spoiled. I told him about my blood oath that I am to take in a month's time. He became so angry that it frightened me. He made me promise not to take the oath and cut my arm to 'help me\n\nremember'. I don't know what to do... I want to take the oath, but Ivan is threatening to kill me if I do. I wish we could just go back to those days in Abresi when father was still here...\n\n\n\n     Snow's Diary\n\n\n\nTo always remember...\n\nEntry 1:\n\nIt's been a few weeks since I took my oath to the di Silvari house. I am now known as Snow Eversong. It seems I am to be a maid for the rest of my life. I don't mind, however. I'm finally free of the prison of nobility. I can go where I please,\n\nwhenever I please. No one tells me how to speak or who I should marry. I can be my own person. The scars in my hands remind me that I am not completely free, but no matter. As long as I can have the wilderness, nothing else matters.\n\nEntry 2:\n\nMonths have gone by slowly, like the crawling of a snail. My hands have become hard with the work I am doing and I find that I'm constantly washing my hair to keep the dirt out of it. Perhaps I should go exploring again...", ""),
        StaticBook("Notebook Vol. 2", "§bZanderaw", "General Compositions for Solo Piano and Cello\n\n\n\n\nLucia de Silvarois\n\n*Even thicker than the first notebook, this contains a wide range of compositions. One can almost tell which mood Lucia was in when she wrote them: in some parts the notes are thickly written and sharp, while in others they seem to flow across the page.\n\nThe margins are in many places once again filled with general notes to herself, and even the occasional poem in Auvergnian, most of which are mediocre at best: simply ways for the author to release stress and think. It's clear that none of this was\n\nintended to be shown to others.\n\nAround the halfway point in the notebook marks when she got her hands on a cello, for these pages are suddenly filled with experimentation with the instrument, mixed in with further piano.*\n\n((More Bach! Hope you aren't completely over it by now. This one corresponds to both the second book of \"Well Tempered Clavier\" and his solo suites for cello, the first of which in particular is excellent.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Samuel di Silvari\n     son of Marcus\n\n\n\n((The book has black binding and gold writing.))\n\nSun's Smile\n        21st\n        1448\n\n\"I arrived at my uncle's lands todays. His anger still burns most hotly at my father. Can I blame him in all honesty? Nay, my father was a fool and an ass. I wonder how my mother and\n\nsiblings are doing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oswin's Memoir's", "Darez14", "Ways to Tackle Hiylu's\nBloodthirsty Urges.\n\n1.Make her hurt the others around her. X\n\n2.Physical and Mental\nTraining. X\n\n3. Use the weird relaxing mushroom to concoct a Potion of sorts.................\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nMade By Oswin Orman..\nThe one that hurts all and is a curse upon everyone... *a tear drop* Hiylu i'm sorry...", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "SirNublet", "Dear Duchess, I wish to buy an area of land in the Duchy of Avurgne for farming purposes. The plot of land is located to the left of the bridge over the river coming from Abresi, if one was coming over the bridge from Abresi. Please reply and tell me if\n\nthis plot of land is for sale.\n\nSigned,\nSheon Ryder", ""),
        StaticBook("Lesson Time", "ski_king3", "Dear Sarah,\n\nI believe it is time for your first lesson. As such, please meet me in Salvus at your nearest convenience. I will be by the fountain.\n\n~Rose", ""),
        StaticBook("Boundwise Brews", "Pepernoot", "The Boundwise homebrews are all made with great care by the halflings of the Vale. The hops and herbs are selected with great care from the lush and fertile farms of Lenfarthing.\n\nCurrently two brews are available;\n\nBounderale\n----------\nA strong lightly coloured ale with a high proof, with a light fruity and sweet taste. Not recommended for the younguns.\n\nBounderbeer\n-----------\nA light beer with a hint of herbs, perfect drink with a meal or after a long hot day.\n\nTo order one of the brews, send a bird to Dudo Boundwise or Pansy Boundwise, Lenfarthing.\n\n((Pepernoot/fbPatty))", ""),
        StaticBook("The Last King", "§b0CT4V10", "The Last King\n\nForgotten and lost\nIn fallen Syrus\nRests the last King\n\nInforsaken Syrus\nWhere the white sun\nWanders the skies\nThere rests the last son of Mephis\n\nDefiant and rot\nIn proud Syrus\nStood the last King\n\nIn gleaming Syrus\nWhose white walls once\nresisted the tide\nThere sood the last son of Mephis\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nWe are purified\nIn the possibility of purpose\nBoth lost and found\nBy the rising tide\n\nIn the idea\nThat solely our god exists\nThere is some solace\nAnd we are found\n\nI walk through this forest\nhounded by the shadow\nIt howls at the edge of my sight.\nIt howls at the edge of my understanding.\nIt is death, and it pursues me relentlessly.\nIt is my shadow, and is behind me at every turn.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nGreat pillars of red stone\nWhite steps of ice\nUnopenable ice doors\nFar away\nClosed.\n\n*Hastily written. The script is messy and scrawling.*\n\nA FLOATING BLACK PALACE\nTETHERED TO THIS WORLD WITH ORICALCUM CHAINS\nTHE DARK ONES HOME\n\nTHE SHADOW IS COMING\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nThe shadow's gaze turns from me. To a group of Teutons.\n\nI am safe.\n\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\n\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\nKILL HIM\n\nKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLKILL\n\nKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILLKILL", ""),
