        StaticBook("Letter to Erito", "Benben582", "To Erito Doragon,\n\nHello Erito. I've heard word that you are interested in joining the force. Sail here and you will be offered a position on the Force. Gallmore and her people await you.\n\n~Senator Ogrim Frostbeard", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Distiller's\n             Journal\n\n          Gestahl\n          VonSchlichten\n\nRubber Mash\n-------------------Vines-Water Breath\nSugarcane-Water breath, Blindness\nWheat-Water Breath\nJungle-Strength,Water breathing, Blindness\nSpruce-Str/Blind/Wtr\nRose-Water Breath\n\nFruit Rubber Mash\n---------------\nCarrot- Heal, Breath, Blind\nRose-Water, Blind.\nYellow Flower-Jump\n\nGreen Speckled Mash\n------------------\nWheat-Poison/Jump\nCarrot-Jump/Mining Fat\nRedShroom- Jump/MF\nRotFlesh- Jump!\nRedRose- Jump!\nVine-Poison Jump\n\nMossy Rubbery Mash\n_________________\nCarrot- Def/WaterBreth\nSugar- Def/WtrBrth\nRose- Wither/Res/Water\nWheat-Water Breath\nPump-Def/Waterbreath", ""),
        StaticBook("A Printed Sheet", "§bMandru VonSchlichten", "THE FIRST PRINTED WORK OF THE 15th CENTURY\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\nIn the beginning was nothing. Then a most supreme being created our world, Aegis. He made Man and Woman, whom had 4 sons: Malin, Horen, Urguan, and Krug.\n\nAll of them were created with their own strengths and abilities. All of them were created equal. They fought Iblees, eventually, in a great war. Each of them were cursed by him: Orcs to be ugly, Humans to have shot lives, Elves to be\n\ninfertile, and Dwarves to be greedy.\n\nThis is the short version of the beginning of our history, as according to the Works of the Wandering Wizard.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "SEA TREK\n      -=-=-=-=-\n\n        Book #1\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nSeries by\nMandru VonSchlichten\nPh. D and M.D.\n\nChapter 1\n=======\nCaptain Rhames P. Quirk sat on the bridge of the G.R.S. Endeavour. The council of the Gallmorian Republic had just given his crew permission to leave port for their year-long mission of\n\nexploration.\n\nHe turned to his Hansetian Navigator, Gestahl.\n\n\"It looks like they're finally letting us leave...\" he mutters.\n\n\"Ja!\" The Hansetian said excitedly.\n\nGestahl was not just a navigator. Gestahl was, indeed, a wizard as well. A fire wizard. Therefore, he also served as tactical officer in addition to navigator.\n\n\"Captain, the labrotory has been fully\n\nstocked for our journey,\" A blue elf, who's name was Varstivus, remarked.\n\nVarstivus was the science officer aboard the G.R.S. Endeavour.", ""),
