        StaticBook("Pass: Shin Snow", "§bCharles_Grimlie", "Name: Shin Snow\n\nOccupation: Freelance\n\nDate of Issue: 16th The First Seed, 1453\n\nIssued by: Ser Rosencrantz\n\nDescription: White Hair, Full Beard, Pale Skin, and Blue eyes.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Fish Catalogue:\nA list of all the different fish I have caught.\n\n-Swordfish\n-Scomber\n-Barrelfish\n-Sunfish\n-Mooneye\n-Lakefish\n-Treefish\n-Cowfish\n\n-Mackerel\n-Herring\n-Bonefish\n-Eel\n-Nemofish\n-Spittail\n-Wormfish\n-Oinkfish\n-Mooshroomfish\n-Ribbontail\n-Catfish\n-Moltenfish\n-Perch\n\n-Mudsucker\n-Piranha\n-Rainbowfish\n-Flounder\n-Anglefish\n-Stonefish\n-Goldfish", ""),
        StaticBook("A Wolvengard", "§bLord Commander Starke McHaryn", "*The sealed envelope \nbears a snarling black wolf, the stamp pressed into the soft wax, the seal unbroken, it bears the arms of McHaryn, Starke's nameimprinted clearly on the letter*\n\n22nd of Snow Maidens, 1442.\n\nHail thy most gracious Master Tuv.\n\nI write to ye with a humble proposition. The Wolvengard have always considered themselves to be friends of Abresi and her citizens.\n\nAt this time the Wolvengard have many fine steeds for sale, in my ventures this passed month to Abresi I noticed her unfortunate lack of horses.\n\nWell my good sir, we have problems that could perhaps solve themselves.\n\nI have vast amounts of horses I don't need, while Abresi has what appears to be a shortage of steeds.\n\nForgive me if this observation is incorrect.\n\nWith utmost respect, and many well wishes.\n\nSigned: Lord Commander Starke McHaryn.\n\nRuler of Storm Shank, and Crowsfoot, humble leader of the Wolvengard.\n\n*The end of the letter is stamped with the McHaryn crest*", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Building Log-Book\n-------------------This is a log book for the progfits of The Heroes Hollow\n-------------------Profits Made: 37+26+8+50+18+12+20+10+60+10+330+100+10+20+30+12+8+50+25+12+25+10+", ""),
        StaticBook("A Battered Book", "Patriotic_Fool", "*The old, weathered tome is full of writing. The title reads 'Raven Manifesto'.*\n\nThere are two types of beings; good and evil. Any alignment results from a mixture of these two essences. A pendulum swinging from side to side, one being the most heinous evil, the other being the purest good.\n\nThere is a term many are familiar with - Justice. Should the scale be tipped too far in one direction, Justice is the force that returns the scale back to neutral. A problem arises, however, when the scale is tipped too far in one direction, for too long.\n\nFocusing on being good and just is the most noble of goals, and these good actions allow negative ones to be cancelled out. What if one commits horrendous crimes, and continually escapes Justice?  What if the scale is never balanced; Justice is never\n\nserved? The Ravens are Justice. We right the wrongs of evil men, and they suffer as their victims have suffered. The Law is an instrument that allows for criminals to escape Justice, and it allows corrupt men to profit from the demise of others.\n\nThere is only one Law, and that is of the Ravens. \n\n=Disobedience is Justice=\n\nBy atoning for the wrongs of the past, the Ravens open a path for salvation and restitution for the criminals. By paying for what they have done, the wicked free themselves and are restored to the natural balance.\n\nThrough their suffering, they are freed.\n\n=Cruelty is Grace=\n\n==Edicts of the Raven==\n\n1.  A Raven must have absolute loyalty to the Ravens, and they must always come first, regardless of all else.\n\n2. A Raven must never kill an Innocent.\n\n3. No Raven shall harm or steal from another Raven, we are brothers and sisters. \n\n4. Secrecy is paramount, for the Ravens do not go around proclaiming their affiliations.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nAbove all, our secrets and status must be kept close to a Raven’s heart, even through torture, even to the grave.", ""),
